window.FWN_LEGEND_OF_SWORDSMAN_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_LEGEND_OF_SWORDSMAN_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":5101,"title":"Chapter 5101 Bricklaying in the Great Desolate Wilderness (1)","paragraphs":["Following that, he changed his tone, saying, \"If you still won't speak, I have many ways to make you suffer a thousand, ten thousand times more than staying in that tiny bone armor!\"","However, the black-robed figure paid no heed to his words, stubbornly repeating the same phrase, \"One who gazes upon the Secret Text shall perish!\"","Zhen Wuyang grew furious and directly swung his arm, instantly unleashing chains formed from the Emperor's aura, which lashed viciously at the black-robed figure.","With a single lash, a menacing crack appeared all around the black-robed figure.","Then, nine chains simultaneously struck down.","The overwhelming dark purple brilliance dispersed as the black-robed figure's body visibly vanished at an incredible speed.","\"It's of no benefit to you to remain silent. Speaking might bring you some relief,\" Zhen Wuyang said calmly.","Even on the brink of life and death, the black-robed figure repeated the same phrase as before.","\"One who gazes upon the Secret Text shall perish!\"","\"You seek death!\" Zhen Wuyang shouted, and all nine chains lashed down together!","It was evident that once all the chains descended, the black-robed figure would undoubtedly disappear.","Jian Wushuang's heart sank, wanting to save the black-robed figure.","However, Yu Chang acted first, raising his hand to stop the nine chains of the Emperor's fate energy, standing in front of Zhen However, Yu Chang acted first, raising his hand to stop the nine chains of the Emperor's fate energy, standing in front of Zhen Wuyang.","\"Yu Chang, what are you doing?\" Zhen Wuyang furrowed his brow, puzzled.","Yu Chang cupped his hands and said, \"My Lord, he cannot die. This involves many matters, and acting recklessly may be detrimental to many things.\"","Zhen Wuyang frowned, contemplating the meaning behind Yu Chang's words. After a moment, he said, \"Very well, imprison him.\"","Upon hearing this, Yu Chang nodded, then turned to look at the black-robed figure. He extended his hand, and layers of dark ink-like auras appeared. Afterward, he enveloped the black-robed figure and tucked it back into his sleeve.","With the disappearance of the black-robed figure, the indescribable oppressive atmosphere vanished completely.","The entire SkySide Cloud Platform returned to its usual state of calm and tranquility.","Unable to extract any useful information from the black-robed figure, Zhen Wuyang was left feeling frustrated.","He then turned to Jian Wushuang, his eyes filled only with resentment.","\"...\"","\"What Secret Text were inside those bone armor pieces that we couldn't even extract information from?\"","\"Well... it's not much. Just when we were about to figure out something, that figure in the black-robed figure burst out and destroyed the bone armor.\"","The voice of Zhen Wuyang rose abruptly. \"So, after all this trouble and nearly destroying half of my Great Mi Heaven, we ended up with nothing?\"","Jian Wushuang felt rather embarrassed. \"...You could say that.\"","Zhen Wuyang was furious, turning to look at the Divine Craftsman Xu Tuo. \"Xu Tuo, I demand the truth. What were the hidden messages on the bone armor?\"","The divine craftsman Xu Tuo slowly opened his eyes. \"Your Majesty, as Young Friend Jian has said, Xu Tuo truly knows nothing about it.\"","Upon hearing this, Zhen Wuyang felt speechless.","At this moment, Yu Chang spoke, \"In this Great Si Region, every speck of dust and every Heavenly Region has gone through countless trials and tribulations to reach its current prosperity.\"","\"The purpose of the Heavenly Court is to shelter countless Heavenly Regions, to ensure their eternal prosperity, and to guide innumerable prodigies towards their own paths.\"","\"However, this unnecessary conflict has turned nearly a hundred Heavenly Regions, along with countless sentient beings, into dust, obliterating everything.\"","\"This has exceeded what the Heavenly Court can tolerate. The previous Grand Yan Immortal who wiped out nearly ten Heavenly Regions was already sealed within the Endless Sea, enduring endless emptiness.\"","\"And now, the extent of destruction you've caused to the heavenly realms far exceeds any previous conflict. Punishment is inevitable.\"","Yu Chang passed judgment and looked at Zhen Wuyang.","At this moment, the disciples of the Sancun Mountain, Divine Craftsman Xu Tuo, Nan Xuan, and Prince Jiu were all extremely nervous.","Punishment from the Endless Sea, the Emperor's punishment, was the most severe of all.","Once these punishments were imposed, it was almost equivalent to a death sentence.","At this point, Jian Wushuang stepped forward, cupping his hands and said, \"This conflict was caused entirely by me. They are all victims and have nothing to do with it. I will take full responsibility.\"","\"Who said anything about punishing them?\" Zhen Wuyang looked at him and said in a deep voice, \"Today, I will only punish you, and it will be a severe punishment!\"","\"I am willing to accept it,\" Jian Wushuang said firmly, cupping his hands in response.","Jian Wushuang had been sentenced to a rather unusual punishment. The Zhen Wuyang spoke in a stern tone, \"Tell me, what kind of punishment do you desire?\"","\"Any punishment will do,\" Jian Wushuang replied.","\"Very well, you spirited lad! Then, I, as your Emperor, decree that you shall go to the Great Desolate Wilderness and labor as a bricklayer for 10,000 years!\"","\"...Bricklaying?!\" Jian Wushuang was left speechless.","\"Yes, off to the Great Desolate Wilderness with you, and you shall serve your sentence for a full 10,000 years!\"","...","The intense and warm energy dissipated, the rolling clouds gradually disappeared, replaced by a gloomy overcast sky. Massive thunderstorms, as formidable as dragons, brewed within the dark clouds, accompanied by colossal whirlwinds, creating an apocalyptic scene.","Amidst this treacherous void, even Yan Immortals dared not linger, and yet, a colossal bird soared through the tumultuous sky.","This enormous bird was as dark as ink, and its wingspan was so vast that it could cover several heavenly realms beneath its feathers.","It was so massive that even the dragon-like lightning within the stormy clouds seemed minuscule in comparison.","Seated upon the back of this giant avian creature were two figures: one was Yu Chang, and the other was Jian Wushuang.","Even the frozen gusts of cosmic energy could be devoured within this void, and even Jian Wushuang felt a bone-chilling cold.","This was a void unlike any they had ever seen before. There were no heavenly realms, no trace of Yan power, only desolation and emptiness.","This was an intensely dark void, devoid of stars, and aside from the occasional bursts of lightning, there was no other color.","Perched on the bird's head, Jian Wushuang had no idea where he was anymore.","The giant bird could traverse thousands of Heavenly Regions with a single flap of its wings, indicating they had ventured far from the central region of the Great Si Region.","'Could it be that the so-called Great Desolate Wilderness is the border of the Great Si Region?' Jian Wushuang thought with a shiver.","At that moment, Yu Chang suddenly turned around, his gentle face looking at him. \"You guessed right; the so-called Great Desolate Wilderness is indeed the border of the Great Si Region.\"","Jian Wushuang was taken aback. \"How did you know what I was thinking?\"","Yu Chang smiled faintly. \"I simply guessed. It would be strange if you weren't pondering this question.\"","Jian Wushuang fell silent, still puzzled about how these Emperors always seemed to know what other Yan Immortals were thinking.","After a moment, Yu Chang spoke again, \"We are now far from the central region of the Great Si Region and heading toward the border.\"","He was slightly stunned. Over 20,000 years had passed since his ascension to the Divine Power Universe, and he had spent nearly that entire time revolving around the Great Si Region."]},{"number":5102,"title":"Chapter 5102 Bricklaying in the Great Desolate Wilderness (2)","paragraphs":["The vast expanse, encompassing countless Heavenly Regions, had even begun to raise doubts in Jian Wushuang's mind.","Did the Great Si Region truly have boundaries?","Now, receiving precise information from Yu Chang's mouth, it made Jian Wushuang feel a slight unease.","If the Great Si Region alone was so vast and boundless, how would the ultimate Great Yan Domain manifest before his eyes?","And where would Xuan Yi, Old Master, and the others exist in this ultimate Great Yan Domain, and in what form?","Just as Jian Wushuang was lost in thought, Yu Chang spoke slowly, \"You've seen it for yourself. Not all the voids in the Heavenly Regions can give birth to Planes. The closer you get to the boundary, the less likely it is for Planes to exist.\"","\"The boundary of the Great Si Region, where the Emperors can expand, is the limit. Here, even the power of creation cannot exist, and further expansion has no meaning.\"","\"So, we define the boundary of the Great Si Region as the Great Desolate Wilderness.\"","In a few brief words, Yu Chang outlined the contours of the Great Si Region for Jian Wushuang, giving him some understanding.","Then, Jian Wushuang stood up, facing the gusts of wind that were enough to make even celestial beings tremble. He gazed through layers of dark clouds into the endless void.","\"Is there a greater expanse beyond the Great Si Region?\"","\"You might be disappointed. Beyond the Great Si Region lies the boundless Great Desolate Wilderness. Even the Grand Yan Immortals can become lost in the Great Desolate Wilderness and eventually turn to dust.\"","Jian Wushuang found it hard to believe. \"So, outside the Great Si Region, is there only the boundless Great Desolate Wilderness?\"","\"Of course not,\" Yu Chang smiled. \"While the Great Desolate Wilderness may be boundless, it still has boundaries. Beyond those boundaries, there are many domains similar to the Great Si Region, dazzling and incomprehensible.\"","Jian Wushuang's heart burned with excitement. He felt that even his dormant heart was beginning to stir.","Infinite existence meant infinite possibilities, and everything was within reach!","At this moment, he thought of something else and looked at Yu Chang. \"Lord Yu, may I ask, what is the nearest great domain adjacent to the Great Si Region called?\"","Yu Chang gazed at him with a smile and asked, \"Why do you ask? Are you thinking of leaving the Great Si Region?\"","\"No, no, I was just curious...\" Jian Wushuang hesitated.","\"This isn't something that can't be discussed, but very few Yan Immortals within the Great Si Region know about this,\" replied Yu Chang.","\"The great domain adjacent to the Great Si Region, at the boundary of the vast Great Desolate Wilderness... that great domain is known as the Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm.\"","Jian Wushuang's heart skipped a beat. \"The Heaven-Reaching... Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm?!\"","The person inquired, \"What's the matter, do you know of that place?\"","\"No, I don't know it. It just sounds somewhat intriguing,\" Jian Wushuang replied.","Yu Chang gazed ahead, as if reminiscing. \"I once had an out-of-body experience there. All the Buddhist leaders there are quite stubborn and extreme, which gave me some unfavorable impressions.\"","'It's too much of a coincidence that the neighboring Great Si Region happens to be the Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm...' Jian Wushuang thought to himself, feeling astonished.","Memories from the past surfaced once again. Although he had never been to the so-called Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm, it seemed to have developed some connection with him unknowingly.","In the Sand Demon Cavern, encountering the Blood Sea led to him being involved with Karma. It was a strange affliction caused great killing tribulations, known as 'karmic calamity'.","Before her death, the Sand Demon Cave's master, Sha Qing, entrusted him with the knowledge that the only way to resolve the karmic calamity was to go to the Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm.","This was what had linked Jian Wushuang to the Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm.","Now, after the passage of over 20,000 years, the Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm, nearly relegated to his memories, surged back into his thoughts.","'Should I go to the Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm or not?' Jian Wushuang pondered in his heart, while also worrying about the karmic calamity he bore.","The so-called karmic calamity was like a crack, initially not posing significant harm, but it was a hidden danger.","This kind of hidden danger would grow with the host's continuous strengthening, eventually becoming impossible to ignore.","Currently, Jian Wushuang had no way to deal with this significant karmic calamity, but he knew that if he did not clear it in time, it would thoroughly destroy his refined Divine Sense.","So, he couldn't overlook any clues related to the Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm.","Because of a woman and a karmic calamity, Jian Wushuang established a connection with the Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm.","Certainly, these were all things that Yu Chang didn't know, and naturally, he didn't think in that direction.","Yu Chang continued, \"So, my knowledge of the Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm is not very good, and even the Emperor looks down on that place.\"","At this point, he looked at Jian Wushuang and continued, \"So what you have to do when you come to this border, the Great Desolate Wilderness is to lay bricks, work hard to lay bricks.\"","\"Ah, really? Is it really laying bricks?\"","\"That can't be fake; the Emperor doesn't jest.\"","...","I don't know how long it had passed, how many leaps through the void had been made, even time had lost all meaning, until Jian Wushuang became completely numb, everything finally made progress.","\"Up ahead is the Great Desolate Wilderness,\" Yu Chang said.","Jian Wushuang's spirit shook, and he got up to look ahead.","He saw that the originally pitch-black void had a dim light and solid ground.","Wait, solid ground?!","How could there be solid ground in the desolate void of the Great Desolate Wilderness where even dust couldn't exist?","But when the giant bird under him landed steadily on that solid ground, Jian Wushuang truly believed it.","Here, at the boundary of the Great Si Region, in the void of the Great Desolate Wilderness, there actually existed in the form of solid ground.","The boundless earth stretched as far as the eye could see in every direction in the void.","The giant bird, standing steadily on the ground, raised its head and let out a long cry, then transformed into a palm-sized Chasing Bird and flew into Yu Chang's palm, disappearing.","\"No, it's not land.\"","Standing on the ground, Jian Wushuang's face changed slightly, and he quickly realized that the ground under his feet was not real earth but was made up of countless Immortal bones!","Yu Chang looked at him approvingly and said, \"Yes, this Great Desolate Wilderness border cannot possibly have solid ground; this solid ground is actually paved with the bones of Peak Cultivators, Yan Immortals, and even Grand Yan Immortals.\"","\"These are all the bones of cultivators and Yan Immortals from the Great Si Region?\" Jian Wushuang's gaze became heavy.","There were simply too many, to the point of being unimaginable.","How many cultivators and Yan Immortals' bones were needed to fill the entire void of the Great Desolate Wilderness like this?!","Yu Chang nodded, as if describing a trivial matter, \"Indeed, they are all the bones of cultivators and Yan Immortals from the Great Si Region, with the bones of Grand Yan Immortals accounting for 70 percent of them.\"","Jian Wushuang was shocked. To completely cover this Great Desolate Wilderness border, what kind of brutal battles must have been fought in that Ancient Era?","The establishment of a Heavenly Court required the extermination of so many Yan Immortals, didn't it?","He also began to understand why Yan Immortals were so rare in the Great Si Region now, and Grand Yan Immortals were almost non-existent.","The reasons for this, I'm afraid, can be traced back to the War of the Emperors in that Ancient Era."]},{"number":5103,"title":"Chapter 5103 Start Bricklaying","paragraphs":["Jian Wushuang had spent nearly 20,000 years in the pursuit of the ultimate knowledge within the vast expanse of time. During these two millennia, he had managed to uncover many of the ancient secrets, even those hidden from the most knowledgeable of Grand Yan Immortals.","The Ancient Era was a time when multiple Emperors coexisted, and countless prodigies emerged, each forging their own supreme Dao.","To Jian Wushuang's knowledge, there were five Emperor Sovereigns, each presiding over their respective Heavenly Courts within the Great Si Region, governing their domains.","They were Yang Jun, Su He, Daodong, Fenghua, and Liu Ya, representing the Great Si Region.","However, numerous other EmperorS existed as well. The Ancient Era was a prosperous era, with a multitude of Emperors, not to mention the Grand Yan Immortals.","However, with the appearance of Zhen Wuyang, everything eventually turned to dust. According to Jian Wushuang's knowledge, nearly ten Emperor had perished at the hands of Zhen Wuyang, and as for the Grand Yan Immortals, they were even more numerous.","Jian Wushuang also understood why there were so few remains of Grand Yan Immortals in the Great Si Region. It turned out that all their remains had been pushed into the Great Desolate Wilderness to fill its borders.","This was a long-buried secret, one that had lost much of its significance, whether known or not.","Stepping onto the boundless land paved with the bones of countless Grand Yan Immortals, Jian Wushuang walked alongside Yu Chang at a leisurely pace.","\"The Great Desolate Wilderness is endless, and the bones beneath our feet are also endless. The Emperor have sent you here as a punishment, but it's a necessary measure to warn and unite the others.\"","\"Moreover, the Emperor decided to send you to the Great Desolate Wilderness as a result of our joint discussions.\"","\"There are two reasons for this: firstly, to serve as a warning and unification; secondly, the Great Desolate Wilderness does indeed require some renovations.\"","\"Renovations?\" Jian Wushuang looked at him, somewhat puzzled.","Yu Chang nodded. \"Indeed, that's correct. This vast Great Desolate Wilderness is also in need of some renovation.\"","Jian Wushuang found it difficult to comprehend. \"Are you saying that even in a place where Yan power cannot exist, there may be Grand Yan Immortals?\"","Yu Chang replied, \"Indeed, it's highly unlikely that any Grand Yan Immortals would come to this place, not even the Grand Yan Immortals themselves would step into this Great Desolate Wilderness. However, in all things, there are exceptions.\"","Yu Chang spoke, and with a wave of his arm, a wild gust of dust swirled up on this Immortal Bone Road.","As the duststorm roared to life, faint traces of something began to emerge on the Immortal Bone Road.","Jian Wushuang instinctively looked down at the footprints appearing on the road of Immortal bones. \"These footprints, what are they?\"","\"They're trouble,\" replied Yu Chang with a faint smile. \"You are the first Yan Immortal to venture into the Great Desolate Wilderness apart from those Monks.\"","\"Those Monks? Why are they here in the Great Desolate Wilderness?\" Jian Wushuang couldn't believe it.","Yu Chang explained, \"They measure the earth with their own feet, and they also seek to convert all Yan Immortal, heading to their Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm for worship.\"","\"Most importantly, they consider this Great Desolate Wilderness a place of trial and have come here one after another.\"","Jian Wushuang was taken aback. \"Their ideas are indeed unique. They see this place as a trial ground?\"","Yan power cannot be retained here, and it is boundless and boundless. Even a Grand Yan Immortal might lose their way here. Comparing this Great Desolate Wilderness to a tomb would be more accurate.","\"That's right, even I didn't expect them to be so determined,\" Yu Chang said, looking at Jian Wushuang. \"Wushuang, what you need to do is stay here and strengthen the barriers of the Great Desolate Wilderness.\"","\"Stay here for 10,000 years?\" Jian Wushuang sighed.","10,000 years is a period of seclusion for Yan Immortal and even Peak Cultivators, not a long time at all. But for Jian Wushuang, it's different. His growth rate is too fast, and 10,000 years is enough time for him to accomplish many things.","Right now, he's going to be exiled in the Great Desolate Wilderness for 10,000 years, which greatly limits any of his actions.","Yu Chang seemed to see the disappointment in his eyes and smiled. \"10,000 years is not that long, but it's just a figure of speech. If the Emperor hadn't said that back then, the Second Prince probably wouldn't have given up so easily. After all, it was his Grand Mi Heaven that was destroyed.\"","\"In 1,000 years, I will come to the Great Desolate Wilderness to get you, but of course, that depends on your performance.\"","Jian Wushuang breathed a sigh of relief secretly. 1,000years is not too distant for him, and he can consider it as an opportunity for training in the Great Desolate Wilderness.","\"Alright, so what am I supposed to do here in the Great Desolate Wilderness next?\"","\"Of course, you'll be building walls and reinforcing barriers.\"","\"Oh, so it really is bricklaying, huh?\"","\"Of course.\"","As they continued their conversation, two figures moved forward at a leisurely pace until they reached a wall that seemed to split the very void in half. It wasn't so much a wall as it was a true Immortal barrier!","It was as if the road of Immortal bones had been rolled up by some supreme power, towering high and almost completely separating the entire void into two halves.","Even the Grand Yan Immortal Immortal, standing beneath this Immortal barrier that felt like the pinnacle of divinity, would still feel insignificant.","\"This is the true boundary of the Great Si Region, and it also marks the edge that separates it from the Great Desolate Wilderness,\" said Yu Chang, looking at Jian Wushuang, who had become somewhat entranced. \"And what you must do now is to gradually repair this boundary barrier.\"","\"Repair, repair this place?\" Jian Wushuang struggled to swallow, a hint of bitterness in his eyes.","\"Yes,\" Yu Chang nodded slightly. \"This boundary barrier was forged by the Emperor and me, capable of repelling all foes and enduring countless ages without damage.\"","\"However, on the other side of the Great Desolate Wilderness, the monks from the Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm managed to damage this boundary barrier using some method, allowing them to enter the Great Si Region.\"","\"And what you must do, Wushuang, is to completely seal off this boundary barrier, blocking all enemies from entering the Great Desolate Wilderness.\"","Jian Wushuang nodded. \"Alright, I will.\"","At this moment, Yu Chang put away his smile and turned serious. \"Remember, Wushuang, this is a punishment. This is the most dangerous place in the entire Great Si Region. Even the Grand Yan Immortal Immortals can hardly be considered significant here.\"","\"As soon as you step into the Great Desolate Wilderness, you must be prepared for anything. You will not only face the weakness of your Immortal body but also the enemies hidden within the Great Desolate Wilderness.\"","Jian Wushuang's gaze slightly hardened. \"Enemies within the Great Desolate Wilderness? Are there other Yan Immortals in the Great Desolate Wilderness?\"","Yu Chang nodded. \"To be precise, they can no longer be called Yan Immortals. They are more like lingering obsessions, wandering lost in the Great Desolate Wilderness.\"","\"After I leave, any Yan Immortals or Monks who emerge from the Great Desolate Wilderness will be your enemies. Your task is to thoroughly block all enemies from entering the boundary, sparing no one.\""]},{"number":5104,"title":"Chapter 5104 Repairing the Boundary Barrier","paragraphs":["Yu Chang departed.","After entrusting Jian Wushuang with some instructions, he left.","Leaving only Jian Wushuang alone on the road of Immortal bones, at the boundary of the Great Desolate Wilderness.","He stood in place, feeling the endless ancient aura while contemplating the meaning behind Yu Chang's words.","\"In this Great Desolate Wilderness, can Yan Immortals still approach and walk within it?\"","\"And what exactly is that so-called Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm beyond the Great Desolate Wilderness?\"","\"And those guys actually consider completing the Great Desolate Wilderness as part of their own trials?\"","Jian Wushuang thought of the group of Monks he had encountered in the Sand Demon Cave, and he had also received some information during his discussion with Konglun.","Those leaders of the monks who roamed the Sand Demon Cave had indeed come from the Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm.","After the events in the Sand Demon Cave, Jian Wushuang had no goodwill towards those Monk leaders, especially the few Grand Yan Immortals among them.","But only Konglun, the monk, had left a positive impression on Jian Wushuang.","The discussion in the Blood Sea had been quite enlightening.","In any case, for Jian Wushuang, the Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm beyond the Great Desolate Wilderness held little appeal.","After roughly sorting out some conclusions, Jian Wushuang began to move forward.","In the boundless and limitless Great Desolate Wilderness, there were no borders, and everything seemed shrouded in thick dust. There were no Heavenly Region Planes or grand suns and stars.","There was only a vague gloom.","Yu Chang had not been wrong when he said that even Grand Yan Immortals would eventually get lost here.","But Jian Wushuang felt no abnormalities. His mind and Divine Sense had long reached a terrifying level of integration and perfection.","In the Great Desolate Wilderness, it had, in fact, proven to be a good place for cultivation for him.","Stepping on the road of Immortal bones, Jian Wushuang looked at the boundary barrier that split the void into two before him, and he quickly understood what Yu Chang wanted him to repair.","In the very center of this vast boundary barrier, there was a crack, only as thin as a strand of hair.","It was as if an external force had torn open a rift, rendering the boundary barrier no longer whole.","This crack appeared as just a thin line, but when Jian Wushuang truly went to examine it, he realized what an insurmountable abyss it was!","The entire boundary barrier was overwhelmingly vast and boundless, so even a single crack, no matter how small, could not be mended.","Jian Wushuang stood in the center of this crack and couldn't help but feel overwhelmed.","This crack was truly too immense; it might take the combined effort of millions of Heavenly Region Planes to completely fill it!","Currently, Jian Wushuang could easily move a typical Heavenly Region Plane within the Great Si Region.","But the difficulty lay in the fact that this was the Great Desolate Wilderness, and as far as the eye could see, it was all desolation.","There were no Heavenly Region Planes here, no Yan power to replenish, only relying on his own slow recovery of Yan power.","In this way, repairing this boundary barrier was an enormous challenge!","Since there were no Heavenly Region Planes to use, Jian Wushuang turned his attention to the road of Immortal bones beneath his feet.","This boundary barrier, much like the road of Immortal bones, was constructed from the bones of ancient immortals. To repair it, he could only use the bones on the ground.","Without hesitation, after roughly calculating the gaps between the cracks in the boundary barrier, Jian Wushuang suddenly unleashed his own energy.","In the Great Desolate Wilderness, Yan power hadn't appeared for countless eons.","So when Jian Wushuang released his Yan poower, the entire boundless void and the Great Desolate Wilderness erupted in turmoil.","Thick dust was drawn into the vortex created by the Yan power, swirling in the void, causing everything to tremble.","Lightning, as massive as dragons, flickered within the vortex, ready to tear the void apart at any moment.","Here, there was no Heavenly Dao, only chaos and primordial conditions.","Then, in the next moment, hundreds and thousands of lightning bolts, each resembling a colossal dragon, simultaneously struck Jian Wushuang, who was radiating Yan power.","\"...\"","Boom!","Even the road of Immortal bones trembled, and vast stretches of Immortal bone fragments turned into dust.","As for Jian Wushuang, who was facing the heavenly lightning with his body, he was fiercely blasted into the depths of the earth.","The heavenly lightning couldn't cause too much harm to Jian Wushuang, who possessed an Undying and Imperishable Immortal Body, but they still left him in a sorry state.","When the thunder and lightning gradually subsided, he walked out of the earth looking quite disheveled.","\"Don't tell me I have to endure this kind of punishment every time I release any Yan power?\" Jian Wushuang wondered.","He decided to give it another try.","The surging and powerful Yan power flowed through his meridians again and radiated outward.","However, this time, it did not trigger any strange phenomena in the void.","Jian Wushuang quickly realized that the previous anomaly had been purely accidental.","However, it was indeed impossible to condense Yan power in this desolate void of the Great Desolate Wilderness. After realizing this, Jian Wushuang began to repair the boundary barrier.","Since there was no birth of a Heavenly Domain plane in this desolate void, he could only cut off the road of Immortal bones and fill the gaps in the boundary barrier with piled-up corpse bones.","The Invisible Sword silently condensed, Jian Wushuang ascended into the void, and then he struck down with a sword.","Rumble...","A crack appeared in the road of Immortal bones, and under the cutting of the Invisible Sword, a square mark was left at the center of the road of Immortal bones.","Then, Jian Wushuang put away the Invisible Sword and landed on the road of Immortal bones.","He stomped his foot, and in an instant, the road of Immortal bones trembled heavily. A square block the size of a divine mountain rose directly from the ground.","Jian Wushuang held the divine mountain-sized block with both arms and placed it in the center of the boundary barrier.","Although the block was larger than a divine mountain, it seemed minuscule compared to the cracks in the boundary.","However, Jian Wushuang paid no heed to this and silently proceeded with the next step.","In this boundless Great Desolate Wilderness, there was no concept of time, and everything existed in a state of primordial chaos.","Even Grand Yan Immortals with weak mental fortitude would become lost in it.","Only one figure tirelessly cut the road of Immortal bones, piece by piece. He piled the mountain-sized blocks that were cut down into the gaps in the boundary barrier.","...","\"Da Ban, where do you think Wushuang is now? I heard that the Great Mi Heaven has suffered severe damage.\"","Amidst the drifting clouds, the Heavenly Palace lay peacefully, a mysterious sight to behold.","Inside a warm chamber, the Young Emperor sat by the window, gazing absentmindedly at the drifting clouds.","The purple-robed elder who had been standing behind him raised his head and said, \"Your Highness, you don't have to concern yourself with this.\"","The Young Emperor snapped back to reality, turned his head to look at the elder, and said in a firm tone, \"What, am I not even allowed to say these things now?\""]},{"number":5105,"title":"Chapter 5105 Digging Out a Disaster","paragraphs":["In a thin, purple robe, Da Ban's head lowered. His voice was steady. \"Your Highness, you are the heir to the throne, and these shouldn't be the concerns of an heir.\"","The voice of the Young Emperor suddenly rose. \"Then what should I be concerned about, the internecine struggles among the Princes?\"","He fell silent, then spoke after a moment. \"I cannot dictate Your Highness's judgment, but Your Highness should consider the future.\"","\"Fine, I understand,\" the Young Emperor replied impatiently, a hint of loneliness in his eyes.","Jian Wushuang continued, \"Your Highness, do not overly rely on Jian Wushuang. You should be aware that he does not depend on you. He has his own purpose, and I believe he won't be bound by any celestial constraints. Once he finds his own path, he will not be far from leaving.\"","Unable to contain himself any longer, the Young Emperor exclaimed, \"Enough, leave!\"","But he did not depart. He continued, \"To prevent Your Highness from continuing down this path, I have already met with the Emperor and arranged for a high-ranking Heavenly Official to be sent to Your Highness. They will arrive shortly.\"","Bang!","The Young Emperor shattered a window in frustration, standing in the warm chamber, his anger reaching its peak. \"What did you say? Have my father send me a high-ranking Heavenly Official? Don't you know that my Heavenly Official is Jian Wushuang?!\"","The skinny purple-robed figure remained calm, \"Jian Wushuang is not willing to be Your Highness's Heavenly Official, and he has not The skinny purple-robed figure remained calm, \"Jian Wushuang is not willing to be Your Highness's Heavenly Official, and he has not received the Emperor's bloodline blessing. Therefore, he cannot be considered Your Highness's Heavenly Official.\"","\"Very well, I'll see how long this new Heavenly Official can survive under my rule!\" With these words, the Young Emperor left the chamber.","The purple-robed man turned slowly, his gaze filled with determination.","...","In the boundless wasteland, beneath the impenetrable boundary barrier.","At this moment, within the chasm-like gap that resembled an abyss, a square roadblock had already piled up, comparable to millions of divine mountains stacked together. The sheer enormity of it was beyond imagination.","But just like that, compared to the border barrier, it all seemed as tiny as dust.","In the center of the crack in the border barrier, on the countless Immortal bones, piling high like a mountain, sat a figure exuding a carefree aura.","He was Jian Wushuang.","In an extremely short period, he had filled the edge of the border crack. Although it might not be much, it was quite commendable.","Staring at the still unimaginable crack, Jian Wushuang contemplated how he could seal it as quickly as possible.","If he continued to cut out Immortal bones from the road as pieces and use them to fill the gap, it would probably take a thousand years to completely seal the border crack.","\"How should I go about this to quickly mend the rift? Should I try using the Wushuang Sword Dao?\" Jian Wushuang muttered silently, but soon dismissed various ideas.","In this desolated wasteland, it was impossible to generate Yan power, which meant he couldn't draw Yan power from the void.","Moreover, the Wushaung Sword Dao consumed Yan power excessively, and if his Immortal body couldn't recover the losses, he would be in a very passive situation.","Jian Wushuang never took such risky actions, especially in this unknown and desolate border of the Great Desolate Wilderness.","No one knew what existed here, especially beyond this border barrier, where the Great Desolate Wilderness stretched endlessly and dangerously.","So Jian Wushuang continued to act according to his previous method.","With a downward stroke of his sword, a thousand Sword Intents surged forth. Each Sword Intent seemed to gain sentience, cutting the road of Immortal bones at the fastest speed.","Then, Jian Wushuang shook the ground, stacking pieces of road, each resembling a mountain, into the border crack.","Perhaps even he himself had never imagined that one day, the Sword Principle of the Wushuang Sword Dao would be used for such things.","Blocks of road, like divine mountains, had been piled into the cracks at the border. And these blocks were actually the bones of Yan Immortals.","Countless bones of Yan Immortals eventually lay in the great wasteland, becoming a part of the ancient desolation.","Jian Wushuang finally understood. Clearly, the Yan Immortals had already transcended the order of the heavens, becoming Immortal beings, so why were there so few Yan Immortals in the Great Si Region?","It turned out that those Yan Immortals from ancient times had long turned into dry bones, discarded in the Great Desolate Wilderness.","Mending the border in this great wasteland was extremely dull, and Jian Wushuang had thought he might encounter some challenges. However, to his surprise, there was not the slightest disturbance in this vast wilderness.","If nothing unexpected happened, he wouldn't encounter any great difficulties in just a thousand years.","But as Jian Wushuang repeated the process of laying bricks, something unexpected suddenly occurred.","Under the excavated bone road that had already formed deep grooves, the pure Sword Intent of the Wushuang Sword Dao was unexpectedly unable to dig deeper, as if it had touched some kind of restriction, making it impossible to advance even a little bit further.","Jian Wushuang furrowed his brow slightly, and a sense of foreboding welled up in his heart.","He knew better than anyone how formidable the Sword Intent of the Wushuang Sword Dao was. It was precisely because he knew that this sense of foreboding became even stronger.","\"Could there be something hidden beneath this road of Immortal bones?!\"","Jian Wushuang swiftly descended from the void to the edge of the deeply excavated pit.","Through layers of Yan Immortal bones, his gaze reached the deepest part of the pit.","But at the same time, a thick black smoke, impossible to ignore, surged out from the deepest part of the pit like a black dragon.","The energy that erupted in an instant, even Jian Wushuang could not ignore it.","The black smoke billowed out, covering the sky and plunging the void into even deeper darkness.","Due to the surging of the black smoke, vortexes appeared once again above the void.","The more violent vortexes spun and resonated with the black smoke, as if they were brewing a supreme punishment.","Jian Wushuang muttered, \"This doesn't look good.\" Without hesitation, he released the Invisible Sword and slashed towards the black smoke column like a tearing of silk.","Swish!","Like tearing apart silk, the black smoke was forcibly severed and ultimately dissipated into the void.","However, Jian Wushuang did not relax his vigilance. He did not believe the black smoke would just disappear like this.","What could be emitting the black smoke? Was it some kind of restriction?","It was important to note that this bone road in the Great Desolate Wilderness had been jointly created by Zhen Wuyang and Yu Chang during that Ancient Era. Its age was unimaginable.","If there was indeed some kind of restriction beneath this bone road, it was likely that once it emerged, it would cause a catastrophe here!","Jian Wushuang furrowed his brow deeply. He had never imagined that digging this road would unearth a great disaster!","Following this, the black smoke that had been severed unexpectedly surged forth once again, carrying an unimaginable aura and shrouding the entire road of Immortal bones.","This was undoubtedly a calamity!"]},{"number":5106,"title":"Chapter 5106 The Enemy of the Past","paragraphs":["In what seemed like an affirmation of Jian Wushuang's inner worries, the road of Immortal bones suddenly began to tremble relentlessly.","Along with this tremor, a voice, as if echoing from ancient times, filled with a sense of decay, rang out.","\"Kill—kill—kill!\"","The shouts of killing resounded from beneath the road of Immortal bones, causing the entire road to become turbulent.","Jian Wushuang's gaze became completely serious; he could sense the terrifying presence beneath the earth's core.","With each cry for blood, it felt as though countless Yan Immortals were engaged in a bloodthirsty battle on a battlefield, exhausting their last drops of divine blood.","The entire boundless border seemed to have turned into a battlefield, returning to that distant Ancient Era.","The road of Immortal bones beneath his feet trembled as if these Immortal bones were about to awaken at any moment, leaving everything with an indescribable sense of awe.","\"Kill—kill—kill!\"","The next moment, from the depths of the abyss, black smoke billowed more intensely than at any previous time, almost reaching the point of obscuring the void.","Jian Wushuang slowly retreated, his brows furrowed. This kind of supreme aura could not be released by ordinary Yan Immortals.","A great calamity was about to occur on this road of Immortal bones.","As if confirming his thoughts, within the all-encompassing black smoke, a pair of eyes, like suns and stars, quietly appeared.","In the midst of the abyssal black smoke, the True Eyes suddenly emerged.","With the appearance of this pair of true eyes, Jian Wushuang immediately sensed it.","As their gazes met, thousands of arrow-like black mists shot out from the black smoke.","Jian Wushuang was taken aback and, almost instinctively, he retreated a hundred steps, wielding his Invisible Sword to cut down each of the oncoming black mist arrows.","\"I'm still alive... I'm actually still alive!\"","From within the black smoke, a voice, desolate and withered, rang out, as if it had released the endless pain of countless ages.","\"Zhen Wuyang, I'm still alive, I'm still alive!\"","The black smoke raged violently, and the top layer of the road of Immortal bones began to crumble into dust.","Jian Wushuang slowly retreated. He could already sense a desolate and lonely aura from this black smoke, and coupled with the words spoken, he could deduce that this entity had existed in the same era as Zhen Wuyang.","To coexist in the same era as Zhen Wuyang and call out his name could only mean they were hostile forces.","Who else but the most formidable beings could traverse the river of time and still remain alive?","After thinking through all of this, Jian Wushuang made no hesitation and prepared to retreat from the boundless border. After all, here, once his Yan power was depleted, he would truly perish.","However, before he could make any moves, the pitch-black smoke that obscured the void suddenly gathered, transforming into a massive hammer that could blot out the sky, crashing heavily toward Jian Wushuang.","He felt a sudden shock, naturally sensing the terrifying power of this force, and hastily leaped aside.","Boom! Boom! Boom!","The hammer, formed from condensed black mist, struck heavily upon the road of Immortal bones, causing a tremendous quake.","The Immortal bones, which had endured for countless eons without decay, couldn't bear such immense pressure, and instantly, craters appeared one after another.","Jian Wushuang had no intention of lingering in the battle. He used his movement ability 'Earth Shrinking Mountain River' to traverse mountains and rivers, quickly leaving the road of Immortal bones.","However, the road of Immortal bones was vast beyond measure, almost as boundless as the Great Desolate Wilderness.","As he departed, the hammer formed by the condensing black smoke transformed once again, this time into thousands of chains that madly shot downward.","Clang! Clang!","Each chain formed from the black smoke easily shattered a section of the road of Immortal bones.","Even with his use of Earth Shrinking Mountain River to traverse mountains and rivers, Jian Wushuang found it difficult to create distance as the chains descended from the heavens, blocking any possible escape route.","His brow furrowed, and an Invisible Sword silently materialized in his hand, releasing a myriad of Sword Intents!","Every sword intent erupted with unparalleled momentum, slashing at the chains.","When the two clashed, light and darkness existed only for a moment before both dissipated.","Jian Wushuang no longer rushed to escape but instead turned to gaze at the void.","In the emptiness, the towering black smoke had gradually converged and was slowly undulating.","As the black smoke continued to dissipate, a pair of True Eyes hidden within it finally fully materialized.","It was a colossal figure reaching tens of millions of feet in height. Even though it was concealed beneath the black smoke, its magnificent stature was hard to conceal.","Presenting the fragmented and battered armor, one could hardly discern it as a piece of battle gear. It had been worn down to the point where it could no longer conceal the colossal body that stood a staggering ten million feet tall.","As the black smoke dissipated, the colossal figure loomed over the road of Immortal bones.","He wore tattered battle armor, his face was angular with wild unkempt hair, and his eyes gleamed like they were forged from divine blood, radiating unmatched true power.","In his hand, he held a sword that was already broken in half.","With his appearance, violent whirlwinds reappeared in the void, and thunderbolts, resembling colossal dragons, descended from within the whirlwinds, wrapping around the figure in the damaged armor.","\"I'm still alive, and I won't live in vain. I will destroy everything as a companion to my master in death!\"","The figure in the battle armor roared with his sword held high, and his eyes seemed as if they were about to bleed.","He had died countless ages ago, yet here he was, awakening in the vast wilderness.","Everything familiar had turned to dust, and all that met his gaze was desolation.","Upon his first moments of awakening, there was only Jian Wushuang by his side, and he instinctively regarded Jian Wushuang as an enemy.","\"You're one of Zhen Wuyang's lackeys?!\" the figure in the battle armor shouted angrily, pointing his broken sword down.","Jian Wushuang took a step back, his gaze serious. \"I have no connection to Zhen Wuyang. You've mistaken me.\"","\"I won't make a mistake. I can sense his aura on you. You must have an intricate connection with Zhen Wuyang!\" the figure in the battle armor roared. \"Since I've come back to life, I'll destroy everything related to Zhen Wuyang!\"","Jian Wushuang muttered to himself, \"This is bad,\" and without hesitation, he unleashed the peak of his Yan power from within his Immortal body.","Boom, boom, boom!","Supreme Yan power erupted instantly in the barren wasteland where Yan power couldn't naturally exist, once again causing spatial anomalies to manifest!","Whirlwinds converged, emitting a suffocating and desolate aura.","The figure in the battle armor stood on the road of Immortal bones, his colossal body exuding an irresistible pressure, almost unbearable to behold. He then swung the broken sword in his hand downward.","The void could not withstand the force of this strike, and it began to rupture, collapsing under an unparalleled weight.","Jian Wushuang's gaze turned intense. He stomped on the road of Immortal bones beneath him, with himself at the center. In that moment, a million Sword Intents surged, pure and intertwined with crimson-gold divine patterns, illuminating the void.","The Wushuang Sword Intent clashed with the broken sword, creating boundless sonic waves.","The bone road was torn apart, turning into powder in the void.","As for the mountain-like roadblocks that Jian Wushuang had piled up in the boundary cracks, they too turned into a handful of ashes..."]},{"number":5107,"title":"Chapter 5107 Battling in the Great Desolate Wilderness","paragraphs":["That is to say, everything Jian Wushuang had done previously became futile in the face of this encounter...","A remnant sword strike caused even the profound Sword Intent of the Wushuang Sword Dao to rapidly crumble!","One could only watch as millions of instances of Wushuang Sword Intent attempted to withstand this descending remnant sword.","The figure in battle armor exuding the aura of ancient desolation and solitude was simply terrifying. Even this single sword strike carried the aura of a transcendent tyrant of ancient times.","In the end, the millions of instances of Wushuang Sword Intent were reduced to dust.","The unremitting momentum of the remnant sword continued to descend, tearing a rift of millions of feet in the road of Immortal bones.","Jian Wushuang swiftly retreated, breathing slightly heavily.","His gaze became completely solemn. In just this first encounter, he could sense that the figure in the battle armor was a Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal!","Against a Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal, even within the Unfathomable Sea, Jian Wushuang had no chance of victory whatsoever.","Only with the Emperor's fate energy could he hope to erase a Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal.","But how could the Emperor's fate energy be easily obtained? Emperor Zhen Wu, who was hiding within the ring, had vanished without a trace, and the last strand of True Soul from Emperor Liu Ya in the Liu Ya Heavenly Emperor Runes was in the deepest slumber, with no possibility of providing the Emperor's fate energy.","Even if it were possible to provide the Emperor's fate energy, it was unlikely that Jian Wushuang would use it again.","Because the Emperor's fate energy brought terrifying damage to him as a Yan Immortal who still retained his Undying and Imperishable Immortal Body.","The Undying and Imperishable Immortal Body was born from the transformation of a Perfect Chaotic Lifeform, turning into something even more mysterious. It was a constitution even more mysterious than that of Perfect Chaotic Lifeform creatures.","However, the Undying and Imperishable Immortal Body would undergo transformations along with Jian Wushuang's growth.","But after using the Emperor's fate energy within the Endless Sea, he discovered that the Undying and Imperishable Immortal Body actually strongly resisted external Emperor's fate energy and would become dormant as a result.","So Jian Wushuang realized that, despite his Immortal body being like a vessel capable of transcending realms to contain and absorb the supreme Emperor's fate energy, it was still subject to immense damage because of it.","Therefore, at that moment, Jian Wushuang could only rely on his own power to shatter this armored figure.","In the boundless wilderness, there was no place for any Yan Immortal, not even a Grand Yan Immortal, to tread upon.","He had to depend on himself.","This was the first time Jian Wushuang had directly faced a Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal, especially one from that Ancient Era.","His chances of victory were nearly nonexistent, and the possibility of escaping the borders of the Great Desolate Wilderness was also quite low.","After all, the Great Desolate Wilderness was just too vast, and Jian Wushuang didn't believe that the Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal would be unable to catch up with him.","As that remnant sword fell, it did not harm Jian Wushuang in the slightest, leaving the armored figure astounded.","Naturally, he could tell that Jian Wushuang was just a Yan Immortal, and it was precisely for this reason that he didn't take him seriously.","Unexpectedly, Jian Wushuang remained unscathed.","This made the armored figure instantly furious, and his true eyes turned crimson to the extreme.","\"I shall return today, and all the lackeys of Zhen Wuyang shall accompany my lord in death!\"","The vortex in the void erupted with boundless momentum, and countless thunderbolts, like colossal dragons, pierced through the armored figure's surroundings, making him even more impossible to look directly at.","Then, the armored figure waved the broken sword in his hand and once again swung it down.","This left Jian Wushuang with a splitting headache, but he had no choice but to deal with it.","Facing such a colossal giant, agility became his advantage.","As the broken sword came down again, Jian Wushuang's figure quietly disappeared.","When his figure reappeared, it was already at the waist of the armored figure.","Jian Wushuang tightly grasped the intangible sword, shining brilliantly, and then thrust it with all his might at the weakest point around its waist.","Clang!","A resounding clash of metal and gold rang out as the silver armor around his waist shattered instantly. The Invisible Sword, adorned with radiant divine patterns, paused for just a moment before effortlessly piercing through the Immortal body within the armored figure.","A surge of power erupted from the wound at his waist, and the armored figure let out a dull roar as an uncontrollable torrent of power gushed forth.","Then, the armored figure swung its left hand viciously, smashing towards its own waist.","Jian Wushuang had sensed this coming and narrowly evaded the strike.","Boom! Boom! Boom!","The armored figure had gone all out, unleashing an unrelenting barrage at its own waist, but it didn't hit Jian Wushuang. Instead, it struck the Invisible Sword still embedded there.","This punch drove the Invisible Sword deep into the waist.","\"Ah!\"","Even though the armored figure was a Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal, he could not endure such agony.","His colossal body, spanning millions of feet, began to tremble before uncontrollably falling backward.","Jian Wushuang's gaze sharpened, and he focused his thoughts, silently reciting the sword technique of the Wushuang Sword Dao.","The Invisible Sword, now deeply embedded in the waist of the armored figure, suddenly erupted with unparalleled divine patterns.","Star River Lake Sea Sword Intent.","River.","The River Sword Intent surged mightily, in perfect harmony with the heavens and earth. In that moment, the immense Sword Intent burst forthe from within the Immortal body of the armored figure.","Using the Invisible Sword as a medium, the magnificent and resplendent Sword Intent became overwhelming and converged into the celestial river.","Sensing the anomaly within its Immortal body, the armored figure, semi-kneeling on the road of Immortal bones, let out a muffled roar and raised its hand to extract the Invisible Sword from within.","Jian Wushuang was alarmed and quickly released millions of strands of Yan power chains to restrain the armored figure's arm, attempting to stop it.","However, there was an insurmountable gap between Yan Immortals and Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal. How could he possibly hinder it?","This was a collision of Immortal bodies!","The millions of Yan power chains only held for an instant before instantly shattering.","Jian Wushuang's ears and nose oozed divine blood, and his Immortal body suffered a severe blow.","However, at that very moment, the Wushuang Sword Dao within the armored figure's body was completely unleashed.","The majestic Sword Intent of the celestial river erupted, and countless Sword Intents, like True Swords, surged within the figure's Immortal body, slashing and tearing.","Even a Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal couldn't withstand such pain.","The colossal Immortal body of the armored figure sprayed out layers of blood mist in an instant. Simultaneously, countless threads of crimson and golden Sword Intent pierced through its flesh, emerged from its Immortal body, and exploded.","It screamed in agony, and its enormous body crashed onto the road of Immortal bones.","The road of Immortal bones, constructed from countless Yan Immortal remains, couldn't bear such tremendous pressure and cracked into deep chasms.","The Immortal body of the armored figure, which was millions of feet tall, eventually crashed into the heart of the road of Immortal bones.","Feeling the intense trembling beneath his feet, Jian Wushuang coughed lightly and wiped the divine blood from the corner of his mouth.","Erasing a Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal with the Wushuang Sword Dao was utterly impossible for him in his current state.","Jian Wushuang did not believe that the armored figure would be annihilated so easily, so he remained vigilant."]},{"number":5108,"title":"Chapter 5108 Young Samanera","paragraphs":["Although the Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal's battle armor couldn't die so easily, Jian Wushuang's Sword Principle was at least able to severely damage it.","Jian Wushuang slowly ascended into the void, his gaze following the fallen form of the battle armor.","The road of Immortal bones was severely damaged, with one crater reaching an unfathomable depth, so deep that not even Jian Wushuang could see what was inside.","As the road of Immortal bones stopped trembling, everything returned to silence.","\"It can't be, is he really dead?\" Jian Wushuang was still somewhat unwilling to believe it as he slowly approached the crater.","However, the next moment, the void suddenly became thick and solid, as if it had turned into a solid substance.","He was startled, but his body could no longer move, as if he were entangled in a million strands of fate energy, rendering him completely immobile.","Then, black smoke quietly rose from the crater, obscuring the sky.","Accompanying the black smoke was a figure towering to a height of tens of millions of feet.","A pair of True Eyes were like two blood-red suns in the sky, filled with unending hatred and resentment.","\"You despicable Yan Immortal, today, you will die in place of Zhen Wuyang!\" The battle armor roared and then rose from the abyss, slashing a sword at Jian Wushuang.","This strike was filled with determination and a deadly aura.","Jian Wushuang, trapped in place, couldn't dodge it and could only watch as this sword fell upon his Immortal body.","Splurt—","Divine blood gushed out, and the Mystic Garb of the Nine Heavens radiated the most dazzling azure light, protecting his Immortal body from being severed.","However, this was the full-force strike of the Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal. Even though it did not cleave Jian Wushuang into two, it shattered his meridians inch by inch, reducing him to dust.","The Mystic Garb of the Nine Heavens dimmed, and Jian Wushuang was like a dying sun, falling rapidly.","The boundary barrier had stood for countless ages in the vast wilderness, enduring numerous ravages, but it still remained unyielding.","Jian Wushuang, falling like a colossal sun and stars, violently collided with the boundary barrier.","The boundary barrier was truly vast and expansive, beyond comparison even if a million Heavenly Region were combined.","Naturally, Jian Wushuang's impact on the boundary barrier caused only minimal ripples.","With a resounding crash, a trace appeared on the boundary barrier, and the now unconscious Jian Wushuang landed beneath it, precisely in the center of the boundary barrier's crack.","Surrounded by dragon-like lightning, the suit of dark smoke armor's figure slowly rose, heading towards the boundary barrier.","He arrived at the crack in the boundary barrier, looking at Jian Wushuang, whose Immortal body had not shattered, and felt a sense of puzzlement.","But quickly, he raised his arm, and an endless gust of wind carried Jian Wushuang, blowing him beyond the boundary barrier into the boundless wasteland.","Inside the boundary barrier lay the domain of the Great Si Region, while beyond the boundary was the Great Desolate Wilderness.","Even a wavering Grand Immortal like Jian Wushuang would lose their way in the wilderness!","It was a true forbidden land, untouched by any Yan Immortal, except for certain specific beings.","The unconscious Jian Wushuang had no awareness of his current location as he lay still in the thick dust.","The figure in the armor let out a deep, mournful roar, seemingly venting ancient grudges.","He looked up, gazing closely at the majestic boundary barrier, as if trying to identify where he was.","\"Where is this place, and why am I here? Has my Heavenly Court truly been shattered?\" His voice, like an echo from antiquity, was filled with sorrow, and his belligerence had vanished completely.","The battle armor's figure was no longer as terrifying as before, and there was only confusion left in its eyes, wandering aimlessly on this road of Immortal bones.","On the other side, Jian Wushuang, who had already fallen unconscious outside the boundary barrier in the Great Desolate Wilderness, was now gently cradled by a pair of hands.","\"Master, look here, there's actually a Yan Immortal in the Great Desolate Wilderness.\"","A still youthful voice rang out in the thick dust.","Immediately, a deep but dignified voice resounded, \"Quickly, dispose of it. It must be a corpse that has long been lost here.\"","\"No, Master, he's still alive. I can hear his heartbeat.\"","\"What? He's still alive? How is that possible?\"","With the clamor of voices, a total of six figures resembling golden Monks emerged from the dust.","These six figures, all dressed in simple Monk robes, exuded an air of authority even when not angered.","At the center of these six figures, there was a young novice monk with rosy lips and white teeth, and a hint of liveliness between his brows. Young novice Bhuddist practitioners like him are also known as 'samanera' or 'shami'.","At this moment, the young samanera's face was full of anxiety as he used his thin arms to cradle a figure covered in bloody wounds, paying no mind to the blood that soaked his Monk's robes.","\"Master, please save him quickly. I feel like he can still be saved,\" the young samanera implored, looking at the group of figures with a worried expression.","The six Monk-like figures exchanged glances, all wearing troubled expressions.","They had ventured into the Great Desolate Wilderness, overcoming countless dangers along the way. Now, after enduring myriad hardships to emerge from the Great Desolate Wilderness, they encountered such a strange situation and had to be cautious.","Among these figures, an older and more composed Monk furrowed his brow slightly, seemingly hesitating.","No Yan Immortal, let alone a Grand Yan Immortal, could survive such severe injuries in the Great Desolate Wilderness. Moreover, it appeared that this young Yan Immortal, who had fallen unconscious, had just experienced a life-and-death battle, making him a potential source of danger.","Various concerns made the Monks hesitate.","At this moment, the young samanera grew impatient. \"Didn't you all always talk about devoting yourselves to goodness? Why are you hesitating now?\"","\"Devoting ourselves to goodness also depends on the situation, Huqing. You're still young and don't understand these matters,\" one of the Monks with a rugged appearance and thick eyebrows said.","\"I'm not young. I've already listened to the scriptures for 30 million years under the mulberry tree,\" the young samanera argued in frustration. \"Master, your actions are not right. Clearly, you have the ability to save him, so why not do it? Just because we don't know him?\"","The older and more composed Monk, who had remained silent until now, spoke with a hint of helplessness, \"Alright, Hu Qing, calm down. We will help.\"","The young samanera quickly nodded and said, \"Thank you, Master.\"","After deciding to lend a helping hand, the six Monks gathered together.","The young samanera quickly lifted the still unconscious Jian Wushuang and placed him in front of the six Monks.","They exchanged glances and then acted together.","Radiant auras, brimming with boundless fate energy, appeared one after another, enveloping Jian Wushuang.","Obscure and incomprehensible inscriptions began to appear and slowly rotate."]},{"number":5109,"title":"Chapter 5109 The Monks Enter the Border","paragraphs":["Accompanied by layers of mysterious runes flowing and spreading like misty dust across the vast wasteland, they began to disperse and recede.","And within this ancient and extremely dark wasteland, a glimmer of hope emerged.","Under the joint efforts of the six Monks, Jian Wushuang's condition began to stabilize.","The divine blood no longer gushed forth, and the shattered meridians started to rapidly mend.","The Undying and Imperishable Immortal Body was already an unparalleled and heaven-defying constitution, and after receiving their care, it was recovering rapidly.","The elderly Monk known as the Grandmaster, who was wise from his countless years of age, couldn't help but be amazed when he saw the terrifying speed of his recovery.","Not long ago, he had felt that Jian Wushuang, who had fallen into a coma, was no different from a corpse, with no trace of life left. His body had been reduced to powder, and even his Immortal Source had disappeared.","How could such a body be revived?","Unexpectedly, in just a few dozen breaths of time, he had already begun to recover, and he could even emit a faint breath.","The six Monks naturally noticed this situation and exchanged glances, expressing their astonishment and disbelief.","\"Could it be that we've truly saved a remarkable genius?\" the elder Monk questioned with some confusion, while his inner vigilance gradually diminished.","Because he did not sense any discomforting aura from Jian Wushuang.","Hundreds of breaths later, all six Monks withdrew their efforts, and the Grandmaster began to investigate Jian Wushuang's condition.","\"How is it, Grandmaster? Is he out of danger?\" the young samanera, Hu Qing, nervously inquired.","The Grandmaster nodded and withdrew his palm, saying, \"There is no serious harm, and his recovery is going well. It seems he will awaken very soon.\"","A Monk with a rough appearance, thick eyebrows, and large eyes, expressed his astonishment, \"This is truly a remarkable event. To endure such heavy injuries in the Great Desolate Wilderness and still have a breath left, this young man is extraordinary.\"","The Grandmaster clasped his hands together, saying, \"Well, saving his life can be considered a good deed, hoping that all the wandering Immortals will no longer suffer in the Great Desolate Wilderness.\"","At this moment, another Monk, slender and clean-shaven, furrowed his brow slightly and said, \"Senior Brother, we've already crossed through the Great Desolate Wilderness, and ahead should be the territory of the Great Si Region Lord. There shouldn't be any more major crises, but why is there such a strong and frenzied aura of killing here?\"","The Grandmaster remained silent and slowly turned to look in the direction of the Great Si Region.","There, an almost completely dark void, nearly integrated with the Great Desolate Wilderness, stretched out, devoid of any radiant suns or celestial planes.","There was only a border barrier that was too magnificent and immense, almost isolating everything, effectively protecting the Great Si Region.","The Grandmaster furrowed his brow slightly, a hint of puzzlement in his eyes. \"Could that killing intent be emanating from the Great Si Region?\"","Following this, the Monk with a rough appearance and thick eyebrows, who was a Grand Yan Immortal, spoke in a deep voice, \"I'm afraid this killing intent is also related to this young man. Should we wake him up and question him?\"","\"No, he is still recovering; we cannot treat him this way,\" Hu Qing, the young samanera, hurriedly protected Jian Wushuang.","The Grandmaster calmly said, \"We have endured the bitter cold of the Great Desolate Wilderness, so why fear these murderous intentions?\"","Another Monk, with three lotus marks on his forehead, nodded and said, \"Senior Brother is right. How can these mere murderous intentions stop us? This time, we must find our other senior brothers.\"","\"Finding them is not the goal. What we need to do is to comprehend the process. We were able to emerge from the Great Desolate Wilderness, but it wasn't solely our own doing.\"","After saying this last sentence, the Grandmaster turned and walked towards the direction of the Great Si Region.","The other Monks followed closely behind.","The Monk with a rough appearance, thick eyebrows, and large eyes said, \"Hu Qing, since he is no longer in danger, leave him here. We have more important matters to attend to.\"","The young samanera Hu Qing shook his head and said, \"No, Third Senior, he is still unconscious. Leaving him here in the Great Desolate Wilderness will surely cost him his life. I believe he must be a wandering Yan Immortal from the Great Si Region. It's better to take him back to the Great Si Region.\"","Seeing that his persuasion was in vain, he had to give up.","A group of Monks walked out into the Great Desolate Wilderness, heading towards the domain of the Great Si Regioon.","\"The karma of killing is too heavy; no wonder the intent to kill is so strong. This Great Si Region is truly not a paradise.\"","They stepped on the road of Immortal bones crafted from the countless remains of Yan Immortals.","They observed that everything in the Great Desolate Wilderness was made up of these Immortal bones. These bones once belonged to Yan Immortals with boundless powers, but now, they had lost everything and stood desolately in the Great Desolate Wilderness for countless ages.","Stepping on the endless Immortal bones, the group of Yan Immortals arrived at the boundary barrier.","\"Is this the passage that our predecessors opened? Truly, they were great practitioners!\" exclaimed the thick-browed Monk, bowing his hands together in admiration. Indeed, breaking open a gap in such a vast boundary barrier was unimaginable.","\"Alright, we still have a long way to go. Let's focus our minds,\" said the Grandmaster, leading the way towards the boundary barrier.","The young samanera Hu Qing, with a frail and slender figure, carried Jian Wushuang on his back and hung at the end of the group of Monks.","The boundary barrier was vast beyond imagination, and they had to travel a considerable distance along the road of Immortal bones to reach the Great Si Region.","Led by the Grandmaster, the group formed a zigzag formation as they advanced.","Around them, a faint and radiant Buddhist light enveloped them, offering protection. They all wore solemn expressions, seemingly prepared for whatever lay ahead.","\"Senior Brothers, have you noticed that the blood aura is getting stronger?\" asked one of the Monks.","\"How could that be? The Great Desolate Wilderness has remained unchanged for countless eons; it's impossible for there to be any lingering blood aura,\" replied another.","At this moment, Hu Qing, carrying Jian Wushuang on his back, raised his head and said earnestly, \"But Third Master, I feel a powerful and distinct blood aura approaching us.\"","Hearing Hu Qing's words, the expressions of all the Monks grew slightly more serious as they looked around the desolate wilderness.","\"Be on guard. We have already left the Great Desolate Wilderness; there should be no obstacles on our way to the Great Si Region,\" the Grandmaster said with a furrowed brow, his gaze intense.","Just then, Jian Wushuang, who had been in a deep unconscious state, slowly began to wake up.","Hu Qing noticed Jian Wushuang awakening behind him and greeted him cheerfully, \"Ah, you're awake? That was quick.\"","Jian Wushuang was initially bewildered, looking at the unfamiliar group of Monks before quickly realizing what had happened. \"You... you saved me?\"","\"Of course, but please don't dwell on it. It's the least we can do,\" one of the Monks replied."]},{"number":5110,"title":"Chapter 5110 Bloody Battle in the Great Desolate Wilderness (1)","paragraphs":["The young samanera, Hu Qing, spoke with a gentle, smiling expression. His eyes filled with kindness like a clear spring, pure to the extreme.","\"Saving a virtuous person's life is also a form of cultivation for us, a great act of virtue,\" Jian Wushuang said with a slightly furrowed brow, then thanked them solemnly.","Hu Qing smiled again and said, \"You don't need to thank me. If you must thank someone, thank my several masters. It was their combined efforts that saved you.\"","He nodded gratefully, then, realizing something, he asked, \"Are you from the Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm?\"","\"How did you know...\" Hu Qing widened his eyes, looking at him in disbelief.","But just as he was about to say more, a Monk turned around, his expression serious, and scolded, \"That's enough, Hu Qing, do not speak further!\"","Hu Qing was startled and quickly nodded, making a hushing gesture.","Only after the Monk turned away did he speak in a low voice, \"I can't say too much; my masters are very strict with me.\"","Jian Wushuang nodded, then moved away from Hu Qing's frail back.","He looked around and quickly recognized the place, his heart sinking.","\"Have you all reached the border?!\"","With these words, all the leading Monks stopped in their tracks, staring at Jian Wushuang like angry Vajrapanis, seemingly ready to act at any moment.","But Jian Wushuang paid no attention to their stares and shouted urgently, \"Hurry up and leave, if you don't leave now, it will be too late. There's something going on at the border!\"","The Grandmaster furrowed his brow tightly, his gaze fixed on Jian Wushuang, as if trying to discern the truth in his words.","And just at that moment, a colossal figure, tens of millions of feet tall, with a murderous intent that could obliterate the void, quietly approached the edge of the border barrier.","In those crimson, nearly fanatical and paranoid eyes, filled with boundless anger, they glared at the group of Monks.","Jian Wushuang was the first to spot the presence of the armored figure and urgently shouted, \"Hurry, he's coming!\"","But it was already too late!","The killing intent, capable of obliterating the void, swept in an instant, and the colossal body of the armored figure descended fiercely.","A massive shattered sword tore through the void, ruthlessly descending!","The group of Monks also sensed something in an instant and acted without hesitation.","Brilliant to the extreme, the Buddhist light, accompanied by their Yan power, at that moment completely blossomed with endless radiance, forming a barrier to resist that sword strike.","The sword tore through the void, carrying boundless killing intent as it fell heavily.","Buzz!!!","The dark bloodstained sword struck the barrier, and the Grandmaster's expression changed drastically, then he spat out divine blood directly.","The situation of the other five Monks was no better; they all spewed divine blood and their vitality instantly withered.","And the Buddhist light barrier also shattered in an instant.","\"Master!\" Hu Qing shouted in alarm.","Jian Wushuang gritted his teeth, released more than ten strands of his Yan power, wrapped around the waists of the group of Monks, and forcefully pulled them out of the range of the shattered sword.","Boom!!!","The road of Immortal bones instantly cracked with millions of feet of fissures, and the ancient Immortal bones turned to dust.","Under the swirling dust, the group of Monks who had barely escaped the danger had pale faces, their eyes filled with disbelief.","Jian Wushuang breathed slightly, \"Hurry, don't stop, go as far as you can!\"","None of the Monks spoke; instead, they looked at their composed Grandmaster.","Then, he spoke, having already made a decision, \"No, we can't retreat even a step! We came here on a mission, and we cannot retreat even a step!\"","Jian Wushuang was momentarily stunned and couldn't find words to reply.","Long before, he had sensed that these Monks were all incredibly formidable. They were all Grand Yan Immortals, except the young samanera.","A formidable group of beings, any one of them alone was enough to bring about the destruction of countless Heavenly Regions.","But there was an even more terrifying presence than them, the armored figure who had already reached the realm of the Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal!","He hailed from the Ancient Era, slumbering until now, awakening with boundless murderous intent. His existence was beyond imagination.","This was fundamentally an incredibly uneven battle.","Facing a Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal, the six Monks seemed to court death!","\"Do you understand? He's a Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal!\" Jian Wushuang furrowed his brow as he cautioned them.","\"Even if he's Nine Revolutions, we can only move forward, not retreat!\" Grandmaster spoke in a deep voice, his gaze sweeping over the other Monk leaders. \"Don't forget how many of our brothers we lost to escape the Great Desolate Wilderness. How can we retreat now?!\"","All the Monks nodded slightly, facing a Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal who had emerged from the Ancient Era, they showed no intention of backing down.","\"Have you all gone mad? Do you know what Nine Revolutions represents?\" Jian Wushuang could not believe what he was seeing. They were facing certain death, so why were they seeking it?","At this moment, Hu Qing, who had been silent all along, seemed to have made a decision. With a resolute gaze, he moved forward.","But before he could take more than a couple of steps, Jian Wushuang grabbed him by the collar and pulled him back. \"Are you also going to throw your life away?!\"","Hu Qing, his face red, argued vehemently, \"Kind sir, please let me go. This is a decision I made alongside my masters, and I will not change it!\"","Jian Wushuang was exasperated. \"Your masters are heading towards certain death, and you're not trying to stop them but are instead willing to die with them? What kind of foolish decision is this?!\"","Hu Qing, still red-faced, continued to defend his stance. \"We are not going to die. The Great Desolate Wilderness is so terrifying, yet we have come this far. How can we fall at the border of the Great Si Region?\"","Jian Wushuang's expression turned solemn. \"Let me tell you, do you know the gap in perception between them? It's like an unbridgeable chasm; there's no way to make up for it!\"","He paused and then said earnestly, \"I don't care about these Monks. Since you saved me, I can't just watch you all go to your deaths. I would love to save everyone, but if I can only save one, so be it!\"","Hu Qing opened his mouth slightly, and for some reason, at this moment, the determination in his heart began to waver.","This was the first doubt he had harbored in his 30 million years of enlightenment."]},{"number":5111,"title":"Chapter 5111 Bloody Battle in the Great Desolate Wilderness (2)","paragraphs":["Under the ancient Bodhi tree, the young samanera contemplated the Dao for 30 million years, firming up his Buddha's heart.","His purity of heart and unwavering determination left all who beheld him in awe, as if they were gazing upon the Buddha himself.","He had never experienced moments of doubt, not even when faced with the most profound scriptures. But now, he was confronted with the enormous matter of life and death. A young Yan Immortal with an equally resolute and pure gaze stared into his eyes, asking startling questions. Hu Qing found himself unable to maintain his inner serenity for the first time.","\"Could it be that our masters' decisions were wrong, that we should not have made such a choice?\"","\"But my other masters have already sacrificed themselves in the Great Desolate Wilderness so that we could escape it. If we were to retreat, how could we face them?\"","These profound questions left Hu Qing unable to maintain his composure. He stood there in a daze, unsure of what course of action to take.","Seeing Hu Qing no longer in a state of impulsiveness, Jian Wushuang released him and turned to look at the battlefield now engulfed in a bloody struggle. He furrowed his brows.","Just then, a small hand quietly tugged at the hem of his robe, and a trembling voice asked, \"Kind sir, you said that you'll save us, even if it's just one person. Will you save my masters?\"","Jian Wushuang turned and looked at the young samanera whose eyes still held a hint of timidity. He nodded solemnly, \"Since I have said it, I will do it, but I may not be able to save them all.\"","\"Then, I entrust it to you, kind sir.\" The young samanera, Hu Qing, folded his hands together in a gesture of gratitude and turned his gaze toward the masters locked in battle in the void. Eventually, a look of reluctance appeared in his eyes.","After making the decision, Jian Wushuang unconsciously raised his palm and patted Hu Qing's bald head. He instantly realized his action, blushed, hurriedly apologized, and then turned without hesitation to charge into the void.","Hu Qing pursed his lips and, in turn, subconsciously patted his own bald head. \"Well, you must save all of my masters!\"","On the boundary barrier, the void had already been shattered and torn apart by the supreme Yan power. The released Yan power formed the most violent whirlpool, with massive lightning bolts resembling giant dragons raging within the vortex, then erupting downward.","At the border of the Great Si Region, chaos had already taken complete hold. Various shades of iridescent divine blood splattered about, unable to descend due to its sheer purity, hovering in the void and making the battlefield even more gruesome.","The colossal war armor, reaching heights of tens of millions of feet, had succumbed to a state of frenzied rage.","But at this moment, the six Monks found themselves in even more dire straits, barely managing to hold their own thanks to their agility.","The gap between them was truly unimaginable, like an unbridgeable chasm.","Even with their combined might, they could not inflict significant harm upon the war-armored behemoth.","Once they reached the cultivation realm of Grand Yan Immortal, each Revolution would propel their skills and strength immensely. It was extremely difficult to compensate for the gap.","Among the six Monks, only one had reached the level of a Six Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal. How could they contend with a Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal?","This was something Jian Wushuang couldn't fathom.","Swinging his sword, each stroke capable of dealing severe damage to the Grand Yan Immortal, the war armor bellowed, \"All of Zhen Wuyang's lackeys shall pay the price for my master!\"","Above the bloody void, the composed and aged Grandmaster, almost single-handedly, bore the brunt of the war armor's relentless onslaught. The aura of his Image Form had dimmed to its limits, seemingly on the verge of vanishing at any moment.","Brilliant and dazzling spells stood guard in front of him, simultaneously drawing the majority of the armor-clad figure's attacks.","A horizontal sword strike sent hundreds of spells, along with the Grandmaster, flying.","Furthermore, the remnant sword continued its unrelenting descent, and once it struck, even a Six Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal like him would undoubtedly meet his end instantly.","\"Senior Brother!\"","The other five Monks shouted, but they were too late to lend assistance, only able to watch helplessly as the sword descended.","In the next moment, a figure quietly appeared beneath the falling sword, raising a sword to meet it.","Clang!","The resounding clash of metal echoed through the ancient void, and an exceedingly pure Sword Intent burst forth, illuminating the profoundly dark void.","All the Monks widened their eyes in disbelief.","The one who had previously resembled a bloodied corpse, lying almost lifeless in the Wild Desolate Wasteland, a mere fledgling Yan Immortal, was now single-handedly withstanding a sword strike.","Keep in mind, that sword strike came from a Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal!","But this scene was undeniably real.","Time seemed to stand still as, beneath that descending sword, Jian Wushuang's eyebrows trembled slightly.","Jian Wushuang tightly gripped the Invisible Sword in his right hand, which had already become fragmented and shattered, his divine blood splattering into the void.","If it weren't for the terrifying defensive power of his Undying and Imperishable Immortal Body, that one sword strike might have turned Jian Wushuang into mere dust.","But he managed it, enduring the full force of the Nine Revolutions Great Yan Immortal's strike head-on.","Even the figure in battle armor was astonished, as if witnessing the impossible.","\"You... you're not dead?\"","Jian Wushuang's brow furrowed, and he quickly tossed an Emperor-grade pill into his mouth. \"You want me dead? It's not that easy!\"","\"Then I'll make you die again!\" The figure in battle armor was enraged, attempting to raise its left hand to strike him.","However, at that moment, six Monks simultaneously acted. They deployed six pure and sublime Buddhist chains of light that wrapped around the battle armor's left hand, preventing it from lifting.","\"Good-hearted one, leave quickly!\" Grandmaster shouted loudly, his expression solemn.","Jian Wushuang did not linger any longer. His figure vanished in an instant beneath the broken sword.","However, when he reappeared, it was in front of all the Monks.","\"Everyone, leave quickly; I'll handle this.\" He spoke with an unquestionable authority.","Facing this young man who was merely a Yan Immortal, the Monks did not underestimate him.","They exchanged glances and then looked at Grandmaster together.","Grandmaster's expression was resolute, though there was a hint of hesitation that quickly vanished. \"We can't retreat, we absolutely cannot retreat; we can only move forward.\"","\"Can't you see the situation? Do you want all of us to perish here?\" Jian Wushuang's voice grew solemn.","Grandmaster gazed at him. \"Even so, we can't retreat. We won't take a single step back into the Great Desolate Wilderness. Even if it means death, we will die within the domain of the Great Si Region.\"","Boom!","In the midst of their conversation, the figure in battle armor swung his sword, scattering all the Monks.","Jian Wushuang narrowly avoided the strike and could not help but curse under his breath.","At this moment, Grandmaster spoke again, \"My fellow disciples, I shall clear the path for you to the Great Si Region!\"","As he uttered those words, a majestic Image Form emerged from pure Buddha's light, illuminating the countless realms.","Grandmaster's injuries instantly healed, and his aura returned to its peak in an instant.","Layers of hazy Buddhist light scripts flowed slowly around him, like the rising and setting of the moon and sun, too dazzling to gaze upon directly.","He clasped his hands together, and two supreme True Eyes emitted an unparalleled aura.","In this moment, his Immortal body and the majestic Image Form seemed to completely merge."]},{"number":5112,"title":"Chapter 5112: Remnant Glimmer of Light","paragraphs":["Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","At that moment, the faces of the five Monks were filled with sorrow, and the Buddhist light dimmed.","“Grandmaster!”","On the road of Immortal bones, Hu Qing knelt heavily, tears flowing down his face.","Grandmaster, who had already merged with the majestic Image Form, remained completely calm from beginning to end.","At this moment, in his True Eyes, there was only one adversary. “Brother Monks, let us go to the Great Si Region together!”","<font <=\"\" div=\"\">","“Go to the Great Si Region together...!”","The majestic Image Form emitted an unparalleled radiance, illuminating the empty space like a light that had never been seen in the Ancient Era.","With his majestic appearance and folded hands, he released a spell with determination and resolution, facing the armored figure.","The dazzling and ultimate spell unfolded in the void, reaching a state of utmost clarity.","The figure in the armor. towering millions of feet tall. let out a low roar at this moment, and the bloodlust in his eyes reached its peak.","Facing the overwhelming Buddhist light spell that covered the sky, he raised his sword to meet it!","This was a sword that transcended any previous move, and the already decaying broken sword even began to shatter from its hilt.","However, the indomitable Sword Intent carried the intention to obliterate the Heavenly Dao, slashing towards Grandmaster and the layers of Buddhist light spells.","When the two collided, the immeasurable force that erupted directly sent Jian Wushuang and several Monks who wanted to rush to the rescue flying, crashing heavily against the vast and magnificent boundary wall.","The void directly shattered, and the violent whirlpools were torn into pieces in an instant.","At that moment, the boundless Yan power dissipated in the void.","The pure milky-white Buddhist light, the Sword Intent tainted with pure bloodlust, and the raging Yan power all intertwined in the void, breaking the silence of this ancient and silent void.","Kneeling on the road of Immortal bones, the young samanera Hu Qing could not bear such overwhelming pressure and spewed a mouthful of divine blood. His slender figure was sent flying backward.","Immediately, a gentle surge of protective force enveloped Hu Qing, pulling him into the void.","“Kind, Kind Sir...” He barely opened his eyes and uttered two words before fainting in Jian Wushuang’s arms.","Jian Wushuang nodded, holding Hu Qing tightly, then turned his gaze to the shattered void ahead.","The void had collapsed and shattered, revealing two figures standing there.","The figure in battle armor had not suffered any substantial injuries, but the sword in his hand was completely shattered.","Even his battle armor showed signs of damage.","As for Grandmaster who had merged with the Image Form, he too had been severely wounded, and the radiant Buddhist light surrounding him had dimmed to the extreme.","The divine blood, shimmering with Buddhist light, fell onto the broken void, gradually illuminating it.","Grandmaster, with calmness in his eyes, looked at the figure in battle armor, and once again, an overwhelming aura surged around him!","He clasped his hands together, and the magnificence of the Buddha manifested through the ages.","“The Thought of the Buddha.”","At this moment, the heavens and the void trembled. Countless rays of Buddhist light ascended like trailing tassels.","Including Jian Wushuang, all the Monks widened their eyes.","At this moment, Grandmaster, shrouded in Buddhist light seemed to transcend his own constraints, reaching an unprecedented realm!","The Thought of the Buddha gave rise to countless transformations.","All things turned to dust, only thoughts endured eternally.","Centered on him, a colossal Buddha manifestation appeared, then quietly opened its true eyes.","In those moon-like True Eyes, it seemed to contain boundless compassion and supreme power.","The supreme Buddhist light covered and extinguished everything.","Jian Wushuang felt as if he were in an empty space, as if he had entered some kind of void, and he did not even know how to escape.","At this moment, everything was empty and silent.","It was hard to say how long this state of emptiness lasted. It felt like an extended period of time, and Jian Wushuang seemed to be immersed in a ethereal sea, with only the sound of long flowing water in his ears.","Until the moment when Hu Qing, cradled in his arms, stirred uneasily, Jian Wushuang snapped back from the void.","The emptiness and vastness in his eyes vanished, and the desolate wilderness reappeared before him.","As he gazed around, the endless void had turned to dust.","Gray matter, resembling tassels, fell from the cracks in the void, scattering across the desolation.","Beneath the shattered void, where Grandmaster had once stood, there was no trace of him, not even a flicker of Buddhist light.","As for the colossal armored figure that had once reached tens of millions of feet, it now appeared pitiful. The ancient armor lay in ruins, and the exposed Immortal body was almost torn apart, with divine blood splattered across the road of Immortal bones, teetering on the brink of collapse.","It was a truly awe-inspiring scene: a Six Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal had forced a Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal to a standstill, even injuring him severely.","If news of this were to spread throughout the myriad realms, it would undoubtedly cause a tremendous upheaval.","This was the first time Jian Wushuang had witnessed another Yan Immortal capable of crossing realms to engage in battle, aside from himself.","However, the price Grandmaster had paid was even more devastating. His","Immortal body had crumbled to dust, his divine consciousness had completely dissipated, all to seize the opportunity to severely wound the Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal.","The boundless radiance of Buddhist light finally dissipated, and the armored figure turned slowly to Jian Wushuang and the others before attempting to move towards them.","But after just one step, the god-like figure heavily crashed onto the road of Immortal bones, unable to stand.","Seizing this opportunity, Jian Wushuang turned and gravely addressed the group of monks, “Why did you all insist on entering the Great Si Region?”","The burly, rough-looking head monk replied, “Because we seek to find our fellow disciples who are lost in the Great Si Region.”","“Is it truly necessary?","“It is.”","“Very well, you may enter, and I will hold this guy off for a moment.”","With those words, Jian Wushuang sent Hu Qing back to the group of monks without hesitation, his determination unwavering.","The five monks hesitated but eventually decided to depart.","“Thank you, Kind Sir. We have no way to repay your kindness, but if we meet again in the future, we will surely return the favor.”","Jian Wushuang nodded slightly and then turned away.","The group of monks, still carrying the unconscious Hu Qing, entered the Great Si Region, leaving Jian Wushuang alone. He faced the armored figure lying on the celestial bone path, his gaze calm to the extreme.","“Senior Brother, are we really leaving him behind and entering the Great Si Region? He’s a Yan Immortal! Leaving him behind is like sending him to his death!”","“We have no other choice now. If we don’t do this, everything we’ve done so far will have been in vain.”","“I hope he can leave safely. Otherwise, this will become our great calamity.”","“No, something doesn’t feel right. He doesn’t seem like an ordinary Yan","Immortal. How could an ordinary Yan Immortal wander in the Great Si Region? Even a Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal couldn’t stay here. Could he be deliberately hiding his true strength? Does he have the confidence to confront that Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal?”","“Without some hidden power, who would dare to confront a being vastly superior to themselves?”","“Let’s hope for the best. I just hope the Kind Sir can leave safely..”"]},{"number":5113,"title":"Chapter 5113: Eliminating a Rank Revolutions Warrior","paragraphs":["Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Jian Wushuang stood on the bone road, his battle armor-clad figure kneeling as if it had suffered the most severe of injuries, rendering him unable to stand.","His eyes tightly shut, and his colossal form displayed numerous menacing cracks. Countless gray threads oozed from these fissures, scattering onto the bone road.","Standing in the void, Jian Wushuang frowned as he observed this scene. He had an intuition that, for the moment, his battle armor figure was completely powerless.","After hesitating for a moment, he pondered whether to strike a fatal blow to the battle armor figure or simply depart.","After some contemplation, a glint of cold determination flashed in Jian Wushuang’s eyes. With a flip of his hand, the Invisible Sword reappeared.","<font <=\"\" div=\"\">","He had decided to eliminate the battle armor figure at this moment.","Having slumbered for countless ages and experienced countless battles of the Emperors during the Ancient Era, his existence was a significant destabilizing factor. If he were to enter the Great Se Regioono from the Great Desolate","Wilderness, it would undoubtedly cause irreparable damage to the ordinary Heavenly Regions.","Therefore, standing on the outskirts of the Great Desolate Wilderness, Jian Wushuang made his decision.","The Invisible Sword in his hand had reached its pinnacle, radiating with intricate divine patterns.","The battle armor figure was a Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal, and even though he had slumbered for countless eons, his strength remained formidable.","The disparity in power between Jian Wushuang and him was simply too vast, almost unimaginable. To truly harm or even obliterate him with a single strike, only one sword technique could achieve it.","The Wushuang Sword Art, the third form of the Star River Lake Sea Sword Intent: Lake.","The Lake Sword Intent disregarded all boundaries of realms and defied all laws and orders. Even in the face of Emperors, it could unleash an indomitable strike.","This was a sword technique that could rival the swordsmanship of the Sword Immortals. Since its inception, it had been used sparingly.","At this moment, the Invisible Sword had reached its peak radiance, and if it had a physical form, it would undoubtedly emit the unique resonance of the Unparalleled Sword.","Jian Wushuang stood in the void, his eyes closed tightly, and an indomitable momentum gathered around him.","This was the prelude to that one sword strike, exuding an unstoppable aura.","However, in an instant, the sword momentum beneath Jian Wushuang vanished, and he opened his eyes, shaking his head slightly. It seemed he had decided not to employ that particular sword technique.","Indeed, the third form of the Wushuang Sword Dao, Lake was his most potent technique, but the price of using it was something he currently could not bear.","Once his own Yan power was depleted, and there was no immediate way to replenish it, it was almost as if he had been sentenced to annihilation in this Great Desolate Wilderness.","Therefore, this price was one that Jian Wushuang could not bear.","Facing the armored figure kneeling on the road of Immortal bone, another surge of sword energy erupted, shrouding the void.","Invisible brilliance radiated from the tip of the sword, filled with an unwavering determination.","This was a sword strike from Sword Immortal Ding Baiyi, a supreme sword technique.","It was a sword that sought death, but at the same time, it was a sword that embraced life through death.","In this moment, Jian Wushuang unleashed a sword from the depths of his heart!","Ding—","The crisp sound of the sword echoed beneath the void, like the tinkling of a bell, its clear notes lingering in the ears.","The Invisible Sword burst forth with pure milky-white intent, as countless strands of Sword Intent converged into one.","This sword strike, although a supreme technique, lacked any extravagance, only the counterattack borne from the desire for death. It was the Extinctive Sword Strike.","The void trembled as a tremendous force descended.","Facing the armored figure kneeling on the road of Immortal bone, this Extinctive Sword Strike was aimed at his head!","Boom!!!","The void could not withstand this sword technique, rapidly shattering.","Jian Wushuang shouted in a low voice, his eyes crimson. This sword strike consumed too much of his mental energy, to the point where he could barely control it.","The shattered void, and the sword, hung menacingly in the air.","However, almost simultaneously, the armored figure kneeling on the bone path suddenly lifted his head and swung a sky-encompassing giant palm, smashing down towards Jian Wushuang!","The two clashed, and this Extinctive Sword Strike directly blasted through the enormous palm that swung down from the armored figure, relentlessly piercing towards the figure’s head.","This was the Extinctive Sword Strike, unstoppable in its advance.","The longsword descended, its chilling radiance imminent.","A sword thrust into the armored figure’s forehead, pausing for just a moment before completely disappearing.","Jian Wushuang was also drained, his right arm, gripping the Invisible Sword, already covered in blood.","The armored figure howled in agony, cracks instantly spreading throughout his colossal body, centered on his forehead.","He struggled, howling in pain, attempting to stand on the bone road.","However, with each sway of his body, the fractures intensified.","Finally, with a deafening roar, the colossal body crumbled to dust, covering the road of Immortal bones.","Endless dust scattered, obscuring the void.","Jian Wushuang gasped heavily, his chest heaving.","This time, he paid a minimal price and managed to erase a Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal, which was truly unimaginable.","However, he still had some concerns; the armored figure wouldn’t die so easily.","After all, the gap between their realms was like an insurmountable chasm, each level a massive transformation and leap.","Jian Wushuang knew he could confront Three Revolutions and even Six Revolutions Grand Yan Immortals, but he was acutely aware that he had absolutely no chance against a Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal.","Beyond the Six Revolutions lay the Nine Revolutions, a transcendent existence capable of perceiving the Emperor’s fate energy, an unfathomable pinnacle.","That’s why Jian Wushuang couldn’t believe that the armored figure had truly perished.","“Could it be that he has really perished?” Jian Wushuang muttered, still somewhat incredulous.","After pondering for a moment, he descended onto the road of Immortal boones, focusing on observing the location where the armored figure had perished.","As he looked, his expression grew even more solemn.","Because he saw that above the spot where the armored figure had perished, countless gray threads were rhythmically pulsating in an orderly manner.","Jian Wushuang silently cursed, learning from the previous experience, and now he did not dare to hold back in the slightest. He released a majestic surge of Yan power with all his might.","The fierce Yan power surged like heavenly fire, rapidly covering every inch of the bone road.","The gray threads turned into wisps of blue smoke upon contact with Jian Wushuang’s Yan power, but more of them burrowed into the bone road.","Crackle, crackle...","Subtle yet noisy sounds quietly echoed.","Echoed beneath the road of Immortal bones.","Jian Wushuang instinctively took several steps back, his expression completely serious.","As the subtle and noisy sounds echoed, the road of Immortal bones began to tremble.","This tremor intensified, and the road’s surface started to collapse, an intense aura suddenly surging from below.","Jian Wushuang was greatly shocked. That intense aura was none other than the Yan power!","In the Great Desolate Wilderness, where Yan Power could not exist, there was now the appearance of an ancient and long-lost Yan power!"]},{"number":5114,"title":"Chapter 5114: The Great Army of the Past","paragraphs":["Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","And, from beneath the road of Immortal bones, a dense surge of Yan power gushed forth to the extreme, almost solidifying, which left Jian Wushuang greatly astonished.","This road had originally been forged from the skeletal remains of long-deceased Yan Immortals, who had perished countless ages ago, their Immortal Source returning to the universe, with no possibility of revival.","Yet, at this moment, such a powerful and concentrated Yan power could not possibly be released by a Yan Immortal.","As Jian Wushuang gazed at the Yan power that nearly obliterated the void, he suddenly realized that something beneath the road of Immortal bones had awakened!","Boom!!!","<font <=\"\" div=\"\">","The road of Immortal bones collapsed, and countless dry bones turned into powder and dissipated.","In the place where the armored figure had originally perished, a withered skeletal hand emerged from the abyssal pit.","Then, a figure with tattered clothes, a radiant skeleton devoid of flesh, stepped out.","Within the chest cavity of that skeleton, a gray substance pulsated.","With the appearance of this skeletal figure, more and more skeletons began to emerge from the abyssal pit.","Five of them...","Ten of them...","Twenty of them...","Increasingly more Yan skeletal figures revived and stepped out.","The solidifying Yan power was released by them.","Jian Wushuang slowly retreated, his eyes filled with unbearable shock.","He had encountered a skeletal army once before beneath the Endless Sea, beneath that Myriad Immortal Blood and Bones River.","However, the two could not even be compared.","Beneath the Myriad Immortal Blood and Bones River, the vast majority were Yan Immortals, with only a few being Grand Yan Immortals.","But now, within the Great Desolate Wilderness, each revived Yan skeletal figure possessed a tremendous momentum!","This kind of momentum was something a Yan Immortal could never possess; only a Grand Yan Immortal could control it!","In other words, at this moment, every resurrected Yan skeletal figure was a","Greater Yan Immortal.","Jian Wushuang continued to retreat, a great sense of crisis flashing through his heart.","Beneath the road of Immortal bones, it seemed as though all the Yan Immortals were resurrecting and continually emerging.","Each Immortal skeleton maintained the battle posture from the eve of their demise.","They held either longswords or various colored treasures, their surging Yan power reaching its peak.","“Time to go!”","That was Jian Wushuang’s only thought. He couldn’t possibly contend with so many Immortal skeletons and could only escape as quickly as possible.","However, the scene that unfolded next made his expression even more grim. He saw that in front of the Immortal skeletons, countless gray threads quietly converged into a figure.","That figure was robust to the extreme, its withered silver armor still reflecting a mottled cold radiance.","Although the figure had shrunk, Jian Wushuang could still tell at a glance that it was the same colossal figure from earlier, which had been tens of millions of feet tall.","At this moment, instead of perishing, he had transformed into a normal-sized form, seemingly having completely recovered from his severe injuries.","All the Immortal skeletons stood behind him, as if they were waiting for a command.","The figure in the armor looked at Jian Wushuang, and a bloodthirsty aura filled his eyes. He held a longsword of unknown material pointed directly ahead.","“The dog of Zhen Wuyang, today, you will surely turn into bones and will not escape!”","Jian Wushuang felt a sense of impending danger and turned around to flee.","The figure in the armor pointed his sword into the air, and the sound almost shook the void.","“Former subordinates, march to Zhen Wuyang’s palace together!”","All the Immortal skeletons responded, then moved towards the Great Si Region and the departing Jian Wushuang.","Jian Wushuang felt an overwhelming force erupting behind him and had no idea how to resist. So, he fled with all his might.","But before he could escape the boundary, a group of figures approached him from the front.","“You, why are you guys coming back?!”","The ones who had returned were the group of Monks who had entered the Great Si Region earlier, and now, astonishingly, every single one of them had come back.","They, with equally anxious expressions, as if they had just gone through a fierce battle, felt their Yan power fluctuating intensely.","The leading Monk had an extremely grim expression, seeming to be seriously injured. He said, “In front of us, an endless number of skeletons suddenly appeared, and they are incredibly powerful. We can’t break through, so we have to retreat and come up with another plan.”","Hearing his words, Jian Wushuang forced a bitter smile and replied, “I, too, have been chased by that army of skeletons.”","“What?!’”‘ exclaimed the other Monks in shock, and then they saw countless Immortal skeletons breaking through the void and chasing after them!","“How is this possible? Are we destined to be unable to enter the Great Si Region?” said a Monk with three lotus marks on his forehead, his expression filled with despair.","“There will surely be a way. These skeletons are not to be feared!” declared a rugged-looking Monk with determination.","A lean and clean-shaven Monk furrowed his brow and said, “But their numbers are overwhelming, and I can sense that their strength is formidable.”","The rugged Monk with thick eyebrows and a strong build didn’t hesitate.","“Second Brother, you take Hu Qing and leave. We’ll clear the way for you.” The other Monks nodded without hesitation.","However, this decision was immediately vetoed by the clean-shaven Monk. “If anyone is to clear the way, it should be me. You all should take Hu Qing with you.”","“There are just too many skeletons. Second Brother alone can’t stop them. I’ll stay too,” said a resolute-looking, muscular Monk.","The Monk with three lotus marks on his forehead calmly added, “I’ll stay as well. ”","The rugged-looking Monk tightened his grip on Hu Qing in his arms and urgently said, “If all of you stay, who will see off Hu Qing?”","“Hu Qing, who will him her off?”","For some reason, at that moment, all the Monks turned their gaze toward Jian Wushuang.","Then, the lean and clean-shaven Monk clasped his hands together and said,","“Kind Sir, could you please ensure Hu Qing’s safe passage into the Great Si Region? We are all willing to clear the way for you.”","Jian Wushuang furrowed his brows slightly. He had already seen that they were surrounded by an uncountable number of Immortal skeletons.","“If we keep discussing, we won’t be able to leave. Let’s go together. I can take him with me,” Jian Wushuang said urgently.","“Good.” The five Monks simultaneously clasped their hands together in agreement.","Following that, the rugged-looking Monk with thick eyebrows swiftly approached Jian Wushuang and placed the still unconscious young samanera, Hu Qing, in his arms.","After completing these actions, all five Monks simultaneously unleashed their spiritual energy.","Five Grand Yan Immortals, all at the Three Revolutions level.","Facing what seemed like an endless army of Immortal skeletons, they calmly took action.","Milk-white Buddhist light, like a colossal sun, suddenly appeared in the void, and their overwhelming Yan power was fully revealed at that moment.."]},{"number":5115,"title":"Chapter 5115: This Is Great Freedom","paragraphs":["Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Clang! Dong! Whoosh!","“Attack!”","With a rumble, a thunderous shout erupted from the void.","Sounds from the ancient past filled the air, like the resonating echoes of a long, ancient blade. Their grey, weathered armor had long since fallen into disrepair, but in this moment, their decaying bodies seemed to rekindle the essence of ancient times.","Jian Wushuang, expressionless, gazed at the approaching phantoms of the Immortal skeletons. His body was enveloped by the gentle yet incredibly sharp Buddhist light emitted by the five Monks, even affecting the karmic calamity within him.","<font <=\"\" div=\"\">","“Kind Sir, seize this opportunity to break free. We shall protect you; there’s no need to worry.”","The burly Monk, with a sudden burst of golden light behind him, may have only been a Three Revolutions, but the Buddha Image Form behind him was as strong as a Six Revolutions warrior. The combined strength of the five Monks created an unmatched force.","“You’re all sacrificing yourselves!” Jian Wushuang’s voice trembled. These Monks were indeed as stubborn as Yu Chang had described; they were determined to protect him and the young samanera, charging through the army of skeletons and into the Great Si Region.","He was originally a Yan Immortal from the Great Si Region, tasked with repairing the boundary wall in the Great Desolate Wilderness. Even if they managed to break through the front lines of the skeletal army, they would still face the boundless desolation. Without Yu Chang’s guidance, it was a dead end.","Moreover, beneath the piles of skeletal corpses lay a truly unbeatable existence. The explosive aura of Yan power in the Great Desolate Wilderness was something they could not contend with.","“You have already saved my life. I promise to fulfill your request. There’s no need for you to sacrifice yourselves to protect me.”","Jian Wushuang’s Sword Intent surged, and his Yan power suddenly manifested, restoring him to his peak strength. At this moment, his combat power was no less than that of the five Monks combined.","In the void, there suddenly arose a series of roars!","“Zhen Wuyang! Zhen Wuyang! Zhen Wuyang!”","Heart-wrenching shouts echoed, causing the skeletal army in the void to pause and turn towards the direction of the voices, kneeling down.","“We humbly welcome our Lord!”","“We humbly welcome our Lord!”","“We humbly welcome our Lord!”","Just as the skeletal army knelt, Jian Wushuang’s sharp eyes flickered. He immediately transmitted, “Now is the time! Follow me!”","The five Monks, who had initially prepared to face death, hesitated briefly, then followed Jian Wushuang, swiftly disappearing into the void.","They moved at an incredible speed, causing ripples in the void.","During their escape, the burly Monk had already concealed his Buddhist Image Form and furrowed his brows as he asked, “Kind Sir, why are we fleeing in the opposite direction? Ahead lies our Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm.” The young samanera held onto Jian Wushuang’s arm and looked up at him.","“We came from the Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm and traversed the entire Great Desolate Wilderness. It’s fraught with danger, and a significant portion of the undead army is clearly on this side.”","The Monks all wore anxious expressions. They weren’t afraid of death, but they feared dying without purpose. Even if all of them died while ensuring one person survived, it would be worthwhile. However, if they followed Jian","Wushuang and died in the boundless wilderness while fleeing towards the Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm, it would be a grave sin.","They had originally come from the Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm, bound for the distant Great Si Region, to perform the supreme merit of converting and enlightening Yan Immortals. Now, abandoning countless eons of cultivation just to stay alive was a complete deviation from their path. Unconsciously, Jian Wushuang had led them astray, causing them to feel uneasy.","But when they thought of the countless undead army they had encountered earlier, they knew that no matter which way they ran, their chances of survival were slim.","Jian Wushuang, with little young samanera in tow, looked back with a fierce expression, then continued to dash towards the Great Desolate Wilderness with undiminished speed.","“Have you not sensed a powerful pressure awakening nearby?”","The Monks showed signs of alarm. They were all third-level Grand Yan","Immortals, with strong sensory abilities, but the pressure they felt was elusive.","“No, that pressure isn’t coming from the undead army, nor the formidable armored warrior.”","The clean-shaven Monk, trembling, said, “Second brother, I’ve sensed it. It’s emanating from the void in the direction of the Great Si Region, beneath the undead.”","The group gasped. The oppressive aura from the terrifying being awakening was comparable to the countless undead, indicating its immense power.","“Such terrifying pressure... It’s as strong as nature itself, with grand ultimate power. W-we’re very fortunate that we have your guidance, Kind Sir. Otherwise, encountering such a being, we would have been instantly obliterated.”","When the Monks looked at Jian Wushuang again, they were certain he was a top-level cultivator from the Great Si Region, at least as powerful as a Six Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal.","Crack!","Shortly after their amazement, in a brief moment of silence, one of the undead, comparable to a Grand Yan Immortal, suddenly turned its neck and looked at the fleeing group. Its jet-black eyes instantly turned crimson. In an instant, all the kneeling undead turned their heads.","The leading skeletal warriors’ eyes shifted.","“I will wait here for my Lord, and you all go ahead and exterminate the lackeys of Zhen Wuyang. Don’t let a single one escape.”","“Yes!”","Below, countless skeletons stiffly moved, but the terrifying aura that erupted afterward shattered the entire void.","The hideous crack in the boundary wall was also expanding rapidly, although it couldn’t completely tear apart the entire boundary wall, it became severely damaged.","Countless skeletons surged forward, attacking Jian Wushuang and the others.","The leader was a Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortals with a severely damaged head, with only a crimson eye and a few pale fangs remaining.","“Obey orders, kill the traitor!”","Boom!","A skeleton warrior held a broken armor spear, with black bloodstains still visible on top.","As they looked at the fleeing group, he tilted his body backward and then hurled the spear heavily towards Jian Wushuang and the others.","The horrifying gray-white spear, in the void, unleashed its power. It shattered the mirror-like void at first, then broke through the shattered void like a mirror, appearing in front of the group in an instant.","Jian Wushuang, holding the young samanera in one hand, abruptly stopped his movement. He stood tall in the void, holding his sword in reverse. His long disheveled hair covered his eyes, but he still saw the spear that was now right in front of him.","His sword instantly struck out, unleashing furious Sword Qi, but it was unable to block the fierce attack of the spear.","“Kind Sir, I’ll assist you!”","The rugged Monk raised his hand and a gigantic golden palm appeared with a burst of golden light. It first entered the void and then shattered it.","In this moment, the rugged Monk exerted all his strength, knowing that now was not the time to hold back.","First one palm, then another, in just an instant, countless palm prints covered the entire void. They overlapped one after another, millions of palms facing the oncoming spear.","“Thousand-Hand Union of the Buddhist Sect.’","“This is the Great Freedom!”","In this moment, the rugged Monk unleashed an unprecedented aura.."]},{"number":5116,"title":"Chapter 5116: Battle of Breakout (1)","paragraphs":["Chapter 5116: Battle of Breakout (1)","Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","In the the boundless Great Desolate Wilderness, Yan power had long since vanished. When it erupted again, it caused the entire wasteland to tremble.","Those lost in the wasteland, the unconscious Yan Immortals, seemed to regain their former consciousness, only to shatter their own bodies in terror.","From the piles of skeletons in the valley, countless skeletons flew out to join the ranks of the great army. The being beneath the pile of skeletons also opened its eyes at this moment. His figure was not particularly large; instead, it was a small golden skeleton.","This skeleton was extremely well-preserved, even the blood-red imprint in the indentation on his forehead remained intact.","However, there were several scratches on his neck, and these marks were healing rapidly.","On the other hand, the battle between Jian Wushuang and the opposing forces turned the once silent wasteland into a hellish battleground.","The resurrected army of skeletons surrounded them, leaving no room to escape, but these were only a part of the skeleton army.","More skeletons rushed towards the source of the overwhelming pressure, but they dared not approach too close. They stopped their forms tens of thousands of feet away and then knelt down in worship.","Among these kneeling skeletons, there were seven gigantic armored giants, each holding a battle axe, sword, longsword, or banner.","Each of them possessed the strength of the previously mentioned armored figure, all at the level of Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortals.","While their strength might be slightly inferior to the elders of the Heavenly","Court, they were undeniably genuine Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortals.","Adding the one who was chasing Jian Wushuang and the others, there were a total of 8 Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortals.","This was an incredibly terrifying force, especially when combined with the countless skeletons still awakening. It was uncertain if there were some formidable entities among them. With these skeletons united, along with their proclaimed ‘Lord’, they were likely capable of sweeping through the entire wasteland. Even the Great Si Region would be hard-pressed to suppress them, perhaps only the Heavenly Court could hold them back.","Moreover, their sworn enemies were the Heavenly Court.","Jian Wushuang gazed into the distance towards the direction of the Great Si Region Heavenly Court. He wasn’t sure if the distant Great Si Heavenly Court had already detected the anomaly in this place, but all of that was no longer his concern.","The spears before them were something they had no confidence in blocking. Countless beings comparable to the Great Yan Immortals were relentlessly obstructing them from all sides, and their chances of escaping were slim to none.","The decapitated head of ancient warrior, a great cultivator of the past, now looked at the despairing crowd. His teeth shattered as he roared, “Zheng Wuyang’s lackeys, remember, remember my name. I will make you remember it for countless eons even in death.’ “Remember the name, Gu Yuan.”","Boom!","The brilliance of the Ancient Era made them seem like gods, second only to the Emperor in strength, the top cultivators revered by billions of cultivators.","However, Zheng Wuyang had reduced them to nothing but dry bones, scattered in the desolation of the Great Wilderness, trampled upon like wasteland.","With the accumulation of countless ages of resentment, Gu Yuan’s figure flickered, and he appeared beside the spears. He grasped a spear and shouted, “Break for me!”","A golden giant palm, like a strike from a deity, began to shatter upon contact.","The rugged Monk suddenly rushed out, standing in front of Jian Wushuang as the giant palm shattered. He faced the two of them, grinning.","“Kind Sir, don’t force it.","He left only these few words and, ignoring the backlash of his severe injuries, charged towards Gu Yuan, who was wielding the spear.","“Seal!”","At this moment, the rugged Monk’s Dharma transformation suddenly changed, and behind him, the Buddha Image Form transformed into a huge bell.","Several Monks who were still resisting the army of skeletons and were witnessing this were filled with sadness.","“Brothers, I’ll be leaving first.”","The bald-headed and white-bearded senior Monk closed his eyes, placed his palms together, and sadly said, “Senior Brother!”","He also unleashed his power, with 3,000 Buddhist beads surrounding him, grinding countless Yan Immortal skeletons to dust.","“I don’t have the strength the two of you. I’m barely even able to wield these 3,000 Buddhist beads. Hu Qing, please don’t blame me for being inferior in strength. ”","Boom! Boom! Boom! Boom! Boom!","The bell, Buddhist beads, Bodhi ancient trees, mustard seeds of the universe, and robes that filled the sky.","At this moment, all five senior Monks went all out. “Kind Sir, may I inquire about your name?”","“Surname Jian, given name Wushuang!”","Jian Wushuang released the young samanera Hu Qing, but he held onto his hand and bowed slightly to the five determined abbots.","“I am Jian Wushuang, a cultivator of the Great Si Region, and I respectfully bid farewell to the venerable Monks!”","“Haha, very virtuous!”","At this moment, the faces of the five Monks became unusually calm. The Great Daoo, which had been flowing for millions of years, poured forth at this moment. The besieged skeletons shattered one after another, turning into countless black mists, completely disappearing into the void of the Great Desolate Wilderness.","Gu Yuan stood above the void, his armor tattered, but the unstoppable pressure emanating from his entire body filled him with fighting spirit.","In the world, all enemies were nothing more than opponents for him.","This unparalleled fighting spirit was the result of years of accumulated grievances.","Perhaps he was no longer the top-notch cultivator he was during the glorious era of the past, and his cultivation had stagnated for billions of years. However, his genuine Nine Revolutions power still shook the void, like a war god. “A mere Three Revolution cultivator dares to challenge me. Are you seeking death?”","The moment the massive bell phantom descended, he suddenly made his move.","“Break for me!”","The plain gray spear split into tens of thousands of residual images and directly aimed at the bell. The originally unbeatable momentum began to shatter upon contact with the bell’s pressure.","“How is this possible?”","Even Jian Wushuang showed astonishment at this moment!","A Three Revolution cultivator suppressing a Nine Revolutions powerhouse!","If this news were to reach the Great Si Region, it would be enough to shock countless clans and sects.","Even the most top-tier Special Life Forms, those with naturally powerful physiques, might not be this strong!","Turning his head to look at the other Monks, they also erupted with power far beyond imagination, suppressing wave after wave of the skeletal army. In the endless space-time, in the distant Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm, under the ancient Bodhi tree, sat a majestic figure. His pair of Buddha eyes slowly opened.","Those two eyes contained countless illusions, and with just one glance, they swept over all sentient beings.","The Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm encompassed 3,000 great worlds, containing the Great Dao of all sentient beings, while billions of small worlds carried the remnants of ancient civilizations.","The entirety of the Buddhist Realm surpassed 3,000 great worlds.","Because he alone elevated the Buddhist Dao to the level of the Heavenly Dao.","So, within these 3,000 great worlds, there were worlds that rivaled or even surpassed the Great Si Region, yet they still regarded the Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm as the supreme authority.","The majestic figures all saw this scene in the Great Desolate Wilderness!","“Virtuous!”","This figure sighed softly and then closed his eyes.","Across the vast void beyond thousands of worlds, another observer was also paying attention to the changes in the Great Desolate Wilderness. However, this observer did not care about the ants being besieged but was focused on the existence beneath the skeletons.","“Hehe, I’ve put in so much effort to bring you back to the Great Desolate Wilderness. I wonder how far you can walk on the path of the Emperor.”","This hidden figure in the endless darkness continued to conceal his presence, no longer paying attention to the disturbances in the Great Desolate","Wilderness.."]},{"number":5117,"title":"Chapter 5117: Battle of Breakout (2)","paragraphs":["Chapter 5117: Battle of Breakout (2)","Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","The Great Si Region was vast, but it ultimately had its limits.","The universe, too, had its confines.","Controlling a domain or a realm did not mean much to those who stood at the pinnacle of the cosmos.","In the Heavenly Palace of the Great Si Region, Emperor Zhen Wuyang had taken the first step in controlling the entire Great Si Region.","To achieve this step was to surpass the brilliance of the Ancient Era.","Although these skeletons did not acknowledge Emperor Zhen Wuyang, in reality, he had already grasped the entire Great Si Region and successfully taken that step. Even if the being beneath these skeletons were to resurrect, they would not be a match for Emperor Zhen Wuyang, not unless they also controlled a complete Celestial Realm and took that same step.","The five Emperors of the Ancient Era were truly spectacular!","In the neighboring Celestial Realms, Emperors were born in different eras, and some eras had no Emperors at all.","But Emperor Zhen Wuyang was different. He not only lived in the era of the five Emperors but also shook the entire ancient world time and time again. In the end, he managed to shatter the ancient Heavenly Palace, seize the Great Si Region Celestial Realm, and become the first among Emperors to take that step.","The Great Si Region, the Heavenly Palace.","Emperor Zhen Wuyang gazed at the serene colored clouds, his golden eyes flickering.","At this moment, he no longer cared about Jian Wushuang; his focus was on the being that was gradually reviving.","“The times have changed. What can you do now?” Emperor Zhen Wuyang remained composed, completely indifferent to the anomalies in the vast Great Desolate Wilderness, standing proudly at the pinnacle of the Heavenly Palace.","In the Great Desolate Wilderness, beyond the realm border, Jian Wushuang and his companions remained unaware, while several powerful beings had already taken an interest in this place.","The phantom of the Buddhist bell became increasingly real, but the ferocious Monk’s aura gradually dissipated.","Under the Buddhist bell, the War God Gu Yuan, with one eye wide open, couldn’t break through the bell’s defenses in a short time.","Jian Wushuang took advantage of the outbursts of the several Monks and had long since retreated.","If he did not leave now, he would be letting down these great karmic beings.","The Buddhist light emanating from the Monks’ outbursts greatly weakened the strength of these skeletons, and the threatening power naturally caught the attention of the central figures among the skeletons.","“Qian He, take your people and kill them. I don’t want our Lord to see any of Zhen Wuyang’s followers once he revives,” spoke the figure in the azure armor, who sat quietly at the highest seat. His entire body was remarkably preserved, except for his face, which had long dissolved, leaving only a dark void and a pair of blue flames.","Qian He was among the Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortals, and she was the only female among them. She had been a top-tier cultivator even during the Ancient Era, her strength placing her at the pinnacle Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortals.","“Understood, I’ll leave right away,” Qian He’s voice was slightly hoarse. Unlike Gu Yuan, she wasn’t as manic, but she wore crimson armor and had a gruesome wound on her chest. Her facial disfigurement was similar to Gu","Yuan’s, both possessing a massive scar. However, her bones remained intact.","Despite being female, she was bald with exceptionally smooth skin, except for the terrifying remnants of her injuries.","The massive sword on her back was also missing half of its blade. She moved incredibly fast, blinking through the void and arriving at the center of the battlefield.","Gu Yuan, still trapped under the Buddhist bell, saw Qian He standing in the void, further fueling his anger.","“You damn worms, you’ve thoroughly infuriated me,” he growled.","Boom! Boom! Boom!","The spears continued to strike the Buddhist bell, but the pressure did not diminish, and Gu Yuan’s strength was gradually waning.","Qian He’s gaze turned icy. “What a fool!”","She had already noticed the oddity of the Buddhist bell from the outside. To break it, one would need strength surpassing it by tens of thousands of times— brute force over magic!","Clearly, Gu Yuan’s strength was diminishing, and he was incapable of breaking it. Even she could only rely on her most powerful strike to shatter the bell. If that single blow failed, the unleashed power would fill the entire bell, making it hundreds of times harder to break.","However, the Buddhist bell had its weakness: even if it could suppress enemies stronger than itself, it could only trap them and posed no real threat. Such a powerful bell could only be maintained by a Three Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal for a short time. Once it broke, the backlash would likely cause the rough Monk to perish.","Instantly discerning the nature of the bell, Qian He turned away, ignoring Gu Yuan trapped within. He faced no immediate threat to his life. Breaking the bell from the outside would also take some time. Instead, she decided to deal with the other foes.","Jian Wushuang held a young samanera with one hand and wielded his sword as he ventured into the midst of a sea of countless skeletons.","Most of these skeletons were ordinary Grand Yan Immortals, and many of them were held back by several Monks who were willing to sacrifice their lives. Moreover, their strength had been weakened by the Buddha’s light. This allowed Jian Wushuang, the eccentric, to go on a killing spree among them.","No one could stop him, not even those with the cultivation of Three","Revolutions Grand Yan Immortals. They were forced back by his Sword Qi.","Jian Wushuang’s eyes remained fixed on the front as a Six Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal rushed towards him.","His body showed no signs of fatigue, and in the face of a Six Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal, he did not slow down either.","The Wushuang Sword Dao ointed directly to his heart, and First move","Galaxy Lake Sea Sword Intent began to separate at that moment.","In the face of extreme adversity, Jian Wushuang’s heart, like a sword, remained calm and began to transform, and his Sword Dao started to evolve.","What is the ultimate?","At this moment, Jian Wushuang asked his own heart.","Star River, Star Lake, Star Sea.","Jian Wushuang, at this moment, was comprehending the Dao among the countless skeletons!","And his Dao expanded as rapidly as his speed.","Countless skeletons in front of him?","Cut down with a single stroke!","Six Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal?","In the narrow passage, a single strike was enough to kill!","Boom!","Jian Wushuang saw this scene in his eyes, as if it had happened countless years ago!","This was his battlefield of slaughter!","“Heart Sword Trial.”","“My heart is the only one!”","The sword of faith in the heart, this is the way of the sword!","This sword technique erupted in the depths of the Great Desolate Wilderness, and no one could feel its power because they had no heart.","At this moment of enlightenment, the Dao was right in front of him, and the cage of the Yan Immortal was completely broken.","At the same time, with the combined efforts of one person, the four Monks who had erupted completely were forced to retreat one by one. This was the power of the Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal. No matter how hard the Three Revolutions Grand Yan Immortals tried, they appeared tiny and powerless.","“Jian Wushuang!”","Surrounded by 3,000 Buddhist beads, the clean-faced Monk lowered his eyebrows and murmured, “Surprisingly, it’s the Heart Power. Outside of Buddhism, there are still practitioners of the Heart Power.”","“Before parting, I will give you another opportunity!”","The clean-faced Monk, at this moment, changed his usual demeanor and shouted angrily.","The Bodhisattva lowered his eyebrows, and the Vajra’s eyes blazed!","A towering Buddha appeared behind him.","“I am willing to pass on this legacy to Jian Wushuang and earnestly request the Supreme Lord’s approval.”","The appearance of the towering Buddha instantly suppressed the entire battlefield, and even the top cultivators in the center skeletons couldn’t","move.","“What is this?” The green-armored figure who sat quietly in the center of the skeletons, holding an axe in his hand, trembled slightly.","The giant statue gazed at the short piece of wood that flew out of the clean-faced Monk’s chest, and the Buddha’s face twitched slightly.","“Karma, karmic calamity, Heart Power... How rare!”","“Virtuous!”"]},{"number":5118,"title":"Chapter 5118: Battle of Breakout (3)","paragraphs":["Chapter 5118: Battle of Breakout (3)","Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","The battlefield suddenly changed, and the immeasurable great Buddha appeared in his Dharmakaya form, suppressing everything.","The strength of this towering Monk was unquestionably at the level of an Emperor, and not just any ordinary Emperor but one who could rival the existence of Zhen Wuyang.","The other Monks prostrated themselves before the towering giant Buddha; this presence was the supreme power of their Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm.","Even beneath the Bodhi Ancient Tree, this great being could easily rank in the top three, second only to the Heaven-Reaching Lord Buddha.","Qian He, and the trapped Gu Yuan, remained motionless at this moment.","If it were said that these Monks exerted themselves to the fullest and the radiance of the Buddha they emitted caused their strength to sharply decline, then the appearance of this towering Buddha directly froze them in the void, rendering them completely immobile.","This was still the case when the great Buddha had no intention of killing. If that presence were to deal with them, it would probably silence them within the Great Desolate Wilderness in an instant.","Far away at the core of the skeleton army, the green-armored giant slowly stood up, bearing immense pressure. His eyes were like bronze bells, and he held a mountain-splitting axe.","“Whoever it is, no one can stop the revival of my lord. The brilliance of the ancient times will once again shine upon the Great Si Region!”","Boom!","The skeleton army, unflinchingly fearless of death, charged towards Jian Wushuang and the others.","“How interesting!”","The towering giant Buddha had a benevolent expression, and with a slight movement of his finger, a short piece of wood flew directly towards Jian Wushuang. Regardless of how the skeleton army resisted, they could not stop it.","It wasn’t until the short piece of wood entered Jian Wushuang’s forehead that the towering giant Buddha withdrew his hand.","However, just as he withdrew his hand, a wave of fluctuations came from a distant desolate area and approached forcefully.","The dim void trembled for a moment, and the towering giant Buddha unexpectedly collapsed with a loud crash.","This scene sent a shiver down the spine of everyone except Jian Wushuang, who was deeply immersed in enlightenment.","This was a completely different power, a force that could invade their bodies at will.","Crack...","Just as everyone was exclaiming in surprise, the Buddha bell suddenly shattered.","Ancient Yuan, who had been trembling at the bottom of the Buddha bell, was stunned.","Then, a piercing sound echoed!","“The affairs of the Great Desolate Wilderness are none of your business!”","This voice came from beneath the skeleton and spread throughout the Great Desolate Wilderness, even to the pinnacle of the entire universe, causing it to tremble.","“How could this be?”","“How dare you!”","The Monk with the white beard, at this moment, had an expression of boundless fear in his eyes, while the other Monks were even more lifeless.","Because of the fortuitous acquisition of the Bodhi Heartwood, the white-bearded Monk could bring the Bodhi Heart Buddha of the","Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm down, but he never expected that the being beneath the skeleton could cause the Bodhi Heart Buddha’s manifestation to collapse.","The Bodhi Heart Buddha was a powerhouse who had long reached the Emperor’s cultivation realm, and he even controlled one of the 3,000 worlds, the Heart Demon Realm, for billions of years. Even the controller of the Great Si Region, Zhen Wuyang, could not break the Buddha’s manifestation in a short time.","Unless it was within Zhen Wuyang’s Dao Arena, where the power of the entire Dao Arena could be mobilized, one could achieve invincibility and effortlessly annihilate the manifestation of an equal-level existence.","“Could this be...?”","The fluctuation in the aura became even more intense after that, and this aura continued to devour the deathly silence of the Great Desolate Wilderness.","“Not good, what’s reviving isn’t just these skeletons, but the entire Great Desolate Wilderness!”","The Great Desolate Wilderness, which had existed for countless years, was actually reviving, and a towering palace rose from the pile of skeleton valley.","The entire ancient palace was bronze in color, with countless inscriptions embedded on its surface.","If Jian Wushuang were awake at this moment and saw the inscriptions on the ancient palace, he would be absolutely shocked beyond belief.","What was embedded on the surface of the ancient palace were the mysterious inscriptions that he had once glimpsed.","A wave of inexplicable and spine-tingling sounds echoed, and the residual Buddha light was instantly dissipated.","The five Monks began to cough up blood, and their manifestations collapsed one after another.","Qian He stood in the void, but she did not take the opportunity to kill these Monks. Instead, she looked towards the ancient palace, her eyes filled with fascination for the Ancient Era. “My Lord has finally revived.”","After lying dormant in the Great Desolate Wilderness for countless years, it had finally awakened.","As the ancient palace from the Ancient Era rose, the entire wilderness was completely ablaze.","“Everyone, follow me and slay the traitors!”","Gu Yuan, no longer suppressed by the Buddhist light, soared into the sky, wielding his spear like a god-king descending.","“You all, meet your end!”","In the heart of the grim battlefield, the burly Monk’s chest was exposed, and blood flowed down from the corner of his mouth.","“This humble Monk will go first!” The rugged Monk closed his eyes, then his entire body erupted in a massive golden wave, shattering the center of the battlefield.","Boom!","“Second Senior Brother!”","Before the white and pure Monk could struggle, the other Monks consecutively detonated themselves, instantly sweeping the entire battlefield.","But in the current wilderness, the endless army of skeletal warriors, despite the self-destruction of these Three Revolutions Grand Yan Immortals, was like a drop in the ocean, causing no ripples. The void that had momentarily cleared was once again filled with skeletal battle armor.","“Hmph! You scoundrels! How dare you harm my sacred body!” Gu Yuan, holding his spear, pierced through the still-undestroyed white and pure Monk and then boldly rushed out, seizing the white and pure Monk who was about to self-destruct.","Qian He lowered her head, her icy eyes shifting, and whispered, “Stop playing around, one of them is about to escape.”","Jian Wushuang, who had struggled several times at the edge of the skeletal army, stood proudly in the void, untouchable by anyone. However, he couldn’t break free from the encirclement of skeletons.","His cultivation had long reached the limit of Yan Immortal cultivation realm, and so had his Dao.","Both his cultivation realm and his Dao were pushing the boundaries, and countless skeletal beings that could rival Grand Yan Immortals shattered under his divine sword.","The skeletal beings, now at the Three Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal level, had regained full consciousness. Their strength was no less than that of their predecessors from the Ancient era, but they still shattered under a single sword strike.","And without realizing it, Jian Wushuang’s Sword Principle already merged and flowed seamlessly with his ultimate Dao. Now, a single sword strike was enough to eliminate a Six Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal.","Such power might only be resisted by a Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal.","Heart Power! It was ethereal!","Jian Wushuang fought recklessly, trapped in his own cage, and this empty space was no longer silent.","Stars burst forth, forming a starry sky.","“Where am I?”","At this moment, there were no skeletons around him, and the young samanera, Hu Qing, whom he had been holding, was nowhere to be seen. He was the only one beneath the starry sky.","A shooting star descended, splashing waves of water, like a river of stars.","In the boundless void, countless universes hung above the starry sky, like lakes and seas.","The Dao of the ultimate Sword Dao existed not in a realm, a world, or any particular universe, and it was not created by any specific space.","Jian Wushuang felt a bit lost, lost in his own Dao.","“Where is my Dao?”","Silence.","On the battlefield of the Great Desolate Wilderness, Jian Wushuang suddenly stopped, standing motionless in the void.","The eyes of the surrounding skeletons shifted, the hands holding their weapons trembled, and then they swarmed towards him.","In the distance, Qian He was also approaching, while Hu Qing, the young samanera, held his prayer beads, bowing his head in silent prayer.","Dong! Dong! Dong!"]},{"number":5119,"title":"Chapter 5119: Stone Axe","paragraphs":["Chapter 5119: Stone Axe","Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","In the endless expanse of the starry sky, Jian Wushuang sat cross-legged on a desolate star, where he felt no passage of time.","Perhaps it had been countless billions of years, or maybe it was just a fleeting moment.","“Sigh, I wonder what’s happening in the outside world. Perhaps I have already perished!”","Trapped within his own cage, Jian Wushuang furrowed his brow. In this silent expanse of stars, he exhausted every method but couldn’t break free.","Yet he discovered that within this starry space, he was invincible.","Guided by the threads of karma, he could even sense that the Great Si Region was also within this starry expanse.","It was just incredibly distant. He flew and traversed for an unknown length of time but couldn’t find any Celestial Realm. He could only follow the guidance of karma and continue on.","It wasn’t until this star came to a stop that he realized, no matter how much he flew, he couldn’t leave this starry space.","Cross-legged on this star for an unknown duration, it was only then that he noticed signs of life.","“Hey! Haha!”","A colossal giant, thousands of feet tall, ran on the surface of the earth. The originally desolate and chaotic star, under the influence of this giant, gradually became clear and revealed its original appearance.","Sitting cross-legged on a mountaintop, Jian Wushuang found all of this quite novel. He had flown for who knew how long without encountering any Celestial Realms or planets with life. Yet, this star-born giant was the first sign of life.","The life of this giant, with a body spanning thousands of feet, was a unique and special existence in the heavens and earth. His entire body had been bestowed by this star, and he possessed extraordinary talents. In just a few thousand years, he had already reached the Supreme cultivation realm.","However, despite his formidable realm and physical strength, his understanding of the Dao was not even comparable to that of an ordinary junior cultivator.","The turbidity between heaven and earth was dispelled, and the giant also noticed Jian Wushuang’s presence. He roared and threw a punch towards Jian Wushuang.","Jian Wushuang, who had long surpassed the limits of Yan Immortal, merely glanced at him and paid him no further attention.","The massive fist shadows descended upon him, but before they could reach","Jian Wushuang, they vanished, and the giant retreated thousands of feet away. However, he remained fearless, charging forward with unwavering determination.","For several years, these two figures confronted each other. The giant, realizing he couldn’t overcome Jian Wushuang, turned and walked toward the towering forest.","Jian Wushuang felt a hint of disappointment in his eyes but then closed them once again. He was contemplating the Bodhi Heartwood, a short piece of wood that had flown from his brow since he entered this place.","The inscriptions on the short piece of wood remained enigmatic to him, their origin a mystery. Yet, out of curiosity, he had continuously held it, either contemplating the inscriptions or calming his restless heart.","Otherwise, the boundless sense of loneliness would have driven him insane long ago.","Within the towering forest, the giant wielded a stone axe, grinning broadly. This treasure had come into existence with the birth of the universe, emerging from the chaos. However, the giant had forgotten about it in the forest while wielding it to chop down giant trees.","After many years, he finally remembered the handy axe and returned to the forest to search for it. Now that he had it in hand again, he decided to cause trouble for Jian Wushuang.","Boom! Boom!","The giant’s footsteps echoed like thunder, shaking the earth beneath him. Jian Wushuang, seated atop a mountain peak, raised an intrigued eyebrow and said,","“Big guy, you dare to come back!”","The giant, shirtless and partially covered in tree bark, had decided to wrap himself in tree bark after seeing Jian Wushuang wearing clothes the last time.","“Not bad, you learn quite fast,” Jian Wushuang commented, glancing at the tree bark on the giant’s body.","The towering giant grew somewhat annoyed, lifted his axe, and swung it toward Jian Wushuang. However, the massive axe slid off Jian Wushuang’s brow without making contact. He had cultivated his strength nearly to the limit of Ascendant Divinity, far beyond what this recently birthed, unique life form, the giant, could match.","Furthermore, the giant had no teacher to guide him; each move he made was extremely clumsy.","Smack!","This time, Jian Wushuang did not dodge. He caught the giant’s axe with one hand and then exerted a sudden force. The tremendous impact traveled through the axe head and into the handle.","Thud!","The handle shattered, and it sent the giant staggering back thousands of feet.","Splurt!","A mouthful of golden blood sprayed from the giant’s mouth. He wiped his mouth and stood up again.","Holding the enormous axe, Jian Wushuang casually tossed it back to the giant.","As he looked at the axe now lying at his feet, the giant’s expression flickered.","This axe had been with him since birth, but now it was covered in countless cracks, resembling secret runes.","The giant carefully lowered his body, his disheveled hair hanging down, with a few leaves still stuck to it.","After picking up the axe, he glared at Jian Wushuang, let out a roar, and then headed towards the towering forest.","Jian Wushuang scratched his head and muttered to himself, “Is he angry?”","After the giant left this time, he never came to find Jian Wushuang again. Instead, he learned from Jian Wushuang’s example and practiced alone in the forest.","And who knows how manv vears passed, an endless murkv Qi descended upon the earth, shrouding the entire land in darkness once more.","But for Jian Wushuang, this murky Qi was insignificant. However, in all these years, he still couldn’t break free from his own constraints. There were even a few times when he wanted to leave, but the deathly silence around him made him hesitate.","This star was alive, and even though the giant no longer paid him any attention, at least there was a living presence nearby.","“This big guy is really stingy, isn’t he? He hasn’t come to see me.”","Jian Wushuang played with the short piece of wood in his hand. This time, he decided to take the initiative and visit the towering forest to see what the big guy was up to!","Boom! Boom! Boom!","The sound of explosions echoed from the forest as the giant swung his arms to disperse the surrounding murky Qi. Unfortunately, his axe was damaged, or else he could have easily dispersed the murky Qi with it.","Standing on a tree branch, Jian Wushuang watched this scene with a faint smile. With a casual gesture, he summoned the axe.","The giant was frantically dispelling the murky Qi and didn’t notice that Jian Wushuang had already taken his axe.","Jian Wushuang reduced the size of the axe, and with a thought, he repaired the cracks one by one. However, many new patterns appeared on the once smooth surface.","The axe was repaired, but the handle was completely shattered, making it difficult to restore.","Now he had nothing on him, and he didn’t know what to find to replace it.","With no clear plan in mind, Jian Wushuang was thinking about secretly visiting other planets or Celestial Realms to see if he could find some treasures to help restore the axe. After all, it was a treasure nurtured by a primordial star, so restoration might be challenging, but repair shouldn’t be a problem.","Just as Jian Wushuang was about to leave, the piece of Bodhi Heartwood he held in his other hand began to tremble slightly, and it unexpectedly merged with the axe.."]},{"number":5120,"title":"Chapter 5120: Breaking Through the Cage","paragraphs":["Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","The Bodhi Heartwood and the axe merged seamlessly, and the patterns on the axe erupted with bursts of light.","Images flooded into his mind one after another: a majestic Buddha with kind eyes and benevolent expression, a rugged Monk standing resolutely, a fair-skinned Monk holding his own severed head, a young samanera with lowered brows and closed eyes, clutching a string of prayer beads.","These scenes played out in his mind until he saw his own figure standing on an ancient battlefield.","As he absorbed these images, the stone axe suddenly flew out of his hand, heading towards the giant.","“Hey! ”","<font <=\"\" div=\"\">","The giant grinned as he saw the intact axe, reaching out to catch it effortlessly as it floated in front of him.","In that moment, the axe seemed to become one with the giant, unleashing its full power in his hands.","The patterns on the axe transformed into mysterious symbols, and with each swing, he learned to harness their power.","It wasn’t until the murky Qi once again surpassed the giant that he finally stopped.","As the obscurity dissipated, the world regained its brightness, and the giant noticed Jian Wushuang in the distance. This time, he didn’t charge forward but instead touched the axe in his hand and roared at Jian Wushuang before departing.","Through the myriad of forest creatures, Jian Wushuang saw the giant sitting cross-legged in a tree hollow, his eyes closed in contemplation of the patterns on the axe.","“Hmm...”","Losing the Bodhi Heartwood wasn’t a big deal, but why did it willingly merge with the axe and then fly to the giant?","There were too many mysteries contained within all of this. Jian Wushuang pondered, deciding to closely observe the giant’s every move.","The giant remained seated in the tree hollow, and after an unknown amount of time, the murky Qi descended once again.","This time, with just one swing of the axe, the giant caused the murky Qi to rise by a great degree. In a matter of a few breaths, he had swung over ten thousand times, exhausted and drained. The murky Qi had risen to an astonishing height.","Despite the simplicity of the patterns on the axe for Jian Wushuang, they were nothing more than faint traces left by his extreme Dao power when it erupted. However, even these faint traces were comparable to the great Dao of an ordinary Ascendant Immortal.","Though no one guided the giant, his comprehension of the patterns on the axe advanced astonishingly quickly.","As the murky Qi descended several times, the giant continued to wield the axe until he was utterly spent.","From the beginning, with ten thousand strikes, to the final million strikes. But the faster he cleaved, the faster the murky Qi sank.","Observing the giant’s actions, Jian Wushuang secretly found an answer! As for the patterns on the axe, they were left by him, so he naturally understood them better than anyone else.","At the beginning, the patterns contained the essence of speed.","So, with each strike, the giant increased the amount of murky Qi several times over.","The path to simplicity!","It’s easy to accumulate quantity, but the challenge lies in reducing quantity and pursuing qualitative change.","Indeed, after reaching the realm of a million strikes, the giant began to stagnate. Fortunately, though he was simple-minded, he wasn’t stubborn and began trying to comprehend the essence of the million strikes.","The murky Qi sank once again.","Hoo!","The giant’s axe struck for the first time, and a heavy aura surged forth, directly elevating the murky Qi by a hundred feet.","Standing in the distance, Jian Wushuang’s eyes flickered. As the top-tier Transcendent Swordmaster, his memory was incredibly strong. He could tell that this strike from the giant was the 3,600th strike out of the previous million strikes. At that time, he had been somewhat surprised by this strike!","Hoo! Ha! He!","With each strike, the giant caused the murky Qi to rise by a hundred feet. This time, he had only struck a hundred times, yet the murky Qi had risen to a height of ten thousand feet. If he were to strike a million times and raise the murky Qi to a million feet, he didn’t do so.","He put away the axe and returned to his tree hollow, continuing to ponder the patterns on the axe.","Jian Wushuang’s figure flashed as he entered the murky Qi.","Hoo!","Closing his eyes, he took a deep breath of the murky Qi.","“This murky Qi is similar to prenatal energy, left behind after nurturing life.","But why does it linger after life is fully nurtured?”","Emperor True Martial Yang, after taking that step, expanded the Great Domain, extending it into the Great Wilderness, effectively pushing it to its limits.","Could this murky Qi be similar to the situation in the Great Domain?","Jian Wushuang’s eyes flickered, and he made a bold guess!","The height to which the murky Qi could rise was also limited, probably reaching around a hundred million feet. Beyond that point, it wouldn’t sink anymore, and the heavens and the earth would forever remain clear and visible.","Jian Wushuang was baffled by the immense power of the giant. It seemed that the giant’s strength could now cause the murky Qi to rise tens of thousands of feet, but the goal was still far from reach.","With no clear understanding of this vast starry sky, Jian Wushuang once again landed in the towering forest and observed the giant.","When the murky Qi descended once more, the giant did not rise this time. With a casual swing of his axe, the murky Qi soared to a height of ten thousand feet.","This sight left Jian Wushuang somewhat astonished.","In his heart, he couldn’t help but marvel, “Could this giant be an exceptionally rare genius of the Dao?”","He was tempted to take the giant as his disciple, but he quickly realized that their situations were no different. Both were trapped in cages, only of varying sizes.","After the murky Qi ascended to ten thousand feet, the giant within the tree hollow made no further moves, continuing his contemplation.","“This guy has changed his demeanor quite a bit; he can actually restrain from using his full strength.”","In the past, the giant would exhaust himself to the point of collapse before stopping, but now, with just a single swing of his axe, even the tree hollow remained intact.","The principles of simplicity in the Dao had become clear to the giant to some extent. At this moment, he was not only comprehending the patterns on the axe but also using it to create his own techniques.","The giant himself didn’t know when this transformation had begun. Perhaps it was because of the axe, or perhaps it was a reflection of his true self.","From the verv beginning of his existence. his original DurDose might have been to combat the murky Qi.","This insight wasn’t exclusive to him; even Jian Wushuang, through spatial manipulation, had examined the workings of the entire star and discovered its secrets.","However, the giant paid no heed to these distractions. He confronted his true purpose: to be born to resist the murky Qi and to continue the battle.","In the following years, whenever the murky Qi descended, the giant within the tree hollow effortlessly shattered it with a single swing of his axe. What had started with ten thousand feet soon escalated to a million feet.","One day, as the murky Qi descended once again, the giant emerged from the tree hollow, his unkempt hair flowing in the breeze.","Facing the murky Qi, his expression remained calm.","His lips moved slightly, not to shout, but to softly utter, “One.”","It was surprising to Jian Wushuang that the giant had learned to speak at some point!","In the instant he spoke, he swung his axe lightly, tearing through the fabric of space. Although it was the space of this star, the sheer power of it left Jian Wushuang utterly astounded.","The axe that tore through space streaked across the sky, causing the murky Qi to disintegrate with a resounding crash. With a single swing, it soared to three million feet.","Then came the second swing, and the murky Qi rose to nine million feet.","“Eleven!”","With each swing of his axe, his voice grew louder. By the time he swung the eleventh time, the murky Qi had risen to a billion feet.","Jian Wushuang knew he was capable of achieving this, but he never expected it to happen so quickly.","Once the murky Qi reached a billion feet, it gradually stabilized and ceased to descend, just as he had calculated.","However, the giant below frowned as he gazed at the murky Qi. While he understood that the cessation of the murky Qi’s descent would result in eternal brightness in the world, this was not what he desired.","He craved freedom and boundlessness.","He yearned to completely disperse the murky Qi, to break free from his prison!"]},{"number":5121,"title":"Chapter 5121: Breakthrough","paragraphs":["Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","The explosive eruption that soared into the sky made the entire star tremble.","The giant resembled a deity of ancient times, splitting open the heavens and the earth with a single strike.","The once thick and murky Qi had considerably lightened, but at a height of tens of millions of feet, it had already reached its limit. It had nowhere to hide, forced to withstand the giant’s axe head.","The brightness of the heavens and earth caused the giant to grin, and his eyes became much clearer, devoid of the previous murkiness.","However, as long as the murky Qi did not dissipate, he wouldn’t rest. He and the murky Qi were the only things that could remain on this star, a destiny that seemed to have accompanied him since birth.","<font <=\"\" div=\"\">","Whoosh!","The giant once again swung his massive arm, and at that moment, his body underwent a transformation. A faint yellow radiance slowly appeared on his chest, and a powerful force gathered within him.","“Fourteen!”","As the roar echoed, a colossal axe shadow reduced the ancient forest to rubble, turning countless towering trees into splinters.","The axe shadow raced through the towering forest, flying toward the sky, like a true dragon roaring into the heavens.","Crackling!","Inside the murky Qi, thunder flickered. After taking this blow head-on, the murky Qi once again grew faint, now almost transparent.","Looking up at the sky from the earth, one could vaguely see several stars.","This sensation greatly excited the giant. His body trembled violently, and the exhaustion in his body erupted at this moment. The faint golden color on his chest burst forth, and golden patterns spread across his face like cracks.","The boundless mysterious yellow energy that was once within him had now completely depleted after that single strike.","Jian Wushuang’s figure was ethereal, standing in the distance, watching it all.","He could see that the giant was already running on fumes. In fact, the murky Qi had become uncontrollable after the eleventh strike. However, the giant had reached a point where he was willing to sacrifice his life to shatter the cage completely.","This left him somewhat puzzled, much like his feelings towards Xuan Yi and the others.","What were these people truly fighting for?","In the glorious era of the Great Si Region, the time of the ancient hopes, they shone brilliantly, with five great powerhouses coexisting, intimidating countless Heavenly Regions and dominating an entire era.","Yet, Zhen Wuyang shattered the glorious Ancient Era. In his quest to unify the Great Si Region, he had slaughtered countless brilliant and dazzling Grand Yan Immortals in the Great Desolate Wilderness.","Destroying the once revered Ancient Era had been Zhen Wuyang’s goal, all for the sake of unifying the Great Si Region, gaining control over the entire Great Si Region, and taking that next step forward.","That had been his purpose.","But what about Xuan Yi? What had been his aim?","Why hadn’t the five great powers of the Ancient Era taken that step forward?","For a moment, Jian Wushuang felt a bit bewildered.","He started to understand.","Zhen Wuyang’s path of cultivation had given him control over the Great Si Region, allowing him to suppress so many Great Primal Immortals of the ancient era. With the establishment of the Heavenly Court, Zhen Wuyang’s path had become utterly unassailable within the Great Si Region.","No one could contend with him. Even the revived entity posed no threat. In the Ancient Era, that entity had been suppressed by Zhen Wuyang, and even in its revived state, it would still be no match for him. On his home turf, it was still not his equal.","As for the Emperors of the Ancient Era, they could at best be considered beginners in the Entry Emperor realm, without a complete grasp of the Emperor’s Great Dao.","Much like Jian Wushuang himself today, although he had comprehended the supreme Dao, he still could not fully control it.","There was one crucial difference, though. He had failed to master the supreme Dao and had become trapped in this starry expanse.","The Ancient Era Emperors, on the other hand, were trapped within the Great Si Region.","The difference between one Dao and another was as vast as the heavens and the earth.","This starry expanse had given birth to countless universes, each containing numerous Celestial Realms.","The Great Si Region was nothing more than a speck of dust in comparison.","That was the supreme Dao, encompassing the entire starry expanse.","If one were to say that the Ultimate Sword Dao was the pinnacle of the world of swords, then the supreme Dao was the highest rule across the entire starry expanse.","Zhen Wuyang’s Dao was the pinnacle of the Great Si Region. If he wanted to progress further, he had two options: either master another Celestial Realm or comprehend the Dao of the universe itself, gaining control over the entire universe. Of course, the latter was highly impractical.","Jian Wushuang had realized how incredibly challenging it was to comprehend the Emperor’s Great Dao. To grasp an even more astonishing path required exceptional talent, but as for the Great Dao of the Universe, he didn’t even entertain the thought.","Based on Jian Wushuang’s current perception, only a handful of the constellations embedded in the starry sky were under human control. Countless universes existed within the vast expanse of the cosmos.","According to his sense of causality, the universe in which the Great Si Region resided remained untamed by any.","From the giant’s body, Jian Wushuang gleaned many insights, such as the scorching energy in the giant’s chest, which shone as brightly as the most dazzling stars in the night sky.","The faint golden lines represented the River of Time and Space, with several of these golden rivers present in the starry sky. These rivers were formed by numerous universes, with the widest being 9 in number, and 99 smaller ones, totaling 108.","Celestial Realms, Universes, the River of Time and Space, and the starry sky— all of it began to make sense to Jian Wushuang. The laws of space expanded at an astonishing rate, reaching the pinnacle of Yan Immortal that he had attained long ago, and at this moment, they began to shatter.","In the starry expanse, both he and the giant started to break through simultaneously.","It was as if they shared some kind of connection, with both of them breaking through their own limitations at this very moment.","One was the first life born within a star, and the other was the first to comprehend the Great Dao across the entire starry sky.","The giant, seated amidst the forest, grasped the handle of his axe, and fissures started turning into inscriptions on his arm. The power within his body surged at this moment.","This power was scorching, and his breath from his nostrils felt like torch flames.","The endless burning power caused his entire body to emit a golden light. These rays of light seeped through the cracks on his body, illuminating everything around him.","Though the pain was excruciating, the scorching energy was simultaneously repairing the cracks on his body.","At this moment, the giant felt an extreme dryness in his mouth. He staggered to his feet and began to run.","He charged out of the ruins in the towering forest, heading towards the largest river on the star.","In the starry sky.","Jian Wushuang’s breakthrough was considerably easier than the giant’s. His constitution was inherently unique within his universe.","As for the Great Dao of Grand Yan Immortal, he had comprehended it long ago in the Great Desolate Wilderness but had always struggled to master it completely.","Now, his breakthrough had increased the probability of mastering it entirely.","The Yan power within him rotated, and the incredibly pure power allowed him to directly ascend to the Three Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal.","The power within him was limitless, comparable to that of a Nine Revolutions","Grand Yan Immortal. Coupled with his Ultimate Sword Dao, he could rival a Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal.","And that did not even account for the Great Dao he had yet to fully grasp. If he truly mastered it, he would become the most dominant figure among the Grand Yan Immortals. Except for the perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortals, he would have no equals.","He clenched his palm, and the formidable force made the entire starry sky tremble.","“Unfortunately, I still haven’t mastered the Grand Dao completely. I still can’t leave.. I’m truly envious of that big fellow!”"]},{"number":5122,"title":"Chapter 5122: Splitting Sky","paragraphs":["Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Rumble!","Each of the giant’s steps created a huge crater in the ground. He was extremely fast, crossing millions of steps with every step. These craters could form lakes and canyons.","Finally, when he used his last bit of strength, he fell to the edge of the river bank.","Looking at the surging river, the giant reached out his hand and drank the clear water.","The water slid from his mouth into his abdomen, but it was a drop in the bucket. The scorching power was still tormenting him.","<font <=\"\" div=\"\">","However, this mouthful of water allowed him to catch his breath. He had a trace of strength to straighten his body. He jumped into the river and gulped down the water.","The river almost surrounded the star, and there were countless tributaries.","Although the river water was almost endless, it could not stop the giant from devouring it. The water in the tributaries dried up continuously, and finally, the entire river was almost dried up, leaking out of the riverbed.","“Phew...”","After drinking the entire river water, the giant finally recovered more than half","of his strength and absorbed all the burning energy in his body.","Straightening his body, the tree bark on his body had already fallen off, and only a few leaves were left to cover his lower body.","His body was already covered in golden patterns. All the cracks were repaired by the golden patterns. Not only had his strength recovered to its peak, but it had also improved further.","Jian Wushuang slid down from the void and stood on a distant mountain peak, sensing the giant’s strength.","This star, or rather, the division of power in this universe, was very different from the Great Si Region he was in. For example, the giant was born with pure Yang, but he had the physique of a Chaotic Divine Demon.","After absorbing the power of the axe, Jian Wushuang could not see the strength of the giant.","In terms of the cultivation realm, giants were born with the primordial chaos and were bestowed with the supreme laws, but they were far from being the masters of the laws.","Jian Wushuang guessed that he should be at the Quasi-Sage realm.","With such strength, he could be considered a powerhouse in the Great Si Region, but in the starry sky, he was not even comparable to an insect.","If one wanted to travel across the universe, they had to be at least at the Grand Yan Immortal realm. With the speed of a Grand Yan Immortal, they could cross the neighboring Celestial Realms, just like how the Monks came to the Great Si Region.","If one wanted to cross the universe, one would have to have the strength of an Emperor. Emperors who controlled Celestial Realms would not easily leave their nest. Only Emperors who had yet to control a Celestial Realm would constantly cross Celestial Realms, or even leave the original universe to find some uncontrolled Celestial Realm in other universes to take that step.","Zhen Wuyang’s luck was considered good. The Great Si Region was fought over by five Emperors, and he took control of the Great Si Region as a future resident.","This caused the revived corpses to curse Zhen Wuyang. Those Grand Yan Immortals had long regarded the Great Si Region as their own. They only recognized the five Emperors of the Ancient Era and did not recognize Zhen Wuyang at all. They felt that he was a villain who monopolized the Great Si Region.","Actually, it was these Grand Yan Immortals who were wrong, and it was also the five Emperors who were wrong. The Heavenly Dao was heartless to begin with, how could it tolerate so many Emperors? One person had to control the Great Si Region. Not only did their strength not increase, but it would also cause their cultivation level to decrease.","The neighboring Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm also had many Emperors.","However, their world was different from the Great Si Region. The Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm had 3,000 macro worlds and trillions of small worlds.","The Heaven-Reaching Buddha controlled the largest Heavenly Realm among the 3,000 big worlds, which was how the Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm was formed. Many of the remaining macro worlds were not weaker than the Great Si Region, and some were even stronger.","These worlds were naturally not empty. They were controlled by many Emperors, but more than half of them remained.","Since the Heaven-Reaching Buddha controlled the Heavenly Realm, the 3,000 worlds naturally respected him and were collectively called the","Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm. In fact, the 3,000 worlds were in chaos. Even if the Heaven-Reaching Buddha controlled the Heavenly Realm, he could not suppress all the Emperors.","However, he had been resisting the Emperors of the outside world, preventing them from controlling the 3,000 major worlds. That was why he was respected by the Emperors who controlled the major worlds.","Jian Wushuang had deduced all these things based on the Bodhi Heartwood. Whether it was accurate or not was still to be verified.","If he could get out of here, he still wanted to go to the Heaven -Reaching Buddhist Realm.","After all, he still needed to make a trip to the Buddhist Realm to deal with the karma calamity on his body.","Now, whether he could leave or not depended on how much he could comprehend from the giant.","Jian Wushuang’s eyes lit up as he stood on the top of the mountain.","The giant standing on the riverbed seemed to have sensed his gaze. It was not because the giant had a strong sense of perception, but because Jian Wushuang did not hide himself at all.","The giant turned to look at him, his determined eyes filled with confusion.","From the moment he was born, his mind was focused on driving away the turbid Qi that had once enveloped him. This mind was eternal.","However, he felt that Jian Wushuang was much stronger than the murky Qi. However, he did not feel any suppression from Jian Wushuang.","This also made him less hostile towards Jian Wushuang. At most, he just wanted to trample on him, but he was not strong enough.","Even though his strength had reached a new level, he still couldn’t see through Jian Wushuang.","As for the murky Qi, his eyes were cold as he looked at the sky.","The first fourteen moves were comprehended by him from the axe’s lines. The lines on the axe were just some Yan power that contained ultimate Dao marks that Jian Wushuang had casually instilled into it. After so many years of comprehension, it was already very impressive that he could comprehend fourteen moves.","However, while he was comprehending the patterns on the axe, the giant had also gained a lot of insight into the secret art of the axe. He had been practicing an axe art in his heart, but he had never used it.","This axe technique did not have the exquisiteness of the previous fourteen axes, but it was simple and pure, as if it was born from chaos like him. “Fifteen.","The patterns on the giant’s body emitted a golden light. His thick and dark arms waved gently, and then the power in his body was circulated to the extreme.","For the last chop, he had used all his strength to perfect the power of this chop.","The murky Qi was like a demon in his heart, which kept pestering him. It was the same as Jian Wushuang’s karmic calamity.","In the early stages of his life, he had just been born, so he did not treat the turbid Qi too seriously. However, now that he was strong enough, his mentality naturally changed drastically. He wanted to shatter the turbid Qi even more. It was as if he was possessed, and he was obsessed with comprehending the axe technique. Now, he had even created an axe that belonged to him.","Golden light exploded from the giant’s body. He let out a furious roar and used all his strength to execute his axe. This axe was called Splitting Sky.","The explosion of the giant blurred everything around him. This was the fluctuation of space.","Jian Wushuang, who was standing in the distance, could not bear to see the land completely destroyed. He stabilized the space and looked at the desperate giant in a daze.","Faced with such power, the turbid Qi in the sky condensed the turbid Qi that enveloped the star, forming a huge storm and engaging the giant in a life-and-death battle.","The fifteenth axe strike, ‘Splitting Sky Technique’, burst forth from the ground. The axe shadow was simple and simple, like a wild man’s casual slash, but the power contained in it was enough to destroy an entire star.."]},{"number":5123,"title":"Chapter 5123: Leaving","paragraphs":["Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","The power that made the heavens and the earth tremble had swept over.","A murky Qi coalesced into an immensely thick, yellow shield. This shield, a million battles thick, harnessed all the impure energy. If it could withstand it, it would be turned into a spirit, and hailed as Saint, becoming the Heavenly Dao of an entire star. If it couldn’t, it would dissipate entirely.","The colossal axe shadow surged into the sky, showing no fear of any existence.","Before it, the yellow divine shield seemed as thin as paper.","When the two collided, there was no upheaval. The axe shadow unilaterally crushed through, directly shattering the yellow shield formed from murky Qi.","<font <=\"\" div=\"\">","Sizzle!","Even the final layer of hazy aura, though not yet transformed into spirit, began to tremble when faced with the axe shadows at this moment.","The divine shield, formed with all its might, could not withstand it. After all, it had not reached the level of spirit transformation.","A sound of unwillingness and commotion emanated from within the murky Qi. Jian Wushuang’s eyes widened in surprise. Both the axe technique and the murky Qi resonated with him.","In this battle, the giant emerged victorious.","Both of them shared a similar fate. One was able to create his own axe technique through profound comprehension of secret methods, breaking free from his limitations. Jian Wushuang couldn’t help but admire him.","The axe shadows completely pierced through the hazy aura, cut through the void beyond, dissipating only when they were billions of miles away.","This strike!","It shocked the heavens and moved ghosts and gods.","Jian Wushuang stored everything he had witnessed in his mind, then closed his eyes and sat cross-legged on the mountaintop.","Fate was indeed peculiar. He indirectly aided the giant, and in turn, the giant reciprocated.","The moment Jian Wushuang sat down, the sky underwent a complete transformation.","From that moment on, there was no more hazy aura above the stars; instead, there was a bright and starry sky.","The giant looked at all of this, his eyes moist. He did not even know why tears welled up in his eyes; perhaps it was instinctual.","All the patterns on his body shattered, but he did not care. In the days that followed, he settled on a mountain adjacent to Jian Wushuang’s.","He created his own script to record his experiences. He also learned to build houses and erected a simple wooden hut on the mountainside, watching the sunset every day.","Unbeknownst to him, he felt his body gradually fading, and his form became much smaller.","As his form gradually dissipated, other life forms appeared on the stars.","There were birds and beasts in the forest, and gigantic creatures in the lakes. Although these life forms were not as powerful as he was, they were by no means weak. They began to band together and wage wars.","And the giant watched all of this until his body completely dissipated into the earth.","The giant dissipated into the heavens and the earth, but his abilities were bestowed upon the mighty beasts.","Not only the giants, but in the millennia that followed, this planet gave birth to tens of thousands of races. They inherited the abilities of the giants and began to comprehend the heavenly path of the giant’s incarnation.","After countless eons, this planet came under the rule of human cultivators. A human cultivator, who astonished the ancient races, dominated the entire planet with a single blazing axe.","The holy land of the human race, the Eastern Saint Divine Mountain.","“Clan Leader, I succeeded.”","In the sacrificial hall of the divine mountain, a burly man with disheveled hair was kneeling in front of the statue with an axe on his back. He was crying tears of joy.","The human race had risen a million years ago. At that time, they were still an ordinary race. Because of the strength of their leader, they had led the human race to the peak of the race. They were known as the five peak races along with the Monster, Divine, Ghost, and Dragon tribes.","The man could never forget the imposing figure of the Clan Leader in his prime. However, after a great battle, the Clan Leader fell, entrusting the human race to him. Without the Clan Leader, the human race fell from its peak status, and their territory shrank significantly. Fortunately, his strength was enough to maintain the various tribes.","Over the years, he felt guilt in his heart for not fulfilling the Clan Leader’s expectations. Instead of leading the human race to prosperity, they began to decline.","Finally, after an earth-shattering battle, he protected the tribe and obtained a priceless treasure that perfectly resonated with him. He comprehended the treasure and created powerful secret techniques, challenging the ancient formidable tribes step by step and leading the human race to its peak, causing all the ancient races to submit.","The strongest figure who made all the ancient races submit now knelt on the ground, crying in pain. If other powerful leaders from different tribes knew about this, they would be utterly shocked.","Although the man’s strength had long surpassed that of the former Clan Leader, he cared deeply. In his heart, the Clan Leader was like a father and a teacher, someone he would respect throughout his life.","At the peak of the Eastern Saint Divine Mountain.","“You have a deep attachment to your people!”","“This child is under tremendous pressure; releasing it is necessary.” At the mountain’s peak, two people sat facing each other, one old and one young.","“Pressure? Are you blaming me for that?” Jian Wushuang chuckled lightly, picked up a tea cup, and took a sip of tea.","The elderly man, quite advanced in age, hurriedly shook his head with a smile. “Master, how could your disciple ever blame you? Without you, our human race would have perished in the Great Peace Mountain long ago.”","The old man recalled the time before the Great Peace Mountain was renamed the Eastern Holy Mountain.","At that time, the human race was at the bottom of the hierarchy, barely surviving. Any ancient wild beast could easily annihilate them.","Jian Wushuang waved his hand dismissively. “Enough, you’re not my disciple. I was puzzled back then; your hair had already turned white, and you bowed to a young man like me. You really have thick skin.”","The old man responded with a playful smile, “Master, your strength is so formidable; you must be an extraordinary person who never ages. Your appearance is just an illusion. Perhaps you’re even older than the Dragon King of the Dragon tribe. Kowtowing a few times won’t be a loss.”","“Haha, you’re not wrong about that,” Jian Wushuang sipped his tea, his eyes revealing a hint of sadness.","After finishing the tea, the old man continued, “Fu Zhu, I want to leave this place.”","Jian Wushuang’s sudden statement startled the old man.","“Why, Master, are you planning to travel the mortal realm again? It just so happens that I’ve been feeling a bit stifled here, so I’ll accompany you.”","Fu Zhu, who had been hiding with Jian Wushuang at this mountain’s peak, knew that his master often ventured down the mountain to visit various tribes. However, it hadn’t been many years since his last journey.","Jian Wushuang looked up, his pale golden eyes fixed on Fu Zhu as he chuckled, “Yes, we’re going on a journey! But this time, it might be a very long one. As for you, you can return to your tribe down the mountain. That young man’s potential has been fully unleashed, and now there’s no rival among the humans.”","“Master!”","The old man had long wanted to descend from the mountain, especially during times of crisis for the human race. However, Jian Wushuang never allowed him to appear back then. In the eyes of the humans, he had already perished, and Jian Wushuang had saved him.","Afterward, when the human race stabilized, he remained on the mountaintop, following Jian Wushuang for a million years.","Now, suddenly being told he could return to his tribe, his eyes turned red with excitement.","“Don’t get too excited. I’ll be leaving tonight, and tonight we’ll have a celebratory feast.”","Jian Wushuang reached into his sleeve and pulled out a short piece of wood, turning it over in his hand.."]},{"number":5124,"title":"Chapter 5124: Feast","paragraphs":["Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","In the night, beneath the starry sky.","At the foot of the Eastern Saint Divine Mountain stood the grandest of cities of the human race, the Eastern Royal City!","On this particular day, the Human Clan was abuzz with excitement, for the mightiest warrior of their people, known as “North Mountain Axe,” was to be wed this very evening. They had extended invitations to powerful beings from countless other races to partake in this unparalleled celebration.","Inside the royal palace, countless members of the Human Clan bustled about, preparing for the grand wedding feast to commence in an hour.","“Wow! Look, it’s the Holy Maiden of the Avian Clan!” exclaimed a young member of the Human Clan upon seeing the Hundred Spirit Clan’s Holy Maiden, who was wrapped in a robe as white as snow.","<font <=\"\" div=\"\">","Smack!","Beside the young man, an elderly figure glared at him and delivered a stinging slap to his head. He then whispered sternly, “Quiet down! She’s a True Spirit powerhouse; a single breath from her could blow you away.”","After admonishing the youth, the elderly man forced a smile and bowed to the Holy Maiden of the Hundred Spirit Clan, before leading the young man towards the royal palace.","The Hundred Spirit Clan’s Holy Maiden, accompanied by only two maids, sighed. Her status was incredibly prestigious, rivaling even the chieftains within the top-tier Hundred Spirit Clan. Even the most formidable members of the peak clans would show great deference to her. Yet now, a young human upstart dared to be so raucous in her presence.","“The Human Clan is truly dominant, unstoppable,” she recalled the words of her chieftain before coming here.","Casting a glance at the majestic formation infused with the essence of the heavens around her, the Holy Maiden of the Avian Clan forced a smile onto her face and continued her journey towards the Human Emperor’s Palace.","As powerful beings from various races took their seats, the grand wedding feast was about to begin.","Within the Human Emperor’s Palace, the majority of the most powerful individuals from seventy percent of the races had gathered. Among them was the Ancestral Dragon of the Dragon Clan and the Ghost King of the Ghost Clan. They conversed with other powerful beings from various races, patiently awaiting the commencement of this grand celebration.","“Old Dragon, I must congratulate you on this occasion!” The Ghost King, with a strange tone, raised his wine glass toward the Ancestral Dragon.","The Ancestral Dragon, dressed in a wide and long blue robe, wore a hearty smile on his face and playfully responded, “Old Ghost, why would you congratulate me on Dong Jun’s wedding today? What’s the reason behind it?”","“Hmph! Don’t play coy with me. Everyone knows that Dong Jun’s partner has","Dragon Clan bloodline. According to seniority, you can be considered Dong Jun’s elder.”","Dong Jun’s breakthrough to become a supreme powerhouse had reached an unimaginable level. If he were to take action, everyone present would be no match for him.","Moreover, just a few days ago, the once-mysterious top ancient lineage, the Ancient Gods, had been completely wiped out.","Rumors had it that Dong Jun personally annihilated them, leaving no bloodline behind.","This sent shockwaves through all the major clans, as they understood that the Human race was unstoppable. Dong Jun’s strength was beyond their ability to contend with.","Now that this ancient Ancestral Dragon, who had lived for countless years, had formed this relationship with Dong Jun, it was likely that the Dragon Clan’s position among the peak clans would become even more stable in the future.","Naturally, everyone took the opportunity to flatter the Ancestral Dragon, but he was well aware that this was just empty praise and waved his hand to dismiss it.","“Everyone, strength is what matters most. Although my Dragon Clan’s young lady has married into the Human race, I dare not claim seniority in front of Dong Jun! Besides, I’ve known Dong Jun for a long time, and I thought of him as a peer from the very beginning.”","The Ghost King curled his lips. He had been in a rivalry with the Ancestral Dragon for millions of years, and now the Ancestral Dragon was taking advantage of the situation, which made him extremely annoyed. He secretly cursed the Holy Maiden in their clan, wondering why he couldn’t have such good luck.","“Brother Ancestral Dragon, you shouldn’t put it that way. I heard that Dong Jun has great respect for the Eastern Saint Candlebearer and has always considered himself a junior. Even the extermination of the Ancient God Clan was because the Eastern Saint was targeted by them in a battle. If we were to speak in terms of peers, wouldn’t you be considered a senior in deference to the Eastern Saint?”","“I consider myself a peer of Dong Jun. Naturally, I have to respect the Eastern Saint as my elder. You don’t have to say anything more, White Old Ghost. A million years ago, I had great admiration for the Eastern Saint.”","The Ancestral Dragon sneered. He knew the Ghost King was trying to stir up trouble, but the Eastern Saint had been gone for many years. Respecting him as an elder wouldn’t change anything. After today, he would be on Dong Jun’s side, and he would have the opportunity to settle scores.","The smiles on the faces of the peak powerhouses sitting above froze as they realized why this Ancestral Dragon had survived since ancient times — because he had an incredibly thick skin.","Seeing that the Ancestral Dragon was shamelessly thick-skinned, the Ghost","King decided not to bother with him any longer and just snorted dismissively.","Boom! Boom! Boom!","In front of the Imperial Palace, a row of red drums resounded with thunderous beats.","“Right on time!”","Following a sharp announcement, Dong Jun waved his hand, tearing apart the void, and slowly walked into the palace with his wife. The powerful beings from all the races stood up.","“Congratulations, Dong Jun!”","“Congratulations, Lord Dong Jun!” “Congratulations, Brother!”","“Congratulations, Senior Brother!”","The congratulations from the myriad of races were indeed a grand spectacle!","Dong Jun turned to look at his wife, and a smile graced his face. He was no longer the wild man he used to be; he looked refined and handsome.","Step by step, he ascended to the highest platform in the hall and then turned to bow respectfully.","“Today, I am getting married. I am delighted that you all could put aside past grievances and join us.”","Although his demeanor was polite, Dong Jun’s aura exuded a commanding presence, surprising those in attendance. Nevertheless, they all smiled and raised their glasses.","As Dong Jun held his wife’s hand and turned around, a fleeting figure appeared out of nowhere. On the once-empty main seat, a young man had materialized.","The young man was dressed in a black robe, with long flowing hair and sharp eyes.","The newcomer was none other than Jian Wushuang!","This was the first time he had appeared in his true form before these formidable individuals. The time he had saved Fu Zhu was merely a manifestation of a law, and these so-called powerhouses were too weak to necessitate his true presence. Even his law embodiment had the power of a Grand Yan Immortal; a casual strike could obliterate countless planets.","Today was Dong Jun’s wedding day, and they hadn’t expected anyone to dare disrupt the celebration.","Dong Jun had deliberately left a seat vacant for Jian Wushuang. Above the main seat, a portrait of the Eastern Saint Fu Zhu hung on the wall, symbolizing the ancestral lineage, a significance not to be underestimated.","When he appeared, there was no discernible fluctuation of power, and outsiders couldn’t gauge his strength. Many people seated below were eagerly anticipating what would happen.","To dare to cause trouble in the heart of the Human race’s stronghold, he was the first.","“Such a grand banquet, how can the Human race not have an elder present!” Jian Wushuang picked up a wine jug and took a sip, then continued, “Isn’t that right, Fu Zhu?”","Whoosh!","An elderly man with white hair appeared out of thin air, causing the surrounding void to tremble. While his strength was suppressed, tearing through the void still emitted a powerful pressure that sent shivers through the crowd.","Many recognized the newcomer’s face, although he might not have the fame Dong Jun enjoyed today, he was a peak powerhouse from a million years ago. He was the one who had led the Human race to prosperity and greatness.","“It’s Fu Zhu! He’s still alive!”"]},{"number":5125,"title":"Chapter 5125: Mastery of the Ultimate Dao","paragraphs":["Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Below, the crowd was filled with shock!","Furthermore, the current strength of Fu Zhu exceeded that of Dong Jun.","This sent chills down their spines. The human race, originally at the bottom among the peak tribes, had risen to the top after Fu Zhu’s fall. Then, Dong Jun erupted, once again casting the glory of the human race, making it a peak tribe.","At this moment, the two powerful figures who had led the human race to the peak tribes were standing on the grand hall simultaneously.","Dong Jun saw Fu Zhu, who had once been like a father and teacher to him, and his eyes turned red.","<font <=\"\" div=\"\">","“Ancestor, is it really you?” At this moment, he could hardly believe it, but he was very familiar with the aura emanating from Fu Zhu.","Fu Zhu smiled and turned to look at Dong Jun, “These years, you’ve suffered!” Their emotions couldn’t be expressed in words.","Dong Jun shook his head, tears streaming down his cheeks, and he trembled,","“I’m fortunate not to have let you down, Ancestor’s expectations.”","At this moment, he had none of the demeanor of the first-ranked expert, directly kneeling on both knees and respectfully saying, “I respectfully welcome the Ancestor’s return to the human race. The human race shall prosper!”","“The human race shall prosper!”","Many strong members of the human race below finally reacted. After all, a million years ago, they hadn’t yet grown, and they did not have much knowledge of this former ancestor. Most of them had only seen his sculptures in the hall on the divine mountain.","“Haha, please rise! Today is your wedding day.”","Fu Zhu looked at Dong Jun with satisfaction. This young descendant of the human race had risen from adversity and had restored the ancient glory. Fu Zhu was very satisfied, and his master, Jian Wushuang, had a special affection for Dong Jun.","“Yes, Ancestor!” Dong Jun stood up and hastily pulled his wife to his side, “Long’er, quickly greet the Ancestor!”","Long’er, wearing a red gown, had a pair of bright eyes and exquisite features that were particularly stunning. Upon hearing her husband’s words, she quickly bowed in respect.","“Long’er, greet the Ancestor!”","Fu Zhu’s face was full of smiles, and he nodded quickly, “Good, good, good!”","“Ancestor, who is this...?” Dong Jun had a guess in his mind, but he still couldn’t believe it.","Although his strength was now extremely formidable, and he even had the confidence to sweep across the entire planet by himself, he couldn’t see through the young man sitting in the main seat. Moreover, the Ancestor actually referred to him as his master.","“This person is the one who has shown great kindness to our human race and is also my master! ”","Fu Zhu’s words shocked everyone!","“Master?”","That young man was actually Fu Zhu’s master!","“Do you still remember that Secret Realm and your giant axe? They were all gifts from your master.”","Jian Wushuang did not pay attention to Fu Zhu but stood up and looked at Dong Jun, saying, “There’s no need to thank me; that axe originally belonged to you.”","“Belong to me?” Dong Jun was a little stunned!","The people below were so shocked that their jaws almost fell off. Dong Jun’s current strength was actually given to him by that young man.","“Yes, you belong to you. You are very similar to an old friend I know. Now that I see that you have inherited his legacy, it is time for me to leave.”","Dong Jun was puzzled and asked, “An old friend... Are you the ancestor of our human race?”","Upon hearing Dong Jun’s words, Jian Wushuang scanned the people around him and replied casually, “You could say that.”","Millions of years following Jian Wushuang, Fu Zhu was about to inquire but was interrupted.","“Alright, I’ve had my share of the celebration. It’s time for me to go.”","As Jian Wushuang’s words fell, he disappeared from the grand hall, leaving the people there in astonishment.","“I didn’t even sense any spatial fluctuations. How did he leave?”","“Master!” Fu Zhu mumbled. Having followed Jian Wushuang for millions of years, he understood his master’s immense power. At most, he had speculated that his master might come from another planet. He consoled himself, “We should be able to meet again.”","They didn’t think that Jian Wushuang didn’t belong to this starry sky at all, or that this starry sky belonged to Jian Wushuang.","Outside the starry sky.","Jian Wushuang turned around!","After billions of years of silence, his state of mind had changed. He had almost forgotten everything that had happened in the Great Si Region. However, he could not forget the battlefield in his mind.","With a thought, he could create the universe.","“Ultimate Sword Dao, the fifth level: Heartsword Cosmos!”","A million years ago, he had mastered the Ultimate Dao. This starry sky belonged to him now. The River of Time and Space, billions of universes, and countless territories were embedded in his Great Dao.","The first level of the Ultimate Dao, ‘Thought Universe.’","On the battlefield of bones, he had actually comprehended the power of the heart. The collision between the Heart power and the Ultimate Sword had allowed him to touch the Ultimate Dao.","The thought that led him to this starry sky had brought him here. Now, it was time to return.","An ordinary sword could harm the Physical body.","But a sword imbued with the Dao could obliterate the soul.","However, a sword wielded with mastery over one’s heart could strike directly at one’s essence. Even if the body and soul were intact, it could cause a sudden upheaval in one’s mental state. On the battlefield, the situation changed in the blink of an eye. Once one’s inner state wavered, it could easily become a breakthrough point, and falling on the spot was not uncommon.","Whoosh!","After consolidating all his thoughts into one, Jian Wushuang’s figure completely vanished from the starry sky, leaving no trace behind.","Hundreds of thousands of years later, a collision occurred among the countless planets beneath this starry sky. A great war that lasted for billions of years shattered the tranquility of the cosmos. A burly man wielding a massive axe rose to prominence and ascended to the position of Emperor. After a brilliant era, another Emperor arrived from beyond the stars and created a vast new world, incorporating countless planets, establishing his dominance.","However, these are stories for another time. Jian Wushuang has now returned to that battlefield.","In the Great Desolate Wilderness, beyond the realm border.","The remains of a massive army littered the void, and the ancient bronze temple resonated with the tolling of bells!","Gu Yuan held a spear in one hand and the severed head of a bald monk in the other, taking a step that brought him beside Qian He.","“These baldies are really uninteresting!” Gu Yuan remarked, crushing the bald Monk’s head in his hand without hesitation.","On the edge of the distant battlefield, a young samanera’s eyes quivered. He could sense that his masters had all fallen, but he dared not open his eyes to confirm.","The armored corpses surrounding them had closed in, but Jian Wushuang, with his eyes tightly shut, remained unmoved.","Taking advantage of this moment, Qian He and Gu Yuan took another step, bringing them just outside Jian Wushuang’s range.","“This man exudes the aura of Zhen Wuyang. I will kill him. As for the little baldy, I’ll leave him to you,” Gu Yuan declared without a hint of negotiation, not caring in the slightest that Qian He was stronger than him in terms of power.","Since the Ancient Era, he had followed his master to conquer the four corners of the world. He might not be the strongest among the Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortals, but he was undoubtedly the most reckless.","Apart from his master, only the leader of the Pleiades and a few other peak Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortals could hold him in check.","Beyond these individuals, even if Zhen Wuyang himself appeared, he would dare to step forward and fight.","With his long spear raised, Gu Yuan did not wait for Qian He to respond. He charged forward.","“Traitor scum, meet your doom!”"]},{"number":5126,"title":"Chapter 5126: Return to the Battlefield","paragraphs":["Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","The sound of the spear tearing through the air was like a collision of thunder!","Countless flickering black lightning surrounded the spear and Gu Yuan, its speed so fast that it reached Jian Wushuang’s forehead in an instant.","Standing beside Jian Wushuang, the young samanera suddenly opened his eyes and looked at Gu Yuan, who was like a Demon God. He was not afraid at all. He could only sigh that his strength was not enough. After 30 million years of cultivation, his strength had not even reached the peak of the Yan Immortal realm. Let alone Gu Yuan, even any corpse had the strength of a Grand Yan","Immortal realm. He was a burden on the battlefield and could not help at all.","His inner frustration and anger made the young Monk’s eyes turn bloodshot.","<font <=\"\" div=\"\">","Now that Gu Yuan was attacking, the righteous cultivators by his side were also destined to fall. He had originally come to guide and help Yan Immortals ascend, but now he had become a burden, relying on others for protection just to stay alive.","He couldn’t understand why, given their mission to guide Transcendent Immortals, they were being attacked by these corpses. Why did several masters suddenly perish? They had even traversed the perilous Great Desolate Wilderness, so why were they falling here?","Filled with questions and frustration, he could only shout in anger, “I... I’ll stop you!”","Tears welled up in the young acolyte’s eyes. His hands, no longer in a prayer position, stood in front of Jian Wushuang’s small and delicate figure. He glared at Gu Yuan.","As if moved by lightning, the long spear paused in its tracks. The young acolyte was also momentarily stunned, looking at Gu Yuan with astonishment in his eyes. His body instinctively took a step back, bumping into Jian Wushuang behind him.","Jian Wushuang, whose consciousness had returned at an unknown moment, gently touched the young acolyte’s bald head with one hand.","“I promised your master that I would take you away.”","In the vast expanse of the cosmos, countless years were but a moment, and this was thanks to that fragment of Bodhi Heartwood.","At this moment, countless memories surged into his mind. He finally understood that it was the white-skinned monk who had summoned the Immeasurable Great Buddha to give him this Bodhi Heartwood.","Now that all the Monks had died in this starry sky, Jian Wushuang, whose state of mind had already changed, was expressionless.","He looked down at the young samanera and nodded at him.","“Kind Sir, don’t bother with me anymore. I’m just a burden. Leave me behind, and you might still have a chance to escape.”","The young Monk looked at Jian Wushuang. He did not want to burden him further, especially since his masters had all perished in this void. He had no desire to leave either.","Jian Wushuang, with a calm demeanor, gave a faint smile.","“Just hold onto my arm, close your eyes, and soon we’ll be able to break free.”","Now, he had broken through to the Three Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal realm. In the billions of years in the starry sky, he mastered the Ultimate Sword Dao up the the fifth level.","At this moment, even if he were to face a Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal, he had confidence in escaping. Of course, if that resurrected being came after him personally, then there wouldn’t be much hope.","However, based on his mental perception, that entity should not have fully revived yet. Although the blue-colored ancient hall had emerged, the corpses inside the hall clearly couldn’t be easily mobilized.","His gaze sharpened as his aura swept the surroundings.","The Wushuang Divine Sword pointed directly at Gu Yuan’s Thunder Spear, and the collision between the two produced no visible power fluctuations, but it halted Gu Yuan’s advance.","This was the terror of Heart power, battling invisibly.","“What power is this!”","Under the influence of Heart power, his body couldn’t help but tremble, and the spear in his hand fell.","Countless skeletal warriors also came to a standstill.","Qian He, who stood in the distant void, looked puzzled and shouted angrily, “Go, you fools!”","“I never expected that a Three Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal could wield such power!”","Qian He’s figure was elusive, her hand held a broken knife, and she unleashed countless afterimages in a continuous series of strikes. Yet, she herself did not approach Jian Wushuang.","Immediately, she sent a message to the leader of the skeletal warriors guarding the road of Immortal bones.","“The enemy is very mysterious, hurry to support, so as not to disturb our Lord!”","In the desolate ruins of Gu Lu, countless corpses continued to resurrect and crawl out of deep pits.","The leader of the skeletal warriors, holding a giant blade in his hand, turned his head to look at the aerial battlefield.","“Youdou, Youcheng, now that you two have revived, guard our Lord here. I will go and exterminate the lackeys of Zhen Wuyang!”","The leader of the skeletal warriors slowly stood up. His figure was sturdy, and his battle armor was covered in dark bloodstains, all remnants from the ancient battles. If Gu Yuan was a maniac, obsessed with battle, then this skeletal leader was a cold-blooded butcher who could sit silently tor ten thousand years or massacre thousands of immortals with a single breath.","He was none other than the renowned ‘Xiang Bingyun’, a Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal in the Ancient Era.","“General Pang, rest assured, we will handle things here with my brother. When the Asura Temple emerges, the grand plan will be irreversible, and no one can stop us.”","Youdou and Youcheng were the guardians of the Asura Temple and the lord’s closest attendants, both perfect ninth-level Daoist Immortals.","This was the terrifying power of Emperor-level forces. In most domains, there were no Emperors, and in each era, there were only two or three Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal.","It was easy to imagine how powerful the Great Si Region had been. With five Emperors coexisting, there were dozens of Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal, not to mention the countless Grand Yan Immortals.","Despite the passage of time since that battle, the Great Si Region had never been able to regain its former glory.","Xiang Bingyun’s eyes were steady, and with a single step, he arrived directly on the battlefield.","At this moment, Qian He was doing her best to hold back Jian Wushuang, while Gu Yuan’s mental state had deteriorated, causing his strength to decline significantly. However, he still refused to let go, firmly holding onto Jian Wushuang and preventing him from moving.","“Another newcomer? I don’t know which Emperor has revived this time, but I won’t be here to welcome him,” Jian Wushuang said.","Suddenly, Jian Wushuang’s sword aura surged, and a faint aura of primordial energy enveloped his entire body. This was the energy that existed at the beginning of the universe, long since disappeared as the vitality of the universe had grown, but he now possessed the complete Ultimate Dao. Not only the initial universe, but even the entire cosmos was under his control.","The powerful primordial energy instantly corroded her entire body, but fortunately, it wasn’t a lethal amount, and it did not take her life.","As for the crazed Gu Yuan, he had no such luck, or perhaps he was just foolish. Instead of dodging, he chose to directly face Jian Wushuang’s attack.","Primordial energy combined with Heart power.","Gu Yuan’s figure instantly froze in place.","Xiang Bingyun, who had just entered the battlefield, couldn’t intervene in time.","“Kneel!”","Jian Wushuang’s figure flashed, and his formidable Heart power quickly eroded","Gu Yuan.","With cloudy eyes, Gu Yuan trembled and knelt down unsteadily, then respectfully called out, “Master!”"]},{"number":5127,"title":"Chapter 5127: The Power of Thought","paragraphs":["Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","The arrogant Gu Yuan knelt on both knees, his eyes glazed over.","He knelt quietly in front of Jian Wushuang.","This scene shocked Xiang Bingyun, who had rushed over, on the spot. He knew Gu Yuan’s strength better than anyone else.","He was a veteran Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal in the Ancient Era, but now, he was enslaved just by a sword technique.","He was confident that he could defeat Gu Yuan in one move and enslave a Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal. Even an Imperial Lord would not be able to do so easily, let alone him.","<font <=\"\" div=\"\">","Only the legendary mightiest cultivators of the illusory realm could do it.","“Sir, are you an illusions cultivator? Why are you here in my Great Si Region?” Xiang Bingyun couldn’t help but ask. If the other party was really an illusions cultivator, then he shouldn’t be someone from the Great Si Region.","Jian Wushuang stood proudly in the void, holding the divine sword upside down. He frowned and said with a cold look, “What? Are you the owner of this Celestial Realm?”","The Monks had all died at the hands of the skeleton army because of him, soo how could he be nice to the other party now? Now, he had the upper hand.","However, that sword had used up all the accumulated primordial Qi, so it would take time to recover. Since the other party was not in a hurry to attack, he was more than happy to do so.","“You must be joking, Fellow Daoist. This desolated wasteland in the Great Si Region was created by my master. May I ask which world you belong to among the 3,000 worlds?”","Xiang Bingyun, who had once dominated the Ancient Era, had also been to the Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm. He knew that other than the Monks, there were other cultivators there. He knew some Grand Yan Immortals there.","Jian Wushuang mobilized his Heart power and spread it across the void.","His main priority now was to escape the siege. As long as he could get out, he would be able to leave this void very quickly with his speed. After all, the skeleton army had to protect that existence from reviving, so they could not leave too far away because of him.","“You know quite a lot, but...” Jian Wushuang tried to calm him down, but he suddenly retreated.","Just now, he had spread out his Heart power, allowing him to discover that there were other existences hidden in the void.","Sure enough, just as he retreated, a bloody light flashed and a black-robed old man appeared where he had just been","Fortunately, when he retreated, he controlled Gu Yuan to retreat along with him.","Jian Wushuang retreated far away and snorted coldly. Then, he ordered Gu Yuan to stall them.","Meanwhile, he tore through the void and kept flashing, bringing the young samanera to escape towards the border of the skeleton army.","The skeleton armor could not stop him in the first place. Now that his strength had increased, they were even less of a match for him.","He did not even need to draw his sword. The endless sword Qi scattered on his body shattered the bones.","“Youdoou, there is something fishy about this person. Qian He and I will chase after him, you go back and guard the divine hall.”","The black-robed old man made a strange sound and replied in a hoarse voice,","“Remember, don’t let the plan fail!”","Xiang Bingyun nodded. They had been buried under the bones for hundreds of millions of years, so they knew how important the plan was. Those Monks and Jian Wushuang were just ants. Since they had appeared, they would destroy them with all their might to prevent them from discovering the existence of the divine hall.","When the plan was set, they did not know when they would be able to recover. Now that they had waited for billions of years to return to this world, this was their only chance.","Nothing could go wrong with such a major event.","“Qian He, go and stop Gu Yuan. If necessary, just kill him.”","Even though the Ancient Era was glorious and had countless Yan Immortals, Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortals were extremely rare as overlords. Unless it was a crucial moment, they would not give up so easily.","However, Gu Yuan was currently delirious and had been enslaved by Jian Wushuang. Even if he was saved, he was not at ease to keep him by his side.","Qian He moved his body and stopped Gu Yuan who was going crazy.","“You idiot, how dare you betray the Lord? Die!” Although Qian He said this, she was still shocked, a Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal was sacrificed just like that. She could not help but feel a little sad.","If she had to sacrifice herself that day, would she end up like this?","Jian Wushuang, who was wandering at the edge of the battlefield, was fighting with all his might. However, the corpse armor surrounded him like a swarm of locusts. No matter how many skeletons he killed, there were still countless skeletons charging at him.","Now, he finally understood that ordinary skeletons did not seem to have any consciousness, only those that were comparable to Three or Six Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal level skeletons had consciousness and knew how to avoid being mindlessly killed.","Although they would not voluntarily throw their lives away, the Three and Six","countless black chains, forming a simple formation that blocked Jian Wushuang’s path.","“Damn it!” Jian Wushuang couldn’t help but curse. He turned his head and looked behind him. Xiang Bingyun’s figure was getting closer and closer. Once he was caught, it would be as difficult as ascending to the heavens for him to rush out again.","Perfected Nine Revolutions and ordinary Nine Revolutions were worlds apart. Even though he had enslaved Gu Yuan with one sword technique, if he were to face Xiang Bingyun, without the primordial Qi, he would not be able to shake a Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal with just his Heart power.","Right now, he could only deal with Six Revolutions or Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortals with an incomplete mental state.","“Heart power cultivator, you won’t be able to escape. If you were to sink or swim, I’ll spare your life!”","Jian Wushuang sent out two sword Qi containing Heart power to sweep through the void and killed the Six Revolutions Grand Yan Immortals hiding behind the army.","Those Six Revolutions Grand Yan Immortals were guided by the Heart force, their eyes were dull as they fell into the void.","“Go ahead and dream!” After those Six Revolutions Grand Yan Immortals died, the binding power of the chains instantly decreased.","Jian Wushuang took advantage of the time to make up for the deficiency and really burst out.","In the world of the Heart, spanning billions of years, he had mastered the complete Ultimate Dao. The transformation in his strength wasn’t just limited to an elevation in the realm of the Heart.","“With a single Thought!”","Drip, drip!","Even the young Monk, at this moment, opened his eyes abruptly. He was too familiar with the sound he had just heard. It was the sound of the","Heaven-Reaching Lord Buddha striking his bowl, a figure held in high esteem in the Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm. His Master had once taken him to the Heaven -Reaching Lord Buddha’s monastery.","In the Heaven -Reaching Lord Buddha’s monastery, he had heard this kind of sound.","This was the power of Thought, something only those standing at the pinnacle of the universe could produce.","Even Zhen Wuyang couldn’t achieve this. Jian Wushuang, who had mastered the Ultimate Dao, could turn a single Thought into a starry sky, and he was the master of the other side of the starry sky.","The fact that the Heaven-Reaching Lord Buddha could emit the power of Thought also proved that he had glimpsed the mysteries of this universe, but there was still a vast gap between him and the controllers of the universe. After all, Jian Wushuang had once discovered in the vastness of the stars that most universes remained uncontrolled, and the number of beings who could control the universe was extremely limited.","Even legends of universe controllers were exceedingly rare.."]},{"number":5128,"title":"Chapter 5128: One Thought Universe","paragraphs":["Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Perhaps those emperors had heard something, but most of them couldn’t even control a realm.","The realms were directly divided into sizes, and Jian Wushuang, who had comprehended the complete Supreme Dao, had already glimpsed the essence of the starry sky.","Beneath the starry sky lay the vast River of Time and Space with nine magnificent currents, as well as the tributaries of these temporal rivers.","Further down was the universe within the River of Time and Space. It was composed of countless stars when it first emerged, and powerful beings later opened up one Celestial Realm after another.","A Celestial Realm as enormous as the Great Si Region could be considered a middle-grade world, equivalent to a Star Region within a universe.","<font <=\"\" div=\"\">","If the Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm and the 3,000 big worlds were not divided, they could be considered a high-grade world. However, they had now been divided into 3,000 middle-grade worlds and countless lower-grade worlds.","However, the Heaven-Reaching Lord Buddha controlled the Heavenly Realm, which was the most powerful territory before the division of the high- grade world. Controlling the Heavenly Realm also meant having authority over the 3,000 worlds.","But the Heavenly Realm was now only a middle-grade world. Yet its foundation was several times greater than that of an ordinary middle-grade world, and ordinary middle-grade world Emperors were no match for him.","All of this was what Jian Wushuang had learned from his exploration of the starry sky. If he ever became a controller, he would ascend to the sky in one step, becoming the master of the starry sky, surpassing everything.","But for now, it was important to stay alive!","Now, within the Great Desolate Wilderness, there suddenly appeared Yan power. With his current knowledge, he had already guessed that it was caused by an old guy from the Ancient Era.","The Great Desolate Wilderness was vast enough to rival a middle-grade world, but there was no Yan power here. Otherwise, this world would have long been controlled by Emperors searching for ownerless worlds.","Now that the Yan energy had appeared, the person behind it was probably planning to take control of the vast Great Desolate Wilderness and take that step to become the controller of this world.","As for why there was such an abundance of Yan power, Jian Wushuang glanced at the countless Grand Yan Immortals around him and sneered. He could only sigh at the merciless Great Dao.","The power of Thought was as calm as water in the void, but it made all the corpses on the battlefield shake. Their bodies seemed to be bound by countless tentacles, and their movements became abnormally slow.","Xiang Bingyun, who was a Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal, could clearly feel the pressure. Although this pressure could not interfere with his movements, it made his soul feel extremely painful and uncomfortable, causing him, who was originally calm, to feel a little anxious.","“We can’t delay any longer; this person is too mysterious. We must kill him quickly! ”","With a mere hand gesture, space instantly ruptured, revealing the totem of an ancient and colossal beast.","The Image Form of Heaven and Earth responded, as if the ancient and colossal beast had heard the call, crossing over from ancient times.","Beneath Xiang Binyun’s feet, the totem spun. As a Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal, his mastery of the Image Form had reached an absolute level. At this moment, he was the ancient and colossal beast.","With gigantic blood-claws, he lunged towards Jian Wushuang!","A swipe that tore through heaven and earth, making it hard to distinguish friend from foe, even shredding the corpses surrounding Jian Wushuang.","Facing such a strike, Jian Wushuang did noot evade. The suppression of his Thought power was not the only thing at play here; his Heart power gave birth to Thought power, and the Thought was all-powerful.","Just as the blood-claws descended, Jian Wushuang angrily shouted, “Universe!” Buzz!","The next moment, the Great Desolate Wilderness began to tremble. The Dao that existed in the Great Desolate Wilderness seemed to shrink in fear, as if a cat had seen a mouse, and it began to retreat.","From the moment Yan power emerged in the Great Desolate Wilderness, a Dao was born. While the Dao was heartless, it possessed a hint of consciousness to govern the rules of heaven and earth. Jian Wushuang’s use of Thought power made it fearful. After all, it was just a Dao on par with a middle- grade world, how could it dare to compare with the Thought power derived from the birth of a universe? When he used the power of the universe with a single Thought, the Dao automatically yielded.","Endless Yan power merged into it, free from the constraints of the Dao, easily adjustable as needed.","A microcosm with a diameter of a million miles instantly enveloped the entire edge of the battlefield.","Though Jian Wushuang could not be called invincible within this microcosm, with the immense Yan power at his disposal, he had more than enough to deal with a Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal.","Xiang Binyun’s blood-claws in his microcosm felt like an itch. With a casual sword stroke, he blocked the claw.","Xiang Binyun was familiar with the suppression of this Dao. It was how Zhen Wuyang had dealt with them back then, using the power of the Great Si Region to trap them within the Great Desolate Wilderness.","Now, this kind of power once again suppressed him!","“How is this possible? Are you perhaps an Emperor?” Xiang Binyun found it hard to believe. If his opponent were an Emperor, there would be no need for all this trouble; a few casual moves would be enough to kill him.","Back in the day, Zhen Wuyang had mobilized the power of the Great Si Region to suppress countless Grand Yan Immortals. This kind of power was not to be used casually; every time it was employed, it would damage the world’s source. Unless it was a matter of life and death, the controller of the world would never activate the power of the world’s source.","Xiang Bingyun didn’t know much about these secret scripts, but he recognized this power. Only the controller of the world could master it.","“Am I the Emperor? You’ll find out if you try!” Jian Wushuang replied, wasting no time on further conversation. Currently only a Three Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal, manipulating a microcosm spanning a million miles was extremely taxing for him. It was a mini universe after all. At least in terms of Heart power, he was almost at his limit.","However, being able to execute this move was already remarkable, thanks to his mastery of the Ultimate Dao.","The microcosm was many times stronger than the Sword World of the past, and within his universe, any Great Dao could be altered.","For example, the current Sword Dao!","The Wushuang Divine Sword swung, and a sword Qi that spanned thousands of miles erupted.","The tip of the sword was aimed straight at Xiang Bingyun, moving at nearly teleportation-like speed. Within this million-mile radius, he could arrive at any location at any time.","Xiang Bingyun didn’t have time to block it, so he could only take it head-on. The sharp Wushuang Divine Sword directly cut off half of his palm.","Xiang Bingyun, who had long ago cultivated his fleshly body to be immortal, didn’t mind in the slightest. Instead, he took the opportunity of being up close to strike with a fierce punch directly towards Jian Wushuang’s chest.","The Wushuang Divine Sword hastily swung horizontally to defend, but a Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal, even within a microcosm, was still terrifying. Despite losing over 90 percent of its power when passing through the Wushuang Divine Sword, the strike still hit his divine body, making his throat feel a sharp pain, almost causing him to cough up blood.","The battle between the two was lightning-fast, with no openings in sight.","Xiang Bingyun was gradually getting used to the microcosm. His close combat skills were already formidable, and while Sword Dao was primarily about offense, the sword’s defense was not weak either.","It was fortunate that this advantage allowed him to suppress Xiang Bingyun, or else he might have been defeated after taking a few more punches.","This was due to the enhancement of his strength within the microcosm, enabling him to rival a Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal and even surpass them in speed.","Whoosh!","Jian Wushuang’s figure disappeared once again!","Step by step, he had finally achieved his goal.."]},{"number":5129,"title":"Chapter 5129: Prototype","paragraphs":["Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","When Jian Wushuang reappeared, he had already reached the outermost edge of the battlefield.","Several Six Revolutions Grand Yan Immortals who had been hiding at the edge had no time to react and were decapitated by Jian Wushuang’s sword. The speed at which he moved was beyond belief.","The main reason he could do this effortlessly was that these Six Revolutions Grand Yan Immortals in their corpse battle armor had no defenses whatsoever. Their conscious awareness had relaxed due to their battle with Xiang Bingyun, thinking that as long as Xiang Bingyun was present, even if they were suppressed by the One Thought Universe, it wouldn’t affect them significantly. Moreover, these Six Revolutions Grand Yan Immortals’ corpses were all on the outskirts and could leave the range of One Thought Universe at any time.","Jian Wushuang slowly released the young Monk in his hand, his gaze fixed on the enraged Xiang Bingyun in the distance. He said calmly, “I don’t know why you’ve been resurrected, and I’m not clear on your intentions. But since you insist on pushing me to my limits, don’t blame me for not being polite.”","“Killing so many of my subordinates with a wave of your hand, you’re really quite polite.”","<font <=\"\" div=\"\">","Although the army of corpses seemed almost endless, the gray-white ancient land had already been emptied of most of its inhabitants. Only about a third remained, mostly battle armor comparable to Grand Yan Immortals, with very few having consciousness and power reaching the third stage. Six Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal-level corpses were extremely rare, and Jian Wushuang casually killed several of them. Even Xiang Bingyun felt a bit distressed.","He hadn’t been heavily involved in the plan back then, as the core figures were the Emperors who controlled it. But since all the corpse armies had been revived, these people must still have their uses. Losing too many of them would be difficult to explain to their superiors.","“They weren’t supposed to exist in the first place. This can hardly be called slaughter; on the contrary, he should be thankful to me!”","A cold smile played at the corner of Jian Wushuang’s mouth as he continued, “Your strength is at least that of a Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal. Do you really not know why these people died? Do you think it’s because Zhen Wuyang was intentionally suppressing them ruthlessly?” He did not hold back and asked loudly!","In the Ancient Era, there were many Grand Yan Immortals, and half of them were under the tutelage of the five Emperors. These Grand Yan Immortals could distinguish between closeness and distance.","If they were third or even fourth-generation disciples, would they really have risked their lives to resist Zhen Wuyang for the sake of those Emperors?","Even if this half of the Grand Yan Immortals had sworn unwavering loyalty, fearless and unyielding, the number of Grand Yan Immortals who had turned into corpses in the Great Desolate Wilderness was not just half of those from Ancient Era.","According to his estimation, if these corpses were once Grand Yan Immortals before their demise, then almost all the Grand Yan Immortals from ancient times had been killed by Zhen Wuyang.","Clearly, he had gained control of the Great Si Region, and what Zhen Wuyang wanted to eliminate were those Emperors. As for the Grand Yan Immortals, he killed them as a matter of course, but there was no need to kill almost 90 percent of the Grand Yan Immortals in the Great Si Region.","There must be something fishy about this!","The strength of their Yan power could explain the problem—when the corpses revived, their Yan power erupted.","These Grand Yan Immortals were very likely forced to die back then, and the mastermind behind it all probably did it for the Yan power within their bodies.","Jian Wushuang furrowed his brows slightly; he was afraid to imagine it.","The deaths of countless Grand Yan Immortals had revived the Great Desolate Wilderness and created a Dao comparable to that of a middle-grade world.","At this moment, the Dao was extremely weak, and anyone with the strength of an Emperor could completely control it. When that happened, they would directly step into becoming the controller of this Great Desolate Wilderness.","These corpses of the Grand Yan Immortals were all pawns, and even those Emperors saw themselves as pawns. If any mistakes occurred in the middle, they would truly fall.","When the Great Desolate Wilderness was resurrected, it would ironically benefit Zhen Wuyang and the Emperors of the Heaven -Reaching Buddhist Realm.","Now that the terrifying presence had resurrected and the grand plan had succeeded, he would never allow him to leave.","Jian Wushuang’s eyes shimmered with understanding, and if he truly wanted to escape from this place, he had no choice but to take a gamble.","Since the corpses had revived, they held value for him. If he could mass-exterminate these corpses, that formidable presence would surely be infuriated.","“Hu Qing, is your purpose in the Great Si Region to guide and convert the Grand Yan Immortals?”","The sudden question made the young novice monk, Huiqing, pause for a moment, and then he nodded heavily!","“I and my master were disciples of the Heaven-Reaching Lord Buddha. The Buddha instructed us to spread the teachings in the Great Si Region,” the young samanera, without any hidden agenda, spoke openly after all his fellow Monks had passed away.","Jian Wushuang chuckled and patted the young Monk’s head gently. “You’ve had a busy day today.”","“Busy? Could the benefactor please enlighten me?” The young Monk was momentarily confused.","Even though they had reached the edge of the army of corpses, the formidable cultivator in green armor showed no intention of sparing them.","“I will send these corpses to meet the Buddha later. Could you please help them with their salvation for now?” Jian Wushuang’s voice was loud, and even Xiang Binyun, who stood in the distance, heard it.","If someone else had said this, he would have scoffed. However, the strange power displayed by Jian Wushuang now made him extremely vigilant. Especially the One Thought Universe technique—He couldn’t fathom its weaknesses, even though its effect was similar to his domain. The internal energy it operated on was extremely terrifying.","A mere million miles in diameter could rival a fully Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal. Moreover, the constant mental pressure made him restless and even gave him thoughts of retreat.","“All of you, obey my command and withdraw from this domain!” Xiang Binyun raised a bronze token in his hand, and his voice rang out like a bell.","The hundreds of thousands of corpses within a million-mile radius all looked toward Xiang Binyun. In just a moment, they began to evacuate in an orderly manner, rushing toward the outside world.","The One Thought Universe technique was at its limit when Jian Wushuang could only control the central origin. It could only be considered a semi-finished product at present.","This small universe couldn’t truly be called a universe yet; at best, it was a","prototype!","To create a true One Thought Universe, according to Jian Wushuang’s estimation, the levels of mental power and thought power required would be inconceivable. Once the universe formed, it could even be maintained permanently. Even if the caster perished, it would still endure.","Back when he was in the starry sky, he had wondered if those universes had been created by some powerful beings.","Now, as he tried to cast the One-Thought Universe, he finally understood that creating a universe was exponentially more difficult than controlling one. Even this small-scale universe, when entrusted to an ordinary cultivator, would pose a significant challenge, solely due to the disparities in Thought and Heart power.","His Heart power was relatively manageable, as the Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm could still produce a few experts in that area.","However, Thought power, this elusive and variable force, varied greatly among individuals. Some people’s Thought power could manipulate objects from a distance, akin to powerful Yan Immortals. However, when it came to creating a universe or condensing a world through thought power alone, the gap was insurmountable.","Nonetheless, Jian Wushuang could now cast a microcosm of a million miles in size, with the added power of the Yan Immortals within. To reach this point, his thought power was far beyond the norm for Emperors.."]},{"number":5130,"title":"Chapter 5130: Zhen Wuyang Arrives","paragraphs":["Chapter 5130: Zhen Wuyang Arrives","Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","The Ultimate Dao!","It was the limit that the starry sky could withstand and the limit that the starry sky could expand.","After grasping the complete limit, one would have already stepped onto the path of controlling the starry sky.","The One Thought Universe was just a miniature of the starry sky. If he was strong enough, the starry sky would descend with a thought. At that time, Jian Wushuang would be truly invincible.","But now, with the One Thought Universe’s miniature version, he could already match a Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal. Even contending against a Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal, he could still keep up. This was the power of the Ultimate Dao.","Jian Wushuang could make the miniature universe shake the Great Desolate Wilderness Heavenly Dao with his hands. All the skeletons and corpses in the miniature universe were suppressed.","Millions of corpses were like puppets, unable to leave. Only a few corpses with the strength of a Six Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal managed to drag their bodies out of the range of the miniature universe.","“What are you doing?” Xiang Bingyun did not quite understand why he had to use more than half of his strength to suppress these ordinary corpses. Wouldn’t it reduce his burden if these corpses left?","Indeed, if Xiang Bingyun was the only one in the miniature universe, his burden would have been greatly reduced. However, Xiang Bingyun was constantly pestering him. Even if there was no corpse, he would not be able to escape.","Since there was no way to flee, he decided to take drastic measures.","“I warned you, things won’t be as friendly as they were before!","His voice had barely faded when he took control of the entire miniature universe, devouring the boundless Yan Power from the void. It coalesced into countless powerful sword energies. As he struck, innumerable sword energies traversed the void, each possessing the might of his ordinary sword strikes. With a simultaneous release of countless sword energies, they cleaved toward the corpses within the miniature universe.","“Stop it!” Xiang Binyun’s body transformed completely into an ancient behemoth, its claw scattering tens of thousands of sword Qi. However, against the billions of sword Qi, it was almost useless.","He could only watch anxiously as a million skeletons turned into dust. With a thought, he killed a million Grand Yan Immortals. This scene reminded him of Zhen Wuyang from the Ancient Era.","Recalling the humiliation of the past, Xiang Bingyun was furious to the extreme at this moment.","“Today, I want you to die!”","Boom!","Countless corpses and dust fell from the void like snow, and Xiang Bingyun turned into a primordial beast.","Jian Wushuang quickly grabbed the young Monk and teleported!","“Are you going crazy? It seems like we haven’t killed enough!","The little samanera lowered his head and rubbed the Buddha beads in his hand!","“Kind Sir, I’ve already converted these Grand Yan Immortals, you can kill them without worry! i ‘","Xiang Bingyun was so angry that he almost vomited blood. If it wasn’t for the Master’s plan, he would have led several Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortals to attack Jian Wushuang.","Outside the ancient bronze temple,","Two figures in black robes sat cross-legged in front of the temple door.","“Who is this person exactly? With such strength during the Ancient Era, they should have some reputation, right? Could it be that they have only risen in recent years?","Jian Wushuang possessed the power of Nine Revolutions and could contend with the Perfected Nine Revolutions strength of Xiang Binyun. In their eyes, he was no ordinary individual.","There was a high probability that he was a superpower who had already made a name for himself in the Ancient Era, or else he wouldn’t have come to the Great Desolate Wilderness at this time to investigate their grand plan.","“Tsk tsk, but I can’t tell his identity from his appearance. However, I can feel the aura of Zhen Wuyang on his body. No matter what, I have to make him stay.”","Youdou sat cross-legged on a high seat. He was one of the Left and Right Guardians of the Lord, the closest confidant of the Lord.","“It won’t be that simple to keep him here. You and I must protect the Qishen Temple and not move again. Zhen Wuyang inside the Great Si Region probably already knows about us. We can’t afford to be careless.”","When the grand plan was set, the two of them, along with their leader, entered the Qishen Temple to sleep. Their leader had instructed that when they woke up again, they must guide the corpses to protect the Qishen Temple and not let anyone approach it.","Now was the crucial moment for their leaders revival, and if anything went wrong, they couldn’t bear the consequences.","“Since we can’t kill him, let’s lead him somewhere else! There must not be any more big movements in this place.”","“Agreed!”","Within the miniature universe.","After annihilating a million corpses, the One Thought Universe had weakened considerably. However, without the burden ot the opponent’s corpses, its strength had not decreased much.","Even so, Jian Wushuang couldn’t match Xiang Binyun’s strength head-on and had to keep evading.","“I can’t keep this up. My Thought power has reached its limit. I must shake him off!” Jian Wushuang furrowed his brows, and his figure changed once more. “The old guy from the Anicent Era is really difficult to deal with.”","Xiang Bingyun’s attack missed. His blood-red eyes turned and he moved his body in an instant. When Jian Wushuang tore open the void and appeared, she predicted his position in advance and stabbed a sharp claw into Jian Wushuangs body.","Golden blood sprayed into the void, but as the spacetime shifted once more, Xiang Binyun quickly moved aside.","It was only after stabilizing his position that he realized everything had been an illusion, and Jian Wushuang had taken advantage of the opportunity to leave a gruesome wound on his back.","“You b*stard!” Xiang Binyun exclaimed.","“Hmph! You’ve got thick skin,” Jian Wushuang retorted.","The battle between the two shook the entire microcosm, and the heavens themselves seemed to howl.","Boom.","A surge of energy, long buried in the ancient era, erupted, sending both combatants staggering.","“Haha, my master has fully awakened! You scoundrel, prepare to die!” The energy emanated from the Qishen Temple, and Jian Wushuang felt a powerful force surging forth.","“Even if the Zhen Wuyang has revived, what can he do? Today, none of you can stop me,” Jian Wushuang declared, his determination shining in his eyes.","How many years had it been? How many battles had he fought? He had often emerged from adversity, but he had never given up on a chance, which had brought him to this day.","“How dare you insult my Lord? Even if the Zhen Wuyang comes today, I will still kill you!’","The glory of the Ancient Era was those Emperors. They, the Grand Yan Immortals, were all illuminated. Insulting His Lord was the same as insulting them, insulting the glory of the Ancient Era.","While the two were locked in battle, a middle-aged man dressed in resplendent attire continually flickered at the edge of the Great Wilderness. Every movement seemed to traverse endless voids, an accomplishment that might take ordinary Grand Yan Immortals hundreds of years, but this middle-aged man could do it in an instant.","When he encountered powerful ancient relics, he simply stormed through them. Formations, spirit guardians, and protectors all instantly crumbled before him, as his strength exceeded the rules of this world.","With a white jade crown on his head and a golden robe, his face exuded n obi lit’ r","This man was none other than Zhen Wuyang.","He had long sensed the disturbances in the Great Desolate Wilderness, originally thinking it was the stubbornness of the Ancient Era wanting to make a comeback. However, he had not anticipated that those old folks would actually control the legendary Qishen Temple.","It was no wonder the Ancient Era had produced five Emperors and so many Grand Yan Immortals.."]},{"number":5131,"title":"Chapter 5131: Qjshen","paragraphs":["Chapter 5131: Qjshen","Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Inside the Temple of Divergence.","The enormous ancient temple, tinted with a mysterious shade, exuded an aura of antiquity. It stood empty, chaotic, and serene.","Upon an ancient throne of gold, a skeletal figure sat perched above, surrounded by dozens of similarly ancient thrones. Behind these thrones loomed a massive, enigmatic statue.","Snickering...","After a strange noise, a glimmer of light flickered in the eye sockets of the golden skeleton.","‘Zhen Wuyang!’","“Hmm, is it really him?”","“I didn’t expect his nose to be so keen, discovering the Temple of Divergence so quickly.”","“Ah, kill him, kill him.”","“Traitor, I want him dead.”","At the same time, all the skeletons on the dozens of ancient thrones awakened, their eyes filled with anger. They roared the name Zhen Wuyang, indicating how much they loathed him.","“We’re in trouble. If we don’t kill him, it’ll be hard to ease the hatred in our hearts, the hatred that prevents us from reaching the pinnacle of the universe.”","“The Great Desolate Wilderness has already given birth to the Heavenly Dao. Although it’s still weak, it can already rival the middle-grade worlds. Plus, the Great Wilderness is traceless. I’ve spent countless ages comprehending the Qishen Temple. I can’t wait to go to the River of Time and Space anymore. By mastering this Dao, I can still elevate it. The position of Universe Master is too distant, and if I can take the second step, I’ll be content.”","The golden skeletons on the other thrones changed their expressions, unwilling to accept it. “Liu Ya, are you really going to do this? If you take control of this Dao now, do you know how difficult it will be for you to progress further in this lifetime?","“Yang Jun, do you really think mastering the universe is that easy? As far as I know, our original universe and several neighboring universes haven’t given birth to Universe Masters, except for what the Temple of Divergence recorded. Have you heard otherwise?","The others pondered in secret but remained dissatisfied.","They had become Emperors during the Ancient Era, all thanks to the existence of the Qishen Temple.","As they looked into the birth of the Great Si Region, they all wore expressions filled with longing.","The Qishen Temple did not belong to the Great Si Region; it had drifted from the void during ancient times and descended upon the Great Si Regiono.","At that time, human cultivators were still very rare. Most of them were ancient divine beasts or unique Special Life Forms.","They had discovered the uniqueness of the Qishen Temple long ago, and from there, they became dazzling existences and became Emperors without much challenge.","Within the Qishen Temple, 18 divine generals were appointed to each of the Emperors in the Ancient Era.","The 18 Emperors mastered the Great Devouring Dao of the Qishen, and as long as they reached the pinnacle of cultivation, they could devour the universe and become the Universe Masters as recorded in the Qishen Temple.","This is why they did not seek to control the Great Si Region or leave it.","The eighteen Emperors all fantasized about quickly becoming the Universe Masters, but they never expected a Zhen Wuyang to emerge.","He was a successor of the True Martial Dao, who climbed to the peak and shattered their own paths, suppressing them in the Great Desolate Wilderness.","Only they knew how powerful the Zhen Wuyang of the Ancient Era was.","Ever since the Grand Secretary Domain was controlled by Zhen Wuyang, he had never used his full strength. No one knew how strong he was now.","“Liu Ya, have you really thought this through? You are giving up the Dao of Qishen,” an Emperor with a glowing glabella bellowed.","Having entered the Qishen Temple from a young age and always revered the Qishen, the appearance of a traitor among them was something that some emperors couldn’t accept.","Liu Ya coldly snorted and turned to the angry Emperor, saying in a cold voice, “Fool, you’ve been copying the statue of the Qishen for so many years, and I haven’t seen you become the Master of the Universe. If you truly become a Universe Master and inherit the position of the Three Great Divine Masters, why would I need to give up the Dao of the Qishen and follow the Dao of the Desolate Wilderness Master?”","Not only did the Qishen Temple establish 18 divine generals, but it also established Three Great Divine Masters and 108 messengers.","The requirements to become a messenger were the lowest; as long as you were a Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal, you could become a candidate messenger. When you reached the Perfected Nine Revolutions realm, you could become a Qishen messenger, inheriting one of the Emperor’s Dao. As long as you followed the Great Dao, you would undoubtedly become an Emperor.","The requirements to become a divine general were higher; you had to become an Emperor before you could inherit it. Once you inherited it, they would impart to you the Great Devouring Dao, which was a path to becoming the Universe Master.","The masters of the universe were legendary figures in the river of time and space. If it became known across countless universes that the Altar of Wayward Gods held a path that could make cultivators ascend to the masters of the universe, it would surely shake the entire cosmos and spark endless wars.","Furthermore, the Altar of Wayward Gods had established a supreme rule: the three heirs of the God Lords could explore the cosmos. Wherever the secrets of the supreme rule were hidden, whoever comprehended it could inherit the Altar of Wayward Gods and become its ultimate master.","These secrets were known only to them, the divine general. They were aware of the benefits hidden within these secrets and were unwilling to inherit a mere realm and climb step by step.","Not to mention inheriting the Qishen Temple, just mastering the complete Great Devouring Dao to become the Universe Master was enough to drive countless Emperors mad.","Silence filled the great hall for a moment.","“Alright, since Liu Ya has chosen the Dao of the Great Desolate Wilderness Master,” said Yang Jun, turning to look at the others, “don’t forget that Zhen Wuyang has already discovered the Qishen Temple. Soon, powerful beings from other Celestial Realms will also discover it. If no one abandons the Great Devouring Dao, who will control the Great Desolate Wilderness? Without control, how can we deal with those Emperors who have taken the first step?”","Even though they had embarked on the Great Devouring Dao, their strength far exceeded that of ordinary Emperors. However, when facing those Emperors who had taken the first step, they were utterly defenseless.","Even if they weren’t within the world controlled by the other party, they were still no match.","At this moment, Liu Ya took control of the Great Desolate Wilderness, mastering the Heavenly Dao. With such a position, he could use the Qishen","Temple to quickly elevate the Great Desolate Wilderness to a high-grade world.","By becoming top-tier Emperor, he could also protect the Qishen Temple. As long as the Universe Master did not appear, they would be absolutely safe within the Great Desolate Wilderness.","“In that case, Liu Ya, we’ll rely on you from now on. Otherwise, we’ll have to carry the Qishen Temple and escape into the River of Time and Space,” Yang Jun concluded.","The faces of the other Emperors changed rapidly. While they believed in","Qishen and held great reverence for him, in the current situation, preserving the Qishen Temple took precedence.","The Emperors quickly reached a decision, with Liu Ya volunteering to take control of the Altar of Qishen Temple.","Meanwhile, Zhen Wuyang had already reached the depths of the Great Desolate Wilderness at an astonishing speed.","“No!” Zhen Wuyang roared.","He could sense that a Heavenly Dao had emerged within the Great Desolate Wilderness and had already fallen into someone’s control.","“That old b*stard! If I can’t have the Qishen Temple, neither can you!’","He produced an ancient-looking token in his hand and then activated its power, transmitting a message throughout the entire universe.."]},{"number":5132,"title":"Chapter 5132: Various Forces","paragraphs":["Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Once the news of the Disambiguation Temple spread, the entire universe was shaken.","The Qishen Temple, which had been rumored since the Ancient Era, had once again descended upon the Great Si Region, causing countless Emperors to go crazy.","During the Ancient Era, the Great Si Region had awed countless territories around it. Even though the Great Si Region did not have a controller, no Emperor dared to casually invade it.","In that era, a rumor had circulated that the Great Si Region possessed a temple that had drifted from the River of Time and Space. It was this very temple that had contributed to the Great Si Region’s glory.","Many people believed this information at the time, but due to the Great Si Region having more than a dozen Emperors, no one dared to investigate further.","<font <=\"\" div=\"\">","It wasn’t until Zhen Wuyang emerged and subdued dozens of Emperor Sovereigns, taking control of the entire Great Si Region, that people stopped believing in the existence of the Qishen Temple.","Now, with disturbances in the Great Desolate Wilderness, Zhen Wuyang personally announced that the Qishen Temple indeed existed within the Great Si Region, sparking the greed of countless beings.","For an artifact that could give rise to dozens of Emperors in medium-grade Celestial Realms, it was enough to drive Nine Revolutions Grand Yan","Immortals crazy and captivate Emperors who had not yet taken the first step.","Even the ‘Dao Ancestors’ who presided over their own Dao Temples, those who had taken the first step, paid great attention.","In the universe, across endless domains.","In the high-grade world, Ancient God Domain.","On the Primordial Demon Mountain, within the resplendent ancient temple that encircled the entire mountain, several Emperors had already gathered.","An ancient god with seven stars on his forehead said respectfully, “Master, news has come from the Zhen Wuyang of the Great Si Region. The Qishen Temple has reappeared.”","Above the grand hall stood an eight-star Ancient God, the ruler of the Ancient","God Realm, a being whose own Dao seamlessly merged with the entire Ancient God Realm. He was the Master of a higher-grade world, and the eight stars on his forehead symbolized the nobility of his bloodline.","In the Ancient God Realm, besides the first-seat Nine-star Ancient God, his bloodline was the highest.","“The Qishen Temple!”","The eight-star Ancient God swayed his tail and pondered for a moment before","saying, “Gather all the Emperors and the Nine Revolutions Grand Yan","Immortals of the Ancient God Clan immediately. I will inform the Ancestor.”","Even though he was the ruler of the Ancient God Realm, matters of such magnitude still required the Ancestor’s decision.","Because the Ancestor of the Ancient God Realm was the only Ultimate Emperor within the entire universe.","Moreover, he was the Ultimate Emperor who controlled the Dao of Destruction, the first Ancient God of the Ancient God Realm, and possessed a perfect bloodline of nine-stars. If it weren’t for the overwhelming power of the Ultimate Dao, the Ancient God realm would never have been able to bear its pressure, nor would it have allowed a later generation to control it.","On the peak of the mountain, outside an ancient cave.","“Ruler Bei Shan, what brings you here?”","Seeing the hurried arrival of the Northern Mountain Ruler, the Emperor guarding the cave entrance was somewhat surprised!","“Emperor Tong Ling, please inform the Ancestor that something unusual has happened in the Great Si Region. A treasure has emerged.”","Emperor Tong Ling was also an eight-star Ancient God, and he had a clone that always followed the Ancestor. His main body controlled a middle-tier world and held a high status. Even though he was a Ruler of the Ancient God Realm, he treated this fellow Clan Emperor with great courtesy.","Upon hearing about the emergence of a rare treasure, Emperor Tong Ling furrowed his brow slightly, feeling somewhat puzzled. However, since Bei","Shan was a Ruler of the Ancient God Realm, he decided not to inquire further. Instead, he asked Bei Shan to wait outside for a while as he entered the","Ancestor’s cave.","What kind of extraordinary treasure could have prompted Bei Shan’s attention, especially one born in the Great Si Region?!","The Great Si Region?","Isn’t that the Dao Arena of Zhen Wuyang?","Could it be?","Tong Ling’s pace quickened. If that divine hall really appeared, he really had to inform the Ancestor immediately.","“Ancestor!” Tong Ling came to a quiet room that was emitting red light.","In the quiet room.","The Ancestor of the Ancient God Clan sat cross-legged beside a pool of blood.","Looking to the front...","That guy!","He was wearing a set of armor that looked very ordinary, but if one looked closely, they would feel that the armor was embedded in his body and would change color from time to time. At the same time, there was a star that symbolized the bloodline of a peak Ancient God revolving between his eyebrows.","The aura emanating from him was unlike any other powerful expert. Not even Ruler Bei ShanNorthmont, who was ranked in the top hundred of the universe, could compare to him.","If Jian Wushuang saw it now, he might be familiar with this aura.","This was because he and this Ancient God both grasped Ultimate Daos.","The only difference was that the Ancient God Ancestor was an Ultimate","Emperor, while Jian Wushuang was only a Three Revolutions Grand Immortal. Even if he had mastered the Ultimate Dao, he was like an ant in front of this Ultimate Emperor.","“What’s the excuse for this disturbance!?” Ancient God Ancestor’s eyes were still closed as he spoke slowly.","“Ancestor, news has come from Bei Shan. A strange treasure has appeared in the Great Si Region, and we need you to make a decision,” Tong Ling said respectfully.","Ancient God Ancestor suddenly opened his eyes and was overjoyed. “The Great Si Regiono!”","“Luckily, I didn’t leave the original universe. Haha, those old guys left the original universe to find the Dao to become Universe Masters. How ridiculous!”","“Inform all the Emperors to gather in the Ancient God Temple within the time it takes an incense stick to burn.”","“Dao Ancestor, is there a need for all of our Great Dream Realm’s Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortals to move out together?”","“That’s right! Dao Ancestor’s power transcended the heavens, dominating an era. The forces in the surrounding Celestial Realms dare not disrespect our Great Dream Realm.”","A slender boat continuously traversed the void, its speed astonishingly fast, crossing over one domain with each passage.","This boat was an eternal treasure, and there were only a few among the Emperor Dao Ancestors who possessed such a treasure.","Above the boat, the Dao Ancestor of the Great Dream Realm listened to his disciples’ discussions and let out a cold snort!","“You underestimate the allure of the Qishe Temple and the Dao of the Emperor too much.”","A female Sword Immortal in a blue lotus dress was somewhat puzzled and asked, “Master, is it really so miraculous within the Qishen Temple that it can help Grand Yan Immortals achieve Emperorhood?”","Other disciples also turned their gazes towards the Dao Ancestor of the Great Dream Realm, hoping for an answer.","“I don’t know much about the mysteries of the Qishen Temple, but one thing is true. In the past, dozens of Emperors were born within the Great Si Region, but none of them took control of it or left. They remained in the Great Si Region, closed off for years in cultivation, and their strength became astonishingly powerful.”","As the Dao Ancestor spoke, he couldn’t help but recall the person he had","encountered in his youth. That person had never controlled a Celestial Realm, yet possessed strength comparable to his own. The strength of the Great Dao","was unimaginable.”Can Emperors who don’t even have a Dao Arena be that strong?”","“Don’t worry too much, everyone. With the Dao Ancestor here, they won’t be able to cause any trouble.”","The complexion of the Dao Ancestor of the Great Dream Realm changed slightly as he looked at the dozens of disciples on the boat, expressing both disappointment and helplessness.."]},{"number":5133,"title":"Chapter 5133: The Emperors’ Strength","paragraphs":["Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","His path to the Great Dao was smooth sailing. Although he was only the controller of a medium-grade world, his strength was not weaker than those Rulers. Thus, their Great Dream Realm had some reputation in the inner slope of the original universe. Because of his unyielding personality, his prestige in the surrounding areas was very high.","The experts of the Great Dream Realm roamed the other realms. They relied on his reputation to do well, but they also lost their respect for him.","It was respect one had for the Emperor and the universe.","However, in the end, he could not be blamed on those disciples. The Great Dream Realm had only produced an Emperor like him for countless years. His rise was also smooth sailing. He came from a famous sect and grew from a prodigy to an Imperial Prince.","In the end, he became an Emperor in one fell swoop. Furthermore, he was an emperor who had grasped an extremely powerful Great Dao.","<font <=\"\" div=\"\">","In his heart, his sect and his master’s legacy had always been paramount, and he had faithfully guarded the Great Dream Realm.","But now, it seemed that his method of guardianship had been overly indulgent, leading to the younger generation of prodigies becoming arrogant “Little Fellows, do you know that there are strong and weak Emperors?”","Everyone nodded eagerly. “Of course, we know!”","“Very well, since you know, do you understand where my strength stands among the Emperors?”","This time, their heads nodded even faster. “Dao Ancestor, you are undoubtedly one of the top Emperors!”","“Why even ask? Our Dao Ancestor is the Emperor who commands respect across countless realms.”","Many took the opportunity to flatter him, while others genuinely admired him, believing that the Dao Ancestor was the strongest of all Emperors.","Suppressing a smile, the Great Dream Dao Ancestor raised his hand to signal, “Alright, as we continue our journey, I will explain how Emperor strength is categorized.”","Watching these third and even fourth-generation disciples, the Great Dream Dao Ancestor began by discussing the various forces participating in the upcoming Qishen Temple expedition.","The lowest requirement for this fight was a Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal. Ordinary Emperors, and even Emperors who had taken the first step, would not be able to cause any trouble. The true experts who knew the secrets of the Qishen Temple were the Rulers.","Emperor power was also subdivided into strict tiers.","In general, it could be broken down into six levels.","The most common type of Emperor, someone who had just grasped the Emperor’s Dao, and whose path was very ordinary, could only control Emperors of the lower realms, making them first-tier Emperors.","Second-tier strength was possessed by those Emperors who controlled the lower-grade worlds, taking a step further but not experiencing a significant change in power.","Emperors who had control over the middle-grade Daos and established their own Daoist Arenas in the middle-grade worlds were also considered second-tier in terms of strength.","Normal Masters of the middle-grade worlds, who established their Dao Arenas and controlled the middle- grade worlds themselves, were considered third-tier in power.","Emperors like the Infinite Buddha in the Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm were considered Emperors of this level, representing the peak strength of most Emperors.","Most Emperors only had mastery over a single Minor Dao, and even becoming a Dao Ancestor of a lower-grade world was an incredibly difficult feat for them. Achieving third-tier status was their lifelong dream.","The 18 divine generals within the Qishen Temple were currently third-tier in power. Their Great Devouring Dao was the Ultimate Dao, and it was on the level of the Universe Masters. Although they hadn’t completely mastered it, the strength of the Ultimate Dao of the universe was incredibly formidable. As long as they could comprehend three layers, they would possess third-tier power. Once they fully mastered it, they would become Universe Masters, capable of dominating the entire primordial cosmos, even if they only understood half of it.","As for fourth-tier power, one would need mastery over the Great Daos of higher-grade Worlds. Ruler Bei Shan of the Ancient God Clan and the Rulers of other high-grade worlds all belonged to this level. They ruled over high-grade worlds and were omnipotent. Dealing with ordinary Emperors was as easy as crushing ants for them.","Emperors with this level of power could roam freely within a universe, with no one posing a threat to them. Each of them was a dominant force, ruling over heaven and earth.","If the third-tier represented the strong among Emperors, then the fourth-tier represented the strong within the universe.","Apart from the Masters of high-grade worlds, some Emperors could also reach this level.","Zhen Wuyang of the Great Si Region and the Lord Buddha of the Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm were two such individuals.","Although they only controlled medium-grade worlds, their Dao was incredibly potent. If it weren’t for the fact that the higher-grade worlds within the original universe were already controlled, they could completely dominate them.","Their Dao could even rival the Ultimate Dao, and with further progress, they could elevate their Dao domains to higher-grade worlds. At that point, they could advance even further.","On the other hand, those who ruled the higher-grade worlds, like Ruler Bei Shan, often only grasped the Great Dao and remained stuck there for their entire lives.","Zhen Wuyang was different; he possessed the True Martial Dao, which was a complete top-tier Dao. With further advancement, he could open up higher-grade worlds and significantly increase his strength, with the potential to break through to the fifth-tier in power.","However, the difficulty was also terrifying, and in the original universe, only a","few individuals could achieve this.","These few fifth-tier experts had long since traveled to other universes because at their level, advancing further was exceedingly challenging.","The ceiling of strength in the original universe was considered to be at the fifth-tier. Currently, in the original universe, only the Ancestor of the Ancient God Clan remained at this level; all other fifth-rank experts had left.","If they knew that the Qishan Temple held a path to the Universe Masters, these top-tier fifth-rank experts would probably regret their decisions.","However, with their strength, it was relatively simple for them to return if they weren’t in some dangerous Secret Realm. They would just lose their priority.","The Grand Dream Dao Ancestor explained the classification of Emperors’ strength to these newly initiated disciples, making them realize that there was always someone stronger.","“Dao Ancestor, which rank are you at?”","“The third-tier!”","The disciples fell into silence.","The Dao Ancestor they had always revered only possessed the strength of a third-tier Emperor. Meanwhile, many Emperors heading to the Qishan Temple were fourth-tier masters, and some fifth-tier experts had come from other universes.","These Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal were nothing more than cannon fodder. Originally, they had thought they could rely on the Dao Ancestor to navigate through troubled waters and resolve any dangers. But now, it seemed that even the Dao Ancestor was at risk of falling, let alone them.","Many of them had never experienced life-or-death adventures, and some of them were having second thoughts.","This generation of Emperors was at least much stronger than the previous old-timers.","The Grand Dream Dao Ancestor also understood the thoughts of these disciples but chose not to discourage them.","However, when he turned his head, a hint of a smile appeared on his lips.","No one knew his true strength, not even the other Emperors within the clan, was aware of his true power.."]},{"number":5134,"title":"Chapter 5134: Vitality","paragraphs":["Chapter 5134: Vitality","Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","The appearance of the Qishen Temple had stirred up a commotion.","Countless experts came, and even the experts of alternate universes began to head to the Great Si Region of the original universe.","To be precise, the location where the Qishen Temple appeared this time was between the Great Si Region and the Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm.","The vast wilderness was silent and desolate.","The towering Heaven-Reaching Buddha stepped into the vast Great Desolate Wilderness with a calm expression.","He was the supreme existence of the Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm, the ‘Heaven -Reaching Buddha’.","His strength was at the peak of tier four, stronger than ordinary Rulers. The Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm he controlled was a special big world. It was once the origin of a high-grade world. Later, the high-grade world shattered into 3,000 big worlds.","However, the power contained in the origin ground of a higher world was comparable to that of a true high-grade world. Furthermore, the Great Dao of the Heaven-Reaching Buddha was an extremely special top-notch Great Dao among Emperors.","Compared to Zhen Wuyang’s True Martial Great Dao, it was not weak at all. In fact, it could suppress Zhen Wuyang.","However, he had been hiding in the Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm for many years. He no longer cared about the things in the primal universe. He only wanted to take a step forward and perfect the Emperor’s Great Dao. From there, he could advance to the Great Dao of the Universe.","Swoosh!","A young man with a tall hat appeared beside Heaven-Reaching Buddha. His face was as white as jade and he wore a long black robe.","“Dongyan, you’re here too!” Heaven-Reaching Buddha smiled.","Emperor Dongyan’s expression was grave as he snorted coldly,” This matter concerns the Great Dao. How can I not come? Moreover, you’re already here, so why can’t I come?”","“The Qishen Temple is a gift from the heavens. Naturally, everyone can fight for it.","Heaven-Reaching Buddha said indifferently and did not say anything else.","There were hundreds of people following behind the two of them, and there was no lack of powerful Emperors among them.","Even though the Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm was the headquarters of the 3,000 big worlds and Heaven-Reaching Buddha’s prestige was extremely high, internally, it was divided into two factions.","Heaven-Reaching Buddha had risen in the Ancient Era. He controlled a Celestial Realm and became a tier four Emperor. As for Emperor Dongyan, he controlled a relatively weaker realm and was only a tier three Emperor.","The two of them had been fighting since ancient times. If it were not for the appearance of Qishen Temple, the two of them would not have joined forces.","Boom! Boom! Boom!","In the depths of the great desolate, two Grand Yan Immortals were engaged in a great battle of pursuit. They had no idea that there were countless experts outside heading towards the mysterious hall.","“Traitor, you can’t escape.”","The dazzling beast’s phantom covered the void, its speed extremely fast.","The two people who were chasing and fleeing were Jian Wushuang and Xiang Bingyun.","Jian Wushuang could still fight with Xiang Bingyun using the Miniature","Universe, but the power of the Miniature Universe was consumed very quickly. The Yan power within a million-mile radius was drained in the blink of an eye, lasting only as long as a cup of tea. Fortunately, he had prepared in advance. He used his Thought power to create a clone, entangling Xiang Binyun while he himself fled the miniature universe at the fastest speed possible.","“Kind sir, escape in this direction. I... I can sense great vitality in this direction!” The young samanera, clinging to Jian Wushuang’s arm, pointed towards the empty void, his eyes revealing a profound understanding.","Swoosh!","A crimson claw swiped across Jian Wushuang’s chest. Thankfully, his complete focus on Xiang Binyun’s every move allowed him to narrowly evade the attack. Yet, the force of the blood claw pushed him to the brink of collapse, blood trickling from the corner of his mouth.","Ignoring his injuries, Jian Wushuang exerted all his strength once again and fled in another direction. It was only now, after this prolonged pursuit, that he realized he had underestimated the power of a Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal.","His clone within the Miniature Universe had delayed Xiang Binyun for a few breaths, but when discovered, Jian Wushuang had already escaped billions of miles away. Yet, Xiang Binyun’s illusion of the giant beast displayed an unprecedented speed. After several hours of chase, he was dangerously close to catching up.","If he hadn’t mastered the complete Ultimate Dao earlier, Jian Wushuang might not have had any confidence. But since he grasped the Ultimate Dao, every major pathway in his body had reached its peak.","Speed was a condensed representation of the Thunder Great Dao. Previously, even after breaking through to the Grand Yan Immortal realm, his Thunder Dao had only reached the fourth level. For ordinary Grand Yan Immortals who used Thunder Dao as a secondary Dao, they would, at most, cultivate it to the second level during the Three Revolutions cultivation realm. This was because they weren’t primarily focused on the Thunder Dao. However, those who specialized in the Thunder Dao could reach the fourth level during the Three Revolutions cultivation realm.","That was where Jian Wushuang stood now. However, a typical Thunder Dao practitioner could only harness about 60 percent of the Thunder Dao’s power. Those who specialized in it could unleash 80 percent, and the ones who mastered the ultimate Thunder Dao could bring out 100 percent of its power. A practitioner of the Ultimate Dao could harness 120 percent of the power. Currently, Jian Wushuang was only at the fourth level of the Thunder Dao. Yet, the power he wielded surpassed that of someone at the fifth level.","As for Xiang Binyun, although he was not specialized in Thunder Dao, his speed was comparable to that of someone at the sixth level. Obviously, this was his second main Dao, apart from his primary Dao, the Dao of Destruction.","His speed equaled that of practitioners who specialized in the Thunder Dao.","Jian Wushuang could not shake it off and could only grit his teeth and persevere.","“Kind Sir, it’s this direction. I can feel it. In the time it takes for an incense stick to burn, we’ll be able to find the source.” The young samanera looked excited.","He followed Jian Wushuang as they fought their way out of the army of corpses. They entered a strange realm and eventually escaped the void, relentlessly pursued by the phantom giant beast.","Throughout this journey, he had been on edge. Now, following his senses, he felt the vibrant surge of vitality growing stronger the closer they got.","“An incense stick worth of time?” Jian Wushuang was exhausted and his Great Dao was trembling, gasping for air under the pressure from Xiang Bingyun behind him.","However, he could endure for the duration of an incense stick, fearing that the young samanera might sense the wrong direction. If that happened, they would have to aimlessly flee once more.","Their only option was to venture into dangerous ruins or the territories of powerful creatures, seeking a glimmer of hope.","This kind of life force was extremely dangerous, but he had no other choice now. He could only hope that the little novice monk’s senses were not wrong.","This hope was exceedingly perilous. Yet, he had no other choice now. He could only hope that Xiaoshami’s senses wouldn’t fail them.","Xiang Bingyun was a Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal. There were very few things in the vast void of the Great Desolate Wilderness that could threaten a Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal.","Most of the powerful ancient ruins were left behind by the Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortals. Some formidable restrictions could bind them, but it was uncertain who would break the restrictions first. They might end up trapping themselves, left waiting for death in place.","In the distant void far from Jian Wushuang, the Heaven-Reaching Buddha and Emperor Dongyan, along with their group, were using rapid teleportation techniques. Their destination was precisely where Jian Wushuang was.","If the vitality mentioned referred to the Heaven-Reaching Buddha and his group, it would take Jian Wushuang at least 1,000 years to meet them.."]},{"number":5135,"title":"Chapter 5135: Entering the Dao","paragraphs":["Chapter 5135: Entering the Dao","Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Swoosh!","Heaven-Reaching Buddha was also moving toward Jian Wushuang and the other man at an extremely fast speed. Every time he moved, they would cross the diameter of an ordinary territory.","With their speed, they would be able to meet Jian Wushuang in less than an incense stick’s time. In that time, they would be able to reach the outside of the Disambiguation Temple.","The smile on the Heaven -Reaching Lord Buddha’s face grew wider as he turned his head to look behind him.","“Wuliang, is there someone ahead who has a great karma with you?”","The Wulliang Lord Buddha was also an Emperor-level existence. He was the controller of the Wuliang Great World among the 3,000 Great Worlds. He was also the most powerful Lord Buddha other than the Heaven-Reaching Buddha. He had the strength of a peak tier 3 expert.","The few Monks who had crossed the Great Desolate Wilderness to enter the Great Si Region were his fourth-generation disciples, and most of the Monks who had gone to the Great Si Region were his disciples. The bold words of ‘I’m willing to spend all my time in the Great Si Region to become Yan Immortals’ were said by the Great Wuliang Buddha himself.","It was precisely this sentence that caused the Monks in the Wuliang Great World to rush forward and rush into the endless Great Desolate Wilderness, crossing half of the Great Desolate Wilderness and crossing the regional wall to enter the Great Si Region.","“It’s my disciple. He seems to be facing a deadly karmic calamity, ” the Wuliang Buddha replied indifferently.","He only mentioned the young samanera and not Jian Wushuang.","After all, he had given the Bodhi Heartwood to Jian Wushuang not long ago. How could he not sense Jian Wushuang’s existence?","Furthermore, he was the Wuliang Lord Buddha who was famous for his deductions. The Great Dao he grasped when he became an Emperor was the Heavenly Dao. Although his grasp of the Dao was only at the intermediate level, he still had the strength of a tier-three Emperor.","“Then let’s save them on the way! It shouldn’t take much time.” Heaven-Reaching Buddha glanced at Emperor Dongyan beside him, then looked at Wuliang Buddha with a meaningful look.","The three of them were considered the strongest existences in the Heaven Realm. When they were born, the Heaven Realm had yet to shatter. They were all princes of their respective sects. Naturally, there were many battles, but in the end, he won.","Dongyan was still alright. He controlled the Land Realm and formed his own faction. He had always been in a competitive relationship with him.","Wuliang entered the Buddhist Sect halfway and became his right-hand man. However, he could sense that Wuliang’s thoughts had never entered the Buddhist Sect.","This meaningful glance made Wuliang feel a little uncomfortable. After suppressing some of the things in his heart, he calmed down and replied, “Of course.”","Heaven-Reaching Buddha retracted his gaze and did not say anything else.","This time, the Qishen Temple had suddenly appeared in the Great Desolate Wilderness. As half of the master of the Great Desolate Wilderness, he did not know about such a secret at all. He actually did not know about it at all.","All these years, Wuliang had been advocating to spread his religion into the Great Si Region, which made him even more puzzled. Now, it seemed that all of this had been premeditated.","Jian Wushuang was fleeing with all his might, but at the same time, he had to be on guard against Xiang Bingyun. He had already reached the point of mental breakdown.","Fortunately, his Heart power was extremely strong due to his Ultimate Dao, comparable to an Emperor. With such a state of mind, he could persist until now. If it was an ordinary Grand Yan Immortal, even a Nine Revolutions would have died several times.","“Kind Sir, hold on. I can feel that life force is right in front of us,” the little Monk said as he played with the prayer beads in his hand.","He was a novice monk from the Wuliang Great World. He grew up on the Wuliang Mountain, which was the Dao Arena of the Wuliang Buddha. He was the sixth-generation disciple of the mountain and had never left the mountain for thousands of years. Now, as soon as he left the mountain, he followed his masters to the most dangerous Great Desolate Wilderness. He passed through half of the Great Desolate Wilderness and arrived outside the regional wall with great difficulty. He was about to enter the Great Si Region that he had always dreamed of. However, he didn’t expect that he would run right into trouble in an instant.","This calamity was a hundred times, a thousand times, ten thousand times more dangerous than any other calamity he had encountered.","All of his masters had fallen in the Great Desolate Wilderness, and they had not even entered the Great Si Region. They had not even converted a single Great Si Region’s Yan Immortal, and now they were being chased. After a day of wandering, he felt as if he had cultivated for billions of years. “Not good!” Jian Wushuang’s tense body suddenly trembled.","Swish!!!","A sharp claw pierced through Jian Wushuang’s chest. Golden blood flowed","down the claw and dripped onto the young samanera’s face.","“Kind Sir!” The little Monk’s eyes were red. The Grandmaster was dead, the Second Master had self-destructed his Great Dao for him, and the Third Master had abandoned everything to let them live. Everything they did was to let him live, regardless of life and death.","Was the Kind Sir who had been protecting him going to die too?","‘Why?”","The young Monk let go of Jian Wushuang’s hand and the Buddha Beads on his other hand was crushed by him.","“Why is this? We just want to live.” The young samanera’s eyes turned red. The moment he let go of his hand, he dashed out and stood in front of Jian Wushuang.","The young samanera clenched his fists tightly and his face was filled with killing intent. Even his thick eyebrows were trembling. At this moment, he stood in front of Jian Wushuang and looked straight at Xiang Bingyun, the Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal.","“Get out of the way!” Jian Wushuang endured his injuries. All the treasures on him had been used up while he was escaping. His armor had long been broken, and even the indestructible Wushuang Divine Sword had long been damaged.","Jian Wushuang desperately swung his sword several times and used up the last bit of Thought power to stop Xiang Bingyun. Then he reached out to pull the little Monk, “Hurry up and go!”","“No!” The young Monk opened Jian Wushuang’s arm. Despite his meager strength, he burst out with an immovable power.","It only took a moment for Xiang Bingyun to arrive in front of the little Monk.","“You reckless thing!” The phantom behind Xiang Bingyun disappeared, revealing his original appearance. His height had shrunk a little, and the green scales on his body fluttered in the wind.","“Go to hell!” After chasing for so long, Xiang Bingyun was already extremely angry. He attacked with a deadly hand as his huge palm directly slapped at the little Monk.","Even Jian Wushuang, who was at his peak, did not dare to take the claw of a Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal head-on. The little Monk was also fearless. He stood there without blinking, wanting to take it head-on.","It was too late for Jian Wushuang to stop all of this. He did not want to die. He had just mastered the Ultimate Dao and his Ultimate Dao was only at the fifth level. He still had an endless future. He did not want to die here.","“Forget it, I won’t escape.” Jian Wushuang touched the broken Wushuang Divine Sword in his hand. His broken body was floating in the air. He looked at the little Monk who was trying to stop Xiang Bingyun with his hands and smiled.","The young Monk opened his arms and let out a breath.","He had vented all of his 30 million years of cultivation.","At this moment, he suddenly understood. There was zen in his eyes, and his heart opened up.","This broad traceless path was as white as jade. There was zen in his eyes, zen in his heart, and only in his heart. His life was extraordinary. In an instant, the novice Monk, Hu Qing, stepped into the Dao."]},{"number":5136,"title":"Chapter 5136: Leaping Through Cultivation Levels in OneStep","paragraphs":["Chapter 5136: Leaping Through Cultivation Levels in OneStep","Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","“Stop!” the young Monk roared. Behind him, a vast avenue materialized, the heavens and earth transforming ceaselessly. A Monk with a massive rosary hanging from his neck appeared behind the young Monk.","The figure behind him was not a Buddha or a large Image Form. Instead, it was an ordinary Monk, quite similar in appearance to the young Monk. He clasped his hands together in a wrathful gesture and held a brown staff in the other hand.","“Break!” The young Monk’s slender body merged completely with the heavens and earth, becoming one with the Monk who resembled him. Together, they wielded the brown staff.","Boom! Boom! Boom!","A claw so powerful that even Jian Wushuang dared not confront it directly was shattered by the young Monk’s staff.","The staff techniques were formless, yet they could resist a Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal, surprising even Jian Wushuang.","He had just entered the Dao, and it seemed like the Ultimate Dao. Perhaps only the Ultimate Dao could be this formidable.","The blood claw dispersed, and Xiang Bingyun, who had already arrived, instantly retreated, putting millions of miles between them before coming to a halt.","“How is this possible? How can you withstand me?” Xiang Bingyun could hardly believe it. He had never regarded the young Monk seriously, considering him nothing more than a small fry who wasn’t even a Yan Immortal. If not for Jian Wushuang’s protection, he would have been crushed by his pressure long ago.","Now, this inconspicuous young Monk suddenly exploded in power, directly blocking his strongest attack. He had lived through countless chaos cycles and had never heard of anyone skipping several cultivation levels in one step, grasping the complete Dao directly.","Could he have been disguising his strength all along?","Xiang Bingyun’s mind was filled with more doubt than shock, but he quickly denied his speculation. “No, it’s not a disguise. If it were, he would have revealed himself earlier.’","“Kind Sir, your injuries!” The young Monk, in the form of a youth with shaved hair and Monk robes, turned to Jian Wushuang.","“I can hold on!” Jian Wushuang endured the dissolution of his body, sitting down directly and mending his injuries with the continuous repair of the Great Dao within him. In just the time it took to finish a cup of tea, he would be completely healed.","Now that the young Monk had suddenly surged in power and could temporarily withstand Xiang Bingyun, Jian Wushuang needed to seize this opportunity to recover his injuries.","In case another Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal emerged from those corpses, even if the young Monk was strong, both of them would perish here today.","“I never expected that after millions of years of accumulation, just as I began to recover, I would encounter you two freaks!” Xiang Bingyun moved his wrist slightly. He was astonished not by the young Monk’s sudden burst of power but by the fact that he hadn’t reached a level where it surprised him yet.","Although the young Monk managed to block his most powerful claw techniques, it did not mean they were equals. As his energy dissipated, it became evident that Hu Qing’s aura was steadily diminishing.","Even though the two before him posed no immediate threat, each of them possessed a power that could rival the Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal, a level that, in the Ancient Era, would have marked them as potential Emperors within their sects.","However, fate had brought them face to face with him now. In the past, he might have spared such talent, but he had been suppressed by the formidable Zhen Wuyang for millions of years, transforming him into something neither human nor ghost. There was no room for the leisure and elegance of ancient times in his current existence.","“The genius of the Great Si Region, if I kill you, I’m afraid even Zhen Wuyang would feel a pang of regret!” sneered Xiang Binyun. He was willing to risk his life to make Zhen Wuyang uncomfortable.","His hatred for Zhen Wuyang had accumulated over millions of years, as if the events of the Ancient Era had happened only yesterday. He could not forget Zhen Wuyang’s disgusting face, nor the glorious era of the ancient times.","“Die!”","His boundless anger erupted in that moment. He wielded a battle axe stained with ancient blood, the very weapon he had used when commanding the heavenly court. The axe left marks in the air, lingering like scars in the sky. Explosions of energy danced and roamed in the vast emptiness.","The Monk’s form, transformed from the young samanera, soared into the sky, wielding a long staff, ready to confront Xiang Binyun head-on.","In an instant, they clashed. The Monk’s staff techniques were natural, as if they were an inherent part of him. Every move was precise, leaving no room for error. Against Xiang Binyun’s bloodied axe, the Monk managed to hold his ground.","With every swing of his brown staff, he left room for his own defense, attacking with seven parts of his strength and reserving three parts for defense. This balance between offense and defense left Xiang Binyun unable to find an opening, unable to exploit any weaknesses.","The Monk remained calm and composed, his mind filled with endless zen wisdom, his staff techniques flowing naturally.","This was the Ultimate Dao of Buddhism, the ‘Zen’.","After three million years of cultivation in the Buddhist tradition, he had finally comprehended his own profound Dao, taking a step that others couldn’t take in millions of years. He had ascended directly to the rank of a Great Vajra in the Buddhist Sect, a power equal to that of a Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal.","Even the accomplished disciples in the heavens couldn’t match his brilliance. If he managed to return alive, he would undoubtedly be hailed as the foremost disciple on the Wuliang Mountain, a path so rare in the original universe.","In the realm of Emperors, there was only one with the Ultimate Dao, the","Ancestor of the Ancient God Clan.","As for the Yan Immortals with the Ultimate Dao, it was elusive, with only a few in each era achieving the Grand Yan Immortal cultivation level due to its extreme difficulty.","Jian Wushuang, thanks to his profound understanding of the Ultimate Dao, practiced for millions of years in the starry sky to break through to the Grand Yan Immortal level. Yet, his Ultimate Sword Dao remained at the fifth level, unable to make progress.","To have a chance at merging Daos, one had to reach at least the seventh level of the Ultimate Dao. Success was a one-in-a-billion chance, explaining why there was only one Ultimate Emperor in the entire original universe, the Ancestor of the Ancient God Clan.","However, the young samanera had seemingly leaped directly into the sixth level of the Ultimate Dao. With one more step, he could attempt merging paths to become an Ultimate Emperor.","An Emperor with the Ultimate Dao! Even without control over any Great World, he had the power of a fourth-tier Emperor.","The Ancestor of the Ancient God Clan, when at the seventh level, successfully merged Daos and later, through countless chaotic cycles, advanced to the fifth- tier Emperor.","This was the pinnacle of the universe, and there was hope for him to ascend further, reaching the ninth level of the Dao of Destruction, becoming truly invincible in the universe. At that point, he could effortlessly become the ruler of the cosmos. Yet, this step was incredibly challenging, requiring immense luck. Success was almost impossible.","Now, with the young samanera taking the first step, his strength had grown immensely. Who knew what he would become with the next step? He was the real genius. Once he ascended to the Emperor-level, even with fourth-tier strength, he would be far superior to most disciples nurtured by major forces. Many who became Emperor Gods in these forces remained ordinary, possessing only first-tier strength, struggling to control even a low-grade world.","Such weak Emperors were not worthy of the attention of these major forces. A true Emperor needed at least second-tier strength to be considered powerful. Third-tier Emperors were the leaders of factions, truly exceptional beings.."]},{"number":5137,"title":"Chapter 5137: Controller of the Great Desolate","paragraphs":["Chapter 5137: Controller of the Great Desolate","Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Qishen Temple.","No matter what happened in the outside world, the 18 divine generals in the hall did not move. The Great Desolate Wilderness’s Heavenly Dao had been unknowingly controlled by Liu Ya.","After all, Liu Ya had inherited the Dao of ‘Desolate’. This Dao was a peak Dao, and the divine lord of the Qishen Temple used this Dao to control a universe’s secret realm.","In the river of time and space, there existed countless universes and many secret realms comparable to universes. These secret realms were like hidden reefs in a river; if the universe nurtured life, these secret realms nurtured danger, containing terrifying cosmic laws within them.","The Desolate Divine Master of the Wilderness had cultivated this Great Dao to its peak, ruling over a cosmic secret realm. Their power was incredibly terrifying, surpassing even the Universe Masters.","“Liu Ya, congratulations!” Yang Jun revealed a faint smile.","With the Great Desolate Wilderness completely under control, the Liu Ya’s power soared to the early fourth tier. Utilizing the Desolate Dao within the Great Desolate Wilderness, they could now overlook the pinnacle of the universe.","In this way, no one dared to peer into the Qishen Temple within the Great","Desolate Wilderness.","“Everyone, I have completely taken control of the Great Desolate Wilderness now. Even if Zhen Wuyang comes again, he won’t be my match. Now, we should discuss our plans for the future,” Liu Ya said, rubbing his hands against the armrests of his stone throne. His power had just undergone a breakthrough, and his energy could not help but leak out.","The other divine generals all had third-tier power and naturally sensed how terrifying the power emanating from Liu Ya was.","Su He’s brows furrowed slightly, his heart slightly moved.","The way Liu Ya had handled things was a disgrace to all Emperors obsessed with the Qishen Dao. However, currently, they still needed him to counter Zhen","Wuyang.","The difference in power between a fourth-tier Emperor and a third-tier Emperor was enormous. Moreover, Zhen Wuyang’s Dao was not weak. It was also a top-tier Dao, giving him the power of a fourth-tier Ruler within a medium-grade world. In the future, with further advancement, he could elevate the Great Si Regionto a high-grade world, further enhancing his power, achieving the pinnacle of the universe, and venturing out of the universe to roam the river of time and space.","Although this path was not as grand as the Qishen Dao, it could quickly manifest power. If they were like other Emperors, attempting to forcefully absorb the Qishen Dao, no matter how long the time stretched, it would be challenging for them to elevate the Qishen Dao to the level of a Universe Lord.","Within the original universe, there were several fifth-tier emperors. They had existed for countless epochs, yet they still could not control the universe, and could not become Universe Masters.","Six Crows could not help but sneer.","“Brother Liu Ya, you are currently the strongest. You also have the ability to protect the Qishen Temple. I suggest we change our plan and stay in this Great","Desolate Wilderness. What do you think?” Su He’s aura slightly declined, giving Liu Ya plenty of face.","However, the other Emperors still looked down on Liu Ya and only snorted.","“I don’t have any attachment to the Great Si Region anyway. I can leave or stay. As for the safety of the Qishen Temple, I don’t care about anyone else’s expressions. At most, I’ll just fight again. I’ve already reached the peak of the seventh level of the Qishen Great Dao. No one under the third level is my match. I’m confident that I can even fight against Zhen Wuyang.”","The one who spoke was the warlike Emperor Fenghua from the Ancient Era. He was the first to die in the battle against Zhen Wuyang.","During that era, the Emperors of the Great Si Region revered the Qishen and the Qishen Dao. They did not take Zhen Wuyang, a second-tier Emperor who had inherited the True Martial Great Dao, seriously at all. Even if he controlled the Great Si Region, he would at most be a third-tier Emperor.","However, what they did not expect was that Zhen Wuyang had actually created his own unique skill on the True Martial Great Dao, forcefully raising the True","Martial Great Dao, which was a medium-grade Great Dao, to a peak Great Dao.","As soon as he took control of the Great Si Region, he already had the strength of a third-tier Emepror.","After that, he conquered the various Heavenly Palaces and suppressed the Emperors under his feet. He even unified the entire Great Si Region and chased them all into the depths of the Great Desolate Wilderness.","Everyone present was willing to recall this humiliating history, especially when they had brought several generations of disciples under them. All of them were at the Grand Yan Immortal level and had begun to open up a world in the depths of the Great Desolate Wilderness.","The people who had been chased out of the Great Si Region had never expected that Zhen Wuyang, who had unified the Great Si Region, would still not let them off. After reaching the strength of the fourth-tier, Zhen Wuyang came to the depths of the Great Wilderness Desolate alone and killed them along with hundreds of millions of disciples.","That day, a torrent of blood surged in the Great Desolate Wilderness. In the silent void, a divine land appeared, formed from the piled-up corpses – the very land that Jian Wushuang had once trodden upon.","This humiliation had turned everyone against Zhen Wuyang to their very core.","Liu Ya sneered, “Fine! If you want revenge, go find Zhen Wuyang. As the candidate Divine Lord, I have an obligation to ensure the safety of the Qishen Temple. You can rest assured about that.”","In his opinion, these Emperors had already fallen into madness, obstinately guarding the unchanged Qishen Dao. Not to mention the Universe Masters, even reaching the ninth level of the Qishen Dao was a massive challenge in this lifetime.","Even if they reached the ninth level, what difference would it make? By the time they reached that level, he would have already elevated the Great Desolate Wilderness to a high-grade world, possessing fifth-tier power and a comprehensively integrated Great Dao, which, when Perfected, could compete for the pinnacle of the universe.","“Don’t think you can be so arrogant just because your power exceeds mine.","Back when I waged war in the Great Si Region, what were you?” Emperor Fenghua had a volatile temper. When he became an Emperor, several Emperors present were his juniors, including Liu Ya, who hadn’t even been born at that time.","“What was I back then? Want to find out?” Liu Ya stirred the boundless energy of the Great Desolate Wilderness, instantly reshaping his body. His handsome face was somewhat pale, his pair of purple eyes slightly moving, and the mark of a wild beast on his forehead kept flickering.","Smack!","Liu Ya tapped the armrest of his throne and slowly stood up. The aura in the hall instantly descended several levels. A terrifying pressure roamed above the hall. As long as Liu Ya willed it, he could suppress all the Emperors directly.","This was the gap in power. The Qishen Dao perfectly overlapped with the Desolate Dao. When he just switched, he elevated the Desolate Dao to the ninth level. Once he perfected his Dao, he could step into the fifth-tier. By relying on his own power, he could establish a high-grade world.","Now, after a lifetime of pursuing the Qishen Dao, he finally understood that the achieved power was true strength.","Everything else was just wishful thinking. If it came down to the strength of Dao, wouldn’t the Ultimate Emperors be able to look down on everyone? After all, mastering the Ultimate Dao and successfully integrating it would quickly allow them to cultivate to the level of fifth-tier Emperors.","Under the immense pressure, the other Emperors hurriedly intervened to defuse the situation.."]},{"number":5138,"title":"Chapter 5138: Ancient Era’s Secret Text","paragraphs":["Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","“Fenghua, don’t argue so much. Brother Liu Ya gave up the Universe Great Dao for our sake.’","“Brother Liu Ya, this is not the time for internal conflicts. Zhen Wuyang has probably arrived by now. Although we are safe inside the palace, we can’t stay closed off on our cultivation paths forever. We need to face strong enemies head-on first and establish a firm foundation.’","While the crowd was still arguing, powerful forces kept arriving at the edge of the Great Desolate Wilderness, except for Heaven-Reaching Buddha and Zhen Wuyang.","In the depths of the Great Desoalte Wilderness, Zhen Wuyang sat cross-legged in the void. He was the only one from the Great Si Region present, but that was enough.","A fourth-tier Emperor, and it was his own territory. He had nothing to worry about, except for the disappearance of the Qishen Temple.","<font <=\"\" div=\"\">","In ancient times, he had driven all the Emperors deep into the Great Desolate Wilderness. He searched every corner of the Great Si Region but couldn’t find the legendary Qishen Temple.","At first, he suspected that some Emperor had acquired the Qishen Temple and became its master. So he ventured into the depths of the Great Desolate Wilderness and slaughtered all the Grand Yan Immortals who had obtained benefits in the Qishen Temple, along with the Emperors.","He had risen to power in the late Ancient Era and had no chance to encounter the Qishen Temple. The 18 Emperors even sealed off information about the Qishen Temple. He only learned about the existence of the Qishen Temple in their Great Si Region when he inherited the True Martial legacy.","The inheritance also described the origins of the Qishen Temple, including the extremely mysterious Qishen Dao.","There wasn’t much information about the Qishen, but Zhen Wuyang was sure of one thing: becoming an Emperor by entering the Qishen Temple was real.","In the late Ancient Era, as his power grew, he learned that besides the Great Si Region, there were other Celestial Domains. Emperors were exceedingly rare in those other domains. In several neighboring domains, only their Great Si Region had over ten Emperors in one era.","With the enlightenment from Zhen Wuyangs Great Dao, he became more convinced that the Qishen Temple held a great secret.","The Dao of the Qishen, the mystery of the Emperors.","It was even linked to the legendary Universe Masters.","In his quest for truth, he unleashed havoc beyond the domain, slaughtering everyone, all in search of the Qishen Temple. However, after killing them all, he never found the temple.","Many years later, he came to terms with it, no longer actively seeking the temple. He buried this matter deep within his heart.","Until now, with the resurgence of ancient Emperors and the emergence of the Qishen Temple, his memories were stirred.","If only those Emperors had revived, he wouldn’t have paid them any mind. In the Ancient Era, he was a fourth-tier Emperor. Now, after countless eons, his power had reached its peak at the fourth-tier. If not for the sudden appearance of the Qishen Temple, he would have planned to leave the original universe.","The original universe’s aid to Emperors had diminished significantly. To advance further, one had to venture into the River of Time; that was where Emperors should go.","Places with great opportunities also held great dangers. Even as a fourth-tier peak Emperor, he still faced the risk of falling.","Now, with the reappearance of the Qishen Temple, he did not know if this was a tremendous opportunity. If this was his only chance, he would give it his all.","“Stepping into the pinnacle of the universe, we cultivators have an unshirkable duty.”","Zheng Wuyangs eyes opened wide, his awareness fixed on the Qishen Temple floating in the void.","He couldn’t go now; he had to wait for other powerful beings to arrive. If he went alone, who knew if those ancient Emperors might take the Qishen Temple and flee.","He did not have the confidence to guard the temple alone, so he had to wait. He waited for other emperors to come, suppress the Qishen Temple together, kill those old folks from the Ancient Era, and then contend with Emperors from other domains.","While one side was unpredictable, the other side was in a life-and-death struggle.","Jian Wushuang and the young samanera Hu Qing still faced the formidable enemy, Xiang Bingyun.","No matter how exquisite their staff techniques were, even if they were flawless, the gap in strength was insurmountable. In just a few breaths, Hu Qing succumbed under Xiang Bingyun’s attacks.","Axe techniques represented the pinnacle of strength; one’s strength could break myriad techniques. No matter how perfect the defense, it would shatter","under absolute power.","Jian Wushuang recalled the giant he had encountered in the starry sky; he also wielded an axe. In his hands, the giant axe could split the sky.","That scene seemed like it happened ages ago, and Jian Wushuang reminisced.","“Ah!” Hu Qing could not hold on any longer; his techniques dispersed, but his figure remained guarding Jian Wushuang, never retreating even half a step, despite his body being severely battered.","“Phew...” Jian Wushuang exhaled, his injuries mostly healed, but it would take time to recover his Heart and Thought power.","However, Jian Wushuangs state of mind had undergone a qualitative change amidst these consecutive dangers. This was tremendously beneficial for the fifth level of Ultimate Sword Dao, the ‘Heartsword Cosmos’. This was because Ultimate Dao required Heart power. He had actually comprehended the Ultimate Dao in the starry sky for countless eons, but he had only reached the third level.","The first level represented his state when he comprehended the Ultimate Dao, the second level was when he realized it on a star, and the third level was when he completely mastered the Ultimate Dao.","Jian Wushuang, having only mastered three levels, could engage in battle with the Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal using his One Thought Universe technique. This showcased the extraordinary strength of the Ultimate Dao.","For ordinary Daos, Three Revolutions Grand Yan Immortals could comprehend six layers. Upon reaching the seventh layer, they would become a Six Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal. The eighth layer led to a Nine","Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal, and achieving the ninth layer made one a Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal. The tenth layer marked the successful merging with the Dao, becoming an Emperor.","Emperors who followed these common Daos, although stronger than the Grand Yan Immortals, didn’t possess much superiority. They were considered the lowest level among Emperors and were even inferior in status to some Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal.","Mastering a single Dao to its pinnacle to attain the status of Emperor demonstrated the weakness of these common Daos. Once they succeeded in merging with the Dao, their understanding of it became profound, but they remained stuck at the first-tier of Emperor for their entire lives. These","Emperors were the most useless, yet the most numerous in the universe.","If one were to categorize the the countless Daos within the river of time and space, they could be divided into five levels.","The fifth level consisted of first-tier Emperors. Regardless of their improvement in cultivation, they were the weakest among their peers. However, with time, they managed to walk to the end of this simple and smooth Dao.","Comparatively, the fourth-level paths underwent a qualitative change compared to the fifth level. Many Grand Yan Immortals followed these paths. If they succeeded in merging with the Dao, they had the hope of further advancement. Once they comprehended the entire Dao, their strength would reach the second-tier of Emperor.","At the second-tier Emperor stage, they could control a lower- grade world. With the world’s blessings in their own Dao Arena, their strength could reach the peak of the second-tier. With the advantage of the Dao Arena, they were not afraid of some third-tier Emperors.","However, the lower- grade worlds in the universe had been divided among major powers. If one did not have a background or identity, they simply had no opportunity to control a world and become a Dao Ancestor."]},{"number":5139,"title":"Chapter 5139: Three Great Daos","paragraphs":["Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","The first two Daos were the ones that produced the most Emperors in the universe.","Although Jian Wushuang didn’t know much about the Emperors, based on what he had found in some relics, the stronger the Emperor’s Dao was, the harder it was to improve it.","Although one’s life was infinite, if one’s grasp of the Dao remained stagnant, it would affect one’s state of mind, causing one to fall into madness and collapse.","Many of those who entered the Great Desolate Wilderness were the same.","Many cultivators comprehended a Dao that belonged to them when they were at the Yan Immortal level. In the beginning, they were still ignorant and could not differentiate the levels of the Dao.","<font <=\"\" div=\"\">","However, some powerful factions would nurture their Princes, Saints, and Dao Children to comprehend some high-grade Great Dao, which was a third-grade Dao.","This path was currently the one that most people in the Yan Immortal stage walked. When they were in the Yan Immortal stage, it was also the bottleneck of the vast majority of Heaven’s Favorites. If they advanced to the Grand Yan Immortal stage, then their status and strength would skyrocket.","This was because when one cultivated this Dao to its peak, they would be able to control a middle-grade world and become a tier 3 Emperor.","Tier 3 Emperors were the most influential figures in the universe, controlling a world or establishing a huge power, reaching the peak of power.","This was the pursuit of the majority of geniuses. However, these geniuses were stuck at the Yan Immortal realm on the fourth level and at the eighth level, they were stuck at the Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal stage forever. Many Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal had lived for countless years and were stuck there. As for those geniuses who were stuck at the Yan Immortal realm, they were either expelled from the sect or they gave up on themselves, their minds destroyed.","Too many outstanding geniuses fell on this path.","If the third-tier path was the ultimate destination for geniuses, then the second-tier path was the goal fought over by the various Princes.","In every era, there were a few dazzling figures, aside from the Zhen Wuyang of the Great Si Region.","When Zhen Wuyang rose, he truly outshone all others.","In the same era, there were still a few people who were comparable to him at the Grand Yan Immortal level. They were all second-grade Great Dao, but those few people were permanently stuck below the Nine Revolutions level and could not even step into the Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal level.","Only Zhen Wuyang’s path was unobstructed all the way, and after becoming an Emperor, he could further advance in a short time, becoming a tier 4 Emperor.","Now that billions of years had passed, Zhen Wuyangs strength had already reached the peak of tier 4, comparable to the Rulers of some higher worlds. If he were to open up another higher world, his strength would increase even more.","The second-grade Dao, when mastered to its peak, could elevate one to the level of a tier 5 Emperor. Countless geniuses had fallen on this path, and despite the accumulation of countless epochs, a few had managed to ascend. However, these Emperors had long departed the original universe, venturing into the mysterious River of Time and Space.","Advancing further within the original universe was simply unrealistic. The remnants and treasures within held little significance for them; there was no need to linger. Within the River of Time and Space, tier 5 Emperors stood at the pinnacle, clashing with peak Emperors from numerous universes was the only way to progress, to vie for supremacy in the cosmos.","This was also the reason why there was only one tier 5 Emperor in the original universe.","Those who comprehended the second-grade Dao were considered exceptional talents, worthy of serious cultivation by major powers. However, practitioners who comprehended the Ultimate Dao were the universe’s darlings.","Not only were major forces eager to nurture them, but the universe itself would bestow various opportunities upon them, granting immense fate energy to those who comprehended the Ultimate Dao. Each practitioner who grasped the Ultimate Dao carried significant cosmic fate energy.","Despite these benefits, there was considerable resistance. The fact that even the supreme cosmic rules refrained from intervening contradicted the rule of balance. Although these rules lacked emotions and were as cold as weapons, they self-adjusted the universe’s balance. To them, those who comprehended the Ultimate Dao were not geniuses but rather pitiable souls toyed with by fate. Hence, the cosmic rules augmented these practitioners’ cosmic fate energy.","Ever since Jian Wushuang had comprehended Ultimate Sword Dao, he had encountered countless opportunities. Naturally, he had obtained the providence from the Supreme Law of the Universe.","From the fourth level of the Ultimate Dao, the ‘Star River Lake Sea; to the fifth level, the ‘Heartsword World’. He had first been saved by the","Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm’s Monks, and then he had cultivated the Dao of Heart power. Later, he cultivated the Dao of Heart, an auxiliary path that allowed him to comprehend the perverted Great Dao.","There were records of the Ultimate Dao, but Jian Wushuang had never heard of the Extreme Dao, nor had he heard of the inheritance secret technique he now possessed. A mere Three Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal could display a One Thought Universe, rich with grand paths. Moreover, his mental strength surpassed that of many Emperors.","Jian Wushuang now had three Great Daos in his body.","The farthest advanced was the Ultimate Sword Dao, reaching the fifth level. The second was the Dao of the Heart, which had unknowingly reached the fourth level. The symbiotic relationship between Heart power and Sword","Principle allowed the Ultimate Sword Dao to reach the fifth level, creating the Heartsword World. Consequently, the Ultimate Sword Dao reciprocally enhanced his Heart power, elevating it to the fifth level as well.","The final one was the recently mastered Extreme Dao. Though only at the third level, it could still employ the absurd technique of a One Thought Universe.","This was Jian Wushuangs greatest trump card. The second was the Heartsword World.","Now, with his physical body completely restored from the brink of collapse and his mental and heart strength significantly enhanced, Jian MJushuang speculated that every major crisis tested his mental state and mental strength. As long as he passed safely, these two Great Daos would improve.","However, this was only the first advancement. Jian Wushuang dared not confirm whether it was true. If it were, he would either grow stronger and reach the pinnacle of the universe or face the next crisis.","Once more, Xiang Binyun swung his arm, smashing the giant axe toward the young monk. The blood-colored axe rolled like a dragon, tearing through space, bursting the surrounding cosmic forces. It stormed the young monk like a furious storm.","Under this immense pressure, the young monk remained calm. Yet, the speed of his physical collapse accelerated. By now, half of his cosmic body had burned away. If there were further losses, his strength would decline again, forcing him to self-destruct like his fellow apprentices, exhausting his cosmic body, fighting until the final moment.","Golden runes faintly flickered on the brown staff. The young samanera’s expression changed, and he roared. His eyes widened as he exerted all his cosmic strength, launching his final strike.","However, with half his divine body lost, his strength had significantly waned, and he was unable to fully unleash this strike. Nevertheless, he gritted his teeth and desperately employed his strongest attack.","Unfortunately, even this formidable strike couldn’t resist Xiang Binyun. Even at his peak state, using this move could only achieve a draw.","“Hmph, break for me!” Xiang Binyun’s internal power surged, and cosmic forces once again flooded into his enormous axe.","Boom!"]},{"number":5140,"title":"Chapter 5140: Leave the Rest to Me","paragraphs":["Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","The clash of the axe and the long staff resounded through the air. After several flashes of mysterious runes on the brown staff, it couldn’t hold on any longer. It flew out of the hands of the young monk, devoid of the empowering runes. Without those runes, the staff was just a hard stick; only with the runes could it be considered a treasure.","The young monk, unarmed, didn’t retreat in the face of the giant axe. Astonishingly, he caught it with his bare hands.","Hiss...","The sound of the blood axe tearing through flesh echoed, and the young monk gritted his teeth, his face pale. His eyes radiated a fierce determination, and finally, blood trickled from between his clenched teeth. His body couldn’t bear it anymore.","“Kind Sir,” the young samanera struggled to utter these words through his clenched teeth. Then, he managed a faint smile and hoarsely continued, “l am going to follow my master’s footsteps. Kind Sir, take care!”","<font <=\"\" div=\"\">","After saying this, the young monk, disregarding his injuries, surged with energy again. Countless cracks appeared on his body, and Xiang Binyun’s eyes trembled violently. He knew this young monk was about to self-destruct.","Whoosh!","Jian Wushuang took a deep breath, drawing in a primordial Qi, and his eyes snapped open.","The moment his eyes opened, his aura began to rise. An ancient and powerful energy radiated from him, it was the power of the Extreme Dao,","Smack!","In a flash, Jian Wushuang was by the young monks side. He lightly patted his shoulder, then with a punch, he sent the blood axe and Xiang Binyun flying.","“Don’t worry, it’s not over yet. Leave the rest to me!” Jian Wushuang comforted softly, then infused his own Yan power into the young samanera’s crumbling divine body.","Golden rays of light bathed the young monk’s deteriorating form. Quickly, they repaired his broken divine body. However, he would need to recover the energy consumed within himself.","“Kind Sir, you can’t!” The young samanera wanted to resist, after all, there were still strong enemies around. How could he let Jian Wushuang help him recover his injuries?","Jian Wushuang smiled faintly. “It’s alright. You stabilize your realm and restore your strength here. I’ll handle him.”","Whoosh!","Jian Wushuang swiftly moved, seizing the moment before Xiang Bingyun could steady himself. With a swift motion, the tattered divine sword on his back was drawn once again.","Clang!","As the divine sword unsheathed, a dazzling light burst forth. Despite its cracked blade, it was infused with the Ultimate Dao, capable of cleaving the heavens with terrifying power, even a tree branch could become a weapon of devastating might under such influence.","Puff!","“How... how dare you!” Xiang Bingyun’s voice trembled as he muttered. Although his body hadn’t yet stabilized, seeing Jian Wushuangs strike, he quickly twisted his form. However, the power in that strike was overwhelming; it tore through his flesh, severing his arm, which now floated silently in the void.","This was not just a physical injury; the previous strike had also contained Heart power. Now, he coughed up brownish blood, his heart sinking. His previously calm state of mind shattered, causing his strength to diminish by a third.","Shaking, Xiang Bingyun coughed violently and wiped the blood from his mouth, his voice trembling. “How could you... How could you recover so quickly? Your divine body was on the verge of breaking, yet you’ve healed in less than an incense stick’s worth of time. Even a second-grade Great Dao wouldn’t allow such swift recovery.”","In his eyes, even if Jian Wushuang was an unparalleled genius from some world, having comprehended a second-grade Great Dao, he couldn’t possibly recover so rapidly.","As per the understanding of Dao from the Ancient Era, similar to Jian Wushuangs analysis, Dao was categorized into five levels. Xiang Bingyun’s mention of the ‘Great Dao’ referred to the second level.","He himself possessed a third-grade Great Dao, bestowed upon him by the former master of the Heavenly Court. Abandoning his initial common Dao, he inherited this third-grade Great Dao. Through his achievements during the","Ancient Era, he ascended to become a Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal, highly valued by the contemporary Heavenly Court. Although the probability of successfully merging dao was small, if he succeeded, he would possess the power of a second-tier Emperor. By controlling a world, he could advance further to become a third-tier Emperor.","This had always been his pursuit. Despite the third-grade Great Dao not being rare in the universe, during the Ancient Era, he was still considered a disciple of a certain sect and had been a stunning genius, admired by many. But now, compared to Jian Wushuang and the young monk, he was just an ordinary Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal with mediocre strength.","Jian Wushuang was a Three Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal, and the young monk was already almost a Nine Revolutions due to his understanding of zen. A Three Revolutions and a Six Revolutions were able to contend with a","Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal for several breaths.","Especially considering Jian Wushuangs current state as a Three Revolutions","Grand Yan Immortal, he was able to injure Xiang Bingyun with a single strike. Although Xiang Bingyun’s strength hadn’t reached its peak at the moment, achieving such remarkable results, not to mention in a certain high-level world, was something that even the Emperor’s sons in some of the superpowers in the universe would find difficult to achieve.","Xiang Bingyun’s state of mind was shattered, and he began to contemplate retreat.","He dared not continue the fight. If that little monks strength fully recovered, he alone might not be a match for these two.","Jian Wushuangs eyes turned ice-cold. His previous strike had completely depleted the Heart power he had just gained. Although Xiang Bingyun’s strength had decreased by a third, in a direct confrontation, he was still not a match.","“It’s my turn to fight you now!” Although he wasn’t a match, he desperately craved that sense of crisis. Only in such perilous situations could he become stronger.","For him, advancing from the Three Revolutions to the Six Revolutions posed no real obstacles. He could sense the Dao. As long as he kept fighting, it wouldn’t be long before he advanced to the Six Revolutions.","At that point, his Thought power and Heart power would also skyrocket.","Heart power was akin to the scabbard of the Ultimate Sword Dao. Nurtured by Heart power, his Ultimate Sword Dao advanced rapidly.","As long as he could become stronger, he would keep fighting!","Life extended infinitely because of battle.","Jian Wushuang stood in the void, his hair rising without wind. His aura kept climbing. At this moment, his mind was as calm as still water, focused only on his thoughts.","“You two are insane!” Xiang Bingyun’s eye twitched incessantly. Not only were these two powerful, but they were also crazily reckless. Was this what true geniuses were like?","It seemed that back in the day, Zhen Wuyang had similarly fought his way through the ancient era and stood out.","“Damn it, I was defeated by Zhen Wuyang back then, and now 1 can’t even kill one of his Princes.” A murderous intent engulfed Xiang Bingyun’s face. The damage to his state of mind had loosened his will, and endless resentment had nowhere to vent.","This was the importance of one’s state of mind. Although most cultivators couldn’t develop Heart power, if they usually maintained a stable state of heart, even without Heart power, they could fear no Heart power cultivator. In their future cultivation, they could calmly face various dangers. This was the benefit of a stable state of heart.."]},{"number":5141,"title":"Chapter 5141: The Emperors Appear","paragraphs":["Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","The state of heart was like the Heart power. It could not be touched or seen by others. It seemed useless, but in reality, it was needed everywhere.","If Xiang Bingyun had a stable state of heart, he wouldn’t have had his mental state shattered by Jian Wushuangs sword, causing his strength to plummet by","30 percent.","Perhaps, this was a flaw in these revived powerhouses; their anger had annihilated their composure.","One was filled with determination, the other contemplating retreat but unwilling to accept it, their positions clearly defined.","<font <=\"\" div=\"\">","Buzz!","Xiang Bingyun couldn’t hold on any longer. In this moment, he recalled Gu","Yuan’s fate and hurriedly struck his own chest, attempting to clear his mind.","“Traitor, how dare you deceive me!” Xiang Bingyun roared in anger, yet his body kept retreating. He genuinely didn’t want to continue this fight.","Moreover, he had been away for too long. This place was close to the Gret Si Region, and with Zhen Wuyangs speed, he could return at any moment.","These two individuals, with such power, must be Princes from some faction. Especially Jian Wushuang, who once exuded Zhen Wuyangs aura, even though it was absent now. But if he was a sitting Prince of Zhen Wuyang, his temperament being what it was, he would undoubtedly notice their absence if he came to the Great Desolate Wilderness. If someone was left alone outside, they would surely perish.","Little did he know that Zhen Wuyang had long arrived in the Great Desolate Wilderness, aware of their situation but utterly indifferent. In Zhen Wuyangs eyes, only absolute strength mattered; Emperors, Heavenly Courts, they were all mere passing clouds.","However, Xiang Bingyun was ignorant of all this, and at this moment, he made up his mind.","“Let’s go!’","Xiang Bingyun retreated and then concealed himself in the void. After a ripple in space, he vanished.","“Gone?” Jian Wushuang was somewhat surprised. Just like that, he left?","Just after Xiang Bingyun left, the space where Jian Wushuang and the others were distorted and changed.","Several majestic figures became faintly visible, then instantly solidified.","In the last moment, these majestic beings were still far from Jian Wushuang and the others. But in an instant, their figures and pressure arrived, followed by their physical bodies.","A wail!","A faint Buddhist chant echoed through the void.","“What’s this?” Jian Wushuang was utterly astonished.","Every one of these majestic beings gave him a unique feeling that was exclusive to Zhen Wuyang. It was the peculiar aura of an Emperor.","So many Emperors?","Jian Wushuang felt uneasy, but his keen intellect made him realize instantly that these beings didn’t come for him. It must be because of that mysterious ancient temple and the revived entity.","But even if that revived being was an Emperor, it shouldn’t have attracted so many Emperors here!","Surprised though he was, Jian Wushuang maintained the necessary respect for the powerful figures around him. He immediately bowed deeply. “Junior, Great Si Region, Jian Wushuang,” he introduced himself, feeling the weight of the gazes from the Emperor-level experts in the room. He continued after taking a breath, “l greet all the Emperor Lords.”","“Virtuous!” The leader of the group was none other than the Heaven-Reaching Lord Buddha.","Heaven-Reaching Buddha’s towering body emitted endless golden fate energy. He looked at Jian Wushuang and said with a faint smile, “Little Virtuous one, there’s no need to be so polite.”","“Thank you, Emperor.” Jian Wushuang had roamed through countless realms and had seen many big scenes. However, this was the first time he had seen so many Emperors.","Emperor Dongyan, who was standing next to the Heaven-Reaching Buddha, did not care about this. He even despised the Heaven-Reaching Buddha for being hypocritical in front of the younger generation. In his opinion, the Heaven-Reaching Buddha loved the so-called etiquette the most. He wanted everyone to worship him.","The little monk, who had regained his senses, also came to his senses. He quickly put his palms together and lowered his head slightly. “Lord Buddha!”","Wulliang Buddha’s eyes were wide open at this moment. He looked at the little monk and said in surprise, “Hu Qing, you’ve comprehended an Ultimate Dao?”","The little monk had lived on Wuliang Mountain since he was young. Although there were hundreds of millions of monks living on the mountain, as the emperor, he knew every single one of the monks living in his Dao arena.","“Yes!” At this moment, the little monk’s expression was calm, and his obsession with Buddhism had faded. Instead, the zen in his heart had allowed him to comprehend the Dao.","“This is extraordinary goodness!” Although Hu Qing belonged to the Wuliang Mountain, in the eyes of the Buddha, he was the holy land of the Buddha realm. Hu Qings comprehension of the Ultimate Dao was a blessing for their Buddhist sect.","“Yes! For how many years, there hasn’t been another who attained the seventh level of the Ultimate Dao within the 3,000 Worlds.” Emperor Dongyan also discerned the profound aura emanating from Hu Qing. It was clearly a certain form of the Ultimate Dao, and it seemed that he had traveled quite far along this path.","Upon careful observation, Wuliang Buddha also noticed the considerable progress Hu Qing had made on the Ultimate Dao.","“Indeed, just as I expected. Impressive,” Wuliang Buddha said, his surface displaying a pleased expression, but deep down, he harbored a hidden threat.","“30 million years, and he has reached the sixth level of the Ultimate Dao.","When Hu Qing returns to the 3,000 Worlds, he can select any Emperor","Supreme Technique from our Wuliang Mountain,” the Heaven-Reaching Buddha praised and then turned to the Wuliang Buddha, saying, “Wuliang, with Hu Qings talent, he can be appointed as an Emperor’s successor.”","Originally a novice monk under the Wuliang Mountain, Hu Qing had received all the compliments from the Heaven-Reaching Buddha. Emperor Dongyan shook his head in amazement. Regardless of whose disciple they were in the 3,000 Worlds, discovering a practitioner who comprehended the Ultimate Dao was cause for celebration.","Emperor Dongyan regarded Hu Qing with a much gentler expression. He could sense that Hu Qings disposition was unlike that of Wuliang or","Heaven-Reaching. Instead, it was an innate quality, one he found increasingly endearing.","As he looked at this young successor, he couldn’t help but think of his own disciple from ages past.","That disciple was his pride and joy. In just a million years, he had attained the seventh level of the Ultimate Dao, becoming the most talented Grand Yan Immortal in the history of the 3,000 Worlds.","A million years, the seventh level of the Ultimate Dao, reaching the peak of the","Perfected Nine Revolutions of cultivation—such accomplishments were unimaginable before. Even Jian Wushuang wouldn’t have dared to assert that he could achieve this in a million years, even with his confidence in mastering the Extreme Dao and Heart power now.","Unfortunately, this genius, who had once captured the imagination of the entire world, succumbed to emotional turmoil. His shattered heart led to an unstable state of heart, rushed attempts at fusion, and ultimately, a failed fusion, which forever denied him the opportunity to advance to the Emperor-level.","Emotions, Dao, both damaged. In the end, he self-destructed, his consciousness utterly annihilated.","Since that incident, Emperor Dongyan had refrained from accepting personal disciples.","Even though the world might have forgotten that disciple’s name, the","Emperor had never forgotten him. He remained in Dongyan’s heart.","“A heavenly miracle.”","The attention of the Emperors was fixed on the young samanera. For the moment, Jian Wushuang was left forgotten. Yet, he didn’t mind.","The others assumed Hu Qing took 30 million years to reach the sixth level of the Ultimate Dao, while Jian Wushuang, a newcomer, had directly stepped into the sixth level of the Ultimate Dao. Although the truth was different, Jian Wushuang chose not to correct their misunderstanding.","“So, this young benefactor saved you, I presume!” Wuliang Buddha said with a smile, looking at Jian Wushuang.","“Yes,” the young samanera Hu Qing replied softly.."]},{"number":5142,"title":"Chapter 5142: Another Heartwood","paragraphs":["Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Jian Wushuang listened carefully, realizing that the little samanera had hidden many details, and now the little samanera was looking at him with a smile in his eyes.","“Junior and Hu Qing supported each other all the way, barely driving away the enemies. It was not my sole achievement.”","Although he had been observing from the sidelines and didn’t know much about the distribution of power in the 3,000 Great Worlds, he could roughly tell that Heaven-Reaching Buddha and Wuliang, despite both being part of Buddha realm, did not belong to the same faction.","And Emperor Dongyan was not a Buddhist practitioner, not someone easy to deal with for both Wuliang and Heaven-Reaching Buddha. This time, they probably came together just for that grand temple.","Being around such powerful figures, he had to be cautious.","<font <=\"\" div=\"\">","“Cause and effect cycle, thoughts are hard to settle!” Wuliang Buddha waved his hand, and a stream of light slid down.","“This item should have some connection with you. Diligently studying it in the future will help your state of heart and mind.”","“Thank you, Senior!”","After clearly seeing the item, Jian Wushuang’s heart trembled. He quickly bowed to express his gratitude.","The treasure in the stream of light was a short piece of wood, perfectly matching the one he had obtained earlier. Could it be?","Jian Wushuang’s heart shook. He now understood that the short piece of wood he received was a gift from Wuliang Buddha. If that was the case, didn’t it mean that Wuliang Buddha knew he was a practitioner of Heart power cultivation? He also must be aware of the existence of the Qishen Temple and little samanera’s original realm.","But he didn’t dare to have any doubts. He wore a surprised expression on his face while hiding his amazement.","“Oh, by the way, the one chasing after you two should be him!” Wuliang Buddha extended his arm and directly grabbed into the void. His arm casually extended for millions of miles, tearing apart the endless void and capturing the escaping Xiang Bingyun.","The Emperors remained very calm, even the little samanera was composed. Only Jian Wushuang was extremely surprised.","There was nothing he could do. He only knew a few Emperors, and the ones he had truly seen were even fewer. He had seen Zhen Wuyang a few times, but it didn’t compare to the awe-inspiring presence of Wuliang Buddha.","“Ah!”","Xiang Bingyun, who was suddenly grabbed from the void, looked astonished. Then, seeing the majestic figures of the Emperors above the void, his eyes widened.","“How is this possible? I was already far away from here. Even if they’re Emperors, they couldn’t have grabbed me from such a distance!” Xiang Bingyun was both shocked and afraid.","He was shocked by the presence of so many Emperors and afraid because he knew these Emperors had come not for him but for his Lord’s grand plan.","“Esteemed Seniors, I am the ruler of the ancient Heavenly Court in the Great Si Region, and my Lord...” Before Xiang Bingyun could finish his words, his throat was crushed by the immense hand of the Wuliang Buddha.","“Dust returns to dust, soil returns to soil,” Wuliang Buddha waved his hand, and countless tiny bone fragments scattered from his palm.","“They should not have appeared in this world!” Wuliang Buddha clasped his hands together, restoring his former compassionate expression.","Emperor Dongyan sneered inwardly, thinking, ‘Revenge is one thing, but if they don’t revive, the secrets of the Qishen Temple might never see the light of day!’","With a wave of his hand, a Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal was lifted into the air. Jian Wushuang was shaken internally but maintained a respectful demeanor.","Such powerful beings could only be looked up to; at any moment, they could extinguish him.","“Both of you wait here for a moment. Later, a Grand Yan Immortal from our","Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm will meet you here,” Wuliang Buddha said.","The Emperors came and left swiftly. As their voices faded away, their imposing figures gradually dissipated until they disappeared completely from Jian Wushuang’s sight.","After several breaths, even the aura of the Emperors vanished from the void. Only then did Jian Wushuang exhale deeply.","The feeling of relief elevated his mood slightly, although the elevation was minuscule.","The injuries on the little monk’s body had mostly healed. He turned to Jian","Wushuang and smiled faintly, “Kind Sir, thank you for earlier.”","“Everyone has their secrets; there’s no need to speak of them,” Jian Wushuang smiled back.","He only wanted to leave the Great Desolate Wilderness, but the path to the Great Si Region was blocked by those corpses and skeletons. Given the imminent battle between the Emperors over there, he couldn’t return for a short while. His only option was to go Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm.","However, after just meeting the high-ranking members of the Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm, his opinion of them was almost nonexistent.","Since the Heaven-Reaching Buddha asked him to wait for such a Grand Yan Immortal, he would wait. He would find an opportunity to leave later.","Now that he had broken through to become a Grand Yan Immortal, he had the ability to travel to other worlds. But the thought of crossing the entire Great Desolate Wilderness, which would take tens of thousands of years, gave him a headache.","Inside the Qishen Temple,","“Hmm, Fenghua, it seems like your High Commander, Xiang Bingyun, has fallen,” Liu Ya, who controlled the Great Desolate Wilderness Heavenly Dao, remarked. Naturally, he was aware of everything happening in the Great Desolate Wilderness. He had sensed Xiang Bingyun’s demise the moment he was killed.","Xiang Bingyun had followed Emperor Fenghua to battle his entire life and had a personality much like Emperor Fenghua’s. Naturally, Emperor Fenghua valued him greatly, thinking he had the potential to become an Emperor. However, now he had fallen just after reviving.","Liu Ya had always been at odds with Emperor Fenghua. Now he couldn’t help but add fuel to the fire, “It seems he was killed while trying to chase down a few Grand Yan Immortals. What a useless waste. He couldn’t even kill those two youngsters and ended up falling himself.”","“You!” Emperor Fenghua was furious, but considering that Liu Ya now controlled the Great Desolate Wilderness, he suppressed his anger and said coldly, “I will avenge him personally. For now, we must consider the bigger picture.”","“Haha, revenge! Do you even know who killed him?” Liu Ya sneered.","“Who else but Zhen Wuyang? Sooner or later, I will kill him and avenge our past disgrace. Have you forgotten how he humiliated you back then?” Emperor Fenghua gritted his teeth.","The other Emperors closed their eyes, contemplating. Upon hearing their conversation, they all sighed.","Who among them hadn’t been humiliated by Zhen Wuyang? Back then, Zhen Wuyang had treated them like stray dogs and expelled them from the Great Si Region.","They had to endure it due to their lack of strength. But who could have imagined that Zhen Wuyang would progress so quickly, advancing from a third-tier Emperor to a fourth-tier Emperor in less than 10,000 years, directly coming to the Great Desolate Wilderness?","In his pursuit of the Qishen Temple’s whereabouts, he humiliated them in every possible way and eventually slaughtered them all in the Great Desolate Wilderness, using their corpses as a path for his cultivation.","“Hmph!”","Liu Ya didn’t want to dwell on the past. Instead, he calmly stated the current situation, “What? People from the Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm have arrived.”","“How did they find out about the Qishen Temple? This shouldn’t be possible!”","“Liu Ya, when did they arrive? How many Emperors came, and what are their strengths?” A series of questions were thrown at him.","The individuals who had been ambitiously planning to inherit the Qishen’s legacy and become the Universe Masters suddenly felt their confidence waver.","Liu Ya looked at them, becoming increasingly convinced that his choice had been right. He had the foresight to cultivate the Desolate Dao from the moment he was suppressed. When he recovered, he had even revived the Great Desolate Wilderness’s Heavenly Dao.."]},{"number":5143,"title":"Chapter 5143: Fighting Against Foreign Enemies Together","paragraphs":["Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Since the Ancient Era, he had felt that everyone’s state of mind had undergone a huge change.","They were reaching for the unreachable, their ambitions soaring high. Such was the opinion of Liu Ya towards these individuals. The Qishen Temple had bestowed upon them a Divine Dao, making them excessively proud.","In the Ancient Era, they could have shared their knowledge with Zhen Wuyang. If only they had joined forces with Zhen Wuyang to explore the Qishen Temple, they might not have met their downfall and fallen into the state they were in now.","When they saw Zhen Wuyang’s potential, they were afraid that Zhen Wuyang would take advantage of them, so they sealed the Qishen Temple and refused to hand it over even if they died.","Zhen Wuyang was so angry that he went crazy and searched for the","<font <=\"\" div=\"\">","Disambiguation God Temple in the Grand Priest Domain. Then, he killed all of them in the great desolate.","Greed, arrogance, jealousy.","With such a temperament, how could they inherit Qishen’s Dao’s Devouring Dao?","The strongest among them was only at the eighth level, and his strength was around the fourth-tier. Qishen’s Dao was endless, and even if he cultivated to the tenth level, he might not be able to control the universe and become a Universe Master.","He might as well settle for the next best thing and study the Dao of the Three Divine Lords.","Now that he had entered the eighth level of the Desolate Dao and controlled the vast Great Desolate Wilderness, he already had the strength of a fourth-tier Emperoor.","is understanding of the Desolate Dao was not inferior to those who practiced the Qishen Dao. Since he gained control over the Great Desolate Wilderness, his insights into the Desolate Dao deepened. It wouldn’t be long before he reached the ninth level of the Desolate Dao. Once he elevated the Great Desolate Wilderness to a high-grade world, he would step into fifth-tier, dominating the entire universe.","The more powerful he was, the more generous the rewards from the Qishen Temple would be. Although he had inherited the Dao of the Three Divine Lords, the rewards would be relatively lesser, but how much less could it be?","Liu Ya caressed his left arm.","This was a gift that he had received after he increased his strength in controlling the Great Desolate Wilderness. It was an arm.","He didn’t know if this arm was the severed arm of that mighty figure, but it had already surpassed the power of a supreme treasure without being refined. Ever since it had been taken over by him, its power had increased by several times. Even now, he had absolute confidence in facing Zhen Wuyang.","As for the many Emperors in the hall, each one was his equal.","Over millions of years, these 18 Emperors included 5 with the power of third-tier and 11 with second-tier. Then there was Daogong, who could rival Zhen Wuyang in the Ancient Era. If Daogong hadn’t possessed third-tier power back then, Zhen Wuyang wouldn’t have needed to banish them to the Great Desolate Wilderness; he could have annihilated them within the Great Si Region.","Unfortunately, Daogong’s strength did not break through again until his death. After this revival, his strength barely reached the level of fourth-tier, so he could not threaten Zhen Wuyang at all.","“Everyone, I’ve said before that I will protect the Qishen Temple, and this is where you all come in.”","Liu Ya scanned the entire hall and continued, “But there’s one thing you all need to understand: power speaks in this world.”","“With numerous Emperors arriving in the Great Desolate Wilderness, not only from the Buddhist Realm but also from other major worlds, some of these powerful beings are no weaker than Zhen Wuyang!”","Daogong, who had always occupied the seat of honor in the hall, opened his eyes at this moment and spoke, “Liu Ya, just say what you want to say!”","“Yes, speak your mind! We have accumulated millions of years, and our strength has improved. Combined with the blessings of the Qishen Temple, we are no longer what we used to be.”","Back then, they had feigned death in the Great Desolate Wilderness, pouring the blood of millions of Grand Yan Immortals along with their own into the","Qishen Temple. Their purpose was to activate the power of the Qishen Temple. However, no one had expected that it would take millions of years before the Qishen Temple reciprocated their efforts.","Their consciousness had been trapped within the Qishen Temple for millions of years, persevering in the cultivation of the Qishen Dao. Naturally, their strength had greatly increased. They also obtained numerous treasures from the sacrificial altar of the Qishen Temple. Although many Emperors had arrived now, it was not as dire as the time during the Ancient Era, where they had no power to resist.","“Alright, let me be clear. I now control the Great Desolate Wilderness. Are there any objections if we make this our battleground?”","“Naturally!” everyone nodded.","“If we engage in battle, all of you will follow my command. Is that acceptable?”","At these words, the atmosphere in the hall grew tense, and everyone fell silent.","“Liu Ya, don’t go too far. We all inherit the Divine Dao of the Qishen Temple. Although you are the newly appointed Divine Lord, you don’t have the authority to command us!”","It was Emperor Fenghua who spoke up. He could tolerate Liu Ya in many matters, but what he couldn’t tolerate was being overshadowed by Liu Ya. Ever since inheriting the Qishen Dao, they no longer needed to look up to Zhen Wuyang. If they could bow to Liu Ya, they would have done so long ago, and there would be no need for Liu Ya to act like this.","“Everyone, don’t you understand yet?” Liu Ya didn’t adopt a harsh tone this time. He knew these people’s temperaments well. The more aggressive he was, the more they resisted.","Being aggressive wouldn’t work; persuasion was the key.","“That scoundrel Zhen Wuyang probably has revealed the existence of the Qishen Temple to the entire original universe. By revealed, I mean everyone in the entire universe knows. It’s very likely that in the near future, even the powerful beings from different universes will know about the Qishen Temple.”","Liu Ya took a deep breath and continued, “Even terrifying entities from the","River of Time and Space will come to the original universe because of the Qishen Temple. Let alone in the distant future, just look at now. In the Great Desolate Wilderness alone, I’ve sensed 5 fourth-tier Emperors within less than a day.”","“5 fourth-tier Emperors!” Everyone gasped.","They had originally thought it was just Zhen Wuyang alone, perhaps with a few Emperors from the Buddhist Realm.","“The Buddhists from the Buddhist Realm, Zhen Wuyang from the Grand Domain, and two unfamiliar faces. Besides these 4 Emperors, there are 7 third-tier Emperors and 16 second-tier Emperors. Let’s not even mention the levels below second-tier...”","Liu Ya resumed his seat on the throne and concluded, “I don’t mind, because this is the Great Desolate Wilderness, filled with endless corpses. As long as I gather them into one entity, they can’t harm me. I will guard the Qishen Temple. But if you think you can preserve your lives here, I won’t interfere either.”","The Qishen Temple was divided into inner and outer halls. They could only communicate with the inner hall through the sacrificial altar. The power they wielded in the outer hall wasn’t significant. Otherwise, they wouldn’t have been suppressed by Zhen Wuyang back in the day.","Now that Liu Ya had become a Dao Ancestor, controlling the Great Desolate","Wilderness, he wasn’t afraid of those foreign Emperors. However, they weren’t Dao Ancestors; the strongest among them were only ordinary fourth-tier Emperors. They had nowhere to hide now; it was too late to escape.","“Damn that Zhen Wuyang. Isn’t he afraid that the Qishen Temple might fall into the hands of those Universe Masters?”","“He’s despicable, truly low. Right now, he can’t defeat us alone, but what if he brings in a large group of Emperors?”","“He hasn’t changed a bit.”","“Just as shameless as before!”","“Everyone, now we need to unite and resist the external enemies together.” Daogong stood up. He understood Liu Ya’ intentions. Although he knew they would suffer losses, he had no choice but to stand up now.."]},{"number":5144,"title":"Chapter 5144: Discussion","paragraphs":["Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","In the depths of the vast Great Desolate Wilderness.","The first batch of major factions that entered the vast Great Desolate Wilderness gradually gathered together.","“Zhen Wuyang, how much do you know about the information from the Qishen Temple?” A majestic figure in golden armor, exuding an aura of arrogance, looked at Zhen Wuyang.","“Donglin Divine Emperor, the information I know about the Qishen Temple is just that much. I have already transmitted everything I know to you.” Zhen","Wuyang smiled faintly, sitting cross-legged in the void, calm and composed.","<font <=\"\" div=\"\">","“Humph, don’t take us for fools. The Qishen Temple drifted here through the River of Time and Space. Who knows what mysteries it holds inside? You are so generous in spreading the news about the emergence of the Qishen Temple. Do you want us to lead the way for you?” The golden-armored Emperor glared at Zhen Wuyang. He was the only supreme Ruler among many surrounding worlds, controlling higher worlds. How could he act as a pawn for Zhen Wuyang?","The Emperors of the Heaven -Reaching Buddhist Realm also appeared around Zhen Wuyang. The Heaven-Reaching Buddha had long known about the strange movements of the Great Desolate Wilderness. When Zhen Wuyang spread the news that the Qishen Temple had appeared, he immediately brought all the Emperors and many Grand Yan Immortals over.","“Brother Zhen, the matter of the Qishen Temple is of great importance. Since we are willing to cross numerous Celestial Realms to come here, you should give us some respect!” Emperor Dongyan spoke first, paying no attention to the leading role played by Heaven -Reaching Buddha.","“I’ve said it before, I only know this much. If you’re afraid, then don’t go. Go back and comprehend the Great Dao. I wish you an early ascent to the pinnacle of the universe.” Zhen Wuyang sneered.","He didn’t dare to take on any danger and only dreamed about the Great Dao of the Universe!","He had spread the news from the Qishen Temple in order to attract the attention of the experts from all over the world and then fish in troubled waters. At this moment, these people wanted an explanation from him. They simply wanted him to be the first to attack.","To be able to become the ruler of a large force, how could he be a reckless person? If he was, he would have been killed long ago.","The Qishen Temple contained secrets that could make one the Universe Master. How could it be safe? Just the 18 divine generals within were comparable to a major force.","“Zhen Wuyang, don’t underestimate us. We came because we trust you. If you’re unwilling to share the information about the Qishen Temple, don’t blame us for being impolite.” The golden-armored Emperor threatened, “I heard that your Great Si Region has expanded to its limit. I wonder if it has caught up with my Donglin Realm.”","As soon as the words of the golden-armored Emperor fell, a terrifying aura erupted instantly. A golden dragon shot out from his palm, its body moving at an incredible speed.","The power of an Emperor could easily shatter the void in the Great Desolate Wilderness. This terrifying dragon, the moment it appeared, treated the void as if it were nothing, directly rushing towards the Great Si Region.","Although the Grand Si Region had expanded to its limit, the Great Desolate Wilderness was not considered large. Because the origin had already collapsed during the Ancient Era, it was difficult to expand the land. Even if Zhen","Wuyang was powerful, he could only open up this Great Desolate Wilderness. If the Great Si Region advanced further, he could only improve his own Great Dao.","The higher the level of the Great Dao, the stronger the world he could control. Zhen Wuyang had been opening up the realm to the limit, which was equivalent to the Great Dao reaching the limit. If it were not for the cancer of the Great Desolate Wilderness, he would have long raised the Great Si Region to the peak of a medium-grade world.","Now that the Emperor in golden armor was using a flood dragon to spy on his Great Si Region, how could he agree? Even if he couldn’t spy on anything, the might of an Emperor would allow the flood dragon to enter the Great Si Region and destroy countless smaller worlds, depleting the prime essences of the Great Si Region","“I don’t even care about the Donglin Realm, and you’re not going to instruct me about my own Great Si Region!” Zhen Wuyang said coldly.","Great Si Region, Heavenly Court.","Zhen Wuyang’s true form appeared, gazing toward the Great Desolate Wilderness, pointing into the void.","Buzz! Buzz!","A muffled explosion echoed deep into the Great Desolate Wilderness. The flood dragon stranded at the edge of the Great Desolate Wilderness before reaching the borders of the Great Si Region. The once lively golden dragon now resembled a motionless image in the void.","The Emperor in golden armor snorted, attempting to retract his divine technique, but he couldn’t call back the golden flood dragon. He tore apart the void with his massive hands, trying to grab the dragon, but it eluded his grasp. The dragon seemed etched into the void, swaying gently with the air but not advancing an inch.","At this moment, Zhen Wuyang rose slowly. With a wave of his hand, the golden Jiaolong was cut from the cracks in the void, which then sealed back up.","“Donglin, don’t think that mastering a high-grade world gives you the right to be arrogant in my presence. I have slain Emperors far more than your Donglin","Realm.”","Crack!","Zhen Wuyang directly crushed the flood dragon into powder.","The supreme treasure shattered in Zhen Wuyang’s hands, scattered casually in the void.","“You!” Emperor Donglin glared in anger. But Zhen Wuyang’s strength was indeed formidable. In his own Dao Arena, they would not fear, but now they were in the Great Desolate Wilderness. Though it wasn’t Zhen Wuyang’s Dao Arena, if a conflict arose, they had no means against Zhen Wuyang’s might.","Moreover, he had several Emperors from the Donglin Realm behind him. Their strength was only at the second-tier Emperor level. If they clashed with Zhen Wuyang, he could easily kill them. That would be a huge loss for them.","Their main goal was the Qishen Temple. There was no need to confront Zhen Wuyang head – on.","“Donglin, this is the Great Desolate Wilderness. Though a Dao Ancestor is here now, this Earth Realm is jointly managed by the Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm and the Great Si Region. Don’t cause trouble, or else...” He finished, nodding meaningfully at Zhen Wuyang.","Heaven-Reaching Buddha thought the situation wasn’t significant enough, so they directly sided with Zhen Wuyang. Their implication was clear: if Zhen Wuyang acted, they would support him. They were on the same boat.","But how could Zhen Wuyang not understand the character of this neighbor Heaven-Reaching Buddha? By aligning himself with Zhen Wuyang at this moment, he implied that the vast Great Desolate Wilderness was jointly managed by both their realms, but it was subtly suggesting ownership of the Qishen Temple.","Zhen Wuyang felt a headache. These Emperors had survived till now, becoming formidable existences in the universe. They wouldn’t charge straight to the Qishen God just because of a simple message. This was an oversight he had made.","“I’ve overlooked something. But regarding the specific situation inside the Qishen Temple, I know very little. It’s right there; if you’re willing to explore together, let’s go. But if you’re hesitant and want to take advantage of numbers, trying to fish in troubled waters, you can leave now,” Zhen Wuyang said clearly. He knew that if he didn’t take these people to Qishen Temple now, more Emperors would come later, asking him the same thing. It was better to bring them along and try their luck now.","Heaven-Reaching Lord Buddha joined his palms, smiling gently. “Virtuous!”","Numerous Emperors dispersed into the air and reappeared at the road of Immortal bones where Jian Wushuang was desperately trying to escape.","The towering temple reached billions of miles into the sky, its bronze-colored surface imbued with elusive and powerful runes, constantly suppressing the void.","Swish! Swish! Swish! Swish!","Dozens of figures appeared outside the Qishen Temple. It was Zhen Wuyang and his group.."]},{"number":5145,"title":"Chapter 5145: Battle of the Emperors","paragraphs":["Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","“Daogong, Liu Ya, Fenghua.” Zhen Wuyang appeared ordinary among the group of Emperors, but his words were exceptionally domineering.","“I have come specifically to pay respects to you Seniors.”","Although he said it was a greeting, he brought a large group of Emperors, making it impossible to move in the Qishen Temple hall.","“Dong Yan, your Yan Divine Array can be set up now,” Zhen Wuyang said, turning his head and smiling.","He had just said he came to pay respects, but he turned around and had Dong Yan set up the array. Zhen Wuyang’s shamelessness embarrassed the Emperors who saw him for the first time.","<font <=\"\" div=\"\">","Indeed, he was a formidable presence that could destroy the entire Great Si Region during that proud Ancient Era.","He had been ruthless when annihilating his own people in the past. Now, cooperating with him, Emperor Donglin sighed inwardly, unsure if it was good or bad.","The Yan Divine Array was created by Emperor Dong Yan himself. It had a great reputation in the surrounding domains. Once the array was formed, even Emperors couldn’t teleport through the void.","Buzz!","“Array formation, rise!” Emperor Dong Yan waved the flag, and a diagram comparable to a small world descended from the sky, suppressing a third of the void in the Great Desolate Wilderness.","After the large array was set up, Zhen Wuyang’s concerns dissipated. At least those old fellows from the Ancient Era couldn’t escape now.","Besides the Yan Divine Array guarding, Heaven-Reaching Buddha also took out the precious Thousand Treasures Kasaya.","Everything outside was clear to the Emperors inside the Qishen Temple. They weren’t idle either, immediately activating the power of the Qishen Temple.","Everything outside was clear to the Emperors inside the Qishen Temple. They weren’t idle either, immediately activating the power of the Qishen Temple.","Boom!","The Yan Divine Array buzzed in the void. Every component of the huge diagram accelerated its rotation. Although the power of the Qishen Temple was strong, those Emperors couldn’t fully unleash their power. Relying on the Qishen Temple, they could only barely contend with many Emperors.","“Liu Ya, get ready to attack!” Daogong shouted angrily. His figure appeared outside the main gate of the Qishen Temple, and an ancient and majestic aura rose into the sky.","The runes outside the Qishen Temple lit up instantly. Daogong’s eyes were dazzling as he rushed toward Dong Yan inside the Yan Divine Array.","The countless corpses surrounding the hall, acting as the outermost defense, turned into powder when a divine force swept over them. They floated toward the Qishen Temple along the ancient road of Immortal bones.","The two Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortals, the Shadow Demons, guarding outside the temple suddenly opened their eyes.","They had been waiting for this moment for too long. This was their Lord, Liu Ya, summoning them.","“Set up the formation!” Liu Ya’s eyes flickered. He gently pressed his left hand, and his blood-red arm suddenly burst with power. This force stirred millions of Grand Yan Immortals.","Swish! Swish! Swish!","“Welcome, My Lord!”","36 Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortals appeared instantly behind Liu Ya. These Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortals used the corpses of billions of Grand Yan Immortals as their bodies, and the endless","Grand Yan Immortals ultimately transformed into the flesh and blood of these 36 experts.","At this point, they had surpassed the realm of Grand Yan Immortals. Each of them possessed the aura of an Emperor, but the Dao within their bodies had withered when they condensed their flesh and blood. Now, they were all like living dead.","“Activate the formation!” Liu Ya roared again.","The grand formation rose, and a colossal figure the size of the Qishen Temple appeared outside the Qishen Temple. This was the dead spirit formation set up by Liu Ya.","Liu Ya obtained this formation from inside the Qi God Temple. During the ancient times, he pursued the Qi God Dao wholeheartedly but never practiced it. It wasn’t until True Martial Yang rose that he bezan practicinz. He didn’t hesitate to let billions of Great Yan Immortals accompany him in death just to perfect this formation. Now, the revived Great Yan Immortals were becoming a part of him, ready to battle for him.","“Daogong, quickly kill Dong Yan and break the formation. The rest of you, suppress Heaven-Reaching Buddha together. Leave the rest to me.” Liu Ya directed the entire dead spirit formation. The human-shaped figures formed by the formation also bore his appearance.","Boom!","Daogong, who had cultivated the Qishen Dao to the eighth level, was indeed fast. Even though the void was sealed, his speed was much faster than Emperor Dong Yan’s. In an instant, he arrived at the location of Dong Yan within the formation.","The formation blockade worked both ways. Dong Yan himself couldn’t use instant teleportation; he had to rely on the large formation at the formation’s core and confront Daogong head-on.","“I heard you were the leader of the Great Si Region during the Ancient Era. Today, I will properly face you.” Although Dong Yan’s strength hadn’t reached the tier 4, he had the defense of the core formation. Against an old guy who had just entered tier 4, he had some confidence.","“I happen to want to meet you, these foreign realm experts, too. Let’s see if your Dao is stronger or mine.” As soon as Daogong finished speaking, he attacked directly.","Once the leader during the Ancient Era, Daogong was already a tier 3 Emperor back then. Now, he had advanced further to become a tier 4 Emperor and received blessings from Qishen. His strength was comparable to Zhen Wuyang of the ancient times.","The current Emperor Dong Yan didn’t pose a threat to him.","A whisk appeared in Daogong’s hand. With a gentle wave, countless white feathers surrounded the entire core formation, then suddenly tightened.","The pressure from the whisk felt like a giant’s palm, but Dong Yan at the formation’s core remained calm and held onto the core formation tightly.","Under the immense pressure, the core formation’s operation sped up rapidly.","“This won’t last much longer if it continues like this,” Dong Yan exclaimed in horror and quickly transmitted a message to Heaven-Reaching Buddha, “Dao Gong is of the fourth tier. I can’t hold on. Quickly have Feng MO save me.”","Heaven-Reaching Buddha, Zhen Wuyang, Donglin Divine Emperor, and Feng MO, four tier 4 Emperors.","16 Palace-Protecting Divine Generals suppressed Heaven-Reaching Buddha in the Qishen Temple. Although it was said to be a suppression, they were actually keeping an eye on him. It was best for both sides not to make a move and wait for others to determine the outcome.","In the current Qishen Temple, Liu Ya, the strongest figure, resisted 3 fourth-tier Emperors alone.","After all, the Great Desolate Wilderness was Liu Ya’s Dao Arena. While Feng MO was powerful, he had just entered the fourth tier and wasn’t as strong as Daogong. Only Zhen Wuyang’s strength was formidable enough to contend with him.","As for Donglin Divine Emperor, he guarded the rear and protected many ordinary Emperors. In battles at this level, those ordinary Emperors couldn’t even intervene. They became burdens instead, wasting the power of a fourth-tier Emperor for nothing.","With the power from the Dao Arena and the Dead Spirit Formation, Liu Ya now had the strength of an excellent tier 4 Emperor. No matter how strong Zhen Wuyang was, he couldn’t gain any advantage from Liu Ya.","“Zhen Wuyang, I originally thought you would come to the Great Desolate Wilderness alone, but I didn’t expect you to bring so many helpers. You truly disappoint me!” Liu Ya said as he attacked.","Enormous fist shadows fell like shooting stars, bombarding Emperor Feng Mo.","Meanwhile, Zhen Wuyang mainly targeted the weakest link. This was his Dao Arena; the more he fought, the stronger he would become. He could mobilize the Great Desolate Wilderness’s Heavenly Dao. He was the Dao Ancestor of this world. Although it was only a middle-grade world, the power it bestowed upon him could still shatter Feng MO’s divine body.."]},{"number":5146,"title":"Chapter 5146: Emperor’s Fall","paragraphs":["Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","“Damn it!” Zhen Wuyang cursed angrily. The current situation was far from favorable for them. Dongyan was on the verge of collapse, and Feng MO on this side was struggling to lift its head. He couldn’t unleash his true strength in such a short time.","This was Liu Ya’s Dao Arena. While fighting against Liu Ya here, he was constantly rejected by the Dao of the Great Desolate Wilderness, suppressing his power by 30 percent.","Meanwhile, Heaven-Reaching Buddha sat above, calm and composed. The power of the Thousand Treasures Kasaya was enough to rival 16 Divine Generals.","There were only a few among them who were at the middle tier 3. If it were not for the Qishen Hall, Heaven-Reaching Buddha would have killed them in an instant.","“Wuliang, Dongyan is in dire straits. Hurry and send reinforcements,” Heaven-Reaching Buddha said calmly, still leisurely allowing Wuliang, a tier 3 Emperor, to deal with the tier 4 Emperor Daogong.","<font <=\"\" div=\"\">","The allure of the Qishen Temple was immense. Just a few pieces of information from Zhen Wuyang were enough to throw the entire original universe into chaos. They were only the first batch; he had never thought of breaking the Qishen Temple now. He would wait until everyone gathered and then explore the temple together.","From the initial stage of the original universe, he had come to the Qishen Temple in the Great Si Region. It was not that simple. There was probably someone behind all of this.","Even though he guarded the Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm all year round, he was well-informed. The tier 5 Emperors had all left the original universe for the River of Time and Space. There was an even greater secret within. The origin of the original universe had started to dissipate when it was born, and now, countless chaos cycles had passed, and the origin was almost depleted.","Inside the Primitive Universe was a powerful being, the Forbidden Demon Lord, who had once dominated the River of Time and Space. If the origin were depleted, and the Forbidden Demon Lord emerged, the original universe would have no choice but to migrate.","The Forbidden Demon Lord was a powerful life form born from the River of Time and Space. It appeared in every cycle of time. In the previous cycle, it appeared in their original universe, swallowing the entire universe. The Forbidden Creature was suppressed to the core of the original universe by the Supreme Rules.","This information was known to very few, only a few tier 5 Emperors and a handful of tier 4 Rulers were aware of it.","The being who created the Buddhist Sect left the original universe after the fragmentation of the Celestial Realm. When he left, he left behind this Cycle Reincarnation Scripture.","That being deduced the future, used the Eye of Heavenly Mechanics to see the future of the original universe. In the future, the original universe was a","traceless starry sky. The entire universe was devoured by the Forbidden Creature, and the Emperors in the universe fled with the Great Yan Immortals. All other life was obliterated.","Even with foresight of the future, that being left the original universe. For that being, this universe would soon perish, not worth staying here.","The Forbidden Creatures were terrifying existences that all experts feared in the River of Time and Space.","For a universe without a master, it represented destruction.","Now, with the sudden appearance of the Qishen Temple, could it be a chance bestowed by the supreme rules, allowing the original universe to overcome this calamity?","Tongtian Buddha pondered this, his gaze sweeping over the many emperors in the Qishen Temple, then shifting to Daogong and Liuyan.","In the end, he shook his head.","Among this group, none were saviors.","What Tongtian Buddha didn’t know was that the Buddhist leader who foresaw the future in those years was eventually killed by the supreme rules and then reincarnated.","Fate was shackled, and the supreme rules left a glimmer of vitality.","Eventually, the Qishen Temple drifted through countless cycles in the river of time and arrived in the original universe.","This grand gift was a chance given by the supreme rules to the original universe. If grasped, it could give birth to a universe master in this era. If not, be prepared to escape!","The slim chance left by the supreme rules, apart from a universe master, no one could drive away that forbidden devil lord. Thus, there was a great possibility of a universe master emerging in this era.","Tongtian Buddha, who had comprehended all this, squinted his eyes. In his view, among all the people present, only Zhen Wuyang had a slight chance. No matter how he looked at others, they were not beings destined to achieve the great path.","Everything had its predestined outcome!","The Qishen Temple would definitely not leave the original universe, so there was no need for him to stay above.","But watching the tigers fight from above was leisurely for him. As for the small fry below, the more deaths, the better, saving him from dealing with those opportunistic fellows.","The many Emperors outside the Qishen Temple, under the protection of Donglin, could only watch a few fourth-tier Emperors battle. He never imagined that in the current great war, even third-tier Emperors couldn’t intervene.","As for Heaven-Reaching Buddha’s words about rescuing Emperor Dongyan, they pretended not to hear. Who would be foolish enough to battle a fourth-tier Emperor now?","Even though Daogong was at the bottom among the fourth-tier Emperors, those at the third-tier were far from being his match.","Liu Ya, as the Dao Ancestor of the Great Desolate Wilderness, had been watching closely. Not only did he single-handedly bring Feng MO to the brink of collapse, but he also had the energy to deal with Zhen Wuyang. If they dared to show themselves, they would probably be instantly killed by Liu Ya.","In the distance, Emperor Dongyan couldn’t hold on any longer. The power of the whisk seemed limitless, steadily rising. At first, he was relaxed, but as time passed, the force of the whisk grew, compressing his own strength bit by bit. In this contest, he quickly couldn’t endure it anymore. The defensive formation around the eye of the array began to shatter. Without the protection of the formation, he couldn’t hold out against Daogong for more than a few breaths.","The Yan Divine Array had nine eyes of the array, and he was hiding in one of them. However, the Great Desolate Wilderness indeed had Dao Ancestors, and Liu Ya directly found his position. He ordered Daogong to kill him. Once he died, the other eyes of the array would naturally be easily destroyed.","Emperor Dongyan now regretted not breaking the Whisk Array himself. Then, he could have used instant movement to escape.","“Ah! Ah! Ah!” Endless pressure enveloped his body. Emperor Dongyan couldn’t hold on any longer. He never expected that he would be trapped by his own formation, creating his own tomb.","Boom!","The eye of the array’s defensive formation was shattered, and Emperor Dongyan’s true body was revealed. Just as he was about to beg for mercy, he was enveloped entirely by the whisk.","“Those who spy on the Qishen Temple, die!” Daogong shouted angrily.","The power of the Feather Duster surged again. Without defensive formations, Emperor Dongyan was like thin paper, instantly crushed.","This was the difference in strength!","Although Dongyan was a top third-tier power, facing a fourth-tier Emperor, even Daogong, who was at the bottom of the fourth-tier, had no difficulty defeating him.","Fighting above one’s tier might happen in the realm of Grand Yan Immortals, but it absolutely did not occur among Emperors.","In the realm of Grand Yan Immortals, there might be instances of fighting above one’s tier due to some external treasures. However, after becoming Emperors, their strength relied on their comprehension of the Dao.","Those who could fight above their tier among Emperors were unheard of in the original universe.","Perhaps the ancestors of the Ancient God Clan could achieve this, but that old fellow became a fourth-tier Emperor the moment he became an Emperor. At that time, the original universe didn’t even have fifth-tier emperors.."]},{"number":5147,"title":"Chapter 5147: Talk?","paragraphs":["Translator: Endless?antasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","With a reluctant roar, Emperor Dongyan fell completely.","This being, one of the top three in the 3,000 Great Worlds, had fallen. Emperor Dongyan followed the Yan Transformation Dao, and he was not inclined towards battle, and therefoore lacked avatars. This time, his fall was genuine.","In the Buddhist Realm, due to their shared celestial origins, Dongyan’s knowledge of tier 4 Emperors was limited.","The original universe was vast, yet tier 3 Emperors were still scarce. Now, within the time it takes for a joss stick to burn, one had fallen.","The emergence of the Qishen Temple marked the beginning of a great era. This era would become a pivotal point for the entire original universe.","<font <=\"\" div=\"\">","“Virtuous! ”","Tongtian Buddha clasped his hands together, chanting silently, guiding Dongyan’s departed soul.","“Daogong, hurry and break the formation,” Liu Ya urged, suppressing his inner agitation!","Once the formation broke, he would unleash a massacre, channeling the accumulated rage of millions of years. He aimed to turn the Great Desolate","Wilderness into a battlefield, slaughtering all those who dared to spy on the","Qishen Temple.","A majestic Dao descended from the heavens, the fall of an Emperor enhancing his Dead Spirit Formation.","If he suppressed a tier 4 Emperor, his power would increase.","Liu Ya clenched his left hand into the void, and a wave of Death Qi instantly pervaded the entire space.","Feng MO, who had been constantly oppressed, seemed to be afraid. Without waiting for Daogong to break the formation, he shattered the Yan Divine Array himself.","He wanted to escape!","Zhen Wuyang is useless, he couldn’t stop Liu Ya! Tongtian Buddha emained inactive in the void above, and Donglin went to protect those useless beings, refusing to act. Liu Ya now began to suspect if this group had conspired against him.","“Feng MO, don’t!” Zhen Wuyang shouted angrily. Once the formation broke, their deaths would come faster. If the void was unsealed, not only could they teleport, but Liu Ya could too!","“What a fool!” Zhen muttered under his breath. The situation was beyond salvage now. He didn’t care if he faced this alone, but the others would suffer. The Buddhist Realm had deployed all its forces, and now that Dongyan had fallen, even more might perish soon.","Donglin felt a twitch in his eyelids. If he didn’t act now, the subordinates he brought with him might all die in the Great Desolate Wilderness.","At this moment, he had no choice but to take action!","“Liu Ya, your opponent is me!” Donglin, flashed a purple light in his forehead, and six purple rhombus- shaped crystals appeared behind him.","Whoosh!","A massive white stone throne appeared beneath Donglin, stabilizing him. The purple rhombus- shaped crystals instantly flew into the divine throne.","This he obtained from a relic in the River of Time and Space, a Purple Crystal Throne left behind by an ancient civilization.","Boom!","A violet light shot out from above the throne, so swift that the Liu Ya had no chance to resist. The purple light pierced through the Dead Spirit Formation controlled by Liu Ya. Relentless, it created six holes exuding deathly aura on the necromantic formation.","Even the body condensed by the countless Grand Yan Immortals was instantly shattered by the violet light. Liu Ya was momentarily stunned, but with his endless vital energy, it meant nothing. The holes were instantly sealed, and he moved even faster. Before Feng MO could teleport, Liu Ya grabbed him.","“Feng MO, where do you think you’re going?” Liu Ya sneered and then exerted force.","Whoosh!","Feng MO, caught by him, turned into a black smoke and disappeared.","“What is this?” Liu Ya was astonished. The Great Desolate Wilderness was his territory; yet, Feng MO managed to switch bodies right under his nose. The entity he had captured was just an energy clone.","Realizing he had been tricked, Liu Ya roared in anger and vanished from the spot. He had lost the time to pursue Feng MO, whom he had momentarily stunned. Now he had to deal with the weaker Emperors.","“Scatter and escape!” Donglin roared.","He had the most followers, but most of the Emperors from the Buddhistic Realms had duplicates. If they died, they would lose at most a physical body and some treasures. His subordinates didn’t have many duplicates; if they died, they were truly gone.","Donglin Realm was one of the rare high- grade worlds, but its heritage wasn’t as strong as other high-grade worlds. He was the only fourth-tier Emperor in the Donglin Realm, and he had only a few third-tier Emperors under him. Originally, when the Qishen Temple appeared, he didn’t want to bring too many Emperors with him. But these Emperors were eager to advance further; he couldn’t stop them.","After all, before the Great Dao, the strong would always contend!","In such a great opportunity, who would give up?","Who would abandon it because of danger? If they feared death, they would not have stood out among the countless experts of the Grand Yan Immortal stage.","“No one can escape!” The figure of Liu Ya appeared behind many Emperors, and a death scythe appeared in his hand.","Swish!","Even teleportation required a brief moment in the world. In this extremely short time, Liu Ya swung the scythe in his hand, and several Emperors instantly fell.","Some quick-witted Emperors left only half of their bodies; the other halves appeared in another place in the vast Great Desolate Wilderness.","The scythe of annihilation emitted a desolate aura; anything it touched would be devoured of life.","The Emperors whose heads were severed screamed and fell amidst their lamentation and unwillingness.","Niany remaining Emperors had already teleported away. The Emperors of the Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm had no choice but to hide within the Thousand Treasures Kasaya.","Wuliang Buddha cast a final glance at the Qishen Temple and then disappeared within the Thousand Treasures Kasaya.","He had fought against Tongtian Buddha for countless years. Now he understood that if Tongtian wanted him dead, he would have died long ago.","The eyes of the Emperor Donglin were bloodshot. Among the fallen Emperors were his disciples and clan members; they were all dead now.","Daogong, who had already distanced himself, stood in his way. Donglin couldn’t save the others even if he wanted to.","“Don’t even think about attacking; it’s better for both of us this way!” Daogong squinted his eyes and sneered.","They had won this great battle decisively!","Tongtian Buddha above the void descended slowly and came before everyone.","“Let’s talk!” Tongtian Buddha put away the Thousand Treasures Kasaya surrounding the Qishen Temple and smiled faintly.","“Talk?” Daogong also squinted his eyes.","“Yes, talk!” Tongtian Buddha’s voice was firm. Zhen Wuyang stood at the outermost periphery.","Talk?","If there was something to talk about, these old folks wouldn’t be dead. Even if they wanted to talk and settle things, they wouldn’t talk to him.","The grudges were too deep; there was no room for negotiation anymore.","“State your conditions!” Daogong said casually!","At this moment, with the reversal of the offensive, the negotiating power was in his hands.","Although Liu Ya was the strongest force and the Dao Ancestor of this realm, the Emperors in the Qishen Temple had pushed Daogong forward to represent them. Now, Liu Ya could only stand aside and let Daogong negotiate.","Tongtian Buddha glanced at Zhen Wuyang in the distance and then looked at Donglin.","“Let’s deal with him first!” Tongtian Buddha’s face carried a smile, and he pointed lightly.","Emperor Donglin’s face turned pale, and then he became furious. “Tongtian have you gone mad? Are you teaming up with them to attack me?” Even in the distance, Zhen Wuyang was stunned. He thought, what is","Tongtian up to?"]},{"number":5148,"title":"Chapter 5148: Daogong, You Are as Stupid as Before","paragraphs":["Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","The pointed finger of the Tongtian Buddha sent shivers down the spine of Emperor Donglin.","At this point, there were three pairs of second-tier Emperors left on the battlefield. Even if they were defeated, they could still retreat safely. Those Emperors would die, but he would survive, and that wouldn’t be a big problem for him.","But now, with the move made by the Tongtian Buddha, his life was also at stake.","“Tongtian, have you gone mad? Cooperating with them?!” Emperor Donglin was beginning to panic.","He was the Ruler of a high-grade world. Although he had avatars, the one that had come to the Great Desolate Wilderness this time was his strongest battle avatar. It possessed invaluable treasures. If this avatar fell here, along with the lost Emperors, it would be difficult for their Donglin Realm to stand in the surrounding domains.","<font <=\"\" div=\"\">","“Donglin, you used the names of protecting those Emperors to kill Dongyan. I have to avenge this great enmity!” Tongtian Buddha revealed a rare ferocious expression.","“Dongyan was an Emperor of my 3,000 Worlds and also the Dao Ancestor of the Dongyan Realm. Now he followed me to the Great Desolate Wilderness seeking opportunities, but he was killed by you. How can I explain if I let you go back?”","The murderous intent in the eyes of Tongtian Buddha grew stronger.","Liu Ya watched everything and pondered on countermeasures. He couldn’t guarantee that everything Tongtian said was true.","Dongyan’s death was indeed related to Donglin, but Tongtian didn’t come to rescue at a critical moment either!","In his view, the Tongtian Buddha was just a paper tiger. He was trying to weaken the forces on the battlefield by utilizing their strength.","If they were defeated, they would probably be the ones surrounded now.","“What? Aren’t you planning to take action?” Tongtian hesitated.","In this situation, if they didn’t support him, Liu Ya and Daogong wouldn’t support him either. After all, they had come for the Qishen Temple. If they could kill a fourth-tier Emperor now, it might intimidate many small fries. After all, there was currently only one fifth-tier Emperor in the original","universe. The Ancient God Clan was very far from the Great Desolate Wilderness. Even if they used their treasures to teleport multiple times, it would still take a long time.","Most of the ones who could arrive here were nearby Emperors and Grand Yan Immortals.","Deal with these people first, let the Death Spirit Array Formation absorb the","Death Qi and reach a perfect state. By then, with the power of the Qishen Temple and the blessing of the Great Desolate Dao, even if a fifth-tier Emperor came, they could still contend.","Daogong first glanced at Zhen Wuyang in the distance and then nodded to Liu Ya.","“Take action!”","Boom!","Daogong took the lead, and his dust whisk instantly covered the sky, leaving no place for Emperor Donglin to escape.","“l will stop Zhen Wuyang. You two quickly kill Donglin’s avatar.” Fourth-tier Emperors on the battlefield were all at a similar level except for Daogong, who was slightly weaker. The other Emperors were all at the normal level of a fourth-tier, especially Tongtian Buddha. He inherited the origin of the high-grade world. Although his Dao was only of a medium world, the origin of the high-grade world still made his Dao immensely powerful.","“Tongtian, you shameless scoundrel!” Emperor Donglin had no way to escape. Facing Liu Ya and Tongtian Buddha, two powerful fourth-tier Emperors, his divine body was quickly defeated, and his battle armor was torn apart by Liu","Ya’s hand.","In the distance, Daogong suppressed the void while blocking Zhen Wuyangs way.","“Zhen Wuyang, don’t worry. It will be your turn soon.” Daogong sneered.","When Tongtian Buddha negotiated with them, he secretly conveyed to them that as long as they joined forces to kill Donglin, he would help them deal with Zhen Wuyang together.","This was also the reason why they cooperated with Tongtian Buddha.","Even if Tongtian Buddha played any tricks, their combat power on the battlefield was not weaker than his. Moreover, in the current situation, Donglin was not far from death.","As long as they killed Donglin, even if Tongtian changed his mind, they could still use the Qishen Temple to restrain him. Liu Ya and him could then besiege Zhen Wuyang and take revenge for the grudges of the past.","“Daogong, you are as foolish as before,” Zhen Wuyang sneered.","In the distant void, Emperor Donglin, unable to endure the humiliation, directly detonated his terrifying avatar.","‘rne self-destruction of a tourtn-tler Emperor was extremely terrifying. Endless white Qi waves rolled, and even a third-tier Emperor falling into it would be instantly strangled.","As a fourth-tier Emperor, Liu Ya relied on the Dao of the Great Desolate Wilderness. The Death Spirit Array could reach the threshold of a powerful fourth-tier. However, he dared not resist it head-on and quickly retreated backward.","“Tongtian, it’s time to close the net.” Zhen Wuyangs eyes were cold, and his aura surged into the sky.","Tongtian Buddha was protected by the Thousand Treasures Kasaya, and his body was unharmed. After hearing Zhen Wuyangs message, he sighed and said, “Virtuous!”","In the vast emptiness, billions of miles away from the battlefield, two figures, Hu Qing and Jian Wushuang, were conversing with Grand Yan Immortal from the Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm.","Suddenly, a terrifying aura emanated from the distant Qishen Temple.","Boom!","A shockwave rolled through, shattering the void in the core region of the Great Desolate Wilderness, leaving numerous horrifying spatial fissures that took a long time to heal.","“This is the effects of Emperors’ fighting?” Jian Wushuang exclaimed, shocked. Even from billions of miles away, that aura managed to inflict wounds on their bodies.","Fortunately, everyone present was at least a Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal. Both Jian Wushuang and Hu Qing were ultimate beings in their paths, and their strength not inferior to Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortals. They could withstand the fluctuations of this aura.","“It’s too terrifying!” exclaimed a Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal from the Donogyan Realm.","Originally, they had followed Emperor’s guidance into the depths of the Great Desolate Wilderness in search of the opportunity to become an Emperor. They were excited and looking forward to the chances within the Qishen Temple.","Now, feeling the fluctuations in that aura, they all had a bad premonition.","“Indeed, the opportunity to allow a Grand Yan Immortal to ascend to Emperor is not that simple.”","“What’s the matter, Brother Jiu Yu, are you scared?” spoke the First Prince from the Dongyan Realm. He was a Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal, ranking among the top in this group of Grand Yan Immortals. Besides a few Emperors, his position was the highest in the Dongyan Realm, making him the most hopeful genius to become an Emperor in the Dongyan Realm’s countless years.","His Dao was still a third-grade Dao. As long as he successfully merged his","Daos, he would have the power of a second-tier Emperor. In the current 3,000 Great Worlds, there were still many worlds without owners. As a native practitioner, after becoming an Emperor, he could naturally control a world.","At that time, with his own Daoist Arena and his comprehension of the Heavenly Dao, he could quickly become a third-tier Emperor, leaping to become one of the peak powers in the universe.","“If I were afraid, I wouldn’t have come!” Jiu Yu’s eyes were cold, murmuring softly.","His appearance was somewhat similar to the pale monk that Jian Wushuang had met before, but their strengths were worlds apart.","When they had just encountered this group, the young samanera had secretly transmitted to him, warning him not to provoke the Chief Disciple of the Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm, ‘Jiu Yu’.","This Chief Disciple, who resided on Tongtian Mountain, had achieved the perfect Nine Revolutions stage countless years ago. It was said that he had comprehended nine great Daos, each reaching the level of perfection in the Nine Revolutions stage. He had been suppressing his strength and refraining from merging his Daos. It was rumored that he had cultivated some special secret technique. Once the technique was perfected, he could merge his Daos. As long as he succeeded in merging his Daos, his Dao would be comparable to the Ultimate Dao.."]},{"number":5149,"title":"Chapter 5149: The Extraordinary Phenomenon, Emperor’s Fall","paragraphs":["Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Drip, drip!","The crisp sound of raindrops gradually echoed!","The raindrops grew denser, transitioning from a drizzle to a downpour.","For a moment, the entire Great Desolate Wilderness was enveloped in heavy rain, puzzling some Emperors and Grand Yan Immortals on the periphery.","“Isn’t this the Great Desolate Wilderness? How can it rain here?” a woman in grey exclaimed in surprise.","<font <=\"\" div=\"\">","Jian Wushuang and others looked up at the sky.","“The rainwater is golden!” many exclaimed.","Could it be... Jian Wushuang caught a raindrop in his hand, his eyes flickering slightly. He saw a shattered Grand Dao within the raindrop.","Manipulating the rain around him with Yan power, he instantly gathered a large droplet.","Studying it closely, he still saw the broken Grand Dao within the rainwater.","Seeing Jian Wushuangs reaction, others turned curiously.","“Wushuang, did you find something?” the grey-clad woman inquired.","“This is Emperor’s Fall!” Jiu Yu, a Yan Immortal who had lived through countless chaotic eras, spoke. He took a clump of rainwater, forming a seal with his hands.","The shattered Grand Dao within the rainwater was peeled off by him, astonishing the onlookers.","“Master Jiu Yu is right; this is Emperors Fall. Only when an Emperor dies does a world experience golden rain,” Jian Wushuang said, filled with emotion.","He had read about this in an ancient script before.","In the endless epochs of the Great Si Region, the last Emperor’s Fall occurred during the era when Zhen Wuyang killed dozens of Emperors, causing the region to be shrouded in golden rain.","However, the rain described in that record was not as immense as this one.","This indicated that more Emperors had fallen in the Great Desolate Wilderness this time, surpassing the number slain by Zhen Wuyang during the ancient era or even rivaling that of a top-tier Emperor’s Fall.","“Wushuang truly has broad knowledge. Indeed, this is Emperor’s Fall. I was fortunate enough to witness it during the Ancient Era in your Great Si Region.” Jiu Yu sighed, vividly recalling the scene from the last Emperor’s Fall. At that time, he was already a Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal, and today, he remained one.","However, he became more convinced of his own Great Dao. Weakness led to being slaughtered, turned into rainwater, but only strength could ensure eternal existence.","He didn’t care about those Emperors with fifth or fourth-tier Dao, not even paying attention to those with third-grade Dao.","He had gained fame early on. Among the outstanding talents of his time who had become Emperors, they were all ordinary, far from being considered strong among Emperors.","He was the strongest among his peers in the Heaven-Reaching Buddha Realm from his youth. It wasn’t until he encountered the Tianji from the Dongyan Realm in the Grand Yan Immortal stage that he understood the gap in their Great Daos.","At that time, he was a third-grade Dao Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal, encountering Tianji, who was a Three Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal at the time, who was pursuing the Ultimate Dao.","The two of them, one from the awe-inspiring talents of the Heaven-Reaching Buddha Realm, the other the strongest Prince of the Dongyan Realm, engaged in a battle witnessed even by the Emperor himself. Daoist Tianji, a Three Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal, faced off against the Nine Revolutions","Grand Yan Immortal, Jiu Yu.","In the end, their battle concluded in a draw!","Three Revolutions against Nine Revolutions, and it ended in a draw. This result was unbearable for the proud Jiu Yu. When he achieved the Perfected Nine Revolutions stage, he challenged Daoist Tianji again.","In this battle, he was at his peak of the Nine Revolutions, and the Tianji was also at the Nine Revolutions stage. This time, there was no draw; he was thoroughly defeated.","Daoist Tianji defeated him with just one move.","From then on, he started to accumulate strength, spending years on Mount Tongtian comprehending the ancient civilization’s secret techniques.","“The Unity of Myriad Daos,” Jiu Yu murmured to himself.","The Ultimate Dao couldn’t be comprehended through enlightenment alone, According to the Tongtian Buddha, he didn’t have the destiny for it.","Later, unable to watch him fall forever, Tongtian Buddha bestowed upon him the secret technique of the Unity of Myriad Daos.","Upon walking the path of the Unity of Myriad Daos, he realized the feeling of power that surpassed the strength of countless peers. He could sense that this Dao was no worse than the Ultimate Daoo, but succeeding in it was even more challenging than the Ultimate Dao.","Up to now, no one within the original universe had become an Emperor through the Unity of Myriad Daos.","Perhaps only a few people had obtained this secret technique, or perhaps this path was fundamentally impossible to succeed in. However, even if no one had succeeded, he would continue on this path. Even if he couldn’t become an Emperor, he refused to be an ordinary one.","“So, Emperors can be defeated,” the woman in grey looked at the golden rain in the sky, her eyes filled with astonishment.","She was just an ordinary Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal, walking a path that was only a fourth-grade Great Dao. In her view, as long as someone was an Emperor, they were the supreme existence. Now it seemed that her perspective was limited.","Many people gained profound insights from the golden rain, especially from the broken Great Dao within it, which greatly aided their cultivation.","This trip was not in vain.","Outside the edge of the Great Desolate Wilderness,","A group from the Great Dream Realm stopped in their tracks.","“Ancestor, what is this golden rain? Is it unique to the Great Desolate Wilderness?” a young girl from the Great Dream Clan asked in amazement as she bathed in the rain.","Apart from a few Emperors who knew the truth, other Grand Yan Immortals had no idea what was happening. After all, Emperors falling was an extremely rare sight. Some Emperors had never witnessed the scene of an Emperor’s Fall until they were killed themselves.","“This is Emperor’s Fall!” the Ancestor of the Great Dream Realm looked towards the depths of the Great Desolate Wilderness. He could sense a terrifying battle happening there; even he might fall in such a battle.","Outside the Great Desolate, various forces had gathered, but upon seeing this Emperor’s Fall, they all came to a halt. Even the fourth-tier Emperors dared not make a move.","Gradually, various forces began to gather and formed a temporary alliance.","The purpose of this alliance was twofold: first, the Qishen Temple, which was the goal of many people present, and second, to counter the Ancient God Clan and other peak forces.","In the original universe, the five peak forces were all overseen by fifth-tier Emperors. Even though the true bodies of these fifth-tier Emperors had gone to the River of Time, they still possessed the combat power of fifth-tier thresholds through their avatars. This level of power was something these people couldn’t contend with.","Moreover, the fifth-tier Emperors who had gone to the River of Time were now rushing back. If they didn’t unite, they wouldn’t gain any benefits from the Qishen Temple.","The purpose of the temporary alliance was to huddle together for warmth, to resist the fifth-tier Emperors, and then get a share of the spoils.","In three days, most of the forces in the East Domain, where the Great Si Region was located, had gathered. Even the most powerful force in the East Domain, the Eternal Tower, had finally arrived.","The Eternal Tower was a peak force in the original universe, built from several high-grade worlds. Now, the ruler of the Eternal Tower was the direct disciple of the fifth-tier Emperor ‘Emperor Zhutian’. Her name was ‘Fengyu’.","She was incredibly strong, and she had several fourth-tier Emperors under her command. If a fifth-tier Emperor didn’t show himself, she was one of the most influential figures in the entire original universe.."]},{"number":5150,"title":"Chapter 5150: Eternal Tower","paragraphs":["Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Emperor Zhutian had long achieved the fifth tier as an Emperor, emerging from the Original Universe and venturing into the River of Time within the space-time continuum. Now, with the emergence of the Qishen Temple, the controller of the Eternal Tower immediately informed his master. However, even a fifth-tier Emperor would require a million years to return from the River of Time to the Original Universe.","They had no choice but to let them explore the Qishen Temple first.","“Demon Lord Fengyu!’","Inside the temporary headquarters of the alliance, a terrifying old man appeared outside the Eternal Tower with just a flicker of his figure.","The name Eternal Tower came from the magnificent divine tower before the old man.","Box","This was the Eternal Treasure that Emperor Zhutian obtained from the River of Time, a creation of the mythical Universe Master.","Even a fifth-tier Emperor would covet such a treasure because it was crafted by the Universe Master, containing the Great Dao of the universe within. It allowed one to comprehend their own Great Dao and suppress all things.","The tower had nine levels, and only a fourth-tier Emperor like Emperor Zhutian could fully unleash the power of the Eternal Tower.","“Chishui, are you going to be an enemy of our Eternal Tower?” Inside the eighth level of the Eternal Tower, Ruler Fengyu shouted angrily. Fengyu was dressed in a long green robe.","She was one of the few female Emperors among the fourth-tier Emperors. Her delicate face frequently changed, and even the weaker Emperors couldn’t see her true appearance clearly.","“I have no choice. A group of little fellows has caught the old man’s attention and insisted on dragging me into their affairs. So, the old man had to step forward,” Wanderer Chishui said with a faint smile.","He was originally a lone traveler from the Eastern Domain. His homeland world had long been destroyed, but he had mastered a secret realm. Although he hadn’t mastered a domain, his strength was that of a genuine fourth-tier top Emperor.","“Oh, since that’s the case, then you’re going to be our enemy!” The expression on Demon Lord Fengyu’s face gradually turned cold.","She earned her title of ‘Demon Lord’ through ruthless means, capitalizing on her brutal tactics. When the Emperors of the Eastern Domain had risen like mushrooms after the rain, she had started looking for high- grade worlds everywhere, trying to seize control opportunistically.","One fourth-tier Emperor, who had achieved mastery in the second- grade","Dao, directly took control of a high- grade world within the scope of the Eternal Tower’s influence and even killed the guardians of the Eternal Tower in that area.","In that era, fifth-tier Emperors entered the River of Time one after another.","The peak forces were momentarily without the presence of these fifth-tier Emperors. Many powerful rulers and Emperors began to detach themselves from the Eternal Tower. At that time, Demon Lord Fengyu was just a Ruler of a high- grade world, his strength merely ordinary among the fourth-tier.","Many of the strong individuals within the Eternal Tower were not convinced.","However, due to her status as the direct disciple of Emperor Zhutian, some people, while not daring to rebel openly, secretly refused to obey her commands.","Without the direct suppression of fifth-tier Emperors, the peak forces were on the verge of collapse. Both internal pressure and external threats required her strength to be validated.","Coincidentally, a top third-tier Emperor appeared, giving her a target to establish her dominance.","This third-tier Emperor first killed the second-tier Emperor guarding the higher world and then took control of the higher world himself.","Although many Emperors emerged during that era, there were still very few who could successfully reach the second-tier through the harmony of their","Dao. Therefore, many higher worlds remained ownerless. As a peak force, the Eternal Tower naturally saw the potential in these higher worlds. They took control of several surrounding higher worlds and planned to have Emperors from their own faction govern these worlds in the future.","This third-tier Emperor was extremely arrogant. After taking control of the higher world, he directly advanced to the fourth-tier Emperor, becoming a Ruler. He thought little of Demon Lord Fengyu and began to provoke the Eternal Tower.","In his Dao Arena, the fourth-tier Emperor who ruled the higher world was considered the ceiling of power at that time. Even within the Eternal Tower, there were only three Rulers.","However, Demon Lord Fengyu managed to manipulate the Eternal Tower and enter that higher world. No one knew what happened inside, but when the","Demon Lord Fengyu came out, the higher world had already become a ruin. One higher world had been destroyed like this.","Since that incident, no one in the Eternal Tower dared to act recklessly, and the Fengyu became the Demon Lord Fengyu.","In the chaotic era of the Eastern Doomain, the number of Emperors who died at her hands was in the double digits.","In contrast, the Wanderer Chishui was a lone wanderer. From the chaotic era of the Eastern Domain to the present, he had no remarkable achievements to speak of.","Although his personal strength had reached the peak of the fourth-tier, his prestige and fame were not significant. He was known for his sneak attacks and had nothing much to show for himself. He had no attachments, controlling only a few hundred special beings within his territory, and he had no relatives. Therefore, he lived aimlessly, as long as he was happy.","He had many enemies, but most wouldn’t seek revenge against him. After all, they didn’t fear the person with nothing to lose. Even some super forces that suffered losses at his hands could only swallow their grievances.","However, this time, the Chishui became the leader of a temporary alliance and directly challenged the peak power, surprising Demon Lord Fengyu.","Wanderer Chishui was barefoot and dressed in tattered robes, resembling an old beggar. But no one dared to underestimate his strength.","“Fengyu, don’t speak so definitively. The appearance of the Qishen Temple is the bestowal of the supreme rules. No one can monopolize it, not even a fifth-tier Emperor!” Chishui changed his usual demeanor and became serious.","Inside the Eternal Tower, the Demon Lord Fengyu stood by the tower window, looking at the defiant Chishui standing in the void, her brows furrowed.","“This old thing, Chishui.” A third-tier Emperor was infuriated.","They were the closest among the peak forces. This time, the opportunity from the Qishen Temple was most likely to fall into their hands.","At this moment, a sudden temporary alliance had emerged, gathering half of the super strong individuals in the Eastern Domain. Even though they were peak forces, until the return of the fifth-tier Emperors, they wouldn’t gain any advantage within this temporary alliance.","“During the chaotic era, this old fellow wandered alone, stirring up many wars. Now, some people actually believe him.”","“Hmph, do you think those people are fools? They are just using each other.”","The temporary alliance gathered half of the strong individuals in the Eastern Domain. Each of them was shrewd. There were more than ten fourth-tier","Emperors among them. With so many strong individuals, they elected the Wanderer Chishui as their leader, obviously fearing being implicated once the fifth-tier Emperors returned.","Chishui was different. He was a lone wanderer. Even if the fifth-tier Emperors returned, he could just pull up his pants and run away. He didn’t need any territory. He could thrive in any universe.","“Forget it. For now, let’s prioritize the Qishen Temple. If we delay any longer, the strong individuals from the other factions will join forces against us, which will be even more disadvantageous for us.” Demon Lord Fengyu made","up her mind and appeared outside the Eternal Tower with a flash.","Inside the tower, no one dared to say more. Demon Lord Fengyu was no longer the little girl who used to live under her master’s shadow.","“Chishui, I don’t want to go to war with you. Those who are sensible, step aside. Let’s explore together....”"]},{"number":5151,"title":"Chapter 5151: Growing Sprites","paragraphs":["Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","The numerous powerful beings in the temporary alliance were closely monitoring the negotiations. If they didn’t unite, Demon Lord Fengyu wouldn’t care about them. It was possible that the Eternal Tower would directly seal off the Great Desolate Wilderness, preventing them from entering.","After a brief conversation between the two tier 4 experts, they each returned to their respective camps.","“Brother Chishui, what’s the situation? Did Demon Lord Fengyu agree?” many Emperors inquired. After all, this opportunity surpassed everything else.","In times of chaos, the struggle was for territory. Now, it was about the chance to ascend as the Lord of the universe. If one truly became the Lord of the universe and controlled the Original Universe, they would be invincible not just in the Original Universe but also in the long river of time and space.","“Friends, Fengyu has agreed. We will explore the Qishen Temple together, and as for the opportunity, it’s every man for himself,” Chishui smiled.","Box","Upon hearing this, everyone breathed a sigh of relief. They were afraid of a direct confrontation with the Eternal Tower.","“Fortunately, Brother Chishui spoke for us. Otherwise, Demon Lord Fengyu would not have allowed us to explore the Qishen Temple together,” the people remarked. With their goals achieved, Chishui, as the apparent leader, received numerous compliments.","“Everyone, let’s set off now and enter the Great Desolate Wilderness!” Wanderer Chishui waved his hand, and a massive palace rose from the ground, appearing behind him.","This palace was an ordinary supreme treasure palace, conducive to gathering everyone in one place.","It wasn’t that they didn’t have more powerful palaces, but no one dared to rashly enter someone else’s supreme treasure palace. If they inadvertently triggered the supreme treasure’s power and got suppressed, it would be a big joke.","If they split up, it would seem disorganized. Walker, understanding them best, proactively brought out an ordinary supreme treasure palace. Even a tier 1 Emperor could easily break the palace’s defenses, but it allowed everyone to gather together, appearing as a unified force.","However, this palace also had its drawback—it wasn’t fast enough.","The massive palace could only follow behind the Eternal Tower.","As numerous powerful beings from the Eastern Domain entered the Great Desolate Wilderness together, they felt an overwhelming desolation, even a chill.","The void, purified by the baptism of the Emperor’s Fall, bred countless sprites, forming many unconscious ghosts and monsters. These creatures weren’t very strong, mostly at the Grand Yan Immortal level.","“How many emperors had to die for so many stray thoughts to appear?” Chishui controlled the palace, standing at the highest point, looking at the ghosts and monsters formed by these stray thoughts.","He had survived from the chaotic era until now and had witnessed many grand scenes.","However, just as the Qishen Temple emerged, they had just gathered, not even starting to explore it when a terrifying battle occurred inside. It seemed like quite a few Emperors had died.","If all the Emperors from the Original Universe were to come to this Great Desolate Wilderness, how many of them would die?","“Brother Chishui, just got the news, all the Emperors from the Donglin Realm were wiped out, even the main battle avatar of the Emperor Donglin fell.”","“Oh, and also, Feng MO was severely injured by Yuandun and was killed by a mysterious person.”","“Feng MO?” Chishui recalled this person and said, “l remember this kid had just broken through the tier 4 not long ago and didn’t have an avatar.”","“Yes, this time he truly perished. Because his world was too deeply fused with his Dao, it directly collapsed, and countless lives perished.”","In the pursuit of opportunities, everyone only thought about benefits; no one ever considered what the consequences of failure might be. When the world collapsed, countless tribesmen all perished!","This was the fate of the losers.","Although the opportunity of the Qishen Temple was great, how many could truly succeed in the end?","One person’s success came at the cost of the bones of tens of thousands!","No matter who this phrase was applied to, it was the most accurate, especially for a strong person. The success of a strong person would undoubtedly lead to many failures.","These Emperors, which one of them hadn’t walked out from piles of corpses and seas of blood? They understood this principle better than anyone.","But after tasting the benefits brought by strength, their desire for strength became even stronger. They became the Dao Ancestor’s desire to become a Ruler.","After becoming a Ruler, they would recruit people and build forces everywhere. Forming a group was just an external statement; taking what they needed was the real deal.","Now there was a chance to ascend in one step; how could they not go all out to seize it?","The powerful figures from both sides scanned the Great Desolate Wilderness, their hearts filled with mixed feelings.","After the Emperor’s Fall, Jian Wushuang encountered a big problem on his side.","Although those sprites were only at the Grand Yan Immortal level, there were just too many of them!","Among them, there were many Perfected Grand Yan Immortals.","“Everyone, protect Wushuang and Hu Qing. I have informed Lord Buddha, and there will be Emperors coming to rescue us.”","Jiu Yu was the strongest among them in strength and seniority. He directly ordered everyone to set up a simple formation to resist those ghosts and monsters.","Hehe...","Countless sprites crawled out from the cracks in space. Their bodies twisted, shaped like little ghosts, draped in illusory robes, wandering in the void. Once they encountered cultivators, they surged towards them.","Everyone present at least had the cultivation level of a Nine Revolutions Grand","Yan Immortal, totaling over a thousand people. Half of the elites from the 3,000 Worlds were here. Each of them was stronger than the elders of the Great Si Region, except for Zhen Wuyang.","“Brother Wushuang, follow me!” The woman in grey clothes waved her hand!","They only knew that Jian Wushuang was from the Great Si Region. He had rescued the little monk Hu Qing midway, and the Emperors had ordered them to take care of these two especially, protecting Hu Qing in particular.","However, Hu Qing was a Six Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal but had been saved by Jian Wushuang, a Three Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal. This puzzled them, but they didn’t dare to ask. After all, he had saved the people of their 3,000 Worlds.","Jian Wushuang found it somewhat amusing. This woman in grey clothes in front of him was just a Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal, yet she actively wanted to protect him.","However, he couldn’t refuse other people’s kindness. He nodded and stood behind the woman in grey clothes.","“I’ll have to trouble you later, Friend Luo Shui.” Jian Wushuang smiled slightly and then stepped back behind Luo Shui.","Luo Shui was an elite from the Donglin Realm and also an elder in the sect. Despite her young age, she had only practiced for 60 million years, which, for many Ninth Transformation Grand Yan Immortals, was merely a simple closed-door cultivation.","Jian Wushuang stood behind a woman, even if other Grand Yan Immortals were polite, some of their actions still showed disdain.","However, he didn’t care about all this. As long as there was a chance, he planned to slip away and leave the Great Desolate Wilderness as soon as possible.","He had a premonition that if he didn’t leave now, he might not be able to leave later.","After taking a deep breath, Jian Wushuang carefully examined Fairy Luo Shui in front of him.","From her back, Fairy Luo Shui had a graceful figure. However, her grey linen robe was too loose to discern her shape clearly. Only her white neck and some stray strands of hair that hadn’t been tied up indicated that Luo Shui was undoubtedly a rare beauty.."]},{"number":5152,"title":"Chapter 5152: Spirit Guardian","paragraphs":["Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","“Too bad!” Jian Wushuang shook his head silently. If these people didn’t leave, most of them would die here.","This kind-hearted Fairy, Luo Shui, was mediocre in strength, even inferior to","Gu Yuan, making her the weakest among them. That’s why she was left with Jian Wushuang.","The young monk, Hu Qing, glanced at Jian Wushuang, smiled slightly, and nodded. Since he stepped onto the path, Jian Wushuang felt that Hu Qing had changed a lot—personality, mindset, and power had undergone a drastic transformation.","He kept his killing intent hidden and his guard up. Looking back at the scene when Hu Qings power surged, Jian Wushuang could hardly believe it. If people could tap into their potential in dangerous situations, boosting their strength by 30 or 50 percent, or even directly breaking through their original boundaries, just like his sudden promotion to Grand Yan Immortal, it could explain this.","Box","Hu Qings original strength was at best that of an ordinary Yan Immortal.","Jumping from an ordinary Yan Immortal to a Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal was astounding. Jian Wushuang hadn’t even dared to think about such a significant temporary breakthrough.","Initially, he thought the disturbance in the Great Desolate Wilderness was because of him. Now, it seemed like Hu Qing was more of a protagonist.","There were too many secrets behind all this—the sudden fall of the Emperor and the terrifying white aura. It indicated that Zhen Wuyang, Tongtian Buddha, and other Emperors had clashed with the resurrected beings.","Who won and who fell remained unknown.","At this level of conflict, they were utterly powerless. Staying in the Great Desolate Wilderness was a burden.","Jian Wushuang closed his eyes slowly; regardless, recovering his strength was crucial now.","While he leisurely restored his Heart and Thought power, outside the crowd, Jiu Yu and others fought desperately against the sprites.","It was impossible. Their numbers were overwhelming. Just as they killed one batch, another crawled out from the cracks.","“Brother Jiu Yu, this won’t work at all!”","“Yeah, there are too many of these monsters; we can’t possibly kill them all.”","Initially, they handled the situation with ease, but these monsters lacked consciousness, were fearless of death, and were exceptionally powerful. Some even possessed the strength of a Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal.","After Jiu Yu eliminated several Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal level monsters nearby, he glanced around and felt a sinking feeling in his heart.","“Not good! ”","Meanwhile, on the other side of the Great Desolate Wilderness.","The makeshift alliance of Chishui and the Eternal Tower was surprisingly relaxed. With numerous emperor-level experts clearing the way, they didn’t need the Grand Yan Immortals to fight desperately.","“This Great Desolate Wilderness is so dangerous.” A girl from the Great Dream Realm leaned on the corridor of the palace, watching the monsters shattered by the aura of emperors.","“You, girl, if it weren’t for the Ancestor, facing so many monsters, not to mention finding the Qishen Temple, it would be incredibly difficult just to survive in this place.” A middle-aged Grand Yan Immortal furrowed his brows.","He didn’t know if the Ancestor’s decision to send them, Grand Yan Immortals who had always lived in the Great Dream Realm, to find the Qishen Temple in the Great Desolate Wilderness was right or wrong.","In the vast expanse of the Great Desolate Wilderness, whether it was the Grand Yan Immortal or the Emperor, their mental states began to change gradually upon entering the wilderness.","In the cracks of the void, a massive black serpent slithered, its head crowned with black horns. Its enormous eyes moved as it continued forward.","“Not powerful enough!” A black smoke suddenly emerged above the serpent’s head, dissipating to reveal a middle-aged Daoist standing there. He wore a mottled white Daoist robe, a tall crown on his head, and a purple eye in the center of his forehead.","He had been observing from afar when the Great Desolate Wilderness first stirred, but at that time, he was not present in this universe.","“Are the chosen ones all so weak? All 18 divine generals were killed, and the strongest among them was only a fourth-tier Emperor. The dignity of our temple has been completely trampled by this group,” the middle-aged Daoist murmured while standing on the serpent’s head.","“Black Qi Snake, your Heart power is becoming more interesting.”","The middle-aged Daoist touched the serpent’s horn, and the purple eye in his forehead kept turning.","“Now that you’re awake, why not come out and see me!” The middle-aged Daoist shouted angrily at a dark corner in the void.","In the pitch-black corner, silence reigned. After the middle-aged Daoist’s voice fell, an old hunchbacked man emerged, holding a dim lamp.","“l am the servant of the old master, not yours. You should be clear about that!” The hunchbacked old man, holding the dim lamp, staggered to the middle-aged Daoist.","This exchange revealed many secrets. Unfortunately, in this narrow space, there were only these two; even a fifth-tier Emperor couldn’t hide from them.","“You, this dog servant, secretly revived the temple, and I thought you could make those useless people take a few steps forward. Yet, as soon as they were revived, most of them died!” The middle-aged Daoist sneered at the hunchbacked old man.","He had drifted with the Qishen Temple from the River of Time to the Original Universe. At that time, he was severely injured and had been accumulating in the cracks of the void until now, and his injuries still hadn’t fully healed.","Originally, he had wanted those divine generals to inherit the Dao of the Qishen Temple, to gain some benefits from the temple, and then step forward himself, killing those inheritors and seizing the treasures.","But these people turned out to be worthless. Even after all these cycles, not a single one had reached the level of a fifth-tier Emperor.","“Enough of the nonsense. I am the only living disciple of the Qishen Temple. His treasures should belong to me. Tell me, how many treasures did you get from the inner hall? I don’t need too much, just enough to restore my strength,” the middle-aged Daoist said coldly, his selfishness and greed emanating from him, utterly domineering and leaving no face for the hunchbacked old man.","“Wu Zuo, I’m not here to give you treasures. I’m here to inform you that you’ve been expelled from the Qishen Temple,” the hunchbacked old man said slowly, his expression unchanged.","“Expelled? You’re not even qualified to remove my name. You’re just a spirit-keeping slave!” Wu Zuo, the middle-aged Daoist, couldn’t help but roar.","Wu Zuo had a premonition of what was coming but still couldn’t believe it. After all, he had nothing left now. If the Qishen Temple expelled him, how could he gain any benefits?","The calm on the hunchbacked old man’s face gradually disappeared, replaced by a lifeless aura. This aura made even the deeply engraved wrinkles on his face tremble slightly.","For a moment, Wu Zuo involuntarily took a step back.","“I might not have the authority to expel you, but the true spirits in the Qishen Temple do!” The hunchbacked old man’s voice was icy, like a sharp blade in the cold wind, piercing into Wu Zuo’s chest, one after another.."]},{"number":5153,"title":"Chapter 5153: Together","paragraphs":["Translator: Endless?antasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Upon hearing the words ‘true spirit’, Wu Zuo froze. Then, he exclaimed in disbelief, “How is it possible? The true spirit’s injuries were even more severe than mine. How could it awaken?”","“I’ve delivered the message; you don’t have the qualifications to know the rest,” the hunchbacked old man said, his voice fading as he slowly retreated","into the corner.","As he was leaving, the hunchbacked old man seemed to remember something.","“Oh, right. The true spirit mentioned that, out of respect for the old master, it will give you another chance. You can undergo the trial at the Qishen Temple along with other practitioners.”","Box","After leaving these words behind, the hunchbacked old man vanished completely into the void.","“Undergo the trial together!” Wu Zuo’s expression changed.","He used to be a registered disciple of the Qishen Temple and was very familiar with their trials. The Qishen Temple’s trials weren’t about gaining benefits based on your strength; the requirements were high, and they demanded exceptional potential.","At his peak, he had touched the threshold of the sixth-tier. But now, with his divine body still injured, he was only at the top fifth-tier level. Despite his arrogance, he knew he had no more potential left.","In ancient times, as a disciple of the Qishen Temple, he had heard the legendary Qishen, a Starry Overlord, discuss the Dao. Despite that, his power remained at the fifth-tier Emperor level.","His Dao was extraordinary, a unique second- grade Dao that merged two ordinary second-grade Daos. He had the potential to reach the top, but he remained stuck at the fifth-tier Emperor. He had comprehended the sixth-tier rules with the help of the Qishen but struggled to control them.","After the Qishen fell and the starry sky fell silent, his strength was unremarkable among the Qishen’s disciples. He was just a named disciple who survived that calamity and followed the Qishen Temple to the Original Universe.","“This is good. Saves me from using those wastrels,” Wu Zuo said, his face twisted with malice.","With his strength, he feared no one in the Original Universe. Regarding talent and potential, apart from the ultimate Emperor, he doubted anyone could surpass him. After all, ultimate Emperors were rare. In ancient times, their status was high; even the Qishen favored them.","Most of the ultimate Emperors who appeared in the River of Time’s many universes bowed under the Qishen’s command. But these people had all perished. Even the powerful three God Lords, who controlled a side of the universe, had disappeared.","Whoosh!","Wu Zuo tore through the void, no longer hiding, heading directly toward the Qishen Temple.","The true spirit’s awakening marked the beginning of the Qishen Temple’s real trial. As for the inheritance the Great Si Region received from the Ancient Era, it was just an ordinary inheritance from the external hall. At that time, thetrue spirit hadn’t revived, so the treasures they received were limited. But now, with the true spirit’s revival and the opening of the internal hall, the true inheritance of the Qishen Temple began.","Countless treasures, powerful legacies—the Qishen had collected treasures from endless ages, all within the inner hall.","Outside the Qishen Temple at this moment,","A towering tower came to a slow stop; it was the Eternal Tower entering the","Great Desolate Wilderness.","The two were similar in size, but their auras were vastly different.","The Eternal Tower was like a battleship in the vast ocean, immense and overpowering, exuding an aura of conquering the entire sea. In contrast, the","Qishen Temple’s aura was like the entire Great Desolate Wilderness, encompassing all things.","As for the temporary alliance formed by Chishui, it was like a sea turtle, following the battleship, wandering in the vast ocean.","“These people move quite fast!” Tongtian Buddha, sitting in meditation in the void, glanced indifferently at the hall of the Eternal Tower and the Chishui Alliance.","The eyes of Liu Ya were bloodshot, completely ignoring Tongtian Buddha.","Recalling the battle just now, he felt somewhat bewildered now!","At first, Tongtian Buddha collaborated with them to suppress the Eastern Forest God Emperor. Everything went smoothly; Zhen Wuyang, constrained by Daogong, couldn’t make a move. Together with Tongtian Buddha and the","Emperors of the Qishen Temple, they forced the Donglin to self-destruct.","But just when he thought the situation was turning, Tongtian Buddha suddenly enveloped the entire Qishen Temple with a Thousand Treasures Kasaya and entered the interior of the temple himself.","This caught Liu Ya off guard. He was dealing with the terrifying waves of white energy while trying to support the Qishen Temple.","The same happened on Daogongs side. Zhen Muyang’s sudden burst overwhelmed Daogong, beating them both. After defeating them, Zhen","Wuyang followed the Thousand Treasures Kasaya into the Qishen Temple.","Later, the aura of the Qishen Temple suddenly surged, followed by the fall of Emperors.","The changes in the Qishen Temple surprised and worried him and Daogong. After the surge, the Qishen Temple emitted an atmosphere akin to a sacrificial altar, clearly different from before.","But they couldn’t enter; the entire Qishen Temple was enveloped by the Thousand Treasures Kasaya. While they were anxiously trying to find a way in, Zhen Wuyang and Tongtian were suddenly transported out of the temple.","Both had stains of brown blood on them, indicating that everyone inside was","likely dead.","Without the protection of the Qishen Temple, a group of second and third-tier Emperors against Zhen Wuyang and Tongtian was a slaughter. Although they cultivated the devouring Dao of the Qishen, each of them was exceptionally strong within their tier. However, facing two top fourth-tier Emperors, they had no chance.","When Tongtian and Zhen Wuyang just left the Qishen Temple, they didn’t immediately attack. Instead, they sat cross-legged in the void. This puzzled Liu Ya and Daogong greatly, but they couldn’t beat them, so they could only stand in a standoff.","“You took quite a while to arrive,” Zhen Wuyang said impatiently.","After entering the hall, they directly killed those Emperors. Then, regardless of how they tried to refine the hall forcibly, they found no success, and there were no treasures inside.","Just when they were about to forcefully break the sacrificial altar, an ancient aura emanated, condensing a powerful spirit. In front of this spirit, they couldn’t move. Then, everything went black, and they were transported out of the Qishen Temple.","However, the spirit left them with a sentence: the trial was about to begin, and they should await the arrival of others.","It seemed like they were here to wait for these people.","He was well awa_re of the Eternal Tower’s peak power. As for the so-called Chishui Alliance, apart from Chishui, he didn’t recognize most of the other Emperors.","But it seemed like most of the strong figures from the Eastern Domain of the Original Universe had arrived.","“Hmph!i","The Eternal Tower descended slowly and landed on the Immortal Bone Road. Numerous Emperors inside jumped out.","“You are Zhen Wuyang, the Great Si Region’s Emperor?” Fengyu scanned the","Qishen Temple with her eyes, then asked, her tone exceptionally domineering.","Before coming here, she had gathered information about the Great Desolate","Wilderness. This place was considered Zhen Wuyang’s territory, and the Qishen Temple initially appeared in the Great Si Region. The news had been spread by Zhen Wuyang himself.","Now that she had arrived, she naturally asked Zhen Wuyang first.","“That’s correct!” Zhen Wuyang stood up slowly, retracting his sharp aura, and replied calmly.","Demon Lord Fengyu’s reputation, he had learned about after becoming an Emperor. She was apprenticed to the fifth-tier Emperor Zhutian, controlling the Eternal Tower, the number one power in the Eastern Domain.."]},{"number":5154,"title":"Chapter 5154: You Don’t Even Care About Your Face","paragraphs":["Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","If he were to use the power of the Eternal Tower, Demon Lord Fengyu’s strength would have reached the threshold of the fifth tier, far surpassing everyone present.","All the powerful beings in the vicinity of the Great si Region had once thought that Emperor Donglin was the strongest, followed by the Tongtian Buddha, Feng MO, and himself.","However, after this battle, both he and Tongtian Buddha had reached the pinnacle of the fourth tier, stronger than ordinary dominators.","Especially Tongtian Buddha’s treasured Kasaya had reached the peak treasure level. Few fourth-tier Emperors possessed such an item. With this treasure and his own strength, he could easily rank among the top ten in the Eastern Domain.","“Not bad in strength. Speak about the Qishen Temple!” Fengyu didn’t beat around the bush. He had come a long way; everything here naturally revolved around the Qishen Temple.","Without waiting for Zhen Wuyangs response, Tongtian Buddha spoke, “Great Demon Lord Fengyu, here are two inheritors of the Qishen Temple. When we arrived, we confronted them, but unfortunately, their strength wasn’t sufficient. We didn’t obtain any useful information from them.”","Tongtian Buddha joined his hands in a harmless gesture, a face that appeared harmless, completely belying the fact that he had recently been on a killing spree, battling Liu Ya and Daogong.","Hearing this, Zhen Wuyang didn’t know what to say for a moment. He realized the extent of the gap between him and the others.","The strategy of attacking Donglin had allowed the Qishen Temple’s Emperor to lower his guard. Now, they had thrown dirt onto Liu Ya and Daogong, a tactic that Zhen Wuyang begrudgingly admitted was quite clever.","Zhen Wuyangs face darkened, he glanced at Tongtian Buddha and finally said firmly, “Tongtian is right!”","Liu Ya and Daogongs faces turned beet red, ready to speak up. However, Chishui, standing in the distance, cast a water spell that made them unable to lift their heads.","“Yes, their aura matches the one inside the Qishen Temple perfectly. It seems these two are indeed the inheritors,” Chishui said, feeling no danger. He appeared in front of Fengyu, grabbing Daogongs neck.","“But their strength is too weak, not even reaching the level of a common fourth-tier practitioner!” Chishui expressed some disappointment. This was not the powerful inheritance he had imagined.","Having been falsely accused by Tongtian and Zhen Wuyang, and further scorned for his weak power, Daogong, once the strongest in comprehending the Qishen Dao, felt his face burn with humiliation. He was infuriated, but his lack of strength was undeniable. If he managed to escape this situation unharmed, he vowed to defend the honor of Qishen Temple and erase the shame of this day.","Liu Ya, cunning and deep in strategy, hadn’t anticipated encountering a figure even more shameless than Zhen Wuyang – Tongtian Buddha. Nevertheless, this was the Great Desolate Wilderness, Liu Ya’s Dao Arena. His strength, though barely adequate, reached the top tier here.","“Enough. This is my Dao Arena. If you want to enter the Qishen Temple, go in first and then talk.” Initially, he had planned to be domineering, to let these intruders step on his body before entering the Qishen Temple. But the fact that Tongtian Buddha and Zhen Wuyang could enter the temple right under his nose drained him of the courage to utter such words.","The impressions left by Chishui and Demon Lord Fengyu surpassed even those of Zhen Wuyang and Tongtian Buddha. Either of these two could overpower him, perhaps even lead to his downfall.","“Oh, almost forgot about you!” Chishui Traveler seized Dao Gong. As the strongest present, she couldn’t afford to leave anyone behind.","Buzz!","The immensely powerful Eternal Tower instantly shrank to the size of a palm, directly suppressing Liu Ya beneath it.","“Alright, now talk! ”","Over a hundred Emperors were present, along with thousands of Nine","Revolutions Grand Yan Immortals, many of whom were elites among the Grand Yan Immortals. The weakest among them had crossed the threshold of the fourth- grade Dao. Seeing Demon Lord Fengyu and Wanderer Chishui casually suppress a fourth-tier Emperor, they displayed unprecedented respect.","So, this was the pinnacle of fourth-tier experts?","Suppressing an equal- grade opponent effortlessly!","There was no need to mention Daogong; he was an Emperor who had crossed the fourth-tier threshold. Yet even Liu Ya, who had touched the pinnacle of fourth-tier level, was effortlessly suppressed.","The distance between Zhen Wuyang and Tongtian Buddha and the others had gradually narrowed. They were all on the same boat now, despite Zhen Wuyang and Tongtian Buddha being at the peak of the fourth-tier. Faced with these two peak fourth-tier Emperors, they had little chance of resistance and could only huddle together for warmth.","“Ever since Tongtian and Zhen Wuyang entered, Daogong and I haven’t been able to get in anymore. Even if you kill us, it won’t change anything,” Liu Ya understood the concept of an irreversible trend. At this point, he chose to yield.","He spoke the truth. He was unaware of the changes inside the Qishen Temple; only Tongtian and Zhen Wuyang knew. After the two of them entered the Qishen Temple, eminent figures like Fenghua fell one after another, and the entire temple was enveloped in the Thousand Treasures Kasaya, impenetrable.","These two individuals had placed all the blame on him, causing him immense distress.","Chishui had long attained a level of profound self-awareness, and with just one glance, he could tell it wasn’t a lie. But if what Liu Ya said was true, it posed a problem. The treasures were within easy reach, yet he couldn’t move an inch himself.","The power of the Qishen Temple surpassed any treasure they had ever encountered. Even the combined might of all the Emperors present couldn’t shake the Qishen Temple in the slightest. It was as if it didn’t exist in this void, visible and tangible yet utterly impenetrable,","“Fengyu, have you informed Emperor Zhutian about the matters concerning the Qishen Temple?” Chishui, anxious and cornered, could only indirectly inquire of Fengyu, the Demon Lord.","Fengyu might not be aware of what he sought, but her mentor, Emperor Zhutian, a fifth-tier Emperor who had traveled the River of Time for years, undoubtedly possessed far greater knowledge than these Emperors who seldom ventured out into the universe.","The Qishen Temple’s fame resonated widely in the River of Time. Numerous legends surrounded it. Some formidable beings even believed that the Qishen Temple had connections with ancient civilizations. In this aspect, it indeed shared similarities; the temple’s aura closely resembled that of ancient civilizations.","However, the Qishen Temple had only appeared once or twice in the River of Time. Each time, it drew innumerable emperors to gather and watch.","However, the temple was utterly unreachable. Attempts to suppress or subdue it failed; they couldn’t even lay a finger on it. They could only watch helplessly as the Qishen Temple soared into the endless expanse of the cosmos.","Chishui, the Wanderer, was vaguely familiar with some of these legends. However, it was his first encounter with the Qishen Temple, especially seeing it standing right there.","It didn’t appear as if it could move at all. Now, with the confirmation that the inheritor of the Qishen Temple had received teachings within, their chances seemed significant.","Moreover, the fifth-tier Emperors within the Original Universe were all within the River of Time. He still had a voice now. But if he waited until all the fifth-tier Emperors returned, he would merely be trailing behind, devoid of any voice.."]},{"number":5155,"title":"Chapter 5155: Cunning Chishui","paragraphs":["Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Don’t be fooled by the multitude of forces now aligning with him, forming the Chishui Alliance. Once a fifth-tier Emperor appeared, these people would scatter faster than birds in flight. Currently, they only sought to vie for power through him. He lacked a clan and faction, but his personal strength was substantial, earning him the admiration of many factions.","After all, his individual capability was limited, making him easier to control. If successful, they could let him make the initial choice. In the end, the spoils of war would be divided based on numbers.","Most factions within the Chishui Alliance shared this mindset. Even if Chishui desired monopoly, they had the strength to resist.","Chishui, who was known for his cunning schemes, found himself in a tight spot this time. This was a situation he couldn’t outmaneuver; he had to face it head-on.","If there wasn’t a dominant force at this moment, even if he was a fourth-tier peak Emperor, he wouldn’t gain much among these many strong contenders. The key was to align with a dominant force to counterbalance other peak forces.","He understood this well; it was mutual exploitation between the parties.","However, when it came to dividing the treasures at the end, it might spark a massive free-for-all. At that time, there would be no allies. Everyone before him could be slain.","In the pitch-black void crevice, Wu Zuo sat cross-legged atop the head of the","Black Qi Snake. This Black Qi Snake was a puppet granted to him by the Qishen when he achieved the sixth-tier Emperor status.","Unfortunately, it had suffered significant internal damage and lost its former strength. In its peak state, he could have repaired it. However, restoring its sixth-tier power required numerous treasures, especially considering the severe damage to its divine body. These treasures weren’t something he could find within the universe; his only hope lay within the Qishen Temple.","Being able to participate in this trial was not in vain. Once his power was restored to its peak, few in this river domain could match him. With the Qishen’s inheritance, he could aspire to the pinnacle of the universe.","Watching the constant quarrels among these native Emperors, he found it somewhat amusing. After all, the Qishen Temple was something they could break into – just a bunch of ants.","When the Qishen Temple was originally forged, he had witnessed several gods under Qishen destroying an entire universe, extracting its source, and","infusing it into the temple.","The source of an entire universe – that kind of power was unimaginable. Even the Universe Masters needed several of them to extract it intact. If destroyed, a single Universe Master could achieve it. The challenge lay in extracting it intact without damage.","The power of the source was the core of the universe, and the core of the Qishen Temple was also a similar source, surpassing multiple universes. What the Emperors entered was merely an outer hall; there were no valuable treasures inside. The only useful thing was probably its source.","There were many outer halls in the Qishen Temple, each containing a miniature source.","These source powers were hatched from the core source of the Qishen Temple. Within the source, the Qishen Dao was also contained. To Wu Zuo, directly cultivating the Qishen Dao was the most foolish method.","Moreover, these people claimed to be the 18 divine generals and the 108 envoys, which, in Wu Zuo’s opinion, was incredibly ignorant.","The Qishen Temple was indeed guarded by three main gods, 18 divine generals, and 108 envoys. However, to obtain their inheritance, one needed the strength of a fifth-tier Emperor, at the very least.","In the present, the divine envoys appointed by these natives were all at the Perfected Nine Revolutions level, with many even achieving the status of Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortals level.","They inherited the source contained in the outer hall, arrogantly attempting to grasp the pathways of the major gods and messengers, aiming to reach the pinnacle. It was utterly ridiculous.","If one could truly ascend to the universe’s peak by merely grasping the surface of the Qishen, which was barely present in the outer hall, even the Qishen itself would marvel at this person’s enlightenment. Unfortunately, he had fallen. If he hadn’t, perhaps even the Qishen would have bowed to him as a teacher.","Amidst the people’s arguments, they failed to notice a superpower sneering at them in the void’s crevices. This superpower was also the only living disciple of Qishen.","“Fengyu, don’t be so absolute in your words,” Wu Zuo lowered his voice amidst the cacophony. “God-Emperor Zhutian has been absent for so long. Even if he rushes back now, even with instantaneous movement all the way, it would take a million years. If we use precious treasures for teleportation, it would still take tens of thousands of years. If we enter now, it’s paving the way in advance for the God-Emperor. If you don’t provide useful information now, in case we encounter danger inside, it will be a significant loss for His Divine Majesty.”","Wu Zuo cleared his throat, his eyes shifting as he spoke in a hushed tone, “Or should I say, His Divine Majesty shared information about Qishen Temple with you, and you kept it hidden privately!’","Indeed, his voice was hushed, but all the major Emperors present, even the Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal, clearly heard this statement.","If mere mortals had been present, it might not have been audible.","However, the person in that seat was no ordinary individual. Even if the voice was as faint as a mosquito’s buzz, it was still distinguishable as originating from there.","Moreover, this statement came from Chishui, a peak tier 4 Emperor. The words spoken by an expert of such stature could be considered law in many smaller worlds.","Especially that last sentence, it practically let outsiders know.","If they truly didn’t want others to hear, a simple barrier could completely isolate them, silencing the words.","Upon hearing these words, regardless of belief, a chill settled into the hearts of all. Regardless of whether anyone trusted her, she was now isolated.","Even the Emperors of the Eternal Tower found their trust in Demon Lord Fengyu wavering.","Though these individuals were overlords in their own realms, exceptional beings among countless geniuses, before the grandeur of the Dao, they were just as fragile.","Human nature thrives on comparison. Hearing this statement, whether they believed it or not, everyone would inevitably compare themselves. If they were in Demon Lord Fengyu’s shoes and possessed certain Qishen Temple-related information, like how to gain entry, would they divulge it to others? This was a philosophical aspect of the path of seeking the Dao.","Might rules alone!","In just one word, the stronger one became, the lonelier they were. This kind of loneliness manifested itself in the ruthlessness displayed when competing for opportunities.","Demon Lord Fengyu was a Demon Lord precisely because she disdained these despicable acts. If she could kill someone, she would never utter another word.","“Chishui, you’re seeking death!”","Swish!","The boundless power of the Eternal Tower shot out from Demon Lord Fengyu’s palm, instantly transforming into countless towering figures suspended above Chishui’s head.","“I’ll say it once. Master has not responded to anything related to Qishen Temple.” A hint of killing intent leaked from Demon Lord Fengyu’s delicate face.","Merely from appearances, it was hard to imagine that this slender girl suppressed all the major forces in the Eastern Region.","“Who knows!” Chishui retreated into the alliance hall.","“Rest assured, since I have been recommended as the alliance leader by all of you, I will naturally protect you all. Just stand behind me. Today, 1 want to see how strong this Demon Lord Fengyu really is and how powerful the Eternal","Tower’s might can be..”"]},{"number":5156,"title":"Chapter 5156: Take Sides","paragraphs":["Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","The passionate words spoken by Chishui might have convinced those who didn’t know his character. First, he confronted Demon Lord Fengyu, and now he used all the forces within the alliance as a shield. If he truly intended to fight against Emperor Fengyu, he could have just gone out and faced her, so why bother returning to the main hall?","In their hearts, everyone cursed silently, but outwardly, they had to praise the righteousness of their leader.","This scene amused Tongtian Buddha and Zhen Wuyang.","Indeed, he was a peak tier 4 Emperor, capable of handling any situation flawlessly.","This maneuver made Tongtian and Zhen Wuyang secretly determined – they would never collaborate with Chishui no matter the circumstances.","His shamelessness surpassed the sum of their own.","Great Si Region didn’t have many strong individuals; there was only Zhen Wuyang, who couldn’t be considered a significant force. He was fine.","Tongtian Buddha was different; he ruled over 3,000 Great Worlds and had dozens of Emperor-level experts under his command. Although Dongyan and Wuliang each led their own faction, the overall situation was now irreversible. They couldn’t stir up any waves.","Dongyan had fallen, and the Dongyan Realm naturally fell into his hands. Wuliang was considerably weaker and also needed him.","Taking advantage of this opportunity, he could consolidate his power, but all of this hinged on Qishen Temple being the primary force.","Behind Chishui, six tier 4 Emperors appeared, two of whom were at the peak of tier 4.","Facing Demon Lord Fengyu alone, he only had a 10 percent chance of winning but a 100 percent certainty of escaping with his life. Even though he wasn’t afraid of Demon Lord Fengyu, he couldn’t let the others in the Chishui Alliance sit back and watch.","“Brother Chishui, we’re here to help you!” several Emperors spoke up, their words respectful, yet their disdain for Chishui!s actions was evident.","“Demon Lord Fengyu, don’t think we small forces are easy targets.”","Following this, several tier 3 Emperors appeared one after another, standing behind Chishui and the few tier 4 Emperors.","The powerful figures from the Eternal Tower emerged, observing the situation. Several tier 4 Emperors and dozens of tier 3 Emperors appeared behind Demon Lord Fengyu, exuding immense pressure. Although these Emperors were displeased with Fengyu’s sudden action, she was the ruler of the Eternal Tower. At this moment, they had to intervene to maintain order.","“Fengyu, hold on!” Chishui suddenly called out, easing the tension among the crowd.","With the Qishen Temple right in front of them and no benefits gained yet, no one wanted a conflict at this moment. A battle involving so many powerful beings would undoubtedly result in casualties. The cultivation path of Emperor-level experts was arduous, and nobody wanted their own people to perish, let alone themselves.","In the chaotic brawl of so many powerful beings, even a tier 4 Emperor could accidentally fall, not to mention the tier 2 and 3 Emperors. As for the ordinary tier 1 Emperors and Grand Yan Immortals, they didn’t even have the ability to participate in the fight.","In battles among powerful Emperors, the residual might of their clashes could annihilate them. They didn’t have the right to participate, let alone to watch.","Fengyu glanced back at her own allies, sensing that they also preferred to avoid conflict for now. She softened her tone. “Chishui, what else do you want to say?”","“Fengyu, everyone knows we will have to fight sooner or later. But before we do, it’s best if everyone picks a side,” Chishui said, casting a glance at Tongtian Buddha, Zhen Wuyang, and others who had already joined his alliance.","The crowd inwardly cursed at his cunning nature. They knew this old man had ulterior motives.","However, his words caught Fengyu’s attention. Fengyu also glanced at the crowd, especially focusing on Zhen Wuyang and Tongtian Buddha. Peak tier 4 Emperors were exceedingly rare, numbering less than ten in the entire one-fourth of the universe in the Eastern Domain.","They represented the absolute pinnacle of power. Particularly since the tier 5","Emperors were absent, the Eternal Tower couldn’t rank at the forefront of peak forces. The main reason was the absence of a tier 5 Emperor. If they could now win the allegiance of two amazing tier 4 Emperors, they could easily suppress the Chishui Alliance in future conflicts.","“In that case, everyone, state your allegiance. If you are willing to join the","Eternal Tower, you are most welcome. My Master will return soon, and the Qishen Temple’s fate will ultimately be decided by the tier 5 Emperors. You all should think it over carefully,” Fengyu warned, her words laced with both threat and caution.","The powerful figures from the Eternal Tower emerged, observing the situation. Several tier 4 Emperors and dozens of tier 3 Emperors appeared behind Demon Lord Fengyu, exuding immense pressure. Although these Emperors were displeased with Fengyu’s sudden action, he was the ruler of the Eternal Tower. At this moment, they had to intervene to maintain order.","Not only were they speaking to Zhen Wuyang and Tongtian Buddha, but they were also trying to shake the confidence within the Chishui Alliance.","For them, a tier 5 Emperor was like a god, an irreversible existence. If they ended up with nothing in the end and offended a tier 5 Emperor, it was better to join the Eternal Tower early on.","“Hmph!” Chishui snorted coldly, looking somewhat embarrassed as he glanced at Zhen Wuyang and Tongtian Buddha, and then at the strong individuals within the Chishui Alliance.","“l won’t hide it from you all. Chang Shentian of the Northern Domain has already contacted me secretly. They still have a position for a Grand Guest Officer. I could join them at any time, but I chose not to,” Chishui said with a touch of generosity in his voice. He continued loudly, “Which one of us isn’t a pride of heaven? Cultivation is not easy, and we still have to endure the oppression from those peak forces. Don’t let their sweet talk deceive you.”","“If you join these peak forces now, you will be cannon fodder. Even if the tier 5 Emperor returns and seizes Qishen Temple, do you really believe they will share the spoils with you, the younger generation without background or strength? Don’t dream. Opportunities are seized, not distributed.”","Wanderer Chishui’s angry shouts actually frightened some ambitious solitary Emperors.","However, most of what he said was true. Joining peak forces at this time meant becoming cannon fodder. Even if they obtained Qishen Temple in the future, the tier 5 Emperor would pick first, followed by a bunch of juniors. They wouldn’t stand a chance.","Although Demon Lord Fengyu was a regional leader, she wasn’t very articulate. Seeing this situation, she could only briefly describe the power of the tier 5 Emperor to pacify them.","But the stronger the tier 5 Emperor was, the more they feared, afraid that they wouldn’t even have the ability to resist in the future.","Zhen Wuyang considered quietly. He had no faction, no background, relying solely on his own strength. Joining the Eternal Tower at this moment seemed like a wise choice. With his strength, he was second only to Demon Lord Fengyu in the Eternal Tower. Even if he became cannon fodder, he still had the power to survive.","As for the Chishui Alliance, he didn’t consider it. Firstly, the distribution of benefits didn’t suit him, and secondly, Chishui was too unreliable, always ready to run away.","“Ruler Fengyu, I am Zhen Wuyang. I am willing to enter the Eternal Tower.” After careful consideration, Zhen Wuyang didn’t hesitate and directly bowed to Demon Lord Fengyu.","He even addressed her with the more flattering ‘Ruler’, rather than ‘Demon Lord’, which sounded more pleasing.."]},{"number":5157,"title":"Chapter 5157: The Fall of Daogong","paragraphs":["Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","“Zhen Wuyang, have you considered carefully? By joining the Eternal Tower alone, you will face exclusion. Why not join the Chishui Alliance with me?” Tongtian Buddha had an urgent look on his face as he shouted. To outsiders, he appeared genuinely concerned for his friend.","Only Zhen Wuyang and Liu Ya understood that Tongtian Buddha had malicious intentions.","“Zhen Wuyang, you...” Wanderer Chishui’s thoughts were cunning. How could he not understand Tongtian Buddha’s scheme? He sighed deeply.","“Zhen Wuyang, your choice is wise. I swear, Demon Lord Fengyu, I won’t let you face death in a losing battle. When our master returns, I will introduce you to him. And your Great Si Region will also be protected by our Eternal Tower,” Demon Lord Fengyu remained pragmatic, offering Zhen Wuyang a reassuring pill.","Tongtian Buddha looked on, a mix of envy and jealousy, yet he couldn’t show it.","Unlike Zhen Wuyang, he didn’t have the freedom to choose. If he were alone, he would have chosen the Eternal Tower. Even in the present circumstances, following Demon Lord Fengyu was undoubtedly more reliable than following Wanderer Chishui.","However, he had a large group of Emperors and Grand Yan Immortals behind him. He could only join the Chishui Alliance and take advantage of the Alliance’s benefits.","Upon hearing Demon Lord Fengyu’s promise, Zhen Wuyang repeatedly expressed his gratitude, “Thank you, Lord Fengyu. I will be at your service in every way. ”","His words greatly pleased Demon Lord Fengyu.","Though she held great influence in the Eternal Tower, the several top-tier Emperors under her command also held significant power. She couldn’t suppress them. Now, with Zhen Wuyang joining, he naturally wanted to pull him into her inner circle.","Zhen Wuyang moved directly to the side of the Eternal Tower, positioning himself near Demon Lord Fengyu. He lagged half a step behind the other top-tier Emperors to show his respect.","The veteran powerhouses of the Eternal Tower, although not knowxing much about Zhen Wuyang, recognized him as someone discerning. They all smiled and congratulated him, expressing their good wishes.","“Alliance Leader Chishui, I am willing to bring my strong warriors under the alliance’s banner!” Tongtian Buddha’s face was earnest as he led his people into the grand hall of the Chishui Alliance.","This outcome didn’t surprise anyone. Tongtian was indeed suitable for joining the Chishui Alliance. Besides, when Zhen Wuyang mentioned joining the Eternal Tower, Tongtian had already made his stance clear.","The powerful beings in the Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm had no choice but to follow him. Even if they had a choice, their strength was so weak that no one would consider them. It was better to follow Tongtian Buddha, enjoying the protection of a fourth-tier Emperor, at least avoiding bullying within the Chishui Alliance.","The Chishui Alliance was vast, with many powerful members. However, the top-tier experts were evenly matched. As a fourth-tier top expert, Tongtian Buddha ranked among the top three in the Chishui Alliance.","The powerful figures in the Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm benefited from this alliance. Upon their recent allegiance, they were placed directly at the top of the Chishui Temple, just below a few other major dominant forces.","Despite the Tongtian Buddha possessing top-tier strength at tier 4, their subordinate forces didn’t quite match up. They were considered major powers, not quite reaching the pinnacle. This was primarily due to the formidable might of the Tongtian Buddha. Without their backing, these individuals wouldn’t have held such prominent positions.","Once these two individuals had firmly taken sides, the gazes of the others turned sharp.","“How about we kill both of them first?” Chishui suggested, looking at the bound Liu Ya and Daogong.","Demon Lord Fengyu nodded in agreement. These two inheritors of the Qishen Temple had refused to divulge any specific information about the temple. Keeping them alive was a threat. It was better to kill them now.","“You scum are unworthy of the great Qishen’s blessing. A group of shallow practitioners daring to kill me,” Daogong raved. He and Liu Ya, just like the heroes of ancient times, refused to bow to Zhen Wuyang. Now, they maintained the same attitude. Since they couldn’t obtain the blessings of the Qishen Temple, no one else should harbor such delusions either.","The brilliance of devouring the Great Dao instantly covered his entire body. Even in death, he wanted to take a few unlucky ones with him.","Boom!","A force comparable to the self-destruction of the Donglin instantly swept across the entire void.","“Enter the Eternal Tower, quickly!” Demon Lord Fengyu’s face turned pale. She hurriedly ushered some second and third-tier Emperors behind her into the Eternal Tower.","As for the fourth-tier Emperors, they had already teleported far away.","Although Daogongs self-destruction couldn’t kill them, it would injure them. Now was a critical moment in the battle for the Qishen Temple. If they got injured, the cost would far outweigh the gain.","The second and third-tier Emperors found shelter within the Eternal Tower, but the fate of the Chishui Temple’s many powerful individuals was grim.","No matter how Chishui Wanderer tried to shield them, countless powerful streams of energy surged into the Chishui Temple. They killed a large number of Grand Yan Immortals and even caused the downfall of several unlucky tier 1 Emperors.","Several breaths later, Daogongs aura finally completely dissipated. This time, he had truly fallen. There would be no chance of revival. The primordial power of the leaning Great Dao transformed back into Yan power and returned to the universe’s source.","Learning from this experience, Wanderer Chishui and the Demon Lord Fengyu immediately charged towards Liu Ya.","“Do not force me. Do not forget, this is my Dao Arena!” shouted Liu Ya in anger. Utilizing the origin within the Great Desolate Wilderness, he broke free from the constraints. With one hand grasping the origin of the wilderness and the other holding the Dao of Desolation, he stood his ground.","Chishui hesitated for a moment. Daogong was merely an ordinary fourth-tier Emperor, while Liu Ya was at the pinnacle of the fourth-tier. Moreover, he controlled the Great Desolate Wilderness, being the Dao Ancestor of this land. If he chose to self-destruct, they would also be harmed.","“Why must you kill me? I can join any one of you, and we can negotiate,” Liu","Ya’s brows furroowed. He had already died once; he did not want to die again.","Millions of years of accumulation left no room for error.","He had given up the path of the Qishen Dao, which was the Great Devouring Dao, and instead, he controlled the Great Desolate Wilderness. He was no longer the person he was in the Ancient Era, and now, he only wanted to survive and then become stronger with the help of the Qishen Temple.","He didn’t dare dream of becoming the Universe Master; achieving the fifth-tier Emperor satisfied him. That was also the reason he abandoned the Qishen Dao.","“Oh, how do you propose we negotiate?” inquired Chishui, his interest piqued.","If Liu Ya could provide useful information, perhaps sparing him was not out of the question.","The main difference between them and Zhen and the Tongtian","Buddha was that Liu Ya and Daogong were both inheritors of the Qishen Temple. They were reluctant to say anything. If they left them alive and they entered the Qishen Temple again and fled with it, they would be in big trouble.","They could feel the power of the Qishen Temple. If they were determined to leave, not to mention them, even a fifth-tier Emperor could not stop them.","When the meat is at your mouth, losing it would be a tremendous loss. If a fifth-tier Emperor returned later, they would have no choice but to kill them.."]},{"number":5158,"title":"Chapter 5158: Looking at the History of the Extinction of the Ancient Era","paragraphs":["Chapter 5158: Looking at the History of the Extinction of the Ancient Era","Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","In the end, the Qishen Temple had never ceased its activities, and there were never any rumors of inheritors before. This opportunity was possibly the only one in countless chaos cycles.","“Liu Ya, speak up! If it’s beneficial to us, sparing your life is not out of the question!” Demon Lord Fengyu also halted her movement.","Both of them stared at Liu Ya, fearing any sudden moves he might make.","“Two esteemed ones, the Qishen Temple isn’t as great as you imagine!” Liu Ya swallowed hard, revealing everything about the Qishen Temple.","As he said, there weren’t many advantages to the Qishen Temple. Perhaps the only advantage was the Dao of the Qishen, incredibly powerful. Achieving the status of the Universe Master was not just a matter of enlightenment, but the crucial issue was Liu Ya didn’t believe anyone could replicate the Qishen’s grand Dao and reach the pinnacle of the universe.","“That’s all I know. If you don’t believe me, then I can only self-destruct!”","Chishui and Fengyu fell into silence.","If what Liu Ya said was true, it seemed like the Qishen Temple didn’t need their presence. The Grand Yan Immortals could handle it; their role was merely to aid in the fusion of Daos.","In the crevices of the void, concealed within, Wu Zuo watched silently, sneering. “Exactly, it’s not suitable for you at all. Hurry up and leave!”","Even if these people entered the trial, they wouldn’t gain much. From Wu Zuo’s perspective, their aptitudes were too poor. They wouldn’t garner the true spirit’s attention. It mainly depended on those fifth-tier Emperors.","“Fengyu, what do you think?” Chishui turned to Demon Lord Fengyu beside him. At this moment, he truly didn’t know what to do.","Clearly disappointed with the Qishen Temple, what they wanted to hear was not this. They hoped to learn about how powerful the Qishen Temple was. They even wished Liu Ya would self-destruct on the spot. Only then would they be more convinced that the treasures within the Qishen Temple were astonishing. They wanted to force the inheritor to self-destruct and still refuse to divulge any useful information.","But everything didn’t unfold as they had imagined.","“Let him live for now, but he will be suppressed within my Eternal Tower. Do you agree?” Demon Lord Fengyu said calmly.","Wanderer Chishui understood. If something went wrong, it wouldn’t be good for anyone. Although he didn’t know if what Liu Ya said was true, since they had inherited Qishen Temple for so many years, not to mention a fifth-tier Emperor, they hadn’t even been able to cultivate a top fourth-tier one. Either they were worthless, or Qishen Temple truly didn’t have the legendary strength.","“Naturally, the power of the Eternal Tower is limitless. It’s perfect for suppressing this person and preventing any mishaps,” Chishui said with a faint smile.","Their relationship had also eased.","Liu Ya breathed a sigh of relief, at least he had saved his own life.","But considering they had only recently revived, and now he was the only one left alive, it was a bit depressing.","If they had knovvn it would end like this, they might as well have joined Zhen","Wuyang in the Ancient Era. With Zhen Wuyangs stunning talents in the Ancient Era, maybe they would all be fifth-tier Emperors by now. They could have been protected, and perhaps their strength would be much greater than it is now.","It was all Daogongs fault. He was someone who truly treated Qishen as a god, an absolute fanatic, just like the leaders in the Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm, utterly stubborn.","Liu Ya, who had come to terms with everything, even gave a slight smile to","Zhen Wuyang as they entered the Eternal Tower.","From that smile, Zhen Wuyang could feel Liu Ya’s sincerity.","This smile also completely dissipated the last glimmer of hope in the Great Si Region towards the Ancient Era.","Zhen Wuyang didn’t feel good either. After all, he was a powerhouse of the","Great Si Region. Although he hated these old guys, now the only surviving Emperor of the Ancient Era had also been suppressed in the Eternal Tower, and he had also joined the Eternal Tower.","How tragic!","If in the Ancient Era, he could have controlled Qishen Temple, how wonderful would that have been?","Even if these Emperors had allowed him to become a messenger in Qishen Temple, he wouldn’t have suppressed them all, and he wouldn’t have ended up in this situation.","Since the Ancient Era was no more, the Great Si Region had also entered the era protected by the Eternal Tower. Zhen Wuyang had become a powerful figure in the Eternal Tower.","And at this moment, the entire universe was undergoing a transformation. The ancient chaotic battles had long disappeared, and the peaceful era accumulated over countless chaotic epochs was now shattered.","Now, the Age of Qishen was about to begin.","A faint glow emanated from Qishen Temple, and an ancient call spread throughout the entire universe.","In this moment, beings in every corner sensed the summons.","It was the brilliance of ancient times, a vast scene presented in the minds of these beings.","At this moment, all the Yan Immortals in the universe took a step forward, entering the world of Qishen.","Inside the Qishen Temple.","The Qishen Temple appeared to outsiders as two separate halls, but it was more than it seemed.","The outer hall of Qishen had spontaneously emerged from the source within the temple after Qishen’s fall. It contained the profound teachings of Qishen and the three divine masters.","Now, Qishen Temple was like a universe itself. It not only encompassed the source of the universe but also continuously created subsidiary worlds. These subsidiary worlds were like outer halls, interconnected with the inner hall, which was the true Qishen Temple.","Yet, even the inner hall was just the tip of the iceberg; the real core was the Source Divine Hall.","The origin of the universe was grand and magnificent. It carried the entire universe’s functioning. Practitioners were merely incidental products. Its power surpassed the imagination of any practitioner, explaining why there were so few Universe Masters in the River of Time.","The Source Divine Hall.","The core of Qishen Temple!","A vaguely discernible elderly figure drifted within the vortex of source. In one hand, he held an ancient book, and the other rested behind his back.","“l never expected to sleep for so long. The Ancient Era feels like just last night!” The ethereal elder sighed as he perused the ancient tome.","He was the true spirit of Qishen Temple, simultaneously a formidable being controlling the essence of the entire temple. His power rivaled that of the lords of the universe. This was why Qishen Temple, even after drifting through numerous epochs, remained unconquered by those Universal Masters.","“Great True Spirit, are you really planning to initiate the highest trial in the Original Universe? This seems different from what our master arranged back in the day!” A guardian respectfully stood by, head bowed.","He was genuinely puzzled, but he was merely a guardian. At most, he could voice his question. The true manager of the entire Qishen Temple was the true spirit.","Hearing his question, the true spirit patiently explained, “AQi, you don’t understand. Indeed, our master didn’t plan it this way back then. However, our master also told me that going with the flow surpasses everything else.”","“Going with the flow? What does that mean?” AQi, the guardian, was somewhat perplexed.","“Life is like a play, fool!” the true spirit laughed and scolded.."]},{"number":5159,"title":"Chapter 5159: Universe Deity-Demon List","paragraphs":["Chapter 5159: Universe Deity-Demon List","Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","As the true spirit of the Qishen Temple and the controller of the primal power, his wisdom surpassed that of the cultivators. Even after such a long slumber, he remained as vibrant as life itself, experiencing joy and sorrow, laughter and sadness.","The guardian pondered. He was once the servant of the old master. After the fall of the Qishen, he became the guardian, along with eight others, tasked with watching over the Qishen’s tomb for years.","“Oh, right. After absorbing the Grand Yan Immortals into the affiliated worlds, temporarily restrain their battles. The living beings in this Original Iniverse are far from sufficient to activate the highest trial,” the true spirit said calmly, dissatisfied with the number of Grand Yan Immortals in the Original Universe.","If the Emperors were to know, they would probably go crazy!","All the Grand Yan Immortals in just one Great Si Region could be counted in billions. How many were there in the entire Original Universe?","“Yes, but the source in other universes are too strong; it’s not easy to plunder extensively!” The guardian felt a bit uneasy. After all, he was just a guardian. He had only recently started accepting the management of the Qishen Temple under the command of the true spirit.","Many things were still unclear to him. If he were suddenly sent to other universes to plunder Grand Yan Immortals, he wouldn’t know what to do.","The Grand Yan Immortals of the Original Universe were manageable because he could use the Qishen’s virtual shadow formed by the source to directly move all the Grand Yan Immortals into the affiliated worlds of the Qishen Temple. But it would be troublesome to bring in Grand Yan Immortals from other universes.","The source of the original universe had been devoured by the Forbidden Demon Lord, making it weak. The universal source of the Qishen Temple could easily suppress others, and combined with the silent approval of the highest rules, he could easily summon all the Grand Yan Immortals into the affiliated worlds. However, the sources of other universes were intact, and the highest rules were emotionless.","‘I’ve done what 1 can to help your Original Universe; 1 won’t risk reaching into other universes,’ the true spirit thought.","“Everything can be flexible. Since we can’t bring all of them over, let’s just bring the prodigies who have comprehended the third-grade Dao. That should reduce the number by 90 percent, right? For universes far away, plunder the second-grade Dao Grand Yan Immortals, and for those even farther, plunder the Ultimate Dao Grand Yan Immortals. There are only a few of those in each universe; this should be simple!” he suggested.","“That’s easy. You are truly wise, my lord!” Although the guardian wasn’t very clever, he knew how to flatter.","“Haha, since it can be done, go ahead boldly! I still need to think about how to deal with the Grand Yan Immortals and the Emperors.” The true spirit smiled and continued to peruse the ancient books in his hand.","The guardian immediately bowed and left the primal hall.","In the vast primal source, only the true spirit remained. He turned the pages of the book. his brows furrowing.","“This universe is quite interesting. So many prodigies were born simultaneously; it’s probably because of that Forbidden Demon Lord,” the true spirit muttered to himself.","“Yes, not bad at all! I’ve finally completed this list.”","Satisfied, the true spirit smoothed out his brows and directly replicated the contents of the ancient book onto a massive stone tablet.","The stone tablet emitted an ancient aura. Although it appeared to be just a stone tablet, its value was no less than a top-tier eternal treasure. In the Original Universe, the only eternal treasure, the ‘Eternal Tower’, was merely a low-grade item. This was because the Emperor Zhutian was notorious for being overly protective. When he left, he couldn’t rest assured about his disciples and old subordinates, so he left an eternal treasure that could assist them to his disciple.","Many fifth-tier Emperors in the river of time did not have an eternal treasure. When the Emperor Zhutian was still a fourth-rank emperor, he obtained an inheritance from an ancient civilization when he first entered the river of time. Not only did he obtain three eternal treasures, but he also inherited the true teachings of that ancient existence, directly advancing to a fifth-rank emperor. He became an incredibly powerful presence among the fifth-tier","Emperors. That was why he generously left the Eternal Tower to his disciple.","Understanding Tongtian’s intention, he immediately realized it was a suspicion aimed at certain Emperors for their underhanded methods. Without delay, he leaped out of the grand hall.","“Fengyu, explain this!” Chishui’s expression was furious.","Tongtian had just pledged allegiance to him, and now, such a thing happened. It was undoubtedly someone’s hidden revenge. Otherwise, who would be so bored as to kill all the Yan immortals from 3,000 Worlds?","“Explain? Do I have anything to explain to you?” Demon Lord Fengyu was perplexed. She couldn’t fathom what schemes Chishui was up to again.","While the two were in a standoff, Zhen Wuyang received a message from Yu Chang. All the Yan immortals within the Great Si Region had disappeared.","Zhen Wuyang promptly informed Demon Lord Fengyu about the situation. This news caused an uproar. Messages from homeworlds kept pouring in one after another, reporting the disappearance of all Yan immortals. “This must be the doing of Qishen Temple!” Chishui nearly burst into laughter.","It was truly audacious. All the Yan immortals in the entire universe had vanished. Leaving aside whether these Yan immortals were still alive, just the scale of this operation was colossal. No Emperor could accomplish such a feat.","As for whether they lived or died, Chishui couldn’t care less!","Buzz!","An ancient aura suddenly surged.","The aura emanated from Qishen Temple but manifested in the void of the entire universe.","A massive stone stele descended from the void, visible to everyone in the universe.","“The Universe Deity-Demon List!”"]},{"number":5160,"title":"Chapter 5160: Ranking","paragraphs":["Chapter 5160: Ranking","Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Original Universe","Countless cultivators gazed up at the starry sky.","A massive stone stele, resembling the sun and the moon, was visible from anywhere. Simultaneously, those Yan immortals who had entered the affiliated world of the Qishen Temple also saw the list.","The Universe Deity-Demon List was divided into Heaven, Earth, and Human categories.","The Heaven category corresponded to Emperor-level experts, the Earth category to Grand Yan Immortals, and the Human category naturally to those Yan immortals.","However, the Yan immortals of the current era had been astonishingly brought into the Qishen Temple’s affiliated world.","As for the Grand Yan Immortals, they had long transcended the world’s constraints, so the Qishen Temple couldn’t astonish them.","Yet, given such a tremendous opportunity, even if the Temple didn’t intervene, these Grand Yan Immortals would come on their own.","As for the Emperors, that went without saying. They were beings beyond the universe’s control, yet they longed for the Qishen Temple even more.","The rankings on the three lists were from top to bottom. The Heaven list featured over 10,000 Emperor-level experts.","The list was arranged based on the strengths of the experts in the Original Universe, If Emperors from other universes arrived, the Universe","Deity-Demon List would accurately judge and include them.","This was an unparalleled eternal treasure, not only boundlessly powerful but also able to accurately calculate an Emperor’s strength.","“Look, there’s the Patriarch’s name on the Heaven list,” exclaimed a young woman from the Dream Clan standing behind the Dream Dao Ancestor.","This exclamation drew everyone’s gaze. “Dream Dao Ancestor, ranked 97th on the Heaven list, a top fourth-tier expert from the medium-grade world, Great Dream Realm.”","The introduction below the name stated clearly, even marking the expert’s strength and the world where their Dao Arena were located.","In another part of the Great Desolate Wilderness, Jian Wushuang and his companions also noticed this list.","However, they had no time to spare. If the Emperors from the","Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm didn’t arrive soon, they would all perish here.","“Brother Jiu Yu, when will the assisting Emperors arrive? We can’t hold on much longer!” gasped Jin Hong, one of the geniuses from the Dongyan Realm. They had been fighting against those monsters for a whole day.","Their Yan power had reached the point of exhaustion. If it weren’t for the fact that, this time because of the Qishen Temple, they had exchanged all their assets for pills, they would have all perished already.","Now, the pills were used up. If reinforcements didn’t come soon, they could only meet their end here.","In addition to dealing with these monsters, a portion of them also had to protect Jian Wushuang and Hu Qing, the two burdens.","“Luo Shui, come back to me. You don’t need to protect those two useless people. Hurry and take my place; I can’t hold on anymore,” Jiu Yu said, ignoring him completely. He had to give up on Hu Qing and Jian Wushuang. It was a matter of life and death now. Even if the Emperors blamed him in the future, he could explain. After all, the Dao was difficult to traverse. He had become a fourth-tier complete Grand Yan Immortal with great difficulty. He couldn’t die for someone else just because of an Emperor’s words.","If he knew that their Emperor Dongyan had already fallen, he didn’t know if he would be happy or sad.","Luo Shui was also in a dire situation. Although the powerful monsters were being held off by those fourth-tier complete Grand Yan Immortals, she still had to deal with two Nine Revolutions-level Sprites.","Even though she only had a fourth-grade Dao, she could still barely cope with these two Nine Revolutions Sprites who had no consciousness. However, she couldn’t break free at the moment. What the Emperor had instructed naturally outweighed that genius from Dongyan Realm.","“The Emperor’s instructions cannot be abandoned,” Luo Shui said softly but firmly. After speaking, she devoted her whole being to dealing with those two monsters, ignoring the genius.","Jian Wushuang hid behind Luo Shui, his eyes fixed on the Universe Deity-Demon List. Hu Qing did the same.","They had initially intended to help, but the sudden appearance of the stone tablet left them utterly stunned. Everyone present was momentarily baffled by its abrupt appearance, unsure of what had transpired. However, amidst the chaos, they scarcely spared it a glance before plunging back into the battle.","Jian Wushuang and Hu Qing, on the other hand, were entranced by the Universe Deity-Demon List.","Whether it was their own intuition or the list assisting them in identifying their rankings, they immediately spotted their names at first glance.","“Hu Qing, Rank 160 million, Six Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal, hailing from the high- grade world of Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm.”","High- grade world?","It seemed that, unconsciously, Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm had already restored the source of the heavenly realm!","Narrowing his eyes, Hu Qing studied the list, which laid bare the true strength of many individuals.","For instance, Tongtian Buddha was no longer just a Dao Ancestor; he had ascended to the position of a Ruler. As for himself, he was ranked 160 million, a considerably high position in the entire universe. Especially considering he was only a Six Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal.","Most of those ranked higher than him were close to the Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortals, with only a few of them being Nine-turn Grand Yan Immortals.","Jian Wushuangs ranking was not too different from Hu Qings, despite being only a Three-turn Grand Yan Immortal.","At the same time, many powerhouses also noticed Jian Wushuang.","“Jian Wushuang, Rank 167,849,099, Three Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal, originating from the middle realm of Great Si Region.”","A Three Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal managing to secure a position around 167 million astonished many Grand Yan Immortals, making them question whether the list was erroneous.","To understand, it’s crucial to know that almost all the five billion Grand Yan Immortals were at the Ninth Revolutions level. There were only a few scattered individuals at the Six Revolutions level among them. Each of these individuals was extraordinary, especially those Sixth Revolutions Grand Yan Immortals who ranked among the top two billion. They represented the pinnacle of the ultimate path.","But a Three Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal somehow managed to secure a position among the 160 millionth rank. This fact was beyond belief for everyone.","The names on the list seemed endless, but only the top trillion were displayed. Among these trillion, less than 10 percent were at the Three Revolutions level, most being at the Six Revolutions level.","This gave an idea of just how remarkable Jian Wushuangs rank was.","Jian Wushuang himself was not surprised by his rank. He was well aware of his own strength, much stronger than Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortals but weaker than those at the Perfected Nine Revolutions level.","He looked upward, all the way to the top.","Information about billions of people appeared in his mind. Such memory capacity was effortless for Jian Wushuang at the Grand Yan Immortal level. He could even easily do this at the Yan Immortal level.","“Luo Shui, Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal, ranking over 400 million!” Jian Wushuang shook his head bitterly.","His focus wasn’t on those ordinary Grand Yan Immortals; he directly turned his attention to the top thousand ranks.","“Jiu Yu, ranking 456, Perfected Nine Revolutions Circle Grand Yan Immortal, from the high- grade world of Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm.”","This ranking surprised Jian Wushuang. He hadn’t expected Jiu Yu to be so powerful. Although he had heard that Jiu Yu had integrated several Dao paths, considering this ranking spanned the entire universe, being within the top 500 was extraordinary.."]},{"number":5161,"title":"Chapter 5161: A Big Deal","paragraphs":["Chapter 5161: A Big Deal","Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","The arrival of the Universe Deity-Demon List initially left everyone puzzled, and then deeply shaken.","People were baffled by the sudden appearance of this list, and then awed by the immense power of the rankings.","Such a grand gesture, coupled with the disappearance of all Yan Immortals, led the remaining Grand Yan Immortals to speculate.","Those with connections were fortunate; they knew that the Qishen Temple had emerged, connecting these two events. However, the lone wanderers without affiliations ventured into perilous lands or secluded domains, attempting to seclude themselves and evade the impending turmoil.","Little did they know, this list’s arrival marked the fairest assessment of all practitioners in the universe. Even the weakest among them could obtain abundant treasures from the Qishen Temple.","Similar to the Yan Immortals who had already entered the affiliated world of the Qishen Temple.","As soon as they entered the affiliated world of the Qishen Temple, they began to comprehend, causing all Yan Immortals in the entire universe to comprehend as well. This was merely a method employed by the True Spirits to prevent them from fighting among themselves.","Such a grand gesture was unprecedented.","In the 97th affiliated world, within a ring-shaped realm, numerous starry continents floated. Not only were there Yan Immortals who had been plundered into this world, but also some powerful wild beasts born within the realm.","However, these wild beasts and indigenous practitioners seemed oblivious to the Yan Immortals who had been displaced here. They continued living their leisurely lives.","Soon, a voice echoed throughout the entire universe.","“The Qishen Temple is officially open.”","This grand voice echoed in the hearts of everyone.","In the midst of the vast void of the Great Desolate Wilderness, the battle was still raging. Jiu Yu and the others felt the summons, but they were currently struggling on the edge of life and death, with no attention to spare for such matters.","On Jiu Yu’s side, one person stood alone, resisting hundreds of ghostly beings at the Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal level. He had reached the point of exhaustion, his strength nearly depleted.","“Damn it, why hasn’t the Emperor arrived yet!” Jiu Yu, usually composed, couldn’t help but curse under his breath. The numbers of these ghostly beings were overwhelming. Although he could kill one at the Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal level with a flip of his hand, he couldn’t contend with their sheer quantity.","Boom!","Another Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal couldn’t hold on any longer. He had to burn his own Dao, unleashing his most powerful strike. Then his entire body began to disintegrate, eventually vanishing into the void.","One after another, the remaining Grand Yan Immortals burned their own origin, unable to escape and unable to exterminate all the ghostly beings. They had no choice but to burn their own Dao sources to make one final contribution for others.","Jian Wushuang also snapped out of his anger amidst the roars. He turned his head and glanced at Hu Qing, hurriedly saying, “Don’t look, they can’t hold on anymore.”","Upon hearing the shout, Hu Qings eyes cleared a bit. Behind him, a rift in space appeared, and a phantom-like ghostly being was desperately struggling to break free from the engulfing void.","“Be careful!” Luo Shui, standing beside her, exclaimed, attempting to retreat and help. But in her haste, the ghostly being seized the opportunity and lunged directly at Luo Shui’s neck.","Clang!","Whoosh!","An incredibly elegant sword energy, along with its peculiar angle, slashed toward Luo Shui’s chest.","The sharpness of the sword energy sent shivers down one’s spine. The power of this strike was even stronger than when dealing with Xiang Bingyun, and it was more stable.","Splurt!","The three Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal-level ghostly beings entwined with Luo Shui directly turned into a wisp of black smoke, then completely disappeared.","Luo Shui stood still for a moment. When Jian Wushuang made his move, all she saw was a seemingly casual sword strike, without sensing any trace of the profound Dao power. However, as the sword energy passed by her, she felt a terrifying aura.","She was certain that if that sword had struck her, she would have undoubtedly perished.","“How can he be so strong?” Luo Shui wondered, but she didn’t have time to dwell on it now.","“Hu Qing, stay here to protect Fellow Daoist Luo Shui. 1 will go help the others!” Jian Wushuang said, flashing a faint smile as he passed by Luo Shui.","“Be careful, Kind Sir!” Hu Qing cautioned, then swiftly turned around, a brown staff piercing through a monster attempting to crawl out of a crack in the void.","Jian Wushuang ascended, surveying the area before launching his rescue mission.","Swish! Swish! Swish!","Several swords were swung, instantly annihilating numerous ghosts at the level of Nine Revolutions.","“It’s strange. These ghosts clearly have no consciousness, so why are they so afraid of Heart power?” Although Jian Wushuang hadn’t deliberately infused Heart power into his casual strikes, he had already grasped the sword","techniques of the Heartsword World. Even his casual strikes contained a bit of power.","Puffs!","Dozens of ghosts dispersed, instantly alleviating the pressure on the local battlefield.","Whether it was the leader of the Tongtian Buddha world or other cultivators, they all wore expressions of disbelief.","A Three Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal casually swung his sword, directly obliterating dozens of ghosts at the level of the Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal. This level of strength difference was staggering.","Especially the prodigy from the Dongyan Realm was dumbfounded. He clearly felt that Jian Wushuangs Dao was weak, so why was his strength so overwhelming?","Others shared the same thoughts, but there was simply no time to discuss this now.","“Leave this to me; you all go help the others,” Jian Wushuangs eyes were sharp. Even without truly utilizing Heart power, if he used the fifth level of the Ultimate Dao’s Heartsword World, he could probably kill ghosts at the level of the Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal.","As Jian Wushuangs voice echoed, everyone finally snapped back to reality, nodding quickly before rushing toward other cracks where battles were taking place.","The Dongyan Realm prodigy still didn’t understand. Jian Wushuangs Dao seemed weak, so why was his strength so overwhelming?","“He must be hiding his true power.”","“His sword technique is unique, perfectly countering these ghosts. Don’t overthink it, everyone, go help the others. Try to delay until the Emperor arrives for support.”","“Understood! ”","The group scattered, going to aid other cultivators.","Just as these people evacuated the area, another large group of ghosts swept in. This time, among the ghosts, there was one at the level of the ninth-stage perfect Grand Yan Immortal.","It emitted a dim golden light, containing fragments of the Emperor’s incomplete Dao within its illusory and ethereal body. Its hollow eye sockets resembled black holes.","Because it contained the Emperor’s fragmented Dao, these ghosts could also use some of the techniques the Emperor had learned in his lifetime, although these techniques were naturally not as powerful as the Emperor’s. Still, it surprised Jian Wushuang greatly.","The other ghosts at the level of the Six too Nine Revolutions Grand Yan","Immortal were one thing, but this Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan","Immortal-level ghost gave him a feeling akin to the deceased Xiang Binyun.","However, dealing with these ghosts now was much simpler than dealing with Xiang Binyun.","Even if Xiang Binyun was weak, he probably ranked in the top 100 million among all the Grand Yan Immortals in the entire universe. This Perfected Nine Revolutions-level ghost was only comparable to Xiang Binyun in terms of strength.."]},{"number":5162,"title":"Chapter 5162: Dao Merge","paragraphs":["Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Fortunately, his speed and defense far surpassed those of the creatures he faced.","Jian Wushuang’s sword roamed, first clearing out the weaker monsters before confronting a formidable ghost at the Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal level. He understood the principle that even ants, no matter how small, could be overwhelming in numbers.","He didn’t fear battle and was not afraid of the trials between life and death. Although the monsters spawned after the fall of the Emperor were qualitatively stronger than the vast army of corpses, their numbers were fewer. Moreover, these monsters wouldn’t exist for long; as the Great Desolate Wilderness’ heavenly laws grew stronger, they would be assimilated into the source.","These monsters were all formed from the foundational avenues of the Emperors, a great supplement for the world’s origin.","Despite killing so many, those who benefited most were the Great Desolate Wilderness’ heavenly laws.","<font <=\"\" div=\"\">","Suddenly, an idea flashed in Jian Wushuang’s mind!","The Great Desolate Wilderness’ heavenly laws had just formed and couldn’t personally suppress these monsters yet. What if he used his One Thought Universe to devour all the monsters within its range?","Jian Wushuang’s eyes lit up. If this worked, absorbing so many fragments of the Emperors’ avenues with his Extreme Dao source would undoubtedly strengthen him significantly. There might even be a chance for a breakthrough.","His Heart power had grown stronger, his soul realm had reached the Six Revolutions level. Such ordinary barriers couldn’t hinder him. If he hadn’t worried about unstable foundations initially, he would have broken through to the Six Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal in the starry sky.","This was also the reason Hu Qing managed to step into the Nine Revolutions directly but fell back to the Six Revolutions later.","The Six Revolutions was a slope; the Nine Revolutions marked the vertical height and was the limit for Grand Yan Immortals.","Advancing to the level of a Grand Yan Immortal meant that even if one remained in seclusion and didn’t venture out, they could become a Six","Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal based on their comprehension of the Dao. However, there was a certain resistance at the Nine Revolutions, requiring both opportunities and battles.","As for achieving the Perfected Nine Revolutions level, this was a hurdle before the Dao merging. Failing to achieve this meant certain death. Only by becoming a Perfected Nine Revolutions, by perfecting everything within oneself, could one attempt the Dao merging.","However, for most Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortals, they only perfected their foundational avenue. Perfecting one’s physical body, soul, and mental state to this level was incredibly challenging.","Perfecting these cultivations doesn’t guarantee successful enlightenment!","So, most of the Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortals sought opportunities, either through a stroke of luck or seizing the moment, to merge their Daos, attempting to cleanse themselves through the flow of destiny. However, in the end, countless Grand Yan Immortals faltered at this crucial step.","For those who had mastered the fifth-grade fundamental origin of the Great Dao, merging Daos was the simplest. Yet, even this seemingly straightforward path had only a one in a million chance of success. If it were as easy as Emperor Tongtian, there wouldn’t be so few Emperors on the Universe Deity-Demon List.","The current Original Universe had reached maturity, a time when the most powerful beings were abundant, and various paths had long been explored. Ambitious strongmen, however, didn’t choose the fifth-grade fundamental origin of the Great Dao as their life path. Even those with moderate comprehension abilities, the Grand Yan Immortals with self-awareness, opted for the fourth-grade Great Dao, aspiring to become elites within their respective factions.","The third-grade fundamental origin was the backbone of a faction, representing the future upper echelons. The second-grade fundamental origin of the Great Dao was relatively ambiguous, ranging from common to exceptionally unique.","For instance, the Divine Emperor of Eastwood had achieved Emperor status through a second-grade Great Dao, yet even after gaining dominion over higher-level worlds, his strength remained average among the fourth-rank Emperors. Zhen Wuyang’s True Martial Dao was also a second-grade fundamental origin of the Great Dao. However, he only controlled a mid-level world and possessed peak fourth-tier power.","Within the second-grade fundamental origin of the Great Dao, the disparity between common and exceptional paths could be immense, spanning tens of thousands of miles in difference.","In the world of immortals, there were Emperor-level beings, holders of second-grade Grand Dao, ranging from the pinnacle of the third stage to the formidable fifth stage.","Such disparities were the norm.","Naturally, with differences come difficulties.","Despite the numerous Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortals listed in the Universe Deity-Demon List, only a handful might eventually become Emperors.","The Grand Yan Immortals, who had achieved the Perfected Nine Revolutions, found it exceedingly difficult to perish in the Original Universe; most of them met their demise on the Dao merging.","Jian Wushuang had also grasped this through cryptic texts. He embodied the","Ultimate Dao, but the challenge of unification was monumental. Now, with the addition of the Extreme Dao, the pressure of Dao unification overwhelmed him, leaving him breathless.","Fortunately, his Heart power had reached the fourth level, making his state of mind stronger than most Emperors.","The momentary darkness from before was instantly swept away.","“Dao merging!” Jian Wushuang shook his head. He was still far from achieving unification. Considering the time in the cosmic realm, it had only been a few days since he had advanced from a Yan Immortal to a Grand Yan Immortal. Contemplating unification at this point was premature.","Since his breakthrough, he hadn’t had time to stabilize his realm. Either he was recovering his divine body or engaging in battles.","For now, he decided to use this opportunity to practice with this ghost at the Perfected Nine Revolutions level in front of him.","Perhaps, just as he imagined, he might really succeed. During this expedition to the Great Desolate Wilderness, he not only nearly died at the hands of Xiang Bingyun but also had all his treasures destroyed, including his divine sword, which was now in a sorry state.","People who didn’t know might assume that the divine sword was always like this!","Although the sword’s body was severely damaged, the source of the Sword Dao was intact.","The ghost’s fangs scraped against the divine sword, emitting an extremely unpleasant sound from the ghost’s mouth.","Jian Wushuang quickly retreated, barely stabilizing his figure while holding the sword upside down.","“Heartsword World!”","The fifth level of the Ultimate Sword Dao, it was Jian Wushuang’s most satisfying sword move to date.","This sword had once made the Nine Revolutionos Grand Yan Immortal Gu Yuan kneel and worship, and had even made Xiang Bingyun, who had attained the Perfected Nine Revolutions, tremble in fear.","Swish!","A vast world of swords descended from the void. Countless sword shadows imbued with Heart power, akin to hungry wolves, pounced on the ghost.","Hiss!","Countless sword shadows pierced through the ethereal bodies of the ghosts and monsters. Each time they passed through, the ghosts emitted sizzling black mist. This was the terror of heart power; once tainted, it could burn their souls.","These ghosts were originally soul entities. Jian Wushuang now understood why these ghosts were so afraid of Heart power.","No ghosts in the heart, no ghosts in the world.","The scope of the Heartsword World began to expand, directly encompassing everyone.","Jiu Yu turned around and looked backward, not paying attention to Jian","Wushuang’s involvement. After all, there were only a small number of weak ghosts behind, which could be handled by the few Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortals there.","He led dozens of Grand Yan Immortals, standing at the forefront. Most of the ghosts here were at the Nine Revolutions level, and even the Perfected Nine Revolutions ones were quite common.","The moment the projection of the Heartsword World descended, the ghosts suddenly took a step back involuntarily.","They had no consciousness, but the fear of Heart power was innate, a supreme rule set by the universe. Regardless of whether they had consciousness or not, any soul would fear Heart power.."]},{"number":5163,"title":"Chapter 5163: Devour the Void","paragraphs":["Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","The hollow eyes of the ghostly apparition showed no fear. Although naturally terrified, they still surged into the world of swords.","“Brother Jiu Yu, what’s happening?” Several Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal, unaware of the situation, thought it was Jiu Yu’s doing and approached, inquiring one after another.","“It’s him!”","Jiu Yu looked towards Jian Wushuang behind him, his eyes narrowing.","Countless Sword Qi surrounded the Heartsword World. With a casual motion, Jiu Yu grabbed a strand of Sword Intent in his hand.","<font <=\"\" div=\"\">","The snow-white Sword Intent in Jiu Yu’s hand was incredibly gentle, like a swimming fish.","“A practitioner of Heart power, hidden quite deeply. Now we have it easy!” Jiu Yu released the sword intent in his hand, looked up at Jian Wushuang, and nodded.","“Heart power?” Strong beings from other worlds were still somewhat puzzled.","“I didn’t expect that beneath the Emperor, there would be someone who could cultivate Heart power to such a level. Impressive!”","The leaders of the Wuliang Realm bowed in respect, their palms pressed together. In their Wuliang World, second only to the Wuliang Buddha was the Heart Buddha.","That Heart Buddha was incredibly powerful, and his methods were mysterious.","He had left several secret methods of Heart power cultivation on the Wuliang Mountain.","Countless Grand Yan Immortals rarely cultivated Heart power, let alone mastering the secret techniques of it.","In their eyes, cultivating Heart power as a Grand Yan Immortal was simply impossible.","Little did they know, on Wuliang Mountain, a Three Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal once touched the threshold of Heart power, only to fall in the vast Great Desolate Wilderness.","This fair-skinned monk had accidentally acquired a transmission from the Heart Buddha, and out of respect, Wuliang Buddha granted him a fragment of the Bodhi Heartwood. It elevated his mental state, significantly aiding his cultivation of Heart power.","Unfortunately, the monk eventually perished. In his final moments, he passed his most significant opportunity, the Bodhi Heartwood, to Jian Wushuang.","At that time, during a fierce battle and aided by the effects of the Bodhi Heartwood, Jian Wushuang experienced an extraordinary enlightenment. It allowed his consciousness to astrally project into the starry expanse.","Realizing the origins of his newfound abilities, Jian Wushuang felt profound gratitude for the departed monk, yet lamented the monk’s incomplete fate.","Having learned the monk’s posthumous name from Hu Qing, Jian Wushuang resolved that if the opportunity arose, he would venture into the Wuliang Realm to witness the monk’s Dharma manifestation.","The posthumous name: Complete Annihilation.","Hu Qing, guarding the Fairy Luo Shui behind him, turned to look at Jian Wushuang suspended in the air, murmuring softly, “Master Uncle, if you are still alive, there might be hope for you to cultivate Heart power in the future!” Luo Shui, standing behind him, also gazed towards the void.","“Friend Wushuang is unexpectedly powerful! Even this little monk, you’ve been hiding your true strength well. I risked my life protecting both of you for such a long time.” Luo Shui rested her hands on her hips, tempted to give Hui Qng’s head a knock but ultimately refrained.","“Well done!” Hu Qing clasped his hands together, bowing his head respectfully.","In the void, Jian Wushuang raised his hand. Gripping the emptiness, an endless Sword Intent filled the entire space. His mental realm was several times stronger than the last time.","“Annihilate!”","With the surge of sword intent, the bursting sword energy transformed into a massive cage, trapping the ghosts that had just invaded his mental realm.","There were millions of these ghosts, among them, several hundred belonged to the Perfected Nine Revolutions of the Grand Yan Immortal realm. With so many ghosts, the sum of the Great Dao contained within them could rival the origin of a small world.","After all, the fall of over a dozen Emperors, combined with the Great Dao origins of two fourth-tier Emperors, exceeded the norm of a small world.","Cackling...","The cries of millions of ghosts echoed, their ethereal bodies completely incinerated by the Heart power within Jian Wushuang’s Sword Intent. Although they lacked consciousness, the profound pain in the depths of their souls made them suffer unbearably.","The weaker ones, ghosts of the Three and Six Revolutions level, were directly slain by the Sword Qi. Those able to withstand the Sword Qi were the Nine Revolutions or Perfected Nine Revolutions ghosts, but enduring the Sword Qi was more painful for them than being instantly obliterated.","Being killed outright was a relief, at least there was a quick end. Those who endured the Sword Qi had to endure the relentless torment of Heart power, making their existence agonizing.","Some powerful ghosts began to struggle, go mad, and rush at Jian Wushuang.","“Be careful! Their strength hasn’t been weakened much!” Jiu Yu’s figure flickered, but Jian Wushuang stopped him.","“I have a treasure that can deal with these ghosts. You go ahead; I’ll cover the rear!” Jian Wushuang said sincerely.","Indeed, he was genuinely earnest. As long as these people went ahead, he could openly incorporate these ghosts into the origin of his Heart power universe. Moreover, he could take this opportunity to escape from these people and make a swift getaway.","As for the Qishen Temple, he never thought of contending for it!","Although he learned from Jiu Yu that there was a secret in the Qishen Temple that could make one the most pinnacle existence, these things were too distant from them.","A large group of Emperors were watching there. Even if there were benefits, it was not his turn as a Grand Yan Immortal. If he went, he would just be cannon fodder.","So Jian Wushuang decided to shake off these people. With the strength of a Grand Yan Immortal, he could travel across the entire universe. Seizing this opportunity, he planned to venture into other great worlds.","“And there are treasures like this?” Jiu Yu was somewhat incredulous.","But at this point, if they stayed here, once those monsters broke through the Heartsword World, they would be trapped here. It might be better to listen to Jian Wushuang and take the chance to escape. Trust him this time.","At this moment, most people had the same thoughts as Jian Wushuang. They all wanted to leave the Great Desolate Wilderness as soon as possible, but their strength was not enough. If they encountered monsters again halfway, without so many strong people sticking together, they wouldn’t survive.","For now, they could only temporarily follow Jiu Yu.","“Hurry! The Sword World can’t hold on for long. My treasure can only kill this batch of monsters. Once the next batch of monsters appears from the cracks in the void, I won’t be able to escape.” Jian Wushuang’s face showed urgency. He had the look of a rough monk persuading someone to escape.","The figure of Hu Qing was mixed in the crowd. His gaze had been on Jian Wushuang, and he understood Jian Wushuang’s thoughts. He was no longer the young novice monk he used to be; anything in the world seemed like a mirror","to him now.","Then he glanced at Jian Wushuang. The two exchanged glances, instantly understanding each other’s thoughts.","“Since you insist on this, we’ll take the lead. Remember, if you can’t fight, escape in the direction we’re heading. Maybe the Emperors are already on their way here.” Jiu Yu reassured them before leaving.","Jian Wushuang did show a bitter smile. Their current location was very close to the Qishen Temple. If the Emperors were really coming to save them, they would have arrived long ago.","If even the Emperors couldn’t break free, it showed how dangerous that direction was.."]},{"number":5164,"title":"Chapter 5164: Millions in One Leap","paragraphs":["Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","When Jian Wushuang and Hu Qing desperately fled, they managed to escape quite far. Even though Jian Wushuang was flying at full speed or teleporting continuously, it still took them a day to reach the Qishen Temple.","But the Emperor was different. If he truly intended to rescue them, he could probably arrive with just one teleport.","Moreover, while they were fighting against the Sprites, he could sense a terrifying aura emanating from the direction of the Qishen Temple.","The being emitting this aura had either fallen or an unprecedented great battle had occurred.","Such a powerful clash between beings could be sensed from such a distance. If they got closer, they might be crushed by the fluctuations of the aura.","<font <=\"\" div=\"\">","Jian Wushuang didn’t know that this was happening under the suppression of Chishui and Demon Lord Fengyu. If Daogong did not suppress it, the aura waves spreading out could have injured their divine bodies.","Watching the figures of the others disappearing, a fierce glint appeared in Jian Wushuang’s eyes.","At this moment, he no longer concealed his strength. The Sword World was even more magnificent and powerful than before. The Sword Intents transformed into sword shadows, effortlessly harvesting those weak demons.","The origin that could rival a small world, Jian Wushuang couldn’t help but lick his lips. If he could absorb the Emperor’s origin and Dao within these demons’ bodies, his strength would probably skyrocket immediately, perhaps several hundred times stronger than his cultivation of billions of years in the starry","SKY.","Whew!","Jian Wushuang took a deep breath, his fate hanging in the balance once again.","If he couldn’t devour them, he had the power to escape. Conversely, if he could consume these origins, he wouldn’t leave the Great Desolate Wilderness so soon. This place was his treasure trove.","“One Thought Universe!”","Buzz!","A bubble, as small as a pinhole, began to expand from Jian Wushuang’s mind!","Boom!","A powerful aura erupted from him. The bubble kept expanding, rushing out of his mind, instantly encompassing the sword world in the void.","“Hmm!” Jian Wushuang was somewhat surprised. When his Thought power surged just now, it was unusually excited, as if very interested in those ghosts.","Manipulated by his Thought power, the bubble kept expanding, gradually spreading across the entire void.","A hundred thousand miles!","Three hundred thousand miles!","Eight hundred thousand miles!","A million miles!","It had already exceeded the scale of his first attempt. The origins in the universe seemed to awaken like a baby, wandering around the bubble, and the scope of the universe was still expanding.","Boom!","Two million miles.","Stars suddenly appeared in the previously desolate universe. Although these stars were illusory, they contained Jian Wushuang’s supreme path.","Three million miles!","The bubble continued to expand, showing no signs of stopping.","This range surpassed some continents in the mortal realms. If it continued to expand, Jian Wushuang’s Thought power would have struggled to endure it.","Boom!","Five million miles, and finally, the bubble came to a halt. The origins of the One Thought Universe returned to Jian Wushuang’s body.","Whew!","“I actually managed to exclude the Heavenly Dao within the Great Desolate Wilderness!” Jian Wushuang was astonished!","The middle-grade universe’s Great Dao was unexpectedly excluded by him. Although the other party had just been born, it was still the Great Dao of a middle-grade universe, yet it was being barred from entry.","“Incredible!” Jian Wushuang exclaimed. If he could expand the scope of One","Thought Universe beyond the Great Desolate Wilderness itself, wouldn’t he be able to devour the entire Great Desolate Wilderness?","As this thought crossed his mind, a warning from the supreme rules appeared in his consciousness.","Evidently, this was not feasible. The Great Wilderness’s heavenly path belonged to the Original Universe; even if he became stronger, he couldn’t swallow it.","He could only devour the origins that existed within the world. However, these origins either resided in cosmic mysteries or were within the personal worlds of some super powerful beings, which were beyond his reach.","It was only during the recent Emperor War that he had the opportunity to take advantage of the situation and devour these Emperor origins.","Although these also belonged to the origins of the Original Universe, they were just minor gains. The Original Universe’s origins simply wouldn’t pay attention to such trivial matters.","Jian Wushuang looked towards the sky. “At the pinnacle of the universe, if my universe could rival the Original Universe, it would probably be the universe peak that Emperors dream of!”","To make One Thought Universe comparable to the Original Universe, he probably had to advance his Extreme Dao to the eighth level. Even reaching the seventh level in Ultimate Sword Dao would require him to achieve Dao Unification. The Extreme Dao would probably need to reach the sixth level before he could merge it.","Dao Fusion!","It was a shackle that transcended the peak of life. Many outstanding talents were trapped at this step, and he had no certainty that he could achieve Dao Fusion.","For now, he should collect all the benefits he had at hand!","Jian Wushuang harnessed the Yan power within a range of five million miles, once again transcending several thresholds in his abilities. His strength now reached approximately the Perfected Nine Revolutions.","Many Grand Yan Immortals outside, especially those who had escaped from the ghosts and monsters, had taken note of Jian Wushuang’s fluctuating rank.","“Brother Jiu Yu, you’ve actually entered the top 500 in the entire universe!” exclaimed many Grand Yan Immortals in awe of Jiu Yu’s power.","The Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm recognized as the outstanding young talent, second only to Jiuyu, barely made it into the top one hundred thousand. The gap was simply staggering. If a real fight broke out, he probably wouldn’t withstand even one of Jiuyu’s breaths.","Jiuyu relaxed at this moment, gazing at the astonishing Universe Deity-Demon List.","He wasn’t overly interested in his rank. Most of those ahead of him were practitioners of Ultimate Dao, and he wasn’t satisfied with his current Dao.","He continued to integrate more Daos; he had comprehended several Daos just within the second-grade alone. He pursued the Unity of Myriad Daos. He still had a long wav to go.","Once he achieved the Unity of Myriad Daos, his Dao would be as formidable as any Ultimate Dao.","“Look, it’s Brother Wushuang; his rank is changing!”","Everyone followed their gaze. They were all powerful Grand Yan Immortals, and the rankings of millions were within their sight.","“150 million!”","“He must have made a breakthrough temporarily! He did mention having a special treasure; he probably utilized that to break through. But being able to surpass millions in one go indicates a significant change in his strength,” casually remarked a genius from the Eastern Domain.","His rank was within the top ten million, making him one of the top Grand Yan Immortals at the Nine Revolutions.","This ranking encompassed the entire universe. There were thousands of higher worlds and countless intermediate worlds. In these vast worlds, there were countless Grand Yan Immortals. Even if becoming a Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal was exceptionally difficult, there were still hundreds of millions of them.","To enter the top ten million among hundreds of millions of powerful beings was truly something to be proud of.","“No, it’s still changing!”","‘What!”","“He just entered the top one hundred million!” exclaimed Luo Shui!","For others, entering the top one hundred million might not be significant, but for Jian Wushuang, a Three Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal, he was the only one in the entire universe.","Jiu Yu’s eyes flickered with incredulity.","“Is this the Ultimate Dao? A Three Revolutions, comparable to the Perfected Nine Revolutions!”","He had great confidence in his Unity of Myriad Daos. However, even against","Nine Revolutions, he didn’t dare to think he could match the Perfected Nine","Revolutions.."]},{"number":5165,"title":"Chapter 5165: To Die and Then to Live","paragraphs":["Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","The Unity of Myriad Daos grew stronger as one progressed, reaching a level where it could attain the Ultimate Dao.","The young novice, Hu Qing, paid no attention to the astonishment around him.","Instead, his gaze was fixed upon the ranking!","He sought a familiar face from his memories.","Ever since he had embarked on this Dao, a flood of memories had surged in his mind. These memories had bestowed upon him knowledge of cosmic secrets—such as the process of reaching the pinnacle of the universe and the collapse of the heavenly realms in the past.","<font <=\"\" div=\"\">","The owner of these memories possessed the strength of a top fifth-tier Emperor, making him a formidable presence in the universe back in the day.","“Brother Jiu Yu, can you discern the purpose of this Universe Deity-Demon List? And why has it suddenly appeared here?” A genius of the Eastern Domain shifted the topic, looking at Jiu Yu.","Jiu Yu shook his head and replied, “I do not know. However, it seems to be related to the Qishen Temple mentioned by the Emperor.”","Indeed, besides the Qishen Temple, there was hardly anyone in the entire Original Universe with such grand ambitions.","Upon hearing this, everyone calmed down.","Initially discussing who could be behind this, they now realized that aside from the Qishen Temple, there was no other plausible explanation. It appeared they had come to the right conclusion this time. Despite the danger, there was also boundless opportunity in this venture.","The Deity-Demon List had just begun.","In the pitch-black void, a sudden burst of intense light erupted, blinding everyone present.","“Open your eyes, that’s the direction our escape lies!” People shielded their eyes from the blinding light, squinting towards the direction they had fled.","“That’s probably the treasure of Brother Wushuang! Truly powerful, worthy of a practitioner of the Ultimate Dao!”","“Hu Qing, you need to work harder too. Brother Wushuang is so strong at the","Three Revolutions. You also follow the Ultimate Dao, and you’re at the Six","Revolutions, but your strength still falls a bit short compared to Brother Wushuang.” Luo Shui covered her face, peeking through her fingers at the source of the intense light, all the while chattering to the young monk Hu Qing.","“Indeed!” Hu Qing closed his eyes, refusing to look, and said slowly, “Brother Wushuang has always been stronger than me. I greatly admire him.”","The blinding light was the eruption of Jian Wushuang’s origin.","At this moment, his body’s supreme Dao origin underwent an unprecedented change, and the entire universe of his thoughts was filled with countless rays of light.","These rays of light were all cracks, signs of the impending rupture of the universe of his thoughts. However, the demons and monsters had not yet been entirely consumed. If the universe ruptured and he was severely injured, he wouldn’t be able to escape even if he wanted to.","The universe, resembling bubbles, gave rise to countless fissures. These cracks, akin to rivers, continually spawned tributaries, spreading throughout the cosmos.","Jian Wushuang, however, couldn’t afford to concern himself with these intricacies at the moment. Desperately, he suppressed the primal origin of the Great Dao. The primal force flowed through his body, no longer merely suppressed but overwhelming him entirely.","The power of the Dao surpassed his innate strength, resulting in a backlash, a consequence of the Great Dao’s formidable nature. Fortunately, his soul had been nurtured to the sixth level through the cultivation of his Heart power, barely enabling him to control this surging force.","“No, I can’t hold on any longer!” Jian Wushuang endured immense torment; the overwhelming might of the origin threatened to rupture his very being.","He had overestimated his abilities. With the arrow already on the string, he had no choice but to change his course on the fly.","Embracing the breakthrough amidst this life-and-death situation!","His Yan power circulated within, enveloped by the external origin. He aimed to use these two forces to counterbalance each other, facilitating his own breakthrough.","Jian Wushuang closed his eyes, and in his mind, the panoramic view of a primordial universe appeared. The golden primordial source flowed like quicksand, descending from the top of the circular universe, nearly covering the entire primordial universe.","Jian Wushuang gritted his teeth, enduring the pain, and began his breakthrough.","The difference between Grand Yan Immortals and Yan Immortals lay in the manifestation of the Great Dao within their bodies, leaking out from their origins.","The broader the Great Dao manifested within, the stronger the power of the Grand Yan Immortal. When at the Three Revolutions level, the Great Dao within them stood several feet tall; by the sixth stage, it needed to be elevated to a hundred feet.","This was the best and most achievable aspect. The threshold from the Three to the Six Revolutions was not particularly high. It wasn’t as high as the threshold from Yan Immortal to Grand Yan Immortal.","The former only required an increase of several tens of times, while the latter needed an increase of a thousand times.","Throughout history, there were far fewer Yan Immortals who could fight Grand Yan Immortals beyond their stage, primarily due to the vast disparity in the levels of the Dao.","Therefore, breaking through from the Three to Six Revolutions was much simpler than a Yan Immortal breaking through to become a Grand Yan Immortal. However, Jian Wushuang was currently trapped both internally and externally. At this moment, the difficulty of his breakthrough was not much different from that of a Yan Immortal breaking through to become a Grand Yan Immortal.","The golden light shimmered. Jian Wushuang concentrated, recalling the giant he had encountered in the starry sky. When he had broken the cage, golden light had burst forth from his chest. In the end, the liberation of life allowed","him to break through.","With a colossal axe and an indomitable force, he shattered countless laws, breaking the supreme rules.","Finally, he shattered the cage of the stars. Although at that time, it was nothing to Jian Wushuang, considering his current state, he was far from being able to achieve such a feat. He was like a giant himself, capable of sacrificing his life and breaking countless laws, liberating himself from his constraints.","However, now, he found it incredibly challenging to accomplish the same feat.","Crash!","Golden sands cascaded down like a thought of the universe, attempting to engulf the entire outer appearance of the cosmos. Meanwhile, Jian Wushuang’s body was being devoured by the golden primordial source.","“Break and then establish!” Jian Wushuang suddenly opened his eyes wide, and his aura reversed!","The divine sword in his hand had long been eroded, yet even without a physical sword, there was a sword in his mind. Thought power materialized!","The sword was everywhere!","He stood proudly within his own universe; at this moment, he was the master of this domain.","Origin? Great Dao? Universe?","All illusions!","“Six Revolutions? Blink, and it shatters!”","Hum!","A powerful aura erupted from him!","This was the power of the Six Revolutions, but Jian Wushuang was unimpressed. Calmly, he raised his hand, and a sword appeared in it. With a simple motion from above, he cleaved down.","Crash!","This strike seemed ordinary but was profoundly dreadful.","“This sword strike is called Immortality!” Jian Wushuang roared. The sword shadows sliced through the universe.","Silence!","Then, a dazzling light burst forth, and with a single thought, the universe split into two halves. He reappeared in the void.","Swish!","The golden origin on his body and the sands of the original universe instantly transformed into a new cosmos.","This universe expanded even faster, directly spreading out millions of miles away.","This was breaking and then establishing, first breaking through his own cage and then constructing his own world.","With a single thought, the universe reformed. Jian Wushuang’s origin and Great Dao were elevated to a new level.","The fourth level of the Supreme Dao, “Great Decay Mastery”.","He did it, not only breaking through to the Six Revolutions but also elevating the Extreme Dao to the fourth level.","At this moment, the Ultimate Dao also loosened. Soon, he would reach the sixth level.","Devouring the origin indeed had boundless benefits. Although it was related to his own abilities, without these ghosts and monsters, he couldn’t have possibly advanced so quickly.","It was safe to say they complemented each other!"]},{"number":5166,"title":"Chapter 5166: Standing on the Wrong Side","paragraphs":["Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","This path of devouring was not without risks; any mistake now, and he would be lost in this vast Great Desolate Wilderness forever.","The journey of enlightenment proved to be more challenging due to the hurdles within himself, not the beings within the universe, a fact that amused Jian Wushuang. He felt like he had transcended the universe itself.","Below, the demonic forces, enshrouded, found their strengths diminished by 90 percent.","The Extreme Dao’s suppression rendered them motionless.","Especially his Heart power; it had grown remarkably stronger, partly due to this. As for his Thought power, these demons were merely countless thoughts of Emperors, transformed into grotesque entities. Yet, his formidable Thought power could still handle them.","<font <=\"\" div=\"\">","Crossing into the fourth level of the Extreme Dao, his Thought power surpassed that of Emperors. The demons formed from these imperial thoughts were no match for him.","“Annihilate!”","With a single thought, the demons perished.","Countless demons ceased struggling and stood silently in the cosmos. Gradually, their bodies dissipated, leaving behind fragmented remnants of the original Dao. These fragments appeared in Jian Wushuangs universe, naturally devoured by his own source.","If it weren’t for Jian Wushuang, these sources would have returned to the","Great Desolate Wilderness’s Heavenly Dao. Now, they were intercepted by him.","If Liu Ya knew that he had devoured all these sources, he probably would have wished to crush him. So many Emperors died in his Dao Arena, and he still aimed to break through. Little did he know that all the benefits from these deceased Emperors had been taken by a Grand Yan Immortal.","However, the Six Crows were currently suppressed by the Eternal Tower, rendering them unable to intervene and compete for these sources.","Whew!","Jian Wushuang exhaled deeply, his hands open, absorbing the remnants quietly.","These remnants contained Emperor Supreme Techniques, and Jian Wushuang meticulously pondered over them. After all, they were techniques at the Emperor level. His current mastery of Sword Dao was self-created. But when it came to the control of his physical body and Yan power, he had yet to obtain any Emperor-level skills. By comprehending these Emperor-level skills now, he could potentially find it easier to cultivate them in the future.","The power of the remnants resembled an ocean, and Jian Wushuang was akin to a black hole, devouring the entire sea.","His strength now sufficient, he absorbed all these remnants to stabilize his own source.","Swiftly, the supreme Dao remnants reached the peak of the fourth level, and the Sword Dao Source directly broke through to the sixth level.","After absorbing all these remnants, Jian Wushuangs Sword Dao Source reached its peak at the sixth level.","This time, Jian Wushuangs gains exceeded his foresight.","He had to thank Zhen Wuyang for banishing him to the Great Desolate Wilderness. In just a few years, he managed to make such significant breakthroughs.","With the recent changes in the Great Desolate Wilderness, Zhen Wuyang might have come as well. If they met, Jian Wushuang would genuinely owe him thanks!","“It’s time to go,” Jian Wushuang thought, and the entire pocket universe folded at his will.","After glancing around, he fixed his direction and prepared to leave.","At the same time, in the direction of Qishen Temple, an Emperor was striding over.","“Qianshou, go fetch them! Bring all these little ones here,” the voice of Tongtian Buddha resonated in his ears.","He was also reminded that Hu Qing and Jian Wushuang must be brought along.","With just a step, he arrived at the empty space where Jian Wushuang had previously devoured monsters.","With his karma-fueled perception, his golden eyes pierced through the endless void.","One hand reached through the boundless emptiness, aiming for Jian Wushuang, while the other grabbed for Jiu Yu and the others.","Jiu Yu and the others were fortunate. They sensed that it was the Qianshou Buddha from the Buddhist Realm and didn’t resist much, falling into the enormous palm without much struggle.","Jian Wushuang, on the other hand, was in a dire situation. He desperately tried to escape the palm’s grasp, but no matter how he struggled, he couldn’t break free.","The Qianshou Buddha grew somewhat irritated and directly seized Jian","Wushuang.","Before the palm returned, Qianshou Buddha took another step, appearing in the Chishui Hall.","The two palms, traversing the void, met and descended onto another palm.","“Wushuang, we meet again!” Jiu Yu smiled slightly, reaching out to help Jian Wushuang up from the ground.","“Are you alright?” Luo Shui and the young monk Hu Qing hurried over to Jian","Wushuang.","“What’s going on?” Jian Wushuang was somewhat bewildered.","“Don’t panic, it’s Emperor Qianshou. We’re saved!” Jiu Yu, as an ancient Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal, naturally recognized Qianshou Buddha Lord’s divine power.","In an instant, Jian Wushuang understood, and in his heart, he cursed in anger!","Having finally managed to shake off those pursuers, he found himself caught again. He truly had no desire to accompany these Emperors to the so-called Qishen Temple.","In his view, even if the Qishen Temple held the opportunity to elevate a Perfected Nine Revolutions to the status of an Emperor, it was probably just a slim chance. It was utterly useless to him. He had just reached the Six","Revolutions; reaching the Nine Revolutions was a distant dream. Going to the Qishen Temple now would only make him cannon fodder.","Unfortunately, Emperor personally brought him back, so he couldn’t leave even if he wanted to.","“Well, I must express my gratitude to Emperor!” Jian Wushuang steadied his stance, his face sincere.","Seeing his sincerity, Jiu Yu softened his tone. “Qianshou Lord Buddha is easy to talk to. I will introduce you later!”","Jian Wushuangs face turned red, his voice low. “No, the Emperor is busy with myriad matters, and now you are vying for opportunities. I won’t disturb him.”","He couldn’t forget the scenes from moments ago, when he had attempted to escape multiple times, only to be caught and brought back each time. He doubted Qianshou Buddha would welcome him warmly either. It was better not to provoke that anger.","Although he could claim ignorance about an Emperor’s methods, there was no need to lie. He decided to take one step at a time.","A massive palm swiftly pierced through the pitch-black void, leading to a bright light ahead.","Crash!","The void tore open and closed again.","Jian Wushuang and his companions landed in a grand hall.","“Come to me!” a stern voice echoed.","They looked up to see a towering Buddha right in front of them.","Before they could say anything, they were teleported behind the giant Buddha.","Gazing at the colossal figure and the enormous palms, it seemed Qianshou Buddha was indeed present.","As they settled behind the Buddha, they could finally see their surroundings clearly.","In addition to the many-armed Buddha, the hall contained several hundred extremely powerful auras, each belonging to Emperor-level experts.","Everyone gasped in awe.","It was the first time any of them had witnessed such a grand spectacle. Normally, meeting even one Emperor was a rare event, akin to a miracle. Yet here, a multitude of Emperors had gathered together.","Some found it hard to believe!","Jian Wushuang was fortunate to have met dozens of Emperors in the Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm, so he could still comprehend the magnitude of this gathering.","Dozens of Emperors had arrived from the Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm alone. Undoubtedly, there were powerful Emperors from other worlds within the grand hall. However, as he scanned the surroundings, he didn’t spot Zhen Wuyang.","Logically, the Great Si Region was very close by. Zhen Wuyang should have arrived by now!","Jian Wushuang felt perplexed. However, upon seeing the eternal collapse of the void outside the grand hall, he thought he might be standing on the wrong side.."]},{"number":5167,"title":"Chapter 5167: A Storm Is Brewing","paragraphs":["Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Inside the Chishui Palace.","Jian Wushuang and his companions’ arrival went unnoticed. At this moment, various Emperors continued to arrive at the grand hall with the Grand Yan Immortals.","“Elder Ancestor, the Emperor from the Great Dream Realm has brought some of the Grand Yan Immortals here,” a respectful Emperor from the Great Dream Clan reported.","“Good, bring these promising talents here first. Let the others figure out their own way to come. The distance from the Great Dream Realm isn’t too far. If they can’t even overcome this, there’s no need for them to enter the Qishen Temple,” the Great Dream Ancestor casually instructed.","He himself had brought all the elite Grand Yan Immortals of the Great l)ream","<font <=\"\" div=\"\">","Clan, among whom were several prodigies ranked in the top thousand of the Universe Deity-Demon List.","As for the other Grand Yan Immortals, he had assisted those he could. The rest was up to them.","Inside the hall, the number of Emperors kept increasing. Soon, there were over a thousand Emperors, and the Grand Yan Immortals numbered over ten million.","Most of the Grand Yan Immortals present were at the Nine Revolutions or","Perfected Nine Revolutions level. Only a few were at the Six Revolutions. As for Three Revolutions, there were none.","“Everyone, I believe almost all of you have arrived,” said Chishui. He operated as a lone figure, devoid of a clan or influence. The unique life forms under his control within a certain mysterious realm were considered his subordinates.","Each of these Special Life Forms possessed a second-grade Dao. Their physical bodies were extremely robust, and their life levels were thousands of times greater than ordinary clans.","However, their cultivation was much more challenging. Only a few dozen of them could become Grand Yan Immortals, and among them, there were only two at the Perfected Nine Revolutions level.","A male and a female, these two Special Life Forms stood behind Chishui.","Their strengths both ranked within the top 1,000 of the Universe","Deity-Demon List. Combined with Chishui’s lack of a clan or influence, any treasures that were not particularly useful to him were given to these two subordinates.","They called themselves subordinates, but Chishui Wanderer always regarded them as his own children. “Master! We’re all here!”","“Chishui, you can begin.”","“l don’t have many Yan Immortals under my command. This time, I’ve brought them all,” he said.","The Emperors spoke up, their eagerness palpable.","After all the Yan Immortals had disappeared, Qishen Temple released a message, informing these Emperors that the trial of was about to commence.","As per the information, the trial had three steps.","The first step was the Great Selection of Yan Immortals!","Yan Immortals from across the universe had gathered in the affiliated worlds of Qishen Temple. They were the first batch to receive the inheritance, and the trial prepared for them by Qishen Temple was quite ruthless.","Only 10 percent of the Yan Immortals in each affiliated world could survive. The top 1,000 would proceed to the next round of the trial.","The rest would be sent back to their respective worlds, receiving the bestowal of the affiliated world’s source. What they received depended entirely on their ranking.","This was the first step of the trial. The second step would be the selection for Grand Yan Immortals.","The Emperors would be the last.","Crack!","The ancient and tranquil Qishen Temple gradually opened its doors!","“Now that we’re all here, let’s go in!’ After understanding the structure of Qishen Temple fairly well, these Emperors felt reassured and temporarily set aside their conflicts.’","“The Grand Yan Immortal enters the first passage, the Emperor enters the second!” echoed the voice of Chishui throughout the entire hall.","In the midst of confusion, numerous Grand Yan Immortals hurriedly entered the Qishen Temple.","“As you enter the Qishen Temple, be vigilant. This is an unprecedented opportunity. Seize it and strive to achieve the status of an Emperor!” Encouraging words resounded. As they had said, this opportunity was unparalleled. If not cherished properly, one might regret it for a lifetime.","Everyone answered in unison. Subsequently, they left the Chishui Hall, moved towards the void, and entered the Qishen Temple.","Inside the Eternal Tower,","Demon Lord Fengyu gazed fiercely at the outside world.","“Indeed, the passage for the Grand Yan Immortals opened first. It seems the Qishen Temple won’t allow us in until the Emperors from the other domains arrive,” remarked Emperor Fengyu in a cold voice.","“This is normal. The Qishen Temple was constructed by the ancient civilization’s mighty beings. It is a relic that sifts through potential inheritors.","The Yan Immortals and Grand Yan Immortals are merely trying their luck.","What is truly needed are powerful Emperors like us,” mused Zhen Wuyang. Their speculations were correct. In the eyes of Oishen Temple, only individuals could enter. That’s why they invited all the Yan Immortals into the temple. As for how many Grand Yan Immortals could come, Qishen Temple truly didn’t care. In their view, there was no difference between Yan Immortals and Grand Yan Immortals.","They were selecting the most outstanding among the exceptional, the paragons among paragons. As for their strength, it could be cultivated later; high comprehension and strong mastery of the Great Dao were enough for now.","These abilities were cultivated through their own efforts; the Qishen Temple had an abundance of external resources. Moreover, this trial initiated by the Qishen Temple was the highest level of trial, and it required numerous inheritors. It seemed more like training a universal army corps within a structured framework.","Each affiliated world selected a thousand Grand Yan Immortals; collectively, there were over a million of them. Training a million Grand Yan Immortals at once was not as simple as nurturing one or two inheritors.","“Go in, all of you!” Demon Lord Fengyu opened the gates of the Eternal Tower.","Inside the tower, all the Grand Yan Immortals bowed, shouting in unison, “Thank you, Emperor! ”","Within the Eternal Tower and the tens of millions of Grand Yan Immortals inside the Chishui Hall, they all entered the Qishen Temple together.","“Ancestors, what about us?” Jiu Yu and the others looked at the people entering the Qishen Temple one after another, feeling somewhat anxious.","“Don’t worry. Entering first doesn’t guarantee benefits,” the authoritative voice of Qianshou Buddha resonated.","Tongtian Buddha and Wuliang Buddha were engaged in conversation with other Emperors.","As for Jian Wushuang, he was even less anxious. He had learned a lot about the Qishen Temple from others. Although he was intrigued, he understood what he needed. The Qishen Temple was undoubtedly mystical, but it might not necessarily help him.","With this time, he might as well devour those ghosts and monsters. There were so many of them in the vast wilderness. Perhaps, while the Emperors were focused on the Qishen Temple, he could achieve Ninth Transformation Consummation in one fell swoop.","Now, that was a tremendous opportunity!","“Tongtian, your people can also go in now!” Chishui smiled.","With so many Grand Yan Immortals, they naturally had to enter in batches. Although the Qishen Temple didn’t prioritize order, these Emperors still tried to ensure that their disciples entered first. The principle of ‘first come, first served’ was deeply ingrained in them; usually, the first entrants held the advantage in various relics and mysteries. Even though the","was different this time, they still followed the old rules.","“Thank you, Alliance Leader!” Tongtian Buddha’s face was filled with a smile.","Then he directly communicated with Qianshou Buddha.","Tongtian Buddha wasn’t concerned about when his subordinates would enter.","Right now, he was more concerned about himself. Since joining the Chishui Alliance, he had been rallying various forces. He had secretly formed alliances with several forces, especially with those solo practitioners. He personally pulled them in. As long as they had tier 4 power, he had formed an alliance with almost all of them.."]},{"number":5168,"title":"Chapter 5168 The Trial Begins","paragraphs":["5168 The Trial Begins","Although the Chishui Alliance was currently in disarray, each member understood the concept of every man for himself in times of crisis.","They had already begun planning for the aftermath of the Chishui Alliance's collapse.","As for Wanderer Chishui, he turned a blind eye to these developments. Ever since he learned how to enter the Qishen Temple, he no longer cared about the fate of the Chishui Alliance.","He had greeted a few top tier 4 Emperors. He could form a new alliance within the Qishen Temple. He didn't care about the other strong individuals anymore; they couldn't assist him in any way.","As a tier 3 Emperor, Qianshou Buddha, belonging to a different circle, was naturally unaware of what the Tongtian Buddha and the others were discussing. However, upon receiving the message, he quickly rallied everyone to prepare to enter the Qishen Temple.","\"Jiu Yu, you are the strongest among us, and we are of the same generation. You are our senior. Inside the Qishen Temple, please protect others as much as you can,\" Qianshou Buddha said, echoing Jiu Yu's sentiments. His temperament was good, unlike other Emperors who were often aloof and domineering.","This was rare among tier 3 Emperors. Generally, tier 3 Emperors were the leaders of significant forces, and they weren't easy to talk to, especially the tier 2 Emperors who tended to be arrogant, particularly when their strength was weaker than others at the same tier. They liked to show off in front of the Grand Yan Immortal.","Most of these Emperors had reached the end of the road in terms of the Great Dao, with little hope of further strengthening their power. Their fundamental Great Dao before integrating with the source was weak, consisting of ordinary fourth-grade or fifth-grade Great Dao. Therefore, they felt intense jealousy towards the geniuses who possessed powerful sources.","This jealousy was somewhat understandable. In fact, some dark- hearted Emperors specifically hunted down the geniuses among the Grand Yan Immortals.","Fortunately, there were many Emperors present this time, so the evil Emperors didn't dare to act recklessly. After all, the Grand Yan Immortals present were the elite geniuses of their respective worlds, and no one dared to incur their wrath at this moment.","\"Thank you, Emperor. I will be careful,\" Jiu Yu's eyes glinted with determination.","Among his peers, he was a tier 3 Emperor, but he was still at the Perfected Nine Revolutions level. While it might seem like he wasn't in a hurry to integrate numerous Great Dao, in reality, he was more anxious than anyone else. However, merging countless Great Dao into one was not an easy task.","Until he reached the Perfect Source level, he couldn't integrate the Dao.","\"Sure, go in!\" Qianshou Buddha waved his hand, and everyone was teleported out of the Chishui Temple.","\"Jiu Yu, I hope that when you return, you will have successfully integrated the Dao!\"","In the void, Jiu Yu turned around. He received a transmission from Qianshou Buddha, nodded, and silently said to himself, \"Definitely! Brother Qianshou.\"","He couldn't forget the joyful expression on his friend's face when they successfully integrated the Dao together. On Tongtian Mountain back then, they were the geniuses of their generation- one succeeded in integrating the Dao, and the other struggled, delaying his integration.","\"Depart!\" Jiu Yu turned around, his eyes filled with madness, and he shouted sternly!","Hundreds of people from the Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm entered the Qishen Temple together.","Jian Wushuang, not being a practitioner of the Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm realm himself, followed at the end, walking parallel to Hu Qing.","Before entering the Qishen Temple, Jian Wushuang felt a pair of enormous eyes watching him. He turned around and looked at the Eternal Tower floating in the void.","A majestic figure appeared in his mind. \"It's Zhen Wuyang!\"","Jian Wushuang hurried into the Qishen Temple.","In the Chishui Hall, he had learned about the previous battle.","Several Emperors fell, including the ancestors of the Eastern Yan realm.","There were also several emperors he had heard about, those powerful emperors from the ancient times in the Great Si Region.","Just being glanced at by Zhen Wuyang, he felt chills down his spine!","But he wasn't a traitor; he was never truly one of Zhen Wuyang's people.","Zhen Wuyang withdrew his gaze, closed his eyes, and thought to himself, \"Good luck to you, young one.\"","He managed to shift some of the Nine Revolutions from the Great Si Region, but there weren't many with potential. Most of them would end up as cannon fodder. Jian Wushuang, however, proved to be a pleasant surprise to him.","In a short span of time, he had broken through to the Six Revolutions of Grand Yan Immortal. He even had the Ultimate Dao. placing him at the top 100 million on the Universe Deity-Demon List.","Being among the top 100 million at the Six Revolutions meant a lot. When he was at the pre-Nine Revolutions level, he could enter the top 1,000. Although he didn't fully comprehend the selection criteria of Grand Yan Immortals, those within the top 1,000 were worth nurturing by the Qishen Temple. Perhaps, in the future, they could become a significant force to aid him.","However, mastering the Ultimate Dao was incredibly challenging. So far, there was only one Ultimate Emperor in the entire universe. He couldn't be certain that Jian Wushuang would succeed. Yet, as the sole practitioner of the Ultimate Dao in the Great Si Region, he sincerely hoped that Jian Wushuang would successfully master it.","\"Phew!\"","Entering the Qishen Temple, Jian Wushuang finally breathed a sigh of relief. He had half-expected Zhen Wuyang to strike him down with a single blow.","In the pitch-black darkness, Jian Wushuang couldn't discern where he was.","\"What's this?\"","He felt bewildered. Everything around him was pitch black, but when he looked up, he saw a sky filled with planets!","Hum!","An ancient aura enveloped him, and in the next moment, he vanished from his spot.","\"Original Planet, Codename Alpha Nine!\"","Before Jian Wushuang could grasp what was happening, a deep voice echoed in his ears.","With a burst of intense light, the darkness dissipated. He could now see his surroundings clearly.","Looking around, he realized he was on a desolate planet. Barren mountain ranges, gray-white continents, and depleted lakes surrounded him.","Only a small fraction of the people who had entered the Qishen Temple with him had been transferred to this original planet. He couldn't sense the presence of the others.","\"In the Qishen Temple, there existed a hidden world!\" Jian","Wushuang's figure flickered, appearing in the sky above the original planet. A barrier blocked his way.","Through the barrier, he could see other original planets, 36 in total, within this world.","\"Brother Wushuang!\"","The young samanera, Hu Qing, flew over from a distance. The current Hu Qing was no longer the innocent and naive monk from before. The loose monk's robe he wore replaced his original tight- fitting attire. His fair face now carried a pair of sharp and fierce eyes.","Seeing Hu Qing, Jian Wushuang nodded but didn't say much!","The two landed on the ground, and other practitioners noticed them. However, due to mutual unfamiliarity, they kept a considerable distance, their guard up.","Ding!","A crisp sound resonated. Above the original planet, an elderly figure with a hunched back appeared. He carried a dark lamp and had a face full of wrinkles, with one white eye revolving in its socket.","\"The Qishen Temple's ultimate trial begins now!\" The hunched old man's voice was hoarse. After uttering these words, he disappeared from this Alpha Nine original planet.","Upon hearing this, the crowd first froze, then various eyes showed hints of murderous intent.","After exchanging a glance with Hu Qing, Jian Wushuang swiftly rushed towards the nearest mountain range.","The hunched old man had given them a piece of information!","Once inside the mountains, the two of them finally let go of their guard. Simultaneously, the sky tilted, casting numerous beams of light.","In each beam, there was a white token.","The hunched old man had instructed everyone: once they obtained their own token, they could unleash their killing intent."]},{"number":5169,"title":"Chapter 5169: Cruel Rules","paragraphs":["Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","The original planet, a dull gray, was covered in mountains and barren lands, making it an easy target for attacks.","Jian Wushuang and Hu Qing managed to meet, but no other factions were allowed to have a presence on this primitive planet. Once they formed a group, they would undoubtedly hunt down any solo travelers.","That’s why Jian Wushuang brought the young monk with him, quickly hiding in the mountains. They concealed their presence, intending to obtain a token first and understand the rules of the game.","Even though the two of them possessed extraordinary strength, their rankings in the entire universe were not significant. Among the tens of millions of Grand Yan Immortals entering the Qishen Temple this time, they were all top-notch experts, ranking within the top one hundred million, with the lowest threshold being Nine Revolutions strength.","And this was only one-fifth of the entire universe. It wouldn’t take long for Grand Yan Immortals from other worlds to arrive.","<font <=\"\" div=\"\">","After obtaining their identity tokens, the two of them moved again, arriving in a dim canyon.","The entire canyon was barren, except for some scattered ancient tree branches and the corpses of some wild beasts.","Hu Qing landed next to Jian Wushuang, looking at the corpses. He bowed his head and murmured, “Virtuous!”","Although these corpses seemed ancient and likely belonged to creatures that might have already gone extinct in the current Original Universe, they could sense that these corpses hadn’t been dead for very long.","The flesh and blood on them had been devoured by some kind of technique.","Jian Wushuang waved his hand, carving out a simple cave. For the ultimate trial, it was likely that some powerful being forcibly created these primitive planets. All vitality was drained from these desolate creatures, withered lakes, and barren forests. Once lively planets were transformed into primitive planets.","The Qishen Temple had truly lived up to its name, transforming a small world into a battlefield of demons.","The two of them sat cross-legged in the cave.","“Let’s check the rules first,” Jian Wushuang said casually.","Since they were in the Qishen Temple, their primary goal was to survive. If they could gain some benefits along the way, that would be even better.","Holding a white token, he infused a thread of Yan power, and countless pieces of information flooded his mind.","The “ultimate trial” of the Qishen Temple was divided into five domain realms. Each realm had 36 primitive planets, and each primitive planet housed millions of Grand Yan Immortals.","“Five domain realms?” Jian Wushuang was somewhat surprised!","According to the Grand Yan Immortals in their Eastern Domain, one domain realm would have been sufficient. Now, there were five domain realms. This meant that most of the Grand Yan Immortals in the entire universe had entered the Qishen Temple!","But wasn’t the Qishen Temple located in the Great Desolate Wilderness?","“No, somethings off!” Jian Wushuang realized; the Qishen Temple had probably appeared in other major worlds as well.","No wonder the Qishen Temple’s ultimate trial for the Grand Yan Immortals was progressing so quickly.","Being divided into five domain realms meant they wouldn’t encounter each other now, which wouldn’t affect him at all.","The selection criteria for Grand Yan Immortals had been significantly relaxed compared to the criteria for Yan Immortals. Yan Immortals were the top one thousand within each world, but the requirements for Grand Yan Immortals’ trials were different.","Each of the Grand Yan Immortals ranked within the top 10,000 in the original planets received blessings from the Qishen. The top one thousand could inherit the essence contained within the original planets.","Following that, a small-scale ranking appeared in their minds.","The 1st, ‘Lei Wanhe’, a Perfected Nine Revolutions, had a record of 330.","The 2nd, ‘Chang Lingxian% a Perfected Nine Revolutions, had a record of 110.","Ranking 769,358, ‘Jian Wushuang, had a record of o.","Records were divided.","Identity token: 100 points.","Perfected Nine Revolutions: 1000 points.","Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal: 100 points.","Note: Killing opponents of higher realms earns 10 times the points.","Trial duration: 30 years.","Jian Wushuang suddenly opened his eyes. He had initially planned to hide here and wait for the trial to end before leaving. Now, it seemed he could gain some benefits.","The Qishen Temple’s trial placed great emphasis on surpassing one’s own realm. Tempted by the allure of tenfold rewards, it forced those Nine Revolutions to confront Perfected Nine Revolutions.","However, Perfected Nine Revolutions didn’t have the same tenfold rewards. They had to relentlessly hunt down Nine Revolutions or kill opponents of the same realm.","Under these rules, the entire original planet could truly become a battlefield of carnage.","“Brother Wushuang!” Hu Qing put away his identity token, his gaze unexpectedly burning with fervor.","“Surround and kill the Perfected Nines!” Jian Wushuangs voice quivered.","They both were Six Revolutions Grand Yan Immortals. If they could indeed surround and kill a Perfected Nine Revolutions, they would receive a hundredfold reward. Killing a Perfected Nine Revolutions equated to 1,000 points, so a hundredfold reward meant gaining 100,000 points.","As long as they killed a few Perfected Nine Revolutions, the two of them would be at the forefront, waiting for the trials to end and reaping the benefits.","Upon hearing his words, Hu Qing hesitated, as if two conflicting thoughts were battling in his mind. Eventually, he nodded.","“Virtuous!” Jian Wushuang smiled.","He could see that the novice monk Hu Qing had undergone significant changes, but everyone had their secrets, and he didn’t pry.","The two of them schemed, setting up a large formation in the valley. One of them would lure the Perfected Nine Revolutions into chasing them outside, and then they would ambush and kill them. As for the distribution of merits and points, Qishen Temple would handle that. The more effort one put in, the more points they would receive.","At the same time, an unprecedented war erupted on the Original planet. The ranking of this primitive planet kept changing as several Perfected Nine","Revolutions Grand Yan Immortals vied for some safety. For a while, no Nine Revolution Grand Yan Immortal dared to show their face on any continent.","These Perfected Nine Revolutions were already bloodthirsty. In the first year, almost all Perfected Nine Revolutions became targets. Fortunately, some lone Perfected Nine Revolutions planetted banding together, barely managing to survive.","However, there were also many powerful Nine Revolution Grand Yan Immortals who could match the Perfected Nine Revolution ones.","For example, ‘Shuiyue’ ranked in the top 1,000, was a Nine Revolution Grand","Yan Immortal. In a major battle, he killed a severely injured Perfected Nine","Revolutions and subsequently killed several other Nine Revolution Grand Yan Immortals in succession. His rank soared, surpassing many Perfected Nine Revolutions.","Three years passed in the blink of an eye.","The great chaos inside the Original planet ceased, and the rankings planetted to solidify. Their struggles became exceptionally difficult. It was no longer just a matter of strength but also a battle of wits and bravery. Those who survived were not weaklings; they were either Perfected Nine Revolutions or true strong ones among the Nine Revolution Grand Yan Immortals.","During these three years, Jian Wushuang and Hu Qing finally set up a powerful formation.","This formation was a simplified version of the Wuliang Great Formation from the Wuliang Mountain, designed by Hu Qing. Although it was a simplified version, as a defensive formation for an Emperor’s Dao Arena, even if it was just a fraction of its full power, it could trap the majority of Perfected Nine Revolutions.","“It’s finally set up. It’s perfect timing; those Perfected Nine Revolutions have also accumulated a lot of achievements by now. We can begin,” Jian Wushuang said, his eyes sharp. The trial had already passed one-tenth of its duration. The remaining time was neither too long nor too short.."]},{"number":5170,"title":"Chapter 5170 But You’ve Been Hooked","paragraphs":["5170 But You've Been Hooked","The weakened Perfected Nine Revolutions were all fallen, leaving only a few strong ones among them. If they intended to surround and kill one of these strong Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortals, it would take them a considerable amount of time.","After all, battles between the strong, lasting tens of thousands of years, were quite common. When the difference in strength wasn't significant, swiftly killing an opponent relied on grand formations or burning divine bodies.","\"Hu Qing, I will lure them away while you hide in the grand formation. Remember, once I enter the formation, be careful when controlling it not to harm me,\" Jian Wushuang instructed earnestly.","Even though this formation was a simplified version, it was still immensely powerful. Only by combining their strengths could they barely hold it. Hu Qing was the only one who could operate the formation, and controlling its power was challenging. Any misstep could backlash and harm both of them.","\"Rest assured!\" Hu Qing's eyes were resolute as he nodded. Whoosh!","Jian Wushuang's figure had already left the canyon. After a quick scan of the surroundings, he felt a fluctuation of Yan power in the nearby mountains. Concealing his own Yan power, he swiftly flew towards the source of the fluctuation.","The original planet, though called a planet, was as large as some small domains. Even a Perfected Nine Revolutions would need a year to fly around it, and teleportation was impossible within the original planet.","During his flight, Jian Wushuang observed the surroundings. The geological structure of the original planet, being a battleground for Grand Yan Immortals, was peculiar. The surface of the planet was exceptionally tough, making it difficult to destroy the mountains with ordinary means. However, after several large battles, many mountains were cut in half, and remnants of Yan power still burned in the ruins, lingering endlessly.","Jian Wushuang had also seen the road made of Immortal bones. He could accept all of this since it was the Qishen Temple. To gain benefits here, one had to fight for them. Even in some cosmic mysteries, many Grand Yan Immortals would perish.","But this time, the appearance of the Qishen Temple was a feast for the entire universe, albeit a feast of slaughter.","After this encounter, it was anticipated that the formidable beings in the Original Universe would likely reduce by half. A decrease in numbers was advantageous for the cosmic source; it lightened the burden.","Although their quantity dwindled, the quality increased several folds. Soon, it was expected that the Original Universe would truly rise within the long river of time, illuminating an entire era.","On a fallen mountain range in the original planet, a sturdy middle- aged man with bare arms stood, holding a long spear in his hand. His face bore several scars, and his muscular upper body displayed numerous cracks—a testimony to irreparable injuries inflicted upon his divine body. He stood motionless amidst the ruins of the battlefield.","The fluctuation emanated from him. Jian Wushuang's senses were keen; as he approached, he honed in on his target's location.","Within the span of a tea ceremony, he arrived at this desolate battlefield. Jian Wushuang descended swiftly, his figure hovering three feet above the ground. He scanned the surroundings and fixed his gaze on the Grand Yan Immortal, Zhong Sheng, whose aura was feeble.","\"Ranked 9,867th in the 'Original Planet Alpha Nine, Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal, Zhong Sheng,\" Jian Wushuang muttered.","Zhong Sheng hailed from a small world, where he was the top expert and the ruler. However, he was merely a tier 2 Emperor in that world, the sole tier 2 Emperor therein. There weren't many Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortals, and among them, only three had reached the Perfected Nine Revolutions level. Zhong Sheng was one of them.","Solitude wasn't exclusive to the powerful; it afflicted the weak more. They lacked connections and influence; once they entered the original planet, they were solitary warriors.","Union seemed impossible-Zhong Sheng's strength was ordinary among his peers, and without a backing, no alliance would accept him. Seeking alliance with other Nine Revolutions beings was akin to volunteering for death.","The Perfected Nine Revolutions had already formed an alliance, scouring the realms for weaker Perfected Nine Revolutions, attempting to trap and kill them.","A formidable expert, a grandmaster in any major world, now found himself hunted across the battlefield like prey.","Jian Wushuang clenched his identity token, holding over 30,000 points within it.","\"My luck can't be this good! Just stepping out and I stumble upon a corpse!\" Jian Wushuang pinched the token of the fallen, acutely sensing the severe injuries it bore, clearly not feigned.","Now that he had the identity token in his possession, even if he was in disguise, he wouldn't casually hang it around his waist!","That distinct ripple, he could feel it even from millions of miles away; he simply didn't believe he would encounter such good fortune.","So, this was a very shoddy set-up.","Jian Wushuang tossed the token to the ground, swiftly retreating.","In the instant he withdrew, concealed Perfected Nine Revolutions around him began to reveal themselves.","17 Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortals appeared simultaneously around this battlefield.","Indeed, just as Jian Wushuang had anticipated, this was a trap!","If he could think of besieging weaker Perfected Nine Revolutions, others surely could too. After all, no one who came here was a fool. It was just that these people's trap was too poorly constructed.","This happened to be his first venture outside. Other Perfected Nine Revolutions might have noticed something was amiss as they approached and left the area immediately.","\"Big brother, this person's cultivation level seems a bit vague; he's probably not at the Perfected Nine Revolutions stage!\" said a rough and burly man, his tiger-like eyes glaring, his stature comparable to seven or eight ordinary men combined.","Jian Wushuang glanced sideways, finding himself blocked at the back by seven Grand Yan Immortals emanating a murderous aura. In front, there were three Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortals, with the rest surrounding him on both sides.","Although there was no grand formation, the way they positioned themselves indicated that if a Perfected Nine Revolutions fell into their trap, it would be challenging to escape. Those weaker in strength would likely meet their end here.","\"Fellow Daoists, we're all at the Perfected Nine Revolutions stage, why must we make things difficult for each other?\" Jian Wushuang's aura fluctuated, his divine sword had long been shattered, and he didn't even have a supreme treasure on him anymore.","Among these 17 individuals. there was a second-grade Origin Great Dao expert, while the weakest among them were third-grade Origin beings. Additionally, a few of them were exceptionally formidable even within the third-grade Origin category.","The young man leading the group wore luxurious robes, and his triangular eyes exuded a cold indifference as he said lightly, \"Kill him.\"","In the past, encountering a Perfected Nine Revolutions might have led them to recruit the person, but now the strong were few, and the weak were many.","\"Once we kill this kid, let's change our location and head to the Flame Demon Valley; there are no more good catches here.\" The man with triangular eyes spoke with a sinister tone.","He had caught quite a few formidable experts here, and his achievements were considerable. Everyone present was ranked within the top 20,000, with himself positioned within the top 10,000.","All of this was thanks to that Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal. They had first besieged and severely injured him, then sealed him in this place, using him as bait to lure other Grand Yan Immortals.","Due to this scheme, he had been elected as the leader by these people.","There was a glint in Jian Wushuang's eyes. None of these individuals were weak; dealing with all of them at once wouldn't be easy.","More importantly, if they couldn't resolve the situation quickly and it attracted other powerful beings, things could turn dire."]},{"number":5171,"title":"Chapter 5171: Transcendent Innate Treasure","paragraphs":["Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","A couple of Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortals approached. Even though he could resist against one or two, if dozens of powerful beings came together, he couldn’t guarantee he could hold them off until they entered the large formation he had prepared in advance.","“Everyone, if you insist on fighting...” Jian Wushuang’s eyes flickered as he scanned the approaching crowd, his figure suddenly flashing.","Clang!","The long spear held by the Perfected Nine Revolutions pierced out violently!","A trail of afterimages followed Jian Wushuang as he mobilized his Yan power, the momentum of his spear no less than that of the Perfected Nine Revolutions directly attacking the man with triangular eyes.","<font <=\"\" div=\"\">","“Die!” Catch the leader first, and the rest will follow. As soon as he moved, Jian Wushuang locked onto the leader with triangular eyes.","The long spear pierced the air like a dragon. In that moment, Jian Wushuang appeared beside the man with triangular eyes.","Before the others could react, the long spear had pierced through the man’s chest. Meanwhile, Jian Wushuang appeared behind him, catching the blood-stained spear with one hand and smashing his fist towards the man’s head with the other.","Boom!","All of this happened in an instant. Before the others could comprehend what was occurring, the man with triangular eyes had already fallen.","Jian Wushuang held the blood-stained spear in one hand and the corpse of the man with triangular eyes in the other.","“A Six Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal has killed another Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal, earning 1,000 points!” A message appeared in Jian Wushuang’s mind.","In addition to the basic points, Jian Wushuang also gained the accumulated points of the man with triangular eyes, which were more than 20,000. However, due to the higher-level kill, even the accumulated points were multiplied by ten.","“Over 200,000 points!” Jian Wushuang’s eyes widened in astonishment; his ranking had instantly shot up into the top 5,000.","This was terrifying beyond belief. He had thought only his basic achievements would double, never imagining that even his accumulated achievements would multiply.","If he killed a Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal with an accumulated record of 100,000 battles, he would gain tens of millions in achievements!","“Tsk!” Jian Wushuang had initially planned to kill their leader and leave, to avoid drawing attention. These Perfected Nine Revolutions were only worth 1,000 points each; it wasn’t worth the risk. Now, it seemed he had no choice but to kill them.","This exceeded his estimates!","What he didn’t know was that this was a special privilege unique to Six Revolutions Grand Yan Immortals, just not documented on their identity tokens.","“Go!” The other Perfected Nine Revolutions sensed the danger and scattered in all directions.","Jian Wushuang could kill their leader in an instant, and he could kill any one of them as well. Even if they ganged up on him, they would still suffer significant casualties.","The risk was too high; it was better to escape directly. As for seeking revenge?","That was practically impossible!","If it weren’t for the cunning of the man with triangular eyes, they wouldn’t have pledged allegiance to him in the first place.","It was a chance encounter, an alliance formed to engage in illicit activities. Now that the ship had sunk, they naturally abandoned it and fled in different directions.","Since these people scattered, Jian Wushuang had no way to pursue them. He could only deal with those who were relatively close to him.","Their achievements poured into his identity token with a clatter. Although the accumulated achievements of those few individuals were only a few thousand, multiplying it by ten meant tens of thousands.","Adding to the tally was the triangular-eyed man; this time, he had amassed a record of 350,000 points, placing him around the top 4.","The distance to the previous thousand was still quite significant.","Jian Wushuang pocketed his token, lowering his gaze to the Perfected Nine Revolutions sealed beneath him.","“After using your weapon, I’ll leave your corpse intact!” Jian Wushuang raised his hand, channeling a powerful Yan power into his opponent’s mind.","Silent in his killing; such was the might of Yan power.","“Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal, Zhong Sheng, has been killed. You have gained a record of 150,000 points!” Seeing the displayed number, Jian Wushuang wasn’t particularly surprised.","He hadn’t exerted much effort in slaying this Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal; gaining 150,000 points was quite good considering.","After stowing away his precious spear, he could already sense several grand and majestic auras soaring toward the sky, rushing in his direction.","Although the commotion earlier hadn’t been significant, it had still attracted the attention of the strong in the surrounding area.","“Let’s go!” Jian Wushuang flickered, swiftly disappearing into the sky.","In just a few breaths, a Perfected Nine Revolutions arrived at the scene. He made no attempt to conceal his aura, his demeanor exuding dominance.","“Arrived late! Over a dozen Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortals managed to escape; their strength is commendable, probably at the peak of Perfected Nine Revolutions level.” Behind the domineering man floated a crescent-shaped flying blade, emanating an incredibly powerful aura.","Even his precious weapon was of the utmost quality.","The power of a regular precious weapon generally sufficed for Yan Immortals up to the Nine Revolutions level, but most top-tier precious weapons were wielded by Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortals. For individuals as formidable as the Perfected Nine Revolutions, ordinary precious weapons were simply insufficient.","Just like Jian Wushuang, his entire set of precious items was barely adequate during his Yan Immortal days. Once he ascended to the realm of Grand Yan Immortal and faced other Nine Revolutions, even Perfected Nine Revolutions, these precious items fell short.","Only transcendent innate treasures or those of a higher caliber could meet the current demand.","In ordinary circumstances, Grand Yan Immortals would, at most, employ pinnacle innate treasures. However, with the opening of the Qishen Temple and major powers unlocking their treasuries, even the Emperor bestowed upon the immensely powerful Perfected Nine Revolutions, born from the source, a transcendent innate treasure. This treasure was a crescent-shaped blade adorning his back.","Already at the peak of the Ninth Revolution, possessing this transcendent innate treasure elevated his strength to touch the threshold of supremacy. He could now rank among the top 1,000 on this primordial planet.","Now, facing a Perfected Nine Revolutions daring to hunt him within his territory, his brows furrowed, a cold glint in his eyes.","After a deafening explosion of air, he shot out, his form disappearing hundreds of thousands of miles in the blink of an eye.","Jian Wushuang hadn’t gone far yet. He wasn’t in a rush. He had come precisely to lure a Perfected Nine Revolutions. If he fled too fast, the other party wouldn’t be able to detect his aura.","After a few more flickers, Jian Wushuang felt a stir in his heart. “He took the bait!”","That overbearing aura permeated the entire mountain range. Though still quite distant, Jian Wushuang could feel it. The other party was heading straight for him.","“Oh no, he’s too fast!”","Jian Wushuang’s form suddenly accelerated, but it was already too late. The dominating aura, enveloping the entire mountain range, was right behind him.","For a moment, he felt a bit panicked. In a usual situation, he might not have been afraid of an ordinary Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal. But this pursuer, judging from his aura alone, was beyond the usual Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortals he encountered.","“You can’t escape!”","The formidable man behind Jian Wushuang roared, his crescent-shaped blade instantly surging forth, slashing towards Jian Wushuang.."]},{"number":5172,"title":"Chapter 5172: Luo Hao, the Prince of the Daluo Realm","paragraphs":["Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","The two of them, one chasing and one fleeing, did not conceal their aura at all, drawing the attention of many powerful beings who approached.","The overwhelming pressure made those who wanted to take advantage of the chaos retreat.","A streak of light descended, and a man and a woman came to a halt.","“Senior Brother, it’s Luo Hao from the Daluo Realm!” The young woman from the Great Dream Clan, dressed in plain white robes, frowned!","She was all too familiar with that terrifying aura. In the first few days of the trial, many of their clan members died at the hands of Luo Hao. If it weren’t for Senior Brother risking his life to protect her and escape, she would have fallen in that battle as well.","<font < div>","She was the direct disciple of the Dao Ancestor of the Great Dream Realm, possessing a third-grade source Great Dao. In the Great Dream Realm, she was one of the top experts. However, after arriving in the original planet, her strength was reduced to the point where she was nearly at the bottom, vulnerable to anyone’s whims.","In the original planet, only those with a second-grade source Great Dao had the qualifications to hunt, while they could only flee.","Now, quite a few weaker Perfected Nine Revolutions had planetted to conceal their presence, waiting for the trial to end.","This trial was simply hell for them. Not to mention receiving the inheritance in the first thousand trials, even the first ten thousand were hard for them to enter.","The Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortals could rely on combined efforts to kill other Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortals and gain a lot of achievements. They couldn’t match those of the same level and could only hunt down lone Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortals.","“Hmph, this despicable person, I will kill him with my own hands sooner or later! ”","“Senior Brother, should we take advantage of the chaos and go over? I see that the person he’s chasing seems to be from the Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm, quite powerful.”","They harbored deep resentment, their hatred itching at them.","Although Luo Hao was strong, his ranking in the entire universe was not high. The First Prince of the Great Dream Realm was a peerless genius who could make it into the top 1,000. Unfortunately, they had bad luck and didn’t end up on an original planet.","Luck seemed to favor Luo Hao, one of the top powerhouses on this original planet. Several other formidable figures on this planet belonged to Luo Hao’s faction. They had communicated beforehand, explaining Luo Hao’s audacious and unrestrained actions.","“Senior Sister, I must face this alone. I can’t risk your safety any further,” the man said, his eyes softening.","Though the Greater Dream Realm was merely a middle-tier world, its prodigies possessed immense pride, a trait influenced by their progenitor, the Great Dream Ancestor. Their influence spanned dozens of worlds in the vicinity.","Avenging their grievances shouldn’t endanger his senior sister. If news spread that she was involved, it would be better if he were dead.","“Senior Brother, I’m going with you,” the young girl from the Greater Dream Realm asserted, her spirit unyielding. “Our realm is one of the strongest in the entire universe. If not for our ill fate, being assigned to this original planet, we wouldn’t have been bullied by that Luo Hao!”","Unable to persuade his determined senior sister, the man stopped trying. Instead, he affectionately patted her head and whispered, “Alright, for the honor of the Greater Dream Realm, let’s do it!”","They exchanged a determined glance before their figures blurred, heading toward the oppressive aura. However, they moved discreetly, neither too fast nor too conspicuous, their presence completely concealed.","They understood that facing Luo Hao head-on was futile. Their only chance lay in ambushing him during his battle.","Daluo Realm!","Jian Wushuang fled rapidly, recalling information about various powerful beings listed in the Universe Deity-Demon List.","The Daluo Realm, one of the ten Princes, Luo Hao, ranked among the top 100,000 experts in the universe. Jian Wushuang had glimpsed his name on the list once.","In the realm of Perfected Nine Revolutions, the top expert wielded a crescent-shaped flying blade that appeared to be a primordial treasure. Possessing such a treasure, combined with his innate strength, Luo Hao was undoubtedly among the top 1,000 experts on this original planet.","This primal world boasted millions of Grand Yan Immortals, and Luo Hao’s strength easily ranked within the top 1,000. It might even have been higher. However, at this moment, he didn’t have the time to check his identity token’s ranking.","The spinning crescent-shaped flying blade was dangerously close, and in an instant, blood and flesh splattered.","“I underestimated him!” Jian Wushuang’s Yan power surged, swiftly healing the ferocious wounds on his back. In his heart, he thought, ‘I shouldn’t underestimate the top expert in the Perfected Nine Revolutions experts. He must not be underestimated!’","Fortunately, Jian Wushuang possessed a robust Yan power within him, comparable to that of a Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal. Furthermore, his source was incredibly potent. Combined with the baptism of golden sands, his divine body was even more robust than an ordinary Perfected Nine Revolutions.","As long as he avoided direct confrontation, he could escape from Luo Hao’s grasp. His current dilemma was that he needed to escape while also luring Luo Hao into the grand formation.","This was the real challenge. If he distanced himself too much, Luo Hao might give up the chase. If he got too close, it would be too dangerous. The blood blade from earlier could sever his divine body even across a million miles. If he got any closer, it could damage his source.","At this point, he didn’t fully understand Luo Hao. If he had known about Luo Hao’s extremely domineering behavior, he wouldn’t have been so conflicted.","He didn’t even need to provoke Luo Hao completely!","“Lo Hao, is this all you’re capable of? Coming all this way just to scratch me from a million miles away!” Jian Wushuang’s figure flickered abruptly, the distance between them widening significantly. He deliberately slowed down, tempting Lo Hao, afraid the opponent might suddenly stop chasing.","This was his first prey; he couldn’t give up so easily.","He had figured it out; most of the mountains now harbored only the weak, hiding and waiting for the trial to end. The truly powerful had gone to the continents on the original planet. That was the real battlefield where strong fighters fell every day.","Lo Hao was fast, trailing behind. When he heard Jian Wushuang’s taunt, he hesitated for a moment. There was no anger on his face; instead, there was a hint of confusion.","Was he deliberately mocking him?","Either he didn’t know Lo Hao’s true strength, or he wasn’t afraid of him?","Jian Wushuang knew his name; he must know his capabilities. Ranked among the top hundred thousand in the entire universe, one of the ten Great Princes of the high-grade world, he was a top-tier expert who had mastered the second-grade source Grand Dao. His Grand Dao was already perfected, ready to merge at any time. If the Qishen Temple suddenly emerged, he would have to close himself off and prepare for the merging.","Jian Wushuang was indeed fast, surpassing Lo Hao by a significant margin for now. But Lo Hao didn’t believe that someone would be so reckless just based on speed.","“I’d like to see what cards you have up your sleeve!” Lo Hao sneered. In this mountain range, he was the only top-tier expert. Even if all the Perfected Nine","Revolutions in the mountains joined forces, they wouldn’t pose a threat to him.","As for the possibility of other top-tier experts ambushing him, he wasn’t concerned at all.","His few good friends, along with the other Princes of the Daluo Realm, exchanged various information at all times. He was well aware of the positions of the top 1,000 experts on the original planet. They were certainly not in this mountain range.."]},{"number":5173,"title":"Chapter 5173: Brother Wushuang, It’s Too Much!","paragraphs":["Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Boom!","Lo Hao’s speed suddenly increased, his body clad in dazzling black armor, emitting a black light that made him even faster.","In the top 1,000, his strength was at the bottom. He didn’t have the courage to compete on the mainland, so he could only hunt down some ordinary Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortals in the mountains to maintain his ranking.","Although this adventure was risky, it was still within his control. If he didn’t take a chance, it would be hard to maintain his position in the top 1,000. If he hadn’t come back empty-handed this time, he would have made up his mind to compete on the mainland.","The top 1,000 had the bestowal of the Qishen, allowing them to comprehend the Qishen Great Dao. This was a tremendous help to him on his path. Even though he was on the edge of merging with the Dao, he had no clue whatsoever. To succeed, he could only rely on gambling. Instead of gambling during the Dao fusion, it was better to go crazy in the Qishen Temple. At least in the top 1,000 of the Original Universe, he had the strength to hold his ground.","<font < div>","A black shining figure tore through the sky, heading straight for Jian Wushuang.","If it were outside, such speed would have already torn through the void. But on the Original Universe, the space was incredibly stable, even stronger than some Patriarchs’ Dao Arenas. If it were any weaker, after a few major battles, the Original Universe would have been shattered.","Jian Wushuang’s eyes shifted until a visible black shining figure came through the air, then he started fleeing!","“It looks like he took the bait!”","At this moment, the gorge where the formation had been set in advance was getting closer and closer. It would only take the time for an incense stick to burn to reach it!","Buzz!","A ripple in the void gradually emerged. Under a certain mountain peak, a young man with a tall crown and dressed in imDerial robes slowlv walked out of a","cave. His eyes emitted a golden light, making him incredibly noble.","“Finally, my divine body is restored. Although it cost me half of my treasures, it was worth it!” The man with the high crown casually took out his identity token. His name, which was originally ranked 97th, after a few fluctuations, settled at rank 562.","“Hiding for a year, and I’ve dropped to the 500 range. It’s truly intense!” With a flicker of his figure, he left the mountains.","This wasn’t his battlefield. Now that his strength had recovered, he needed to go to the main battlefield on the continent. That’s where he could earn real achievements. Killing a 1,000 expert would yield a substantial amount of credit. Of course, the danger was commensurate, but true experts never feared danger.","“Hmm?” The man in the Emperor’s robe sneered slightly. His eyes, piercing through the void, spotted Jian Wushuang charging straight at him.","This was unexpected. He had just restored his divine body, and as soon as he stepped out, he encountered a fat opportunity. It seemed the opponent’s strength was not weak.","He slightly retreated, striking out with a fist toward Jian Wushuang. A tremendous fist shadow erupted, sweeping across countless mountains. For a moment, boulders tumbled down in succession.","In the depths of the ravine, Hu Qing abruptly opened his eyes. The immense aura caused ripples in the array formations.","“Wushuang, you’re pushing yourself too hard!” He sighed and stabilized the formations again, calmly awaiting the upcoming fierce battle.","However, he didn’t know that the aura had already exceeded Jian Wushuang’s control.","“Almost there, we’re about to reach!” Jian Wushuang breathed a sigh of relief. The gorge was in sight. With the large array there and his collaboration with Hu Qing, they had no fear of the Prince, Luo Hao.","“What’s going on here?”","Without waiting for Jian Wushuang to see clearly what was happening in front of him, a massive fist shadow crashed into his body.","Boom!","The deliberately charged punch, a supreme technique of an Emperor, belonged to a young man with an incredibly powerful background. While he wasn’t a Prince of any specific power, he was a son of a powerful Emperor.","In this world, he wasn’t just a Prince; he was an Emperor!","His father had even allocated him 30 percent of the territory to govern. This territory encompassed one-third of a high-grade world, larger than even a middle-grade world. Within his sphere of influence, even Emperors respectfully called him “Your Majesty, the God Emperor.”","But in this primitive planet, where strength surpassed background, even though his father was a Ruler, he had almost been killed on the spot. Only by sacrificing a transcendent innate treasure did he manage to escape death.","Jian Wushuang was sent flying millions of miles backward by the force of the punch, even passing by the pursuing Luo Hao.","“What does this mean?” Luo Hao was puzzled. No matter how audacious the other party was, he hadn’t expected them to be audacious enough to fly past him and mock him.","But before he could erupt in anger, he felt a powerful aura approaching, tearing through the air.","“He’s not dead!” The Emperor youth, after glancing at Jian Wushuang, turned his gaze toward Luo Hao. His voice trembled as he said, “A kid from the Daluo Realm! Very good, very good indeed.”","At this moment, he no longer cared about Jian Wushuang, who had been sent flying by a single punch. Instead, he looked at Luo Hao with great interest.","In the main continent, he had been severely injured and nearly killed. The son of the Daluo Realm had even taken the opportunity to ambush him. He remembered the background of the other party, originating from a high-grade world in the Daluoo Realm, not inferior to their Tiansuo Realm.","Luo Hao also realized what was happening, but it was already too late to escape. He couldn’t fathom how such a powerful being had appeared in this place.","“You are God-Emperor MO Long!” Luo Hao’s battle spirit was high, even though he knew the opponent was a peak powerhouse, the son of an Emperor, and possessed various treasures.","“Kid, today you will die. Blame it on the other Princes of your Daluo Realm!” God -Emperor MO Long said coldly.","If it weren’t for that Prince of the Daluo Realm ambushing him, he wouldn’t have been so severely injured. Now, just the rapid recovery of his divine body had cost him half of his treasures.","His countless years of accumulation, combined with the various treasures bestowed upon him by his father, made his total worth comparable to some tier 3 Emperors. It took half the treasures of a tier 3 Emperor just to restore his divine body. One could imagine how severe his injuries were.","He had almost fallen into a deep slumber. If he hadn’t used treasures to repair his divine body, relying solely on cultivation to recover would have taken several chaos cycles. With a single mishap, his divine body might have collapsed and he would have perished.","Now, after a year, he had restored his peak divine body. One could imagine how many treasures he had spent.","He would definitely settle this account. If he didn’t make it into the top ten this time, his trip here would be considered a loss.","Even if he made it into the top 10, the treasures bestowed by the Qishen Temple wouldn’t be too many. Understanding the usefulness of the Qishen Great Dao for him was more significant.","It was all because of that Prince from the Daluo Realm. At a critical moment, he ambushed him. In the chaotic battle of peak powerhouses, it was like a group of hungry beasts fighting each other. Whoever weakened first became the prey. Only by maintaining peak combat power could one have dominance.","Once someone’s aura weakened, other powerhouses were like sharks smelling blood, instantly pouncing on their prey.","God -Emperor MO Long, well aware of this, blamed everything on that Prince from the Daluoo Realm. Now, just as he had restored his strength, he encountered Luo Hao, one of the ten Princes of the Daluo Realm.."]},{"number":5174,"title":"Chapter 5174: God-Emperor MO Long","paragraphs":["Chapter 5174: God-Emperor MO Long","Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Although he had no personal grudge against him, he didn’t mind taking care of this top-tier expert among the Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortals as a form of revenge.","While recovering his divine body in seclusion, he had specifically investigated the strong figures in the Daluo Realm on this original primitive planet.","Six out of the ten Princes were on this primitive planet, a rare occurrence. Among them, two possessed peak strength, while the remaining four were top-tier experts.","In a one-on-one battle, God-Emperor MO Long was fully confident in defeating them one by one. “Prince, Luo Hao!”","He was the first target.","God-Emperor MO Longs aura erupted, his fist striking towards Luo Hao, a punch ten times stronger than the one he had used against Jian Wushuang moments ago.","“Emperor’s Fall!” He roared, instantly appearing in front of Luo Hao. Boom! Boom! Boom!","Their fight made the entire mountain range boil. Although Luo Hao was slightly weaker in power, he possessed innate treasures, coupled with peak-grade armor, enough to bridge some of the gap.","But he forgot the fact that his opponent was the son of an Emperor.","In just an instant, they exchanged blows hundreds of times.","Golden fist shadows smashed against peak-grade armor, producing crackling sounds.","“I’ll shatter that turtle shell of yours!” God-Emperor MO Longs hands transformed into golden dragon claws, surging with power, striking at Luo Hao once again.","The immense force made Luo Hao’s heart tremble.","“This is bad!”","He had no room to retreat. A crescent-shaped flying blade appeared in his hand, swinging with all his might toward God-Emperor MO Longs head.","Using one move to counter another!","Placing oneself in a desperate situation for a chance of survival!","“Spectacular! It’s truly spectacular!” Two members of the Great Dream Clan","hiding on a distant mountain peak watched, their blood boiling!","They hadn’t anticipated the sudden appearance of God-Emperor MO Long, who directly overwhelmed Luo Hao with a barrage of punches!","There was even hope of slaying Luo Hao!","“Senior Brother, am I unable to take revenge myself?” murmured the young woman from the Great Dream Clan.","“Fear not, Junior Sister. I’ve heard of God-Emperor MO Long. His father once visited our Great Dream Realm, seeking assistance from our ancestor,” said the man from the Great Dream Realm, his face tinged with pride. “Once the situation stabilizes, 1 will personally go and talk to him. Out of respect for our ancestor, we’ll handle Luo Hao ourselves!”","Confidence filled the man’s face. In their eyes, no one could disrespect the","Great Dream Realm, except for those petty individuals from the Daluo Realm.","In their view, the Great Dream Realm was one of the core powers in the entire universe.","Thousands of miles away, Jian Wushuangs body was embedded in a mountain peak. His body had crashed through several peaks before finally landing in a pile of rocks within a mountain.","Puff!","His body trembled, and a mouthful of scalding golden blood sprayed from his mouth. It took him a moment to recover.","The echoes of explosions in the sky reverberated in his mind.","“God-Emperor MO Long!” Jian Wushuang cursed under his breath. Peak experts who could injure his divine body with just one punch were truly unfortunate encounters!","He was in deep trouble this time.","A single punch had left him dazed. Fortunately, due to his strong mental state, he recovered within a breath and emerged from the chaotic rubble.","He happened to see Luo Hao, who was currently engaged in battle with God-Emperor MO Long.","“It’s not entirely hopeless yet, but it’s a pity. They’re just a step away. If only these two could fight within his grand formation!” Jian Wushuangs eyes flickered. He could escape now, but if he did, this trip would be in vain. Although he had gained nearly four hundred thousand battle achievements, he was still far from the top 1,000.","Little novice monk Hu Qing was still waiting naively within the grand formation. If he gave up now, where could he go to attract Perfected Nine Revolutions experts?","There were too few Perfected Nine Revolutions in these mountains, and the mainland was too dangerous. There was simply no opportunity to set up agrand formation.","In the pursuit of wealth and danger, Jian Wushuangs sharp mind conceived a bold idea.","What if he could lure the top thousand superpowers into the grand array and then wait until both sides were injured?","It wasn’t entirely impossible. At the moment, God-Emperor MO Long held the absolute advantage on the battlefield, already causing injuries to Luo Hao, who possessed peak-grade battle armor. If Jian Wushuang could distract God-Emperor MO Long from a distance and lead Luo Hao into the formation, he could ensnare God-Emperor MO Long as well.","The plan was viable, but tremendously difficult. Firstly, it depended on whether Luo Hao would believe him. Before the situation became a matter of life and death, it was hard for Luo Hao to trust his words, especially since Jian Wushuang had led Luo Hao here, coincidentally encountering God-Emperor MO Long.","Someone unaware might think Jian Wushuang had intentionally led Luo Hao here, allowing God-Emperor MO Long to deal with him.","God-Emperor MO Long was incredibly powerful, and his methods were even more extreme than Luo Hao’s. Both were domineering figures. If he appeared and the two of them teamed up, it was entirely possible for them to kill Jian","Wushuang.","“Wait!","Jian Wushuang decided. He would wait until Luo Hao couldn’t hold on any longer, needing reinforcements, and then he would strike.","“Yes, that’s it!” Jian Wushuangs figure flickered a few times, disappearing into the void millions of miles away from their battle. He concealed himself and communicated with Hu Qing, preparing to face the enemy at any moment.","Inside the canyon’s grand array, after receiving Jian Wushuangs message, Hu Qing replied with a simple ‘Understood’.","His aura imperceptibly grew stronger. This wasn’t strength cultivated through practice; it was a reviving force.","In his mind, two sets of memories intertwined. Hu Qing understood his true nature. Although the consciousness in his mind was incredibly powerful, he slowly devoured it bit by bit.","“l have only one purpose: to suppress all evil thoughts!” Hu Qings delicate face carried a hint of ruthlessness. Scenes of black evil thoughts invading him played out in his eyes.","The battle of the two consciousnesses was surprisingly no weaker than the struggles of the top external experts.","In the midst of a brutal hand-to-hand combat, where flesh met flesh, and amidst the clash of mortal and celestial forces, the tranquility of the mountains was shattered.","Bang!","Once again, Luo Hao was smashed to the ground by a powerful punch, reducing the towering mountain that once stood there to nothing but a leveled plain.","In the sky above, the Dragon Claw Gauntlet of the God-Emperor MO Long was stained with crimson blood, dripping from its razor-sharp edges.","“Look at this, it’s a piece of your own flesh!” MO Long sneered, shaking off the nauseating chunks of flesh in his hand.","Splat!","Luo Hao managed to pull his body from the sunken earth, clutching his chest. Even his peak-grade supreme armor had shattered.","Normally, it was incredibly difficult to damage such peak-grade supreme armor under an Emperor’s level. Even with the help of innate treasures, it was a daunting task to destroy armor of this caliber.","However, the strength of the God-Emperor MO Long was overwhelming. A Perfected Nine Revolutions, he possessed multiple innate treasures.","The mysterious artifact at his brow, in particular, wielded the power of a top-grade innate treasure. Even Emperor-level experts envied this mysterious item, which had been bestowed upon him by his father during the last opening of the Qishen Temple.","The last time he almost fell, he hadn’t even been willing to use it. Before entering the Qishen Temple, his father had warned him that this artifact was difficult to control. It wasn’t a treasure born within the universe, but an ancient relic that had drifted through the river of time and space, passed down from ancient times.."]},{"number":5175,"title":"Chapter 5175: Delaying Each Other","paragraphs":["Chapter 5175: Delaying Each Other","Translator: Endless?antasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","The ancient artifact he possessed was merely a component of an ancient treasure. It had the ability to amplify his divine power. Once activated, it could make his divine power more than ten times stronger. However, controlling it was extremely difficult, making it unsuitable for chaotic battles. It could be used effectively in one-on-one combat without distractions.","That’s why God-Emperor MO Lone hadn’t used this artifact in their previous encounter. He was confident that he could eliminate all the emperor’s children of the Daluo Realm in one-on-one combat.","Breathing heavily, Luo Hao clutched his chest.","‘No, I must hold on. The message has been sent out, but it will take time for the strong members of the clan to arrive. I can’t fall here,’ he thought, his determination fierce.","He couldn’t accept defeat!","He had carefully planned this mountain range, turning it into his hunting ground. He had good relations with other peak experts. He had a great hope to maintain his position in the top thousand and receive the divine gift from the Qishen Temple to comprehend the Qishen Great Dao. He couldn’t fall here.","For his clan, for himself, he couldn’t fall. He was the proudest Grand Yan Immortal of the Guca Clan. He couldn’t fall.","“l am Guca-Luo Hao!” he raised his head, his eyes wide with determination. “l will not be defeated by you!’","Boom!","His previously weak aura skyrocketed again, surpassing even the mighty aura he had at his peak, piercing the sky.","A majestic column of energy shot straight into the clouds!","His strength surged, fragmentary bolts of lightning covering his body, flickering with the power of thunder.","Although his aura surged, he didn’t rush to attack. He could buy some time. If he struck now, he wouldn’t be able to hold on until the strong members of the clan came to his aid.","“What’s this? Burning the source of the Great Dao already?” mocked God-Emperor MO Long. “Not bad, this supreme technique can convert the burning source into triple divine power. It can be considered a top-notch supreme technique! It’s one of the best among the intermediate supreme techniques. ”","God-Emperor MO Long shook his head.","“If you think this can match my strength, then you’re underestimating me.”","The Perfected Nine Revolutions were stratified, their strengths varying widely, dependent on the power of their source Dao.","Among the fifth-grade source Dao, Perfected Nine Revolutions were considered commonplace. Even with peak treasures, they could only stand out moderately in this category.","Fourth-grade source Dao Grand Yan Immortals, relying on peak treasures, could touch the threshold of top-level Grand Yan Immortals with their exceptional cultivation.","Only those Perfected Nine Revolutions with third-grade Dao could be deemed top-tier experts. With peak treasures, they stood at the pinnacle among Perfected Nine Revolutions.","Second-grade source Dao experts, after completing their cultivation, generally touched the peak threshold. Take Luo Hao, for example. He practiced second-grade source Dao, reaching the peak threshold with his cultivation, albeit his treasures weren’t sufficient.","If he possessed half the treasures of God-Emperor MO Long, he would have the battle prowess of a peak Grand Yan Immortal.","God-Emperor MO Longs Dao wasn’t top-tier among second-grade Dao, but it wasn’t the worst either. With abundant treasures, he was the most outstanding among peak experts, just below extreme Grand Yan Immortals like Jiu Yu, capable of slaughtering hundreds of Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortals single-handedly.","To accurately categorize, there were stages of initial, ordinary, top-grade, peak, extreme, and half-step Emperor.","Half-step Emperors, experts at this level, were almost always using Ultimate Dao, either peerless geniuses who comprehended the fusion of myriad Daos or cultivators of the Ultimate Dao.","There were very few of them in the entire universe, and as far as the current situation was concerned, not a single one existed on this primitive planet.","In the Five-Fold World, each world had 36 primitive planets, totaling 180 planets. With a bit of luck, one wouldn’t encounter such monsters. If luck turned sour, escape was the only option.","Every primitive or orignal planet was a slaughterhouse for that half-step Emperors. Undoubtedly, such powerhouses occupied the throne of first place in this regard.","As long as the Qishen Temple operated smoothly, the two half-step Emperors would never clash. Ultimately, the Qishen Temple was here to sift through strong beings. Those like them, ordinary Grand Yan Immortals on the path of the original Great Dao, were unlikely to be chosen. In the end, those who truly stood out were the ultimate existences or geniuses who comprehended the Unity of Myriad Daos.","God-Emperor MO Long looked down upon Luo Hao with disdain. “A lowly creature dares to challenge me!”","Boom!","Instantly, the two ascended to the sky, and every move they made resonated with a dull sound.","God-Emperor MO Longs every move was precise, targeting non-vital points, only disturbing Luo Hao’s veins. The divine power he could burn with his source was limited after all. Luo Hao was anxious, but not at all hurried.","He knew why the opponent was resisting like this: waiting for the other strong beings of the Daluo Realm!","These strong beings in the Daluo Realm were also incredibly fortunate. Six out of the ten Emperor’s descendants had descended upon the ‘Original Planet Alpha Nine’. They complemented each other quite well.","In his eyes, Luo Hao had been guarding this mountain range. Eight chances out of ten, he was here on the orders of the First Prince of the Daluoo Realm. If injured, he could hide here, recover his divine body, and consider Luo Hao as a retreat.","The fact that Luo Hao was left with the back door clearly showed that the other descendants had great trust in him. If he called for help now, those other descendants would undoubtedly come to his aid.","He could play his cards right, first severely injure Luo Hao, then expose a weakness, waiting for the Princes of Daluo Realm to arrive. Then, one by one, he would eliminate them. Even if they came together, he was willing to use his secret treasures, enough to kill one or two and still escape unharmed. This way, he would both avenge his grievances and accumulate significant military merits.","In this mountainous battleground, there was no need to worry about old enemies sneaking up on him. The Princes of Daluo Realm wouldn’t be foolish enough to expose their home base, luring other strong opponents to deal with him. His displayed strength was not far behind Daluo Realm’s chief. Plus, feigning unhealed injuries, they would surely relax their guard. If he got a chance to kill Daluo Realm’s chief, it would be a huge victory.","The current chief of Daluo Realm was ranked 76th, with a combat record easily in the tens of millions.","Ha!","Luo Hao gripped a spinning flying blade in one hand, blocking the heavy punches of God-Emperor MO Long. In his other hand appeared a black rhombus-shaped crystal pillar.","He was never good at close combat. His enlightenment was the Great Dao of","Gold. His divine body wasn’t exceptionally strong. Unlike God-Emperor MO Long, who had an Emperor as his father, even if he didn’t focus on strengthening his physical body, he could still spend a considerable amount of treasures to refine his body to perfection. Combined with the Dao of the Mountain, his strength was terrifying, his defense akin to a towering divine mountain, and his speed, needless to say. Mastering the Dao of the Mountain, he could shrink space and escape without a trace.","God-Emperor MO Long’s strength could be described as reaching perfection. This was the advantage of a strong background. Without such support, just having a perfect physical body would require all the assets of an ordinary","Emperor. Where could one find the resources and treasures for a Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal?","Luo Hao had his own background, although powerful. He was just one of the top 10 Princes of his generation. If he couldn’t successfully merge the Daos","within the time limit or lacked the strength to do so, he would be sent to a","distant place, losing access to resources and training. He would find it nearly impossible to merge the Daos successfully throughout his lifetime.."]},{"number":5176,"title":"Chapter 5176 Give Me Face","paragraphs":["5176 Give Me Face","Therefore, he had no choice but to gamble. Before entering the Qishen Temple, in addition to the transcendent innate treasure bestowed by the Emperor, he had exchanged an Emperor-grade Destruction God Crystal, a relic of the Emperor's own destruction, with all his accumulated wealth.","This Emperor-grade Destruction God Crystal was crafted by a formidable expert who had achieved Emperor status through the path of destruction. Though it was merely a first-grade god crystal, it possessed three-tenths of an Emperor's power. Once detonated, it could easily kill a Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal, severely injure a peak powerhouse, and even pose a threat to an inattentive peak expert.","This was his ultimate trump card, and revealing it now meant he truly had reached a dead end.","\"Mo Long, stop pretending. I know that you were severely injured the last round. I suspect you haven't fully recovered your strength yet!\" Luo Hao raised the Destruction God Crystal high, continuing, \"This is an Emperor-grade Destruction God Crystal. If you don't cease, I will detonate it, and we will all die together. Even if you can withstand the explosion, your divine body will be on the brink of collapse, disqualifying you from competing for the top 10 spots.\"","He had long sensed that God-Emperor Mo Long was not at his best, a deduction based on intelligence gathered a year ago. God- Emperor Mo Long was likely operating at only 80 percent of his full strength, currently secluded for recovery. This sudden emergence was probably due to Jian Wushuang's influence.","Thinking this, Luo Hao clenched his teeth. He almost forgot about Jian Wushuang. If not for that young man, he wouldn't have ended up in this dire situation. He was now facing the risk of falling.","However, he didn't have time to worry about Jian Wushuang now.","He needed to deal with the immediate threat. As long as he survived this ordeal, even if he had to turn the mountains upside down, he would find Jian Wushuang and obliterate him completely!","Even if they escaped the Qishen Temple, he wouldn't let Jian Wushuang off the hook!","Thinking about the legendary Grand Yan Immortal, 'Dao Lord Jiu Yu, in the Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm sent shivers down his spine.","Anyone who became a Dao Lord was not to be trifled with. An Emperor represented the success of combining Daos, and a Dao Lord represented the immense power of the original source, reaching a limit comparable to an Emperor. Only those who could rival Emperors earned the title of Dao Lord.","Those at the peak or half-step Dao Lord level were beyond their reach. Especially in the absence of an Emperor, these individuals were the strongest entities.","Even the mighty God-Emperor Mo Long didn't dare provoke a Dao Lord. Despite his formidable background, if faced with absolute power, even his most potent treasures could be easily neutralized. For instance, high-grade Destruction God Crystals.","\"An Emperor-grade Destruction God Crystal!\"","God-Emperor Mo Long sneered, saying, \"How foolish. Even if you detonate it, even if I die with you, do you dare?\"","In his view, if Destruction God Crystals were useful, he would simply buy a hundred of them. If he encountered someone stronger, he could throw one out, rendering him invincible.","These Emperor-grade Destruction God Crystals only caused physical damage. Having a peak treasure armor was enough to withstand 99.9 percent of their destructive power. The remaining fraction could be neutralized by inner armor. Killing a peak Grand Yan Immortal was difficult, let alone a top-grade Perfected Nine Revolutions. At most, these crystals could intimidate the poor souls who couldn't afford peak treasures, a feeble attempt to frighten them. It was utterly laughable.","\"You fool!\" God-Emperor Mo Long mocked his opponent mercilessly, gradually eroding Luo Hao's mental defenses, causing him to collapse completely.","\"Fine, if that's the case, then let's all die together!\" Luo Hao, for the first time, activated the Destruction God Crystal. He had only heard of this kind of prohibited-grade disposable treasure before. He knew it might not kill his opponent, but he didn't expect God- Emperor Mo Long to be so unbothered.","God-Emperor Mo Long's eyes narrowed.","Whoosh!","A thread of Yan power seeped into the interior of the Destruction God Crystal, then it was thrown fiercely at Mo Long.","The black shining battle armor instantly enveloped Luo Hao, and he quickly retreated.","\"This madman really dares to use it!\" God-Emperor Mo Long chuckled. To prevent himself from being blown up by the Destruction God Crystal, he had to take out a suppressive type of innate treasure, directly suppressing the Destruction God Crystal in a cyan bamboo building.","\"Transcendence Innate Top-Grade Treasure, Suppressing Jade Pavilion!\"","Buzz!","A muffled sound, and the Destruction God Crystal detonated within the Suppressing Jade Pavilion.","\"Is that it?\" Jian Wushuang was stunned.","He lowered his hands from covering his head, put away his only high-grade treasure shield, and let out a sigh of relief.","\"Luo Hao's trump card!\"","Jian Wushuang shook his head. In his heart, he thought, \"I can't delay anymore. Luo Hao's state of mind has changed. If I don't help, he might really end up dead here.\"","From a distance, he could tell that God-Emperor Mo Long had been toying with Luo Hao all along. Although he didn't know the depth of their enmity, judging from the situation, it seemed that God- Emperor Mo Long was preparing to play Luo Hao to death.","His form halted; he had just intended to move, but he realized that someone had beaten him to it.","A man and a woman, both wearing colorful robes, their backs adorned with dreamlike feathers unique to the Great Dream Realm.","\"Brother Mo Long, I have brought the 6th generation Chief Daoist of the Great Dream Realm. Could you please give me face and hand over this person to me?\" The woman spoke, her voice firm.","Before God-Emperor Mo Long could react, Luo Hao, who had blocked his path, burst into laughter.","\"Haha!\" Luo Hao laughed arrogantly, dispelling his earlier frustration. He sneered, \"I don't regret dying at all. With you two fools accompanying me, the journey won't be lonely!\"","\"You despicable scoundrel! How dare you speak so arrogantly in this situation!\" the Great Dream Clan girl shouted angrily, her hands gripping a precious red long knife.","God-Emperor Mo Long stood still for a long time before he finally comprehended the situation.","\"Are you people from the Great Dream Clan?\" he asked.","They nodded in affirmation.","\"Now, while you haven't provoked my wrath, get lost!\" God- Emperor Mo Long's mind swiftly searched for information about the powerful beings in the Great Dream Realm. Then he shouted in anger, \"Get out of here right now!\"","The Great Dream Realm was just a medium-grade world; the strength of the Great Dream Dao Ancestor alone was formidable enough to rank among the top one hundred in the entire universe. His father indeed had some connections with the Great Dream Dao Ancestor, but Mo Long considered those connections as mere acquaintanceships.","Even if he had those connections, so what? The entire Eastern Domain, strictly speaking, was dominated by just two major forces: the Chishui Hall and the Eternal Tower.","Did they mean to imply that he could only kill powerful beings from the Eternal Tower based on this?","It was ridiculous. This alliance was temporary at best. When they entered the Qishen Temple, no one cared about alliances unless they were from the same clan or world.","Moreover, a Grand Yan Immortal who hadn't reached the Perfected Nine Revolutions level dared to come and demand respect at this moment.","He didn't know what to do.","Even peak-level experts wouldn't dare to demand respect at this moment, let alone someone who was just a Grand Yan Immortal on the edge of the Nine Revolutions. And he was asking for respect for this superpowerful being ranked within the top 1,000 on this original planet, a being with numerous achievements.","Such a fat lamb, he would gladly send them off.","Apart from the Dao Lords, even a Perfected Nine Revolutions wouldn't be tolerated at this moment.","\"Mo Long, our ancestor has helped your father immensely. How dare you treat us so disrespectfully!\" The Great Dream Clan girl's face was filled with anger, her expression one of incomprehension."]},{"number":5177,"title":"Chapter 5177: Which Family Doesn’t Have an Emperor Stage Expert?","paragraphs":["Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","The senior brother beside her tugged at her sleeve and whispered, “Junior","Sister, something seems off!”","God- Emperor Mo Long sneered and nodded mockingly, “Alright, alright, very well!”","“Luo Hao, I’ll give you a chance to explain. Why should 1 give them face?”","God-Emperor MO Long was planning to delay time anyway, waiting for the Daoists from the Great Luo Realm to take the bait. He decided to play along.","<font < div>","He had heard that people from the Great Dream Realm were like madmen. Today, he finally understood why those people avoided them.","“Explain?” Luo Hao felt a glimmer of hope. He thought, ‘This God-Emperor MO Long must have been enraged by these two fools before him. He wants to humiliate them through me.’","God-Emperor MO Long nodded, his anger evident. “Yes, explain it to me properly. Why the hell should I give them face?”","“For the alliance?” Luo Hao cautiously ventured.","God-Emperor MO Long shook his head, his voice filled with rage. “Wrong, think harder! ”","“It can’t possibly be for me!” Luo Hao chuckled self-deprecatingly.","“I’ll give you one last chance. Explain it to them properly!!","This time, Luo Hao fell into deep thought. This was a perfect opportunity to delay. He had to seize it.","However, the two members of the Great Dream Clan couldn’t bear it any longer.","“God-Emperor MO Long, if it’s inconvenient, my junior sister and I will take our leave!” The man from the Great Dream Clan said and then pulled his junior sister, preparing to leave. “Junior Sister, let’s go!’","“You’re leaving?” God-Emperor MO Long waved his hand, and a sky-piercing barrier descended, blocking their escape route. He smiled faintly, “Don’t be in a hurry. You wanted face, didn’t you? I’ll give it to you.”","“Have you figured it out, Luo Hao?” God-Emperor MO Long asked calmly.","“l have,” Luo Hao nodded. His expression turned icy, and his eyes gleamed with killing intent as he looked at the two members of the Great Dream Clan. “Remember, it’s not that God-Emperor MO Long doesn’t give you face, it’s that you fools aren’t worthy of killing me.”","Boom!","Despite sustaining severe injuries, he was more than capable of dealing with these two fools!","“MO Long, I never expected you to be this despicable. You refuse to give face and resort to such tactics, letting Luo Hao, this scoundrel, handle us!” The young woman from the Great Dream Clan shouted angrily as she retreated.","Jian Wushuang, concealed in the void, couldn’t stand it any longer. If it weren’t for these two fools disrupting him, he might have already led God-Emperor MO Long and Luo Hao into the grand array.","He could see that Luo Hao had the strength to swiftly deal with the two members of the Great Dream Realm. However, in order to buy time, he was entangled in a back-and-forth battle with the two fools from the Great Dream","Clan.","If this continued, his plan couldn’t be executed at all.","Swish!","His figure flickered, and he appeared directly above the two Great Dream Clan members. With a swift half-circle sweep of his long spear, he sent the two men tumbling back tens of thousands of miles.","“You fools!” Jian Wushuang muttered under his breath, then turned to look at Luo Hao.","“Luo Hao, I’m sorry for being late!” Jian Wushuang said, a faint smile on his","Luo Hao couldn’t help but tilt his head to look at Jian Wushuang. If it weren’t for the God-Emperor MO Long, he would have wanted to strangle Jian Wushuang right then and there. He had finally found a reason to stall for time, and now Jian Wushuang had ruined it.","“Another one?” God-Emperor MO Long was starting to question his life choices. Weren’t these weak Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortals supposed to flee as far as possible when faced with a situation like this?","Normally, these Perfected Nine Revolutions, who were too afraid to even watch from the sidelines, were now jumping in front of him one by one, seeking death. This was the first time he had encountered such a situation in the Original Universe.","“What, are you here to save face too?” God-Emperor MO Long didn’t seem to be in a hurry, speaking nonchalantly.","Jian Wushuang retracted his long spear and held an illusory long sword in his hand. He spoke earnestly, “Your Majesty, God-Emperor, Luo Hao and I share a bond of life and death. I had no choice but to come to his rescue. I hope you understand.’","As his words fell, Luo Hao was dumbfounded. Were these people intentionally making a mockery of him?","First, two fools came looking to save face in front of God-Emperor MO Long and ended up being killed by him. And now, another one had come to save Luo Hao from the hands of God-Emperor MO Long.","After this back and forth, he was really having trouble understanding the situation.","God-Emperor MO Long, however, looked with interest at Jian Wushuang, nodded, and said, “Jian Wushuang, I know you!’","The two members of the Daming Clan who had been overturned in the distance were still somewhat unwilling to accept the situation. However, they also recognized lian Wushuang at this moment. Both sides had encountered each other in the Chishui Hall.","Tongtian Buddha, with his immense power, was someone they had witnessed firsthand. So, they had a rough idea about some of the Grand Yan Immortals in the Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm. In their eyes, Jian Wushuang seemed no more than an ordinary Grand Yan Immortal at the Perfected Nine","Revolutions stage. Weren’t they the ones being chased by Luo Hao? Why would Jian Wushuang come to rescue Luo Hao?","Not only were the two of them puzzled, but even Luo Hao himself was unclear why Jian Wushuang had turned back to save him.","“Your Majesty, it’s my honor to be remembered by you!” Jian Wushuang showed great humility. He didn’t want to anger the God-Emperor MO Long. If he could lead both of them into the grand formation without provoking the God-Emperor, it would be perfect.","In the outside world, he was at most comparable to a Perfected Nine Revolutions, but neither of these two individuals was his match. However, once inside the grand formation, he would have confidence.","“You’re impressive. Being comparable to a Nine Revolutions at the Three","Revolutions level. You probably have the strength of an ordinary Perfected Nine Revolutions by the time you are Six Revolutions!” God-Emperor MO Long vividly remembered Jian Wushuangs astonishing performance on the Universe Deity-Demon List, ranking 160 millionth at the Three Revolutions and entering the top 100 million when he reached Six Revolutions.","An existence that mastered the Ultimate Dao!","“What? He’s a Six Revolutions!” exclaimed a man from the distant Great Dream Clan. “Being comparable to a Perfected Nine Revolutions at the sixth stage, how is that possible!”","Among the numerous powerful beings in the entire universe, only a few paid attention to Jian Wushuang. Most of the powerful beings, apart from focusing on their own rankings, remembered the top 1,000 peerless geniuses in the universe.","Luo Hao stood in the air and looked at the two members of the Great Dream Clan, saying coldly, “Fools, just because you can’t achieve something doesn’t mean others can’t.’","Then his tone softened, “It seems Brother Wushuang has mastered the","Ultimate Dao, unexpectedly reaching the level of being comparable to a","Perfected Nine Revolutions when you’re only at the Six Revolutions stage. When you reach the realm of a Perfected Nine Revolutions in the Great Dao, you will probably be a half-step Emperor.”","However, the young woman from the Great Dream Clan sneered, “Half-step","Emperor, after all, is still just a half-step Emperor. Our ancestor is a true","Emperor.”","“Hmph!” Luo Hao snorted and cursed, ‘E ls there no Emperor in your Great Dream Realm? Does my Daluo Realm lack Emperors?”","“Isn’t Brother MO Longs father an Emperor?”","“In the Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm where Brother Wushuang is from, isn’t there an Emperor? Have you forgotten the strength of the Tongtian Lord Buddha?”","“That guy is stronger than your ancestor!”"]},{"number":5178,"title":"Chapter 5178: You’re Being Very Disrespectful","paragraphs":["Chapter 5178: You’re Being Very Disrespectful","Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","What Luo Hao said wasn’t entirely wrong. Indeed, who among them didn’t have an Emperor backing them up?","The strength of the Great Dream Dao Ancestor was unquestionable. He had ranked within the top 100 throughout the entire universe. In the Eastern Domain, one of the five major regions, he was among the top 20. Such power demanded respect.","But in the Qishen Temple, individual strength mattered most, followed by the backing of one’s faction. While the Great Dream Realm had considerable reputation, its influence was far from top-tier. The Dao Ancestor of the Great Dream was incredibly strong, yet he had few Emperors under his command.","Especially the sixth- generation disciples of the Great Dream Realm present there were pitifully weak. A mere third- grade source of the Great Dao and a Perfected Nine Revolutions – with such strength, they dared to seek face?","They were speaking arrogantly, looking down on half- step Emperors!","It was simply a death wish. The trial had just begun, and the powerful beings of the Great Dream Realm on this primitive planet had almost been annihilated. Yet, they hadn’t learned humility. They still clung to the external standards of the outside world.","Here, no one cared how powerful your ancestor was. If your individual strength wasn’t enough, you were nothing.","God-Emperor MO Long, despite being a Prince, had been severely wounded by others. If he hadn’t been a bit slower in his escape, he might have perished. Yet, he hadn’t invoked his father’s name to intimidate others.","A true strong individual had self-awareness. Invoking the power behind you would only invite disdain and ultimately lead to humiliation and death.","In the Qishen Temple, no one would chant praises for your ancestor, no matter how strong he was. Even if you were the son of a fifth-rank Emperor, you’d be crushed!","“You!” The young woman of the Great Dream Clan was left speechless by the retort.","In her heart, the Great Dream Dao Ancestor and the Great Dream Realm had always been the core of the universe. How had they encountered such arrogant people just after leaving the Great Dream Realm?","The man from the Great Dream Clan, however, bowed his head in silence. He had accepted his fate. In the Qishen Temple, things were fundamentally different from their homeland. No one fell for their tricks anymore.","“Hmph, just leave already!” Jian Wushuang couldn’t help but shout in anger.","These two were simply wasting time. Wasn’t it better to live peacefully? They insisted on courting death. How was it that God-Emperor MO Long was so patient? Why hadn’t they obliterated them already?","“Sister, let’s leave!” The man from the Great Dream Clan couldn’t bear it any longer. He was starting to get scared. No one present was to be trifled with.","Jian Wushuang could easily crush both of them in his Six Revolutions cultivation. If they didn’t leave, the Great Dream Clan might never have strong individuals again on the Alpha Nine Original Planet.","The young woman from the Great Dream Clan’s face turned red with anger. She didn’t care anymore and shouted loudly, “Senior Brother Yang, how did you become so spineless? We are disciples of the Great Dream Realm. You disappoint me.”","The man from the Great Dream Clan glared at her, then said in a low voice,","“Sister!”","Saying this, he grabbed the young woman’s arm and pulled her back.","“What are you doing?” The young woman from the Great Dream Clan struggled free from her senior brother’s grip and shouted, “Don’t you want to avenge Sister for her humiliation?”","Slap!","A crisp sound of a slap echoed. The man from the Great Dream Clan had a blackened face. Without waiting for the young woman’s reaction, another slap landed on her left cheek.","The young woman from the Great Dream Clan stood in mid-air, staring blankly at her once familiar senior brother, her small red face now bearing two distinct slap marks.","Her eyes turned red, and she was on the verge of tears. But seeing her senior brother’s stern face, she felt fear now and dared not cry.","“Everyone, my apologies for the abruptness, but we must leave now,” said the man from the Great Dream Clan, his Yan power enveloping his dazed junior sister, preparing to depart.","Meanwhile, Luo Hao, who had been observing the spectacle, changed his focus. These two fools were about to leave, leaving the three of them to an inevitable fierce battle. Instead of letting them go, Luo Hao decided to detain them first, delaying them for a while, After settling his attention, Luo Hao spoke up.","“You think you can just come and go as you please? Do you underestimate us?” Luo Hao glared at the two men, blades flying out behind him, blocking their way.","God-Emperor MO Long watched from the side, considering it quite a spectacle. Since Luo Hao wanted to play, he dared to prolong the situation.","As for Jian Wushuang, he intended to kill him while his strength was still","weak. With only Perfected Nine Revolutions-level strength, he could be easily crushed and posed no real threat.","Both of them were waiting, one for reinforcements and the other fishing.","Jian Wushuang had no reinforcements; he had to be his own bait for the fishing. He couldn’t afford to delay, but seeing the calm demeanor of the two men, he had no choice but to wait, without any solution.","The more anxious he became, the more flaws he would reveal. It might raise suspicions with Luo Hao and the others, making the situation worse.","“l wonder how we could earn your mercy,” said the man from the Great Dream Clan, his demeanor no longer proud.","Luo Hao glanced at God-Emperor MO Long first, realizing he was in no hurry. Then he continued, “We can spare you, but don’t you think you’re being very disrespectful to not even kneel in front of someone as powerful as Brother MO Long?!”","“Do you understand my meaning?”","The man from the Great Dream Clan nodded.","“We understand! ”","Whoosh!","His figure rapidly descended, landing on a relatively flat stone surface. He bent his knees and knelt down.","“The Great Dream Clan, a humble cultivator, Yang Yuan, pays his respects to God-Emperor Your Majesty!’","Yang Yuan, a cultivator from the Great Dream Clan, bowed his head between his knees. His body trembled not out of fear, but because of the immense shame he felt. This shame birthed a determination within him, a determination to become strong, unimaginably strong, so that no one would dare underestimate him.","He wanted to grow powerful, to the point where everyone would respect him. At this moment, he truly understood the teachings of his ancestors, regretting his lack of insight back then.","“That’s more like it!” Luo Hao chuckled.","“Now, you can leave!” he said.","“Thank you!” Yang Yuan slowly stood up, and with his junior sister, he soared into the sky, soon disappearing from view. This humiliation would change Yang Yuan’s life. When he became strong enough, however, he would never find Luo Hao and God-Emperor MO Long again.","Jian Wushuang breathed a sigh of relief. It was finally over. Now it was his turn to perform.","“Luo Hao, my friend, it’s time for us to leave too!” Jian Wushuang said with a hint of amusement, looking at Luo Hao. The three of them formed a triangle, each maintaining a distance of thousands of miles from the other.","This distance wasn’t much; if they attacked, they could reach each other in an instant.","“Indeed!” Luo Hao smiled slightly, and in an instant, he charged toward Jian","Wushuang.","“Kid, do you really think MO Long and I are fools?”","He had sensed something was amiss the moment Jian Wushuang arrived. A Six Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal suddenly appeared to save him, especially from the hands of God-Emperor MO Long. This move was even more foolish than the actions of the two people from the Great Dream Clan.","However, Jian Wushuang did not seem like an idiot. He knew that there had to be a reason behind his actions. Both he and MO Long were peak-level Grand Yan Immortals. There was no way they would allow a Six Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal to take advantage of the situation.","“Die!” Flying blades instantly struck, and Jian Wushuang swiftly fled in the direction of the valley.."]},{"number":5179,"title":"Chapter 5179: Fated to Be an Emperor","paragraphs":["Chapter 5179: Fated to Be an Emperor","Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Indeed, the peak experts of Grand Yan Immortal were no fools. When the situation was exposed, he had no choice but to flee, relying on his extraordinary speed, a confidence he had maintained, a risk he wouldn’t have taken otherwise.","“God-Emperor MO Long, Luo Hao is clearly stalling for time, Why don’t we join forces and kill him first?” Jian Wushuang said urgently, unwilling to let the opportunity slip away, shouting to God-Emperor MO Long, who was catching up behind them.","“Jian Wushuang, if you were just an ordinary Nine Revolutions, I wouldn’t bother with you. Blame yourself for grasping the Ultimate Dao. Your threat is much stronger than Luo Hao’s.”","God-Emperor MO Longs speed was astonishing. In an instant, he overtook Luo Hao and headed straight for Jian Wushuang.","A Yan Immortal who mastered the Ultimate Dao could, with the backing of a major power, reach the level of a half-step Emperor. With the significant cultivation support from Qishen Temple, as long as Jian Wushuang entered the top 1,000 and received the bestowed treasures, comprehending the Qishen Grand Dao, his strength would ascend rapidly. He would soon become a Perfected Nine Revolutions. Achieving Perfected Nine Revolutions was just an opportunity, not a significant bottleneck.","Such half- step Emperors in the making had to be eliminated early!","One less opponent meant one less threat.","Although his Dao was considered top-notch, the disparity between his path and the Ultimate Dao was still enormous.","He was confident about entering the top 100 on this original planet. But in the entire universe, he was inconsequential, merely possessing more treasures and relatively stronger combat power. His true potential was not exceptionally high.","Being able to effortlessly kill a future half- step Emperor excited God-Emperor MO Long greatly.","In some worlds, there wasn’t even a glimpse of the Ultimate Dao. Across the entire universe, there were only a handful who had reached the Perfected Nine Revolutions stage.","Boom!","Golden fist shadows transformed into a wandering dragon, charging at Jian Wushuang!","“So close!” Jian Wushuang desperately shielded himself toward the gorge. The speed of the chasing dragon behind him was faster than God-Emperor","MO Long himself, catching up to the fleeing Jian Wushuang within a breath.","“Heartsword World!” Jian Wushuang roared, “Hold it for me!”","The world of swords descended in an instant, significantly slowing down the pursuing dragon. Then it began disintegrating the source of the Great l)ao within the dragon.","His Ultimate Sword Dao had already reached the sixth level, capable of suppressing an eighth-level source Great Dao. The dragon, after all, was just a technique executed by God-Emperor MO Long; its power, while formidable, was merely a separated part of the original source.","“What?” God-Emperor MO Longs figure swiftly surpassed the crumbling dragon, astonished by the immense power of the Ultimate Dao. Could it really suppress his source of the Great Dao? Was this the might of the Ultimate Dao?","Fated to be an Emperor!","On this side , Luo Hao’s figure spun around, avoiding the wandering dragon. At this moment, he was considering whether to take the opportunity to escape in the opposite direction.","Among the three, MO Long was the fastest, followed by Jian Wushuang, and he was the slowest.","He had a chance to escape at this moment, as long as Jian Wushuang could hold off the God-Emperor MO Long for just two breaths, he could get away.","Unfortunately, he had chosen the wrong side just now. If he had cooperated with Jian Wushuang, he might have been tricked. However, there would have been a slim chance of survival.","If he cooperated with MO Long, after Jian Wushuang fell, it would be his turn.","Fortunately, Jian Wushuangs combat power was not strong, but his speed was very fast, enough to barely hold his own for a while.","On Jian Wushuangs side, the canyon was getting closer and closer. Although the Heartsword World had blocked the wandering dragon, it couldn’t hinder the God-Emperor MO Long, not even affecting Luo Hao.","“We’re almost there, just 1,000 miles away, we’ll be there in a breath!” Jian Wushuangs eyes lit up.","However, in MO Longs heart, there was some impatience. He felt a looming threat all around him!","“Who could it be?”","The experts of the Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm were not well known to him, only Dao Lord Jiu Yu. His strength was among the top 500 in the entire universe. However, he hadn’t even earned a spot on this primitive planet. The remaining strongest ones were only Peak Grand Yan Immortals, ranking behind him. He wasn’t afraid at all.","As for the Great Si Region, as a Prince, he had extensive experiences accompanying his father. He knew that Emperor Zhen Wuyang had aligned himself with the Eternal Tower.","Meanwhile, Jian Wushuang, a Grand Yan Immortal of the Great Si Region, had appeared among the crowds in the Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm. Clearly, Jian Wushuang had joined the Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm. The biggest challenge would likely be the Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal of the Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm.","“What are his trump cards, exactly?” God-Emperor MO Longs figure drew nearer to Jian Wushuang, the threat intensifying. “Who is this threat?”","“l don’t care. Kill him first!” God-Emperor MO Long, with a sudden motion, summoned a sealing scroll that instantly suppressed the land for millions of miles around.","Buzz!","The sky birthed the Yin-Yang Sealing Diagram, and the earth shifted, revealing an eight- sided prison.","“You can’t escape!” God-Emperor MO Long bellowed angrily, releasing a majestic aura.","A beam of light shot out almost instantaneously, piercing through Jian","Wushuang’s body.","“No!”","“Just one more step, hurry!” Jian Wushuang roared in frustration within his heart.","In the moment before his divine body completely disintegrated, he flickered once again, falling into the Great Canyon Formation.","God-Emperor MO Long revealed a satisfied smile. He could sense Jian Wushuangs aura growing weaker, devoid of any resistance.","“Luo Hao, go into the canyon and bring out Jian Wushuang. Don’t play tricks; you know what I’m capable of,” God-Emperor MO Long threatened.","The sealing scroll was a prehistoric treasure that only Emperor-level beings could fully utilize. MO Longs Perfected Nine Revolutions strength could only cover millions of miles. With Emperor-level power, it could extend to billions of miles, even covering an entire world, suppressing countless powerful beings.","Such a treasure was now in the hands of a Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal. Luo Hao felt both envious and jealous. As one of the ten Princes of the Daluo Domain, he had only acquired an ordinary innate treasure after entering the Qishen Temple. Moreover, it was just a moderately valuable single- target offensive treasure.","Even 1,000 such treasures wouldn’t compare to the innate treasure like the Sealing Scroll.","“Aren’t you afraid I’ll enter the canyon and join forces with Jian Wushuang against you?” Luo Hao, standing side by side with MO Long, asked, his feet on the crescent- shaped flying blade.","“You’re welcome to try!” God-Emperor MO Long replied calmly.","Luo Hao posed minimal threat to him, to the point that he could be considered no threat at all. MO Longs treasure was extremely effective against someone like Luo Hao, who lacked speed and proficiency in close combat as a Grand Yan Immortal.."]},{"number":5180,"title":"Chapter 5180: Bait Succeed","paragraphs":["Chapter 5180: Bait Succeed","Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","In terms of strength, Luo Hao could maintain the peak state of the Grand Yan Immortal by burning his source. Root issues were not a concern.","Inside the canyon.","Jian Wushuang sat cross-legged within a formation. Luckily, he had killed several Grand Yan Immortals and obtained numerous pills from them. At this moment, he swallowed them all in an attempt to accelerate the recovery of his Yan power, which had been depleted in the recent battle.","That last strike had nearly completely shattered his divine body. If it were an ordinary Grand Yan Immortal of the Ultimate Dao, that strike would have been fatal. Fortunately, he mastered the Extreme Dao; his divine body was a hundred times stronger than the Ultimate Dao. His Yan power was more abundant than any other Grand Yan Immortal, but even so, that blow had instantly torn through his body, causing a significant loss of Yan power.","Currently, the only way to repair his body was to use pills to replenish his Yan power. The restorative power of the Extreme Dao’s source was incredibly potent. Although his divine body was injured by that strike, it hadn’t caused any harm to the source’s Great Dao.","As long as the source remained intact, he could rapidly recover his divine body.","This was the advantage of the Extreme Dao over the Ultimate Dao. The source was exceptionally powerful; ordinary attacks could hardly harm it. Possessing the source also allowed for a rapid recovery of the divine body.","This single point made countless people envious. God-Emperor MO Longs divine body was on the brink of collapse and took countless treasures a year to recover. In contrast, injuries in the Ultimate Dao required just a day, while those in the extreme path, especially for Jian Wushuang, only required the time it took to drink a cup of tea.","“l need the time it takes to drink a cup of tea, Hu Qing, can you hold on?” Jian Wushuangs voice was somewhat weak as he looked at the young novice monk, Hu Qing, in front of him.","At some point, Hu Oing had become remarkably upright. He held a brown-red staff in his robe, his thick eyebrows giving his exceptionally determined black eyes an imposing air. His aura was several times stronger than before.","Hu Qing nodded.","“Brother Wushuang, rest assured. 1 will do my best to delay them,” Hu Qing said with a faint smile.","In the art of Zen, one excels in battling within formations; as long as it concerns the ultimate way, there are no weak primal sources.","Even though he had just broken through the Nine Revolutions, his combat power was comparable to that of a peak Perfected Nine Revolutions. Relying on formations, he was no weaker than God-Emperor MO Long.","With a swift movement, Hu Qing entered the center of the formation, his long staff tilted, waiting calmly for the enemy to arrive.","In just a breath’s time, Luo Hao from the outside world descended into the formation. However, he couldn’t sense the presence of the formation at all. All he saw was the young monk Hu Qing standing alone on the slope of the gorge.","“Are you Jian Wushuangs protector?” Luo Hao sneered!","The person before him seemed to be at the Nine Revolutions level. He couldn’t believe he would encounter two beings who controlled the Ultimate Dao in one day.","Without the Ultimate Dao, a Nine Revolutions, no matter how strong, could only match an ordinary Perfected Nine Revolutions at best.","Hu Qing suppressed his sharp aura. He knew there was another person in the outside world; he had to lure that person here as well.","He needed to reveal a flaw first, so that God-Emperor MO Long could see it.","Once both of them entered the formation, he would activate the Wuliang Grand Formation, trapping the opponent and slowly depleting their strength.","“If there’s no one else, then prepare to die!”","Luo Hao sensed no danger whatsoever. He immediately took action, and his flying blade shot towards Hu Qing.","“Moonlight Shadow! ”","He went all out from the start. He wanted to see the true strength of this leader of the monks from the Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm. If, as he suspected, the monk’s strength was mediocre, he would kill him effortlessly and then find his way out.","If you could withstand his attack, he would switch sides and cooperate with the opponent. Jian Wushuang had mastered the Ultimate Dao, recovering rapidly. As long as they could hold God-Emperor MO Long back, waiting for Jian Wushuang to fully regain his strength, the three of them could join forces and have a chance at survival.","While Luo Hao was making plans, he was unaware that the God-Emperor MO Long outside had already seen through everything.","Smack!","Hu Qing stomped the ground fiercely, soaring into the sky, his Moonlight Shadow cleaving a towering mountain into two halves.","This was just one Moonlight Shadow attack; countless more followed, leaving","Hu Qing with no place to hide.","Countless Moonlight Shadows, shattered with a single strike!","A towering reddish-brown staff smashed down, colliding with the Moonlight Shadows.","Countless moon blades clashed against the brown staff, but they couldn’t inflict any damage, falling to the ground like shattered ice.","The staff swept through the entire canyon, dispersing numerous Moonlight","Shadows. Luo Hao leaped out of the valley just in time to evade that terrifying strike.","“Not bad, some real power!” Luo Hao turned around and smiled, the crescent moon blade beneath his feet slashing out.","A buzzing sound tore through the air, assaulting the ears. Hu Qing gritted his teeth, his staff returning to its original size, barely managing to block the crescent moon blade with his impeccable staff techniques.","The transcendent innate treasure, the crescent moon blade, clashed violently with the staff several times.","Luo Hao, manipulating the blade from afar, frowned. He murmured, “Is Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal also equipped with an innate treasure?”","Initially, he had thought that, among the numerous great worlds, being a Prince from a higher world and obtaining a transcendent innate treasure when he entered the Qishen Temple was already a mark of significant attention.","Now, encountering the eccentric God-Emperor MO Long, the amount of treasures he possessed was staggering. He had far more treasures than an average second-tier Emperor, with several top-grade transcendent innate treasures alone.","Common innate treasures were even more abundant!","This monk from the Heaven-Reaching Buddisht Realm before him also possessed innate treasures. The power he displayed was much stronger than his crescent moon blade, just by revealing a fraction of its might.","Without this reddish-brown staff, he wouldn’t have been able to hold him off for so long.","One innate treasure could make a Nine Revolutions comparable to a top-tier Perfected Nine Revolutions. That was the charm of transcendent innate treasures.","Just like Demon Lord Fengyu, who wielded an eternal treasure, she possessed the strength of a peak Emperor, perpetually suppressing all enemies.","Chishui had to lead a large group of strong individuals just to negotiate with","Demon Lord Fengyu. If those forces hadn’t formed a coalition, Demon Lord Fengyu, with the Eternal Tower, could have subdued any top-tier force in any region.","Even within other peak forces, not everyone necessarily had an eternal treasure. After all, the power of eternal treasures could affect the battle prowess of a tier 5 Emperor, making these treasures rare even among tier 5 Emperors. Emperors would only bestow them upon disciples if it didn’t impact their own battle strength.","Just like the Ruler of the Daluo Realm, who possessed an outstanding set of transcendent innate treasures, the remaining innate treasures became insignificant. During the Qishen Temple’s opening, the treasury was unlocked, and half of the treasures were bestowed upon their subordinates.","Of course, most of these were given to the Emperors under his command, as they were the main core of this conflict.","The other Emperors would only be given innate treasures that the ten Princes and some chief disciples didn’t find appealing.","Apart from the ten Princes in the Daluoo Realm, there were also some chief disciples of Emperors who would receive innate treasures.","These ten Princes were only cultivated under the reign of the Daluo Realm’s Ruler. Although they had prestigious status on the surface, in terms of treasures, they were not as well-off as the direct disciples of those Emperors.","Especially figures like God-Emperor MO Long; he simply looked down upon these so-called Princes.."]},{"number":5181,"title":"Chapter 5181: Once and for All","paragraphs":["Chapter 5181: Once and for All","Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","He was the true Prince of an Emperor, the only one at that. The Emperor’s bloodline, after successfully merging with the Dao, was incredibly potent, making it almost impossible for him to have more offspring. This sole heir was doted upon extravagantly. The Emperor even allocated a third of the world’s territories to be managed by MO Long, indulging his imperial desires.","In terms of innate talent, God-Emperor MO Long was rather ordinary. It was only due to his father’s formidable bloodline that he comprehended the immensely powerful Great Dao of the source. Additionally, he possessed numerous mystical treasures, which granted him peak strength.","However, these were all external factors. Every Grand Yan Immortal sought the same ultimate goal: merging with the Dao. Only by successfully merging could one become an Emperor and truly transcend the universe, becoming a supreme being.","This was the Dao pursued by Luo Hao.","At this moment, he couldn’t afford to fail. Even if it meant death, he was determined to perish in the process of merging with the Dao.","“Excuse me, may we talk?” Luo Hao transmitted his voice.","Although Hu Qings power was not as strong as his, he still possessed the strength of an ordinary top-tier Grand Yan Immortal. Along with Jian","Wushuang and the others burning their innate Yan power, there was hope to contend against God-Emperor MO Long. If they persisted for a few more hours, the First Prince of their Daluo Realm would arrive.","At that time, despair would befall God-Emperor MO Long.","Hu Qing hesitated for a moment and then cautiously inquired, “What do you want to discuss?”","“Cooperation.”","On the surface, they clashed fiercely, but in the shadows, they plotted against the external God-Emperor MO Long.","Jian Wushuang sat cross-legged in a mountain cave, oblivious to the conflicts of the outside world.","Channeling his Yan power from the source, he continuously repaired his damaged divine body. From an external perspective, the speed of his bodys restoration was visible to the naked eye, a pace unheard of in the entire universe.","“Just a bit more. I wonder if Hu Qing can hold on!” Jian Wushuang felt a sense of urgency.","His gaze flickered over the floating identity token.","Trial Participant: Jian Wushuang","Achievements: 400,000 Ranking: 4,768","Trial Time: 3 years","Trial Duration: 30 years","There were still over 20 years left. Although he wasn’t in a hurry, opportunities like today were rare. If he could defeat the top 100 participants, both he and Hu Qing could enter the top 1,000 rankings, a position they could maintain until the end of the trial.","This was a once-in-a-lifetime opportunity, one he couldn’t afford to let slip away.","He glanced at the rankings of God-Emperor MO Long and Luo Hao—one in the five-hundreds, the other in the nine-hundreds.","According to Luo Hao, these powerful beings were mostly not near the mountain ranges; they mostly fought on the main continents. Even though 30 percent of the original planet’s Grand Yan Immortals had fallen, leaving roughly a million, realistically speaking, only tens of thousands dared to battle.","The rest of the Grand Yan Immortals who knew they had no chance mostly hid within various mountain ranges.","70 percent of the original planet’s territory consisted of mountains, 20 percent were deep pits left by lakes, and the remaining 10 percent constituted the continents.","In this realm, which was exceedingly small for Grand Yan Immortal, one could easily encounter numerous Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortals with just a casual stroll.","Various factions banded together, sweeping the four corners and hunting down solitary wanderers.","In such a perilous environment, breaking into the top thousand required numerous battles. His strength could at most match that of top-grade Grand Yan Immortals, with perhaps a slight advantage in speed.","On this continent, his speed would no longer be an advantage because there were far too many formidable individuals. Surrounded and pursued, he couldn’t effectively utilize his speed advantage.","Now, the only opportunity lay right before his eyes, and he had to seize it firmly.","“Whew!” Exhaling sharply, Jian Wushuang slowly got up.","“Faster recovery than the last time!” His narrow escape this time had further strengthened his source and his Thought power had grown significantly stronger than before.","A deep hum echoed through the air as a pitch-black, elongated spear burst out from the cave. With an unstoppable momentum, it pierced through the entire mountain peak and headed straight for the God-Emperor MO Long, who stood proudly in the sky.","Nio Long turned slightly, catching the spear that streaked past him in front of his eyes.","“He isn’t injured at all. Could that aura have been a disguise?” God-Emperor MO Long was somewhat surprised.","He knew that Hu Qing had intercepted Luo Hao below. Ever since Luo Hao had gone down, he hadn’t felt that sense of impending danger. This had puzzled him. Now, Jian Wushuang had suddenly emerged again, and it seemed like he hadn’t been harmed at all.","“Perhaps I’ve been too cautious,” murmured God-Emperor MO Long to himself, his figure suddenly descending deep into the ravine.","On the other side, Jian Wushuang emerged from the cave.","“MO Long, your fate is sealed today!” Jian Wushuangs eyes glinted with cold determination.","After much planning, the two of them had finally walked into their trap.","“Hu Qing, activate the grand formation!”","Hu Qing, who had been fighting with Luo Hao, revealed a slight smile. He directly addressed Luo Hao, “I take my leave for now.”","“What?” Luo Hao was stunned. What did this mean? Weren’t they just having a peaceful conversation moments ago?","How could this seemingly honest monk just flee like this?","Before he could react, the entire canyon was filled with flying sand and rolling stones, the world spinning around him.","The grand formation shifted, relocating Luo Hao from an open space to a hillside. The sky that was once above his head now appeared beneath his feet, and the mighty divine mountain stood above him. A tremendous pressure engulfed him instantly.","“Huh?” God-Emperor MO Longs face also paled. “How can there be such a grand formation here?”","He had been keeping an eye on Luo Hao and the monk. They couldn’t possibly have set up the formation in such a short time, could they?","Whoosh!","In an instant, MO Long was also transported to another location.","“Luo Hao!” MO Longs face darkened.","“MO Long!” Luo Hao’s expression was equally grim.","They exchanged a glance and instantly understood – they had been tricked by Jian Wushuang!","The threat they felt was escalating, sinking MO Longs heart.","Whoosh! Whoosh!","Jian Wushuang wielded an ordinary long sword that appeared before them instantly, accompanied by Huiqing.","“Brother Luo Hao, we’ve come to assist you!” Jian Wushuang said with a faint smile.","Hu Qing nodded in agreement.","Upon hearing this, God-Emperor MO Long hurriedly retreated, putting some distance between himself and Luo Hao.","The grand formation had weakened his power by 30 percent. At this moment, he was just an ordinary peak Grand Yan Immortal. Once Luo Hao activated his source, he would be on par with MO Long. Although he had some treasures and tricks up his sleeve, facing a one-on-three situation, he dared not be careless.","“God-Emperor MO Long!” Luo Hao opened his mouth, glancing at Jian Wushuang and Hu Qing. Eventually, he took a deep breath and shouted, “Your time has come!”","Although it was just a breath, he had already calculated countless times in his mind. Instead of being a dog to MO Long and risking being killed in the end, he decided it was better to cooperate with Jian Wushuang. Together, they could confront MO Long.","In his view, Jian Wushuang and the others were relatively strong. Even with the grand formation, the three of them could at most contend with MO Long.","It they could delay a little longer, the First Prince of the Daluo Realm would arrive. By then, the initiative would be in his hands.","Moreover, this was also an opportunity to weaken MO Longs strength. When the other Princes from his clan arrived, he could reap the benefits without doing much, making it the best course of action.."]},{"number":5182,"title":"Chapter 5182 Luo Hao’s End","paragraphs":["5182 Luo Hao's End","\"Brother Wushuang, today we join forces to slay God-Emperor Mo Long and share his achievements!\" Luo Hao said earnestly.","Mo Long, standing at a distance, was furious. He had been careless this time, falling into the hands of Jian Wushuang.","\"Jian Wushuang, don't blame me for not warning you. Several Princes from the Daluo Realm are rushing this way. If you cooperate with Luo Hao to deal with me, you'll only be playing into their hands,\" Mo Long said, though he was confident he could avoid this battle.","If this formation could truly harm him, dealing with the other princes from the Daluo Realm afterwards would be troublesome.","Jian Wushuang shook his head, displaying a disbelieving expression. Coldly, he said, \"Stop the nonsense, let's fight!\"","\"Hu Qing, activate the formation. Release the constraints on Luo Hao. He's valuable,\" Jian Wushuang transmitted his message to Hu Qing.","\"Attack!\"","Luo Hao felt his body lighten as the constraints lifted. He was overjoyed. Without hesitation, he charged at God-Emperor Mo Long. Jian Wushuang and Hu Qing followed suit.","The three of them besieged Mo Long!","In this formation, Luo Hao's strength not only didn't diminish, but it even increased due to the formation's power. Gradually, his power became comparable to that of a peak Grand Yan Immortal. He alone could keep God-Emperor Mo Long occupied.","The crescent moon-shaped blades sliced across God-Emperor Mo Long's chest once more. Before he could react, Hu Qing struck from behind, sending Mo Long crashing into the mountainside.","Jian Wushuang comprehended the Ultimate Sword Dao. His essence was always about killing. His figure flickered, his eyes glinting with bloodlust. He consecutively struck out several times. Although this long sword was just an ordinary treasure, with the blessing of the Ultimate Dao, its power still posed a threat to God- Emperor Mo Long.","Puff!","Under the onslaught of the three, God-Emperor Mo Long found himself faltering. He hadn't anticipated that this grand formation not only suppressed his powers but also allowed the controller to enhance the abilities of Jian Wushuang and the others.","This intricate grand formation couldn't be set up in just a few years; moreover, it was beyond the grasp of ordinary people. In his divine realm, there was a formation that his father had paid a hefty sum for, one set up by a Formation Emperor. He had investigated it back then. Emperor-grade formations were generally not passed down, only available for purchase.","If an Emperor crafted a formation, unless it reached a world-grade, it could be easily retracted. Such formations were immensely valuable and served great purposes for Emperors. Consequently, they came at exorbitant prices.","Emperors with weaker power, unable to recruit a Formation Grandmaster, would buy a mobile formation, placing it in their own Dao Arena to suppress Yan power.","If the formation in the canyon was mobile, its setup would have been much simpler.","Mo Long's body twitched, his brows furrowing. He turned his gaze to Hu Qing, secretly thinking, 'It must be the monk who set up this formation!'","As long as they killed the controller of the formation, it would naturally collapse.","A flash of killing intent flickered in his eyes as he immediately launched a counterattack.","Sensing Mo Long's intentions, Jian Wushuang hurriedly transmitted, \"Hu Qing, retreat quickly!\"","A massive octagonal diagram appeared. Mo Long, previously suppressed, caught his breath. His strength instantly surged as he attacked Hu Qing.","Seeing this, Luo Hao naturally understood the situation. The formation had been set up by Hu Qing. If Mo Long succeeded now, all their previous efforts would be in vain.","\"Let's go all out!\"","'Once we kill him, and all the treasures will be mine!' He thought. With determination, he once again ignited the power of his source. His blade swiftly spun, and despite not being adept at close combat, Luo Hao directly stood in front of Hu Qing, engaging in hand-to- hand combat with Mo Long.","Boom!","\"Looking for death!\" God-Emperor Mo Long could no longer feign arrogance; his heart brimmed with intense killing intent.","He had initially thought of keeping Luo Hao as bait, but now it seemed unnecessary.","Ding!","The treasure on his forehead shimmered. Mo Long's entire divine body expanded explosively; at that moment, his aura soared, causing the boundless grand array to tremble.","The seal was broken!","An ancient aura erupted from within God-Emperor Mo Long. The power surged, surpassing the peak of Grand Yan Immortal, heading straight for top-tier.","Luo Hao, who had been confident, felt a bit dazed. It was too late to retreat; all he could do was shout, \"Brother Wushuang, come quickly to my aid!\"","Jian Wushuang stood at a distance, silently observing everything.","\"God-Emperor Mo Long has unleashed his trump card; there's no need to spare Luo Hao anymore.\"","Hu Qing's clear and wise eyes showed no mercy, just a slight nod.","One might have thought Hu Qing would feel uneasy, but now he was resolute, decisively abandoning the situation.","It was different from when they first met. Jian Wushuang secretly decided that after this incident, he would separate from Hu Qing. The secrets this person carried were undoubtedly significant, and both were walking the path of the strong. Sooner or later, they would end up on opposite sides. It was better to part ways sooner rather than later.","Qishen Temple, the highest trial, original planet!","Jian Wushuang had a feeling that the appearance of Qishen Temple was not merely a coincidence in the Original Universe's manipulation.bender","The original planet was just the first step; there would be more trials to come. He wondered when he could leave Qishen Temple.","There had to be some connection behind all this, perhaps known to those Emperors.","Maybe even the Emperors didn't know!","The connection with the Qishen Temple was too significant. Hu Qing had also stepped into the Daoo after the emergence of the Qishen Temple, displaying overwhelming power.","Jian Wushuang couldn't help but suspect that this person might be a reincarnation of some mighty being.","Sighing, Jian Wushuang considered. Ever since leaving the Great Si Region, the entire original universe had become chaotic, from the road of Immortal bones to the army of corpses, and then suddenly grasping Heart power and comprehending the Extreme Dao, his consciousness entering the starry sky, and finally, the opening of Qishen Temple.","Could these events be related?","\"If only that old guy Xuan Yi were here!\" This cosmic secret script, that old guy understood it best.","Unfortunately, it had been years since Jian Wushuang had seen Xuan Yi since their last parting.","From his current perspective, Xuan Yi's strength remained a mystery. He could traverse the universe, roam freely, and was unafraid of the existence of Zhen Wuyang. At the very least, Xuan Yi must be a fifth-tier Emperor, right?","Such a powerful old guy wouldn't be thinking about him, a little guy, all the time. Jian Wushuang wondered if Xuan Yi would show up this time when Qishen Temple made its move.","But these thoughts quickly vanished from his mind.","What mattered now was figuring out how to take down these two individuals. Pondering these things was not the priority at the moment.","God-Emperor Mo Long's sudden eruption caught Luo Hao off guard. In just a few moves, Luo Hao's divine body began to crack.","Jian Wushuang and Hu Qing showed no intention of stepping in to help, leaving Luo Hao in despair!","Weren't these two afraid that he would die? Would Mo Long go after them next?","\"God-Emperor Mo Long, I'll cooperate with you, spare my life!\" Luo Hao couldn't bear it anymore. He could feel the killing intent emanating from God-Emperor Mo Long; fear gripped him.","The journey of cultivation had not been easy; he didn't want to fall like this."]},{"number":5183,"title":"Chapter 5183: Fall In Madness","paragraphs":["Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","The God-Emperor MO Long, who had already opened all the ancient and mysterious treasures, was resolute in his murderous intent. He knew that the only way to ease the hatred in his heart was to see blood spilled.","“Haha, stop struggling, just perish already!” MO Long, with a mighty hand, shattered Luo Hao’s skull, nearly tearing apart his divine body.","Luo Hao’s origin source within him began to dissipate. Unwillingly, he roared, “MO Long, spare my life, and I will give you my identity token, all my achievements, everything, they’re all yours.”","Boom!","All Luo Hao received in response was a relentless barrage of heavy punches, showing no intention of stopping.","<font < div>","“I...” Puff!","Blood spurted out of his mouth. Yet, Luo Hao persisted, pleading,","“God-Emperor MO Long, spare me, and 1 will join forces with you to kill the Crown Princes of my clan. They have millions of achievements, and I know their weaknesses.’","MO Long, his eyes devoid of mercy, continued to rain blows upon Luo Hao’s head.","“Let me tell you the truth. The reason I kept you alive this long was to lure those Princes from your Daluo Realm.” MO Long grabbed Luo Hao by the neck, his other hand clenched into a fist and slammed ruthlessly into Luo Hao’s face.","“You were just bait, nothing more, you fool!”","Luo Hao was utterly desperate. He knew he was going to die today.","He began to curse Jian Wushuang and Hu Qing, his entire being consumed by madness.","The second- grade origin source was vast, an immensely broad Great Dao. Now on the verge of collapse, Luo Hao directly burned the last remnants of his origin source, pushing his strength to its peak. In that moment, he managed to escape the clutches of the God-Emperor MO Long.","“Haha, I never expected that l, Luo Hao, would meet my end here today!”","He was a top-tier Grand Yan Immortal, with numerous allies on this primitive planet. Despite the opportunity to fight on the main continent, he chose to hide in these mountains, specifically hunting down weaker Grand Yan Immortals. Clearly, he valued his life greatly.","In complete despair now, one could only imagine how desperate he had become.","“Haha, so be it! Let’s all die together!”","The mad Luo Hao, after shaking off God-Emperor MO Long, raised his transcendent innate treasure high and charged at Jian Wushuang and Hu Qing.","“Is he planning to self-destruct his source?” God-Emperor MO Long grinned wickedly.","His golden gauntlets still bore traces of Luo Hao’s blood, dripping off slowly, as if symbolizing Luo Hao’s life gradually fading away.","Swish!","Jian Wushuang, who also held control over the grand formation, instantly shifted his position, vanishing on the spot.","To think they could drag him down with them within this formation was utterly laughable!","“Huh?” Jian Wushuang was taken aback, thinking, “What about Hu Qing?”","Considering the distance just now, there was enough time for Hu Qing, who was not weak in strength, to teleport away with him!","Although Hu Qing seemed significantly different now, there was still their deep bond. Jian Wushuangs figure flickered, and he returned to his original spot once more.","Luo Hao had already fallen.","There was not a trace of Luo Hao left in this world, he had vanished completely.","Hu Qing still stood in the same spot, his hands extending a reddish-brown staff, with Luo Hao’s innate treasure suspended above it.","“Huh?” Jian Wushuang was taken aback.","He had only left for a moment, and Luo Hao had fallen without a sound? In the distance, God-Emperor MO Long had unsealed all the ancient seals. His divine body instantly strengthened tenfold, and his power naturally increased tenfold. However, despite the suppression of the Wuliang Grand Formation, he resisted for only a moment; the pressure still weighed heavily upon him.","Although his strength was suppressed by nearly 30 percent, it increased tenfold afterward. Now he had the strength of a peak Grand Yan Immortal, just shy of the threshold for Perfected Nine Revolutions in the outside world. Unfortunately, this array weakened his power by 30 percent.","MO Long glanced at Jian Wushuang first, then fixed his gaze on Hu Qing, clearly wary.","Jian Wushuang now understood – Luo Hao had fallen at the hands of Hu Qing!","Regrettably, he hadn’t witnessed any of this. Instead, God-Emperor MO Long had observed it all – Hu Qing, who could instantly kill a peak Grand Yan Immortal, and not just any peak Grand Yan Immortal but one who didn’t care for his life. How strong must Hu Qing be?","Jian Wushuang found it incredibly hard to accept!","He had cultivated diligently for so long, step by step, only to barely match the top Grand Yan Immortals at the peak of Perfected Nine Revolutions. Hu Qing, on the other hand, had entered the Dao and immediately displayed the strength of a Perfected Nine Revolutions expert. After entering the original planet, Hu Qings power had increased significantly, comparable to his own, both possessing the strength of a top-tier Nine Revolutions expert.","But now!","Just after he had been gone for a day, Hu Qing had broken through again. It seemed his strength was no weaker than God-Emperor MO Long, who could wield the innate treasure. Otherwise, MO Long wouldn’t be so wary.","Jian Wushuang took a deep breath to calm himself. Hu Qing had his secrets; he shouldn’t pry too much. He didn’t know how to broach the subject.","“Brother Wushuang, I’ve made some recent breakthroughs and forgot to inform you!” Hu Qing seemed to sense Jian Wushuangs thoughts and broke the silence.","Jian Wushuang smiled and shook his head. “No need to be formal!”","Specific details about everyone’s strength were vague; no one would willingly reveal their true power. It was normal for Hu Qing not to inform him after their breakthrough.","God-Emperor MO Long, however, stared at the two of them as if he were observing monsters.","“Jian Wushuang, is this friend of yours from the Buddhist Realm of Tongtian Buddha?” MO Long God-Emperor probed.","Because of Tongtian Buddha’s influence, he had paid attention to the strong figures in the Heaven-Reaching Buddhist Realm. Apart from Dao Lord Jiu Yu, there were only a few worth noticing. The strongest among them was just a top-tier Grand Yan Immortal. How could there suddenly appear a limit-defying Grand Yan Immortal from the Tongtian Buddha RealmO on this original planet?","Jian Wushuang didn’t reply. He glanced at Hu Qing and merely nodded faintly.","God-Emperor MO Long carefully recalled. He had clear memories of those on the Universe Deity-Demon List who were stronger than him. Yet, he had no information about the person before him.","Within the canyon, the atmosphere gradually solidified, thick with killing intent!","Outside the mountains, the three Princes of the Daluo Realm gathered together, swiftly flying toward the direction of the canyon.","“Luo Hao has fallen!” said a burly man, his eyes radiating a golden glow. His entire body was tightly wrapped, revealing only a pair of faint golden eyes. His voice sounded exceptionally deep and gloomy.","Boom!","The three accelerated once more, heading straight for the canyon.","The burly man was none other than the chief imperial son of the Daluo Realm, with strength comparable to a limit-defying Grand Yan Immortal. The other two with him possessed the power of peak Grand Yan Immortals. When these three gathered, they feared no one except for a few Dao Lords ranked at the top of this original planet.","God-Emperor MO Long was merely a peak Grand Yan Immortal, and according to the late Luo Hao, God-Emperor MO Long hadn’t fully recovered, and his divine body was damaged.","In his madness, Luo Hao hadn’t told them that there was another peak expert as formidable as God-Emperor MO Long.","Back in the Daluo Realm, the ten Princes fiercely competed against each other. However, it was only upon entering the orignal planet that they started forming alliances.","Even if they were forming alliances, without certainty, it wasn’t wise to rashly venture so far to rescue Luo Hao."]},{"number":5184,"title":"Chapter 5184: Chapter ﻿5184 - 5184 What Else Would We Do","paragraphs":["5184 What Else Would We Do","In the pursuit of advantage, there had to be a significant gain. For instance, God-Emperor Mo Long bore wounds, a peak Grand Yan Immortal injured and yet still ranked over 500. His achievements were plentiful. It was the prospect of this ripe opportunity that had driven them to traverse such distances to rescue Luo Hao.","Now, with Luo Hao fallen, they were left only with the echoes of their previous connection, searching for the whereabouts of God- Emperor Mo Long.","If they couldn't find him, so be it. If they did, they planned to exact revenge under the pretext of justice, severing God-Emperor Mo Long and dividing his spoils of war.","Among the three top-tier Grand Yan Immortals, the strongest accelerated their pace once more.","Within the canyon, the grand formation teetered on the brink of collapse amidst the chaotic battle, ready to crumble at any moment.","The power of God-Emperor Mo Long surpassed the imaginations of the two. Within the grand formation, his strength approached the limits of a Grand Yan Immortal. Outside this mystical space, even their combined efforts would be futile against Mo Long. Fortunately, the Wuliang Grand Formation continuously weakened God-Emperor Mo Long, greatly enhancing the duo's strength, and enabling them to hold their own against him.","Perfected Nine Revolutions of the extreme rank were exceedingly rare on this primitive planet. Each one of them ranked among the top 100, except for a few Dao Lords, making them the strongest entities.","After years of tumultuous warfare, they had not heard of any extreme Grand Yan Immortal meeting their end.","Each of them could hunt freely on the main continent, showing no fear towards those united Perfected Grand Yan Immortals.bender","It was no wonder that Mo Long had never been in a rush while dealing with Luo Hao; this was his trump card.","\"Jian Wushuang, my list of achievements isn't extensive. Are you really going to force my hand?\" Mo Long discerned their intention; the two of them meant to detain him this time.","\"What else would we do?\" Jian Wushuang's voice was icy. \"To lure you out, I nearly perished. How could I let you go now?\"","\"Haha, good!\" Mo Long laughed triumphantly. Even if he managed to kill Jian Wushuang and Hu Qing at the cost of his life, he wouldn't gain much merit. He might even end up severely injured again.","Jian Wushuang's strength was decent, not overly formidable even within the grand formation. However, Hu Qing was different. Empowered by the formation and possessing the peak strength of a Grand Yan Immortal, he could match Mo Long even within the formation.","Now lacking the advantage in strength, Mo Long could only rely on his treasures to turn the tide.","Hu Qing stood tall in the canyon, wielding a long staff with infinite power. His aura was overwhelming, impossible to ignore.","After a brief pause, the three of them clashed once again.","Boom!","Hu Qing's figure instantly moved, causing countless mountains and rocks around him to tremble and shatter. In an instant, he appeared next to Mo Long.","Bang!","His staff technique was mysterious and unpredictable, colliding with Mo Long's fist technique. Both sides suffered losses, but before they could fully recover, they were locked in combat once more.","Jian Wushuang, relying on his speed, targeted Mo Long's weak points with various sneak attacks.","\"Kill!\" Jian Wushuang suddenly appeared behind God-Emperor Mo Long and swung his long sword directly at his waist.","The profound and sharp intent of the Starlake Sword Intent was displayed to its fullest extent, showcasing its terrifying power.","Swish!","While Mo Long's upper body continued to battle Hu Qing in mid- air, his lower body had already been severed.","Due to the eruption of the secret treasure, his divine body's power had increased tenfold. His physical body damage was","inconsequential, instantly healing in the blink of an eye.","Jian Wushuang also realized that Mo Long, at such a mastery of his cultivation, was impervious to simple techniques. Although his attacks could break through the physical body, they couldn't harm the overall divine body. иσν??нυ?к.¢σм","And Mo Long possessed a divine body protected by a supreme treasure, his physical form eternal.","Fortunately, Hu Qing's staff techniques were powerful; every move and strike carried immense power, enough to deplete a fraction of Mo Long's divine body.","However, the amount he depleted was negligible to the mighty Mo Long.","\"No, it's impossible to wear him down!\" Jian Wushuang furrowed his brows.","A grand spectacle descended, \"The fifth level of the Ultimate Dao: Heartsword World!\"","The surge of Heart power and Sword Intent propelled Jian Wushuang's momentum to the heavens.","\"Heart Sword Trial!\" This was the strongest sword technique he comprehended during the sixth level of the Ultimate Dao.","Even though he hadn't had the chance to create more sword techniques after breaking through the mirror of the Ultimate Dao, his current strongest sword strike, enhanced by both his Heart power and the power of the great array, had reached its peak.","With the augmentation of Heart power, this strike caused the heavens and earth to change colors.","The God-Emperor Mo Long, who was battling Hu Qing, felt a jolt in his eye sockets and a tremor in his heart, thinking, \"This is bad!\"","The power of this strike might not have been overwhelmingly strong, but the underlying principles contained within it made it hard for him to catch his breath.","Boom! Boom! Boom! Boom!","Hu Qing's staff techniques were perfect, leaving Mo Long with no opportunity to break free. Taking advantage of his distraction, Hu Qing instantly unleashed tens of thousands of strikes, firmly suppressing the God-Emperor Mo Long.","The long staff smashed into his flesh every time, causing damage to his divine body. Thousands of strikes in succession, he couldn't defend against most of them due to his distracted state. They all landed solidly on his flesh, carrying the potent power of the source, instantly eroding his divine form.","\"Damn it!\" God-Emperor Mo Long's mouth was now stained with golden blood.","These were minor wounds, just scratches. The real blow came from the sword strike behind him!","That sword strike shattered his state of mind, and at that moment, even the source began to tremble, making him incredibly anxious, frustrated, and restless.","\"Haha, God-Emperor Mo Long, how does it feel?\" Jian Wushuang distanced himself, looking at Mo Long from afar.","His strongest sword strike, enhanced by the grand array, barely managed to injure the God-Emperor Mo Long. However, Jian Wushuang was just a Six Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal!","As long as he advanced one step further, reaching the Nine Revolutions, mastering the Nine Revolutions Yan Power, his strength would undergo a qualitative change. At that time, even without the grand array, he wouldn't fear any peak Grand Yan Immortal.","\"Jian Wushuang, you have angered me!\" God-Emperor Mo Long roared. At this moment, he completely ignored Hu Qing's long staff. Buzz!","A dazzling light instantly illuminated the entire canyon.","\"The Eye of the Beast God!\" It was the golden eye in the center of God-Emperor Mo Long's forehead.","At this moment, the Eye of the Beast God completely opened.","Its function was not just to allow the divine body to burst with ten times its power. It had a terrifying domain of its own.","\"Beast God Shadow!\"","A howl!","A call from ancient times echoed out, and behind God-Emperor Mo Long, the shadow of an ancient beast god appeared.","It had a row of sharp, white fangs, a towering and majestic body, and a perfect flesh that matched every inch of its bones.","Every part of its structure was exceptionally compatible. Despite its huge body, its head was surprisingly small, perhaps because it lacked ears, making its skull look very round.","However, its blood-stained large mouth was extraordinarily fierce, especially when its pale eyes stared at Jian Wushuang and others. It could affect a cultivator's state of mind, instilling fear in their hearts.","If used against other powerful beings, the fear from the beast god's domain alone could terrify weaker Grand Yan Immortals to death.","But Jian Wushuang was a practitioner who mastered Heart power, an extremely rare ability in the entire universe. He had encountered very few Heart power practitioners, perhaps only Wuliang Buddha. Controlling Heart power, the slight fear within the beast dod's domain couldn't affect him at all."]},{"number":5185,"title":"Chapter 5185: Do You Think You Can Do Whatever You Want Just Because You Have Many Treasures?","paragraphs":["Translator: Endless?antasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Regarding Hu Qing, he had comprehended the ‘Zen Dao’ in the Ultimate Dao, making him impervious to such domains that influence mental states.","The Zen Dao allowed Hu Qing to perceive his true nature clearly. It was the most suitable path among all Ultimate Dao. Anyone who mastered the Zen Technique faced almost no bottlenecks before reaching the Perfected Nine Revolutions. Understanding that everything in his mind was illusory, he became invulnerable.","Only Dao merging could obstruct those who had mastered the Zen Technique. If the Dao merging succeeded, it was unimaginable how powerful an ultimate Emperor like him, well-versed in the Zen Technique, could be.","God-Emperor MO Long also sensed that something was amiss. Astonishingly, he couldn’t discern any change in Jian Wushuang and Hu Qings expressions.","“This is impossible!” MO Long was growing frantic. This was his strongest reliance, possessing the realm of Beast Gods. He feared not even the extreme Grand Yan Immortal and could even contend with them. But now, he couldn’t affect Jian Wushuang and Hu Qing in the slightest.","<font < div>","Jian Wushuang, mastering the Ultimate Dao, infused his Sword Intent with Heart power. Being able to resist was one thing, but how could that monk resist as well?","“Could he also be a practitioner of Heart power?” MO Long, with his extensive knowledge, was aware of the few powerful Heart power practitioners in the universe. However, he hadn’t heard of anyone in the Grand Yan Immortal stage cultivating Heart power!","If he wasn’t a practitioner of Heart power, then he must have comprehended the Ultimate Dao!","Encountering two Ultimate Dao practitioners all at once, he didn’t know whether he was incredibly lucky or terribly unlucky!","Unlucky because he encountered two freaks; lucky because these two hadn’t fully matured yet. If both of them attained Perfected Nine Revolutions with the Ultimate Dao, they would have been equivalent to two half-step Emperor-level figures.","Jian Wushuangs eyes glinted with hostility. It seemed that MO Long had exhausted his trump cards. Now, it was his turn.","“Do you think you can do whatever you want just because you have many treasures?” Jian Wushuang sneered, sheathing the long sword and gesturing","with one hand.","“Today, I’ll show you what a true domain is!”","Buzz!","Hu Qing subtly adjusted his footing, his gaze fixed on Jian Wushuang, secretly astonished. “Could it be?”","“One Thought Universe!” Jian Wushuang clenched his right hand.","The Yan power within millions of miles around the gorge instantly surged, and a grand illusion of the origin source Great Dao emerged, suppressing everything.","The countless Great Dao contained within the grand formation began to tremble!","The beast god’s domain, displayed by God-Emperor MO Long, started collapsing directly. When the beast god’s phantom saw the starry sky of the One Thought Universe, a longing expression appeared in its pale eyes for a moment. However, it instantly crumbled, unable to cast its gaze one last time.","Outside.","The three Daluo Realm Princes, who were very close to the valley, trembled as they stared at the circular barrier in the distance.","“Somethings wrong; there’s another powerful being!” The First Prince’s eyes flickered with surprise.","They were worried about not being able to find God-Emperor MO Long.","Unexpectedly, a battle had broken out nearby, showing the might of a peak Grand Yan Immortal. It must be that MO Long hadn’t gone far.","Peak Grand Yan Immortals were rare in the mountains. Now that Luo Hao had just fallen, MO Long, with his cunning mind, would definitely quickly leave and conceal his aura. They came here with the hope of catching him; perhaps they had found something after all.","Now, in hindsight, the situation unfolded even more perfectly than they had imagined.","MO Long and the other formidable beings confronted each other, and they could now reap the benefits of others’ efforts.","“Quick!” urged Daluo Realm’s First Prince, barely containing her excitement.","Although they were not far from their destination, they still feared unexpected surprises. After all, they were facing a Grand Yan Immortal, albeit one who was already injured — a ripe piece of meat waiting to be devoured.","If they could kill MO Long, the three of them could retire comfortably for the rest of their lives in the mountains.","Meanwhile, Jian Wushuang and his companions were unaware that several","Princes of the Daluo Realm had already noticed them and were swiftly closing in.","“This is a domain!” God-Emperor Mo Long said, his eyes scanning the illusory universe spanning millions of miles around him, a look of disbelief on his face.","No! The universe wasn’t illusory; it was a real, existing miniature world devoid of life but containing a vast and magnificent Great Dao.","In this place, Jian Wushuang was in his element. The first time he unleashed his One Thought Universe, it spanned only a million miles. At that time, with the power of a Three Revolution cultivator, he could contend with a Perfected Nine Revolutions expert like Xiang Binyun.","Although Xiang Binyun had just recovered and wasn’t exceptionally strong among Perfected Nine Revolutions experts, the One Thought Universe was merely a million miles in size back then!","Now, its range had expanded tenfold. However, his combat power didn’t merely increase tenfold but surpassed it by a hundredfold.","This was Jian Wushuangs trump card, the One Thought Universe, a universe created with a single thought.","Within millions of miles, he reigned supreme!","This was his Dao Arena, his domain, a mobile one at that.","The amplification of the Wuliang Grand Formation endowed him with the strength of a top-tier Grand Yan Immortal. The Heartsword World enhanced his Sword Intent to its peak level.","And the One Thought Universe allowed him to increase his combat power tenfold. This was not like MO Longs Eye of the Beast God, which was only unsealed, eliminating potential future troubles, and thus, strengthening him tenfold. Jian Wushuang had genuinely transformed this increase into actual combat strength, effectively tripling it.","One Thought Universe amplified Jian Wushuangs power tenfold, propelling him to the pinnacle of Grand Yan Immortals.","Within the Heartsword World, his Sword Intent equaled the combat prowess of the extreme-level Grand Yan Immortal.","Jian Wushuang hovered in the air, an ordinary treasured longsword materializing in his hand, Sword Intent emanating.","“Heartsword World! ”","Empowered by Yan power spanning millions of miles, within the Heartsword World, myriad sword energies condensed, eventually forming an immensely colossal sword shadow.","Swish!","The sword shadow shot straight toward God-Emperor MO Long, who frantically resisted using his complete set of golden dragon armor.","Yet, the sword tip still pierced his flesh, an unprecedented murderous intent beginning to devour his divine body, impervious treasures unable to staunch the assault.","Bang!","“Ahhhhhh! ! ” MO Long endured immense pain, breaking free from the illusory longsword only after a fierce struggle.","Just one strike shattered his perfected physical body, depleting a thousandth of his divine essence. And this was just a fleeting moment!","Hum! Hum! Hum!","The illusory longsword split into nine swords, encircling God-Emperor MO Long!","Although the illusory longsword had divided, the contained power showed no decrease.","Based on the illusory longsword deduced from the Heartsword World, it differed from the Heart Sword Trial. The former was aligned with the One Thought Universe; only within this universe could he condense the illusory longsword. In a universe spanning millions of miles, he could manipulate at most nine illusory longswords.","“Let’s call it the Illusion Sword Trial!” Jian Wushuang said lightly.","Given his mastery of the Sword Dao, the move he had just spontaneously created still required refinement, such as the nine illusory longswords forming a sword array to enhance its killing potential.","However, he didn’t have time to ponder these matters now; nine illusory longswords were more than enough to deal with MO Long.","“Hu Qing, go intercept him!” Jian Wushuangs eyes narrowed; he noticed a crimson crystal pillar suddenly appearing in MO Longs hand.","Having seen Luo Hao’s black crystal pillar, he knew how terrifying these items could be.."]},{"number":5186,"title":"Chapter 5186: Blood Jade Palace","paragraphs":["Chapter 5186: Blood Jade Palace","Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","MO Long possessed the Seal of Suppression, along with the transcendent innate high-grade treasure, the Zheng Jade Tower. Both treasures had the power to suppress; the Seal of Suppression was akin to a mobile miniature formation.","In times of danger, he could take refuge within it. Jian Wushuang, however, had no such treasures now. He only had an ordinary long sword, not a single one of the Grand Yan Immortals he killed possessed any exceptional abilities or treasures.","Ever since witnessing the treasures of God-Emperor MO Long, Jian Wushuangs horizons had broadened. What he had once coveted as supreme treasures seemed trivial now. Aside from peak treasures, all other treasures appeared as worthless as scrap metal.","That crimson crystal pillar sent shivers down Jian Wushuangs spine. That thing was definitely not something benign.","Hu Qing, upon hearing Jian Wushuangs words, rushed forward attempting to stop God-Emperor MO Long. However, he was too late. God-Emperor MO","Long placed the crimson crystal pillar into the groove on top of the Zheng Jade Tower.","A surge of blood-red light began to rise. The crimson crystal pillar was not the destructive god crystal Jian Wushuang had imagined. It didn’t explode.","Instead, it transformed into a stream of blood, pouring onto the top of the Zheng Jade Tower.","This stream of blood flowed down the top of the tower, irrigating the entire structure before dripping onto the Seal of Suppression.","The blood merged into the eight array eyes, and a scarlet mist started to rise. God-Emperor MO Longs eyes turned bloodshot.","Under the irrigation of the blood, the Seal of Suppression unexpectedly fused with the Zheng Jade Tower!","“This is my father’s transcendent innate treasure that ruled the world. You have the privilege of witnessing the might of the Blood Jade Palace. Consider yourselves fortunate!” Even God-Emperor MO Long hadn’t anticipated that this was only the first step of the trial, forcing him to reveal his ultimate card.","If the ancient treasure, the ‘Eye of the Beast God’, was an item used to enhance one’s strength, then this ‘Blood Jade Palace’ was the life-saving treasure his father had bequeathed him.","Although the Eye of the Beast God possessed extraordinary power, there was no similar treasure in the entire Original Universe. It was an ancient treasure his father had acquired from the River of Time and Space. Despite its unique power, once one reached the level of a tier 4 Emperor, his father found no use for it.","He was bestowed with it. Few knew the true posmer of this secret treasure; if its secrets were revealed, even tier 3 Emperors would go mad with desire.","At the Emperor level, treasures that could enhance an Emperor’s strength were never put up for sale; even if they were, the prices would be exorbitant.","The Blood Jade Palace was undoubtedly the pinnacle among innate treasures, the most precious palace-type treasure in existence.","MO Longs father had roamed the Original Universe with it, even drifting through the River of Time and Space. If not for the Qishen Temple, he wouldn’t have given such a treasure to his son.","This treasure was akin to an adult gifting a spirited horse to a three-year-old child; it was simply squandering a priceless gem!","MO Long lacked the ability to control the Blood Jade Palace; it was only because his father condensed his own crystalized blood essence that he could partially unleash the palace’s power.","Nevertheless, this power was enough for him to maintain secrecy.","Jian Wushuang stared at the Blood Jade Palace, his astonishment deepening.","This treasure, something he had never seen before, MO Long, the God-Emperor, had several of them.","MO Long hadn’t anticipated that killing a Six Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal would be this difficult, nor did he foresee that in such advantageous circumstances, he would be so unlucky as to encounter God-Emperor MO Long, a peak expert who was over five hundred places ahead of him.","The Blood Jade Palace felt unshakable to him.","If God-Emperor MO Long escaped sitting on the Blood Jade Palace, the grand array wouldn’t stop him, and neither would his One Thought Universe.","“It’s so close!” Jian Wushuangs eyes narrowed to pinpricks. After a lot of effort, he couldn’t catch anything, and now he had to watch MO Long escape on the Blood Jade Palace.","This was hard for Jian Wushuang to accept. Even with a strong mentality and the ability to see through everything, he sighed internally.","Hu Qing, on the other hand, remained calm. His power had grown rapidly; he had already reached the peak of Grand Yan Immortal. Even if this plan failed, he could still go outside and kill other Nine Revolutions with his strength to gain achievements.","Although he was now a Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal and could only get ten times the points, with a bit of luck, if he managed to kill a group of Perfected Nine Revolutions, he might enter the top 100. After all, he had just killed Luo Hao, gaining a significant achievement and entering the top 1,000. “Brother Wushuang, it’s irreversible!” Hu Qing had a glimpse of enlightenment and calculated the development of the situation. They couldn’t shake the power of the Blood Jade Palace. If they forcefully attacked, they might be counterattacked.","Jian Wushuang floated in mid-air, nine long swords returning to his side. He didn’t speak, just nodded.","The Wuliang Grand Formation was riddled with holes; this move was ineffective. If MO Long could really escape, they would have to find another way out.","Although this place was deep in the mountains, such a big commotion might have already been reported to the main continent by those weaker Perfected Nine Revolutions who stayed behind in the mountains.","Since Daluo Realm had left Luo Hao in the mountains, other forces must have had spies hidden deep in the mountains to observe the situation. After all, the mountains occupied 90 percent of the opriginal planet’s territory.","“Why, afraid to attack me?” MO Long sneered while sitting on the throne.","If Jian Wushuang and the others didn’t attack the Blood Jade Palace, MO Long truly had no way to deal with them!","MO Longs strength couldn’t control the Blood Jade Palace. If he wanted the Blood Jade Palace to suppress his opponents, he had to make them attack the Blood Jade Palace first.","As a peak-level transcendent innate treasure, the Blood Jade Palace had self-defense capabilities. When attacked by a strong enemy, it would automatically raise a blood shield. Not only could it defend the Blood Jade Palace itself, but it could also shoot out blood pillars to kill enemies attacking the Blood Jade Palace.","However, once the power of the crimson crystal pillars was depleted, the blood shield would dissipate.","“No more words?” MO Long kept raising the Blood Jade Palace higher!","The Wuliang Grand Formation trembled and was shattered by the blood pillars.","Hu Qing controlled the grand array, trying to hold off the Blood Jade Palace for as long as possible.","This was a super strong individual ranking in the top 500. If he escaped now, they would suffer a significant loss. They had to delay him as much as possible.","His mind moved, and the information from the identity token flowed into his mind.","Trial Participant: Hu Qing","Cultivation: Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal","Achievements:1,040,0","Ranking: 716","This ranking wasn’t very stable even within the top 1,000, let alone breaking into the top 100.","When he killed a Perfected Nine Revolutions, he gained 100,000 achievement points. Coupled with the points he obtained from Luo Hao, which numbered in the millions, multiplied by ten, it became over ten million achievement points.","Some of these were shared with MO Long and Jian Wushuang, considering their respective contributions based on the damage they caused.."]},{"number":5187,"title":"Chapter 5187: Mi Luo","paragraphs":["Chapter 5187: Mi Luo","Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","The grand arrays barrier began to shatter incessantly, cascading down from the sky.","Once devoid of the array’s support and suppression, Jian Wushuang and his companion found themselves bereft of any advantage.","“This sucks!” Jian Wushuang stood tall in the open sky, helplessly gazing at the Blood Jade Palace.","After fighting for such a long time, all he had gained was a few hundred thousand battle achievement points. Luo Hao’s death hardly affected him; his substantial gains were mainly due to the exponential increase in achievements from fighting opponents of higher realms. In a normal battle within the same realm, he would have gained only a few thousand achievement points.","Currently, his ranking hadn’t even reached the top 3,000, let alone the top 1,000.","“Hu Qing, is there really no way?” he asked desperately.","Hu Qing shook his head. “The array is about to collapse; we must leave this place. ”","His words had barely fallen when the grand array’s barrier completely shattered, and the countless array nodes of the Wuliang Grand Formation automatically disintegrated.","Under tremendous pressure, the grand array could no longer operate and collapsed automatically.","“Jian Wushuang!” God-Emperor MO Longs eyes gleamed with killing intent. With the array now broken, he could engage in another battle. However, he was feeling somewhat apprehensive. Even without the grand array, he didn’t dare to fight again.","“The treasures are abundant, truly allowing one to do as they please!”","Jian Wushuangs face turned ashen. He wanted to argue but couldn’t find a reason. No matter how much he said now, God-Emperor MO Long would completely leave. He would be left with nothing but wasted effort.","Hu Qing, who had killed Luo Hao, was at least now ranked in the top 1,000. If he went out and killed a few more Perfected Nine Revolutions within 30 years, he could comfortably secure his position within the top 1,000. Entering the top 100 wasn’t an impossible feat either.","As for himself, he was truly in a miserable situation. His strength was neither high nor low, comparable to the peak Grand Yan Immortals only by relying on the potential of One Thought Universe. He had to work tirelessly for 30 years to squeeze into the top 1,000.","The ‘Priest Shuiyue% who ranked among the top 1,000, found himself struggling towards the end. While he could amass significant achievement points in the earlier chaotic battles, it became increasingly challenging to defeat the Perfected Nine Revolutions experts in the later stages. Preserving his position within the top 1,000 seemed exceedingly difficult.","Jian Wushuang, in his pursuit of strategic formations, had lost the precious advantage of engaging in the early chaos. Now, surpassing numerous formidable opponents ahead of him appeared nearly impossible.","The Blood Jade Palace continued to ascend, though it was still confined within the boundaries of a One Thought Universe, a range Jian Wushuang couldn’t obstruct. He could only watch helplessly.","God-Emperor MO Long gazed at Jian Wushuang’s grim expression, laughing arrogantly before steering the Blood Jade Palace and vanishing into the void.","“Let’s depart as well,” Jian Wushuang sighed. Just as he was about to retract the One Thought Universe, Hu Qing stopped him. “There’s still a chance, Brother Wushuang!’","Boom!","The Blood Jade Palace, now nearing the edge of the One Thought Universe, was suddenly struck by a force of annihilation, sending it millions of miles away. God-Emperor MO Long, who had just left, swiftly passed by Jian Wushuang and Hu Qing.","Simultaneously, within the One Thought Universe, three peak experts emerged.","They were the three Princes from the Daluo Realm.","“Damn it, what kind of treasure is this? It’s actually rebounding against my origin source Great Dao!” The Chief Prince of the Daluo Realm scowled deeply.","Upon their arrival, they witnessed God-Emperor MO Long trying to escape while steering the Blood Jade Palace. Naturally, they couldn’t let him go, From a distance of a million miles, the Chief Prince of the Daluo Realm unleashed his spear of annihilation, directly smashing into the Blood Jade Palace’s blood shield.","Although he managed to halt the Blood Jade Palace, the scarlet energy also affected his consciousness. The blood-red mist seeped through causality, beginning to invade his origin source Great Dao.","“Mi Luo, what’s happening?” The other two Princes beside him noticed something was amiss and hurriedly inquired.","They were unaware of the mysteries of the Blood Jade Palace, their caution instead reserved for the One Thought Universe.","“Be wary, MO Long. Do not act recklessly!” Chief Prince Mi Luo endured his pain, cautioning them. The three of them swiftly appeared before Jian","Wushuang and Hu Qing.","Recognizing the newcomers, Jian Wushuang felt a surge of joy.","Mi Luo, the peak Grand Yan Immortal of the Daluo Realm, and a formidable expert. Jian Wushuang had encountered him at the Chishui Hall. The Ruler of the Daluo Realm, the Emperor, was exceptionally powerful. Mi Luo, regarded as one of the foremost Princes, was renowned for his strength. He ranked just below the extreme-level Grand Yan Immortals.","The contemporary Princes were remarkably young. Only Grand Yan","Immortals with the potential to advance to Emperors could be bestowed the title of Prince. Those Grand Yan Immortals who had cultivated for countless chaotic eras lacked the qualifications to be named Princes; their potential had long been exhausted. Even with the strength of a Limit Grand Yan Immortal, it was challenging for them to successfully merge with the Dao.","However, the situation was different for these Princes. Their relatively brief cultivation periods, coupled with exceptionally high talent, set them apart. The Grand Yan Immortals in the Daluo Realm, including those like Mi Luo, had not practiced for more than 100 million years. In the eyes of the Emperors, they were still adolescents. Possessing such strength at this age meant they had the potential to become Emperors.","Hence, their status was even higher than that of extreme-level Grand Yan Immortals. After all, they were Grand Yan Immortals with the potential to become Emperors in the future.","However, this time, with the opening of the Qishen Temple, those Grand Yan Immortals who had lost hope in merging the Dao were once again valued. Ironically, these old fellows became the protagonists, and the Princes were overlooked.","However, there was an exception, the Chief Prince of the Daluo Realm, ‘Mi","Luff. He had cultivated for 70 million years, attaining a power comparable to that of the extreme-level Grand Yan Immortals. The Emperors had high hopes for him. To enhance his chances of survival, he was bestowed with innate treasures: one to protect his divine body, the other to guard his origin source. He himself was a powerhouse who mastered the Dao of Destruction from the origin source, his attacks already on par with the extreme-level Grand Yan Immortals.","“Hu Qing, be cautious of Mi Luo; his strength rivals that of God-Emperor MO Long,” Jian Wushuang remained outwardly calm but transmitted his thoughts to Hu Qing.","If it were just the two of them, they wouldn’t fear, but now they faced three peak-level experts, with Mi Luo being no less formidable than God-Emperor","MO Long.","Without the support of the grand array, their strength significantly diminished. They had also lost their means to suppress the opponents, making their situation even worse.","“Now, the two of you, answer truthfully. Have you understood?” Mi Luo suppressed the bloody mist in his mind and looked at Jian Wushuang and Hu Qing.","Before Jian Wushuang could respond, the Blood Jade Palace flew out from the ruins of the canyon, its majestic and domineering voice echoing in all directions.","“Mi Luo, you dare to come!” God-Emperor MO Long was infuriated.","Initially, he had calculated to lure Mi Luo over through Luo Hao, and that plan had succeeded. However, he hadn’t anticipated that Jian Wushuang and Hu Qing would force him to resort to using the Blood Jade Palace.","It was too late now. If they had arrived a bit earlier, before Luo Hao’s fall, he might have had the confidence to detain them.","“MO Long, I spared you last time. Do you dare to be arrogant again?” Mi Luo snorted coldly. In their previous battle, Mi Luo had attempted to take advantage of MO Long but failed to kill him. He had almost perished in that battle himself.."]},{"number":5188,"title":"Chapter 5188: 15 Million","paragraphs":["Chapter 5188: 15 Million","Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Enemies meeting often sparks intense emotions, and Jian Wushuang was","quick to strategize the situation on the battlefield. As long as the fighting persisted, he could find gains amidst the chaos.","The arrival of these three individuals couldn’t have been timelier. Yet, profiting amidst the tumultuous battles of four peak experts was no easy feat. Fortune lay amid danger; life and death were momentarily set aside, for wealth and prosperity were the true path.","Jian Wushuang cautiously spoke, “Fellow Daoists, we had no intention of fighting; we concealed ourselves here.”","“Oh, then speak the truth of what you witnessed,” Mi Luo remarked, recognizing that Jian Wushuang and Hu Qings abilities were not formidable enough to cause concern.","However, God-Emperor MO Long furrowed his brow. Although unfamiliar with Jian Wushuang, he sensed the depths of his cunning from their recent encounter.","“My brother and I just entered this canyon and saw God-Emperor MO Long battling Luo Hao. Due to our limited strength, we joined forces with Luo Hao, attempting to fend off God-Emperor MO Long. Regrettably, we were defeated, and Luo Hao fell,” Jian Wushuang said earnestly, his voice carrying a deep resentment towards God-Emperor MO Long.","Mi Luo nodded knowingly, saying nonchalantly, “Just as I expected!”","He was genuinely indifferent; he only wanted to understand the truth behind the situation.","“Let’s do it! I’ll deal with these two; you all stop MO Long!” Mi Luffs figure suddenly surged forward, his spear soaring into the sky, its destructive power filling the entire valley.","The aura of Sword Intent behind Jian Wushuang also surged. He knew these people weren’t easily deceived. Nine illusory swords burst forth, aiming directly at Mi Luo.","The Illusory Sword Trial was created based on the Ultimate Dao, the sixth level of the Heart Sword Trial. It leaked the Heart power from the Heartsword, evolving it into illusions, forging the strongest Sword Intent today: the Illusory Sword Trial.","Whoosh! Whoosh! Whoosh!","Jian Wushuangs figure retreated, but his nine illusory swords swiftly charged in the opposite direction!","“Help me hold him back!” Jian Wushuang shouted.","The power of the long spear was too overwhelming; even a slight brush could lead to his downfall right there. Fortunately, this was the One Thought Universe. His speed was remarkable, covering thousands of miles in an instant. He could match the speed of the Perfected Nine Revolutions, barely evading the deadly strike. Cold sweat trickled down his back after narrowly escaping that fatal blow.","The trials between life and death further honed his supreme path.","His mental power surged, expanding the universe once more!","Eleven million miles!","Twelve million miles!","Fifteen million miles!","“Reached the limit!” Jian Wushuang gritted his teeth against the oppressive force brought by his Thought power. He maneuvered the illusory swords to block Emperor Mi Luo as much as possible.","Hu Qing had arrived by this time. His brows furrowed slightly, but his staff erupted with formidable power.","Without the support of a grand array, Hu Qings strength only reached peak-level. Against Mi Luo, who matched the Perfected Nine Revolutions, Hu Qing gained no advantage and even faced the risk of falling. Fortunately, Jian Wushuang manipulated the illusory swords from a distance, constantly ambushing Mi Luo, forcing him to divide his attention. This gave Hu Qing a momentary relief.","The trio’s battle perfectly replicated the earlier siege against God-Emperor MO Long. However, back then, they had the upper hand due to the grand array. Now, with the array in ruins, Jian Wushuang and Hu Qing could only resist Mi Luo, who was on par with extreme-level Nine Revolutions, lacking the power to truly threaten him.","On another battlefield in the distance, two Daluo Realm Princes, much stronger than Luo Hao, surrounded the Blood Jade Palace, uncertain about how to intervene.","“Suppress him, don’t personally engage!” Mi Luo, unable to break free, transmitted his message to the two Princes.","Jian Wushuang and Hu Qings strength and coordination astonished Mi Luo. Both individuals weren’t exceptionally powerful, yet they couldn’t defeat him. Especially within this circular universe formation, the longer he stayed, the more uneasy he became. It felt far from simple.","“Whoosh!”","Jian Wushuang flickered and appeared at the topmost part of a One Thought Universe. With his Thought power merged with the universe, his strength doubled. However, suppressing Mi Luo proved exceedingly challenging.","Without the reinforcement of an array, he could manage ordinary peak Grand Yan Immortals. Still, Mi Luo’s power was overwhelming, already reaching extreme-level Nine Revolutions. Jian Wushuang found it impossible to suppress him.","Unless the Extreme Dao and Heart power were elevated, he could not suppress","Prince Mi Luo.","However, the Extreme Dao, as vast as it was, could not be elevated at will, and Heart power was an intangible and elusive concept. It wasn’t a path one could breakthrough just because they desired to.","At this moment, his only hope lay in channeling his Thought power entirely into One Thought Universe, enhancing the might of that One Thought Universe, to suppress Mi Luo.","As for the Princes from the other Daluo Realm, even though they could suppress the peak-level Grand Yan Immortals, at this moment, the two of them were dealing with MO Long. There was no need to bother with the other Princes.","Jian Wushuang even planned to suppress MO Long when the chance came along. This would force MO Long into a situation where he had to fight back. Once his strength was suppressed, the power of the Blood Jade Palace would also decrease. The two peak-level Grand Yan Immortals would still have a chance to hold back the Blood Jade Palace with their full strength.","Even if they couldn’t hold back the Blood Jade Palace at that time, he could divert Mi Luffs attention and let Mi Luo break through the Blood Jade Palace. By then, in the chaos, Jian Wushuang wouldn’t be under too much pressure.","Buzz!","His Thought power continuously poured into the One Thought Universe. This time, instead of expanding, the universe began to contract.","There was no other way. Jian Wushuangs current strength was insufficient.","He could only narrow down the range of the universe to five million miles. Although the range was smaller, the power increased tenfold.","Other powerful beings instantly noticed Jian Wushuang. God-Emperor MO","Long had witnessed Jian Wushuangs abilities before. He shouted loudly,","“Hurry and stop him, fools!”","Before the other Princes from Daluo Realm could react, Jian Wushuangs Yan power trembled, evaporating the sweat on his body. Weakly, he said, “It’s too late!”","Boom!","Waves of energy rippled across the cosmic barrier, causing both Mi Luo and MO Long below to shudder. It felt as though their bodies were being compressed.","“How is this possible?” Mi Luo could hardly believe it. He sensed his power being suppressed, significantly, at least by 30 percent.","MO Long was familiar with this sensation. He didn’t express surprise, just sighed.","The two Princes from the Daluo Realm, however, felt no discomfort. But they could sense that both Mi Luo and MO Long had significantly weakened.","This turn of events was a tremendous boon for them.","The strength of two beings on par with the utmost limits was diminished.","This meant their own power surged, instantly putting them on equal footing. They could now fairly compete for victories.","In the Daluo Realm, these Princes were equals, each unwilling to yield to the other. It was the constraints of the Emperor that kept them from harming their own kind. Otherwise, Luo Hao wouldn’t have uttered those words before his fall.","Everyone was striving for their own gains. These Princes were working together and forced to play by the rules.."]},{"number":5189,"title":"Chapter 5189: The Wind Blows","paragraphs":["Chapter 5189: The Wind Blows","Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Jian Wushuang was a person outside the influence of major powers. He had no significant background, except for the Emperor in the Great Si Region, Zhen Wuyang.","However, he had chosen the wrong side, aligning himself with the Chishui Hall, while Zhen Wuyang joined the Eternal Tower.","Now, his connections were primarily with the Tongtian Buddha Realm. In the future, he would need to visit the Tongtian Buddha Realm to settle the karmic calamity in his body and seek their help.","Since advancing to the Six Revolutions, the karmic debt and calamity on him had gradually increased. Although it didn’t affect him at the moment, it had to be resolved before he merged the Dao.","He managed to befriend the monks within the Great Desolate Wilderness, which seemed to be the universe’s favor toward him. If he were to become enemies with the Tongtian Buddha Realm, he didn’t know how to resolve the karmic debt in his body.","Hu Qing had become skilled in the Ultimate Dao and his strength had greatly increased. After becoming a half- step Emperor in the future, he would definitely receive attention from the Tongtian Buddha Realm. At that time, his status would be very high. Jian Wushuang could seek help from Wuliang Buddha through this relationship to resolve his karmic calamity.","However, all of this had to wait until the trial of the Qishen Temple ended.","Only one-tenth of the first step, the Original Planet Trial, had passed. Everything was still far away.","He didn’t know where those Emperors were. Countless Yan Immortals had been plundered there.","They, the Grand Yan Immortals, were just a part of it, and everything was still unclear and confusing.","Jian Wushuang held his breath, focusing his mind, and hurriedly replenished his energy. Infusing Thought power into One Thought Universe had overdrafted his abilities significantly. Fortunately, the power of the Original","Universe was formidable enough to prevent any damage to the origin source.","“Kill!” Jian Wushuang raised his eyebrows, and the nine auras, enhanced once again, burst forth in a myriad of illusions. Comparable to the killing power of a extreme-level Grand Yan Immortal, they shattered countless mountains and headed straight for Prince Mi Luo.","Originally having the upper hand, Prince Mi Luo, now suppressed in strength, was managing against Hu Qing. However, he had to be on constant guard against Jian Wushuangs sneak attacks, making him utterly miserable.","Although his treasures were perfectly attuned to his being, their quality paled in comparison to God-Emperor MO Longs. The combined power of all the treasures on his person was still inferior to the components of the Blood Jade Palace controlled by God-Emperor MO Long.","Faced with this life-threatening situation, he had no hidden cards for protection; he could only endure the onslaught!","“Pay no attention to MO Long; help me kill this little bald donkey!” Mi Luo was starting to falter, directly calling out for assistance from the other two Princes.","However, the situation had just turned in favor of the others. The blood shield had been shattered, and although the two of them had sustained minor injuries, it didn’t significantly impair their abilities.","At this moment, God-Emperor MO Long, now without the protection of the","Blood Jade Palace, looked somewhat desperate. Being besieged by two peak Grand Yan Immortals at full strength, his situation was even worse than that of Prince Mi Luo.","“MO Long, today you will die. The treasures on your body will belong to the two of us!”","Every time MO Long was severely injured, the two of them became even more frenzied in their attacks, not hesitating to harm themselves in the process, exchanging injuries for injuries to deal with MO Long.","If they could obtain the supreme treasure of God-Emperor MO Long, even if they didn’t advance in the top 1,000, they wouldn’t suffer losses. The treasures of God-Emperor MO Long were enough to make even an Emperor covet!","No matter how powerful Qishen Temple was, and no matter how many benefits it had, they couldn’t possibly bestow such treasures upon the two of them!","They attacked insanely, paying no attention to Mi Luffs shouts!","Originally, Mi Luo was the main force, and they only had to restrain. Of course, the benefits they received in the end were also the least because their strength couldn’t match Mi Luo’s might.","But now, with the constant exchange of power, their strength could rival both the suppressed Mi Luo and MO Long. Such a golden opportunity, how could they possibly let it slip away?","As for Mi Luo, they couldn’t care less. Once they seized MO Longs supreme treasure, they would no longer fear Mi Luo.","“Kill him! Don’t give him a chance to catch his breath!”","Two separate supreme treasures couldn’t suppress them at all. MO Long fled in a sorry state, trying to escape the boundaries of the universe of a single thought, but the imperial sons of the Daluo realm didn’t give him that chance.","“Damn it, all of you deserve to die!” MO Long gritted his teeth in anger and roared, “You’ve all been deceived! Once Mi Luo falls, we’ll all die! Hurry, go help Mi Luo kill Hu Qing. He embodies the Ultimate Dao, and Jian Wushuang also embodies the Ultimate Dao. If you don’t go now, there won’t be another chance.’","Splurt!","An incredibly sharp flying disc tore through MO Longs physical body, directly piercing him, causing significant damage to his divine body.","“Unbelievable, a single slash damaged one percent of my divine body!” MO Long completely lost his composure.","These two madmen had started burning their origin sources. Weren’t they afraid of leaving hidden injuries?","“Junior Brother, I burned one-tenth of my origin source just to break through one percent of his divine body. His defense is too strong. 1 need to find an opportunity to severely injure him and then burn my origin source again; otherwise, I won’t be able to defeat him.” The white-haired Prince from the Daluo Realm spoke with a hint of malice in his eyes.","“Good, you endure for three breaths, and I’ll deal him a heavy blow!” The young Prince laughed manically.","Were all the Princes from the Daluo Realm like this?","Jian Wushuang sneered, his Thought power trembling. Now he was just like them, burning his Heart and Thought power to enhance his One Thought Universe. It was a matter of who could endure longer.","“Since you’re all so crazy, let me help you a bit more!” Jian Wushuangs Thought power moved, using One Thought Universe to enhance the strength of the two men by 30 percent.","This was his limit, boosting the strength of Hu Qing and the two Princes from the Daluo Realm, suppressing the peak powerhouses who could rival extreme-level Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortals.","“Haha, Senior Brother, I feel my origin source has been strengthened!”","“Me too!”","“Quick, take advantage of the enhanced origin source and kill MO Long in one fell swoop!’","MO Longs pale purple skin turned even whiter with anger. He had been beaten so badly that he was starting to lose his sanity, muttering to himself, “Fools, fools, all must die!”","Countless rotating flying blades, under the enhancement of their origin sources, kept harvesting MO Longs divine body. He had no choice but to burn his origin source to resist.","Mi Luo barely dodged Jian Wushuangs illusory sword again, his mouth dripping with blood. He roared in fury, “You deceived me!”","Swish! Swish! Swish!","He dodged one sword but couldn’t avoid the remaining eight. Mi Luo screamed wildly as several illusory phantom swords pierced his body, causing him unbearable pain. Not only was his divine body damaged, but his origin source was also being consumed rapidly.","Jian Wushuangs figure approached, his Thought power moved, and nine phantom swords were instantly pulled out. Along with the swords came not only bright red blood but also a large amount of origin source energy.","In the instant they were pulled out, the Thought power contained in the phantom swords began to devour the origin source power within Mi Luo’s body.","Jian Wushuang was overjoyed. With a movement of his psychic power, he said, “Devour!”","Splash!","Following several wounds, the phantom swords continued to devour the origin source power inside Mi Luo’s body. Meanwhile, Jian Wushuang remotely absorbed this origin source power to replenish himself.","Originally heavily depleted and injured, he almost instantly restored his peak strength. Controlling his One Thought Universe was no longer difficult; instead, he became adept at it.","The power he devoured once again allowed him to be reborn from the dead.."]},{"number":5190,"title":"Chapter 5190: Devour","paragraphs":["Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","The plan this time had approached perfection, uniting everything and making him invincible!","“Kill!","The devouring power turned Jian Wushuang into a frenzy, his strength continually ascending.","“Ahhhhhhhh!” Mi Luo roared incessantly, clutching his head. His origin source was being devoured, causing him immense agony.","Seizing the opportunity, Hu Qing swung his staff, a staff that could shake heaven and earth, smashing it onto Mi Luo’s head.","<font < div>","Bang!","Mi Luo, suspended in the sky, was struck down into the ground, creating a deep pit of a hundred miles.","Jian Wushuang and Hu Qing showed no mercy, descending directly into the crater caused by Mi Luo.","The already healed wounds were once again torn open by the illusory phantom sword, relentlessly stabbing into Mi Luo’s origin source. As long as there was a gap, the nine phantom swords would greedily devour Mi Luo’s origin source power.","A plain and ordinary second-grade Great Dao, not yet the Dao after the fusion, couldn’t withstand Jian Wushuang’s devouring. He could devour even Emperor-level Daos, let alone Mi Luo’s minor Dao.","“I’ll fight you to the end!” Mi Luo struggled to stand up, his body slightly hunched. He raised his head, which was now somewhat lowered.","Now, he was even more desperate than MO Long. Ever since his origin source was damaged and devoured, his combat power had continuously declined. Not to mention Jian Wushuang, even the current Hu Qing could easily slaughter him.","As a powerful being and the Chief Prince of a high-grade world, he, Mi Luo, would never kneel and die!","Although he had no fondness for the other Princes, and even engaged in secret struggles with them, he still tilted his head, glanced at them, and uttered two words, “Leave quickly!”","Then his entire body transformed into a dazzling light!","Hu Qing quickly retreated, while Jian Wushuang desperately charged forward, shouting, “No!”","Oh, the exquisite origin source!","It shouldn’t self-destruct.","Jian Wushuang was like a young girl who had seen a withering flower, feeling deeply despondent.","Such a delicious feast, destroyed just like that.","The fall of the Grand Yan Immortal was vastly different from that of the Emperor. It couldn’t form an Emperor’s Fall at all, merely dispensing a considerable amount of origin source power in the air.","Looking at the pervasive aura of the origin source in the air, Jian Wushuang didn’t let it go to waste. He controlled his hands and began to devour it.","This origin source power was only one-tenth of Mi Luo’s, which was too little. If Mi Luo hadn’t self-destructed his origin source, he could have devoured much more. The more he devoured, the stronger he would become.","Jian Wushuang could now sense that even without using the One Thought Universe, he possessed power equal to top-tier Nine Revolutions. Once he unleashed the One Thought Universe, he would have genuine peak-level combat strength and could cross levels with his illusory sword, challenging the utmost limits.","Jian Wushuang, enjoying the power of the origin source, could never have imagined that his actions would catch the attention of the highest authority in the Qishen Temple, the ‘true spirit’.","In the heart of the Qishen origin source.","The true spirit roamed the sea of origin source. This was a cosmic-level origin source, no longer a grand pillar but more like an endless expanse of water.","Even during the initial stages of the highest trials, the true spirit couldn’t be bothered to intervene. Even trials at the level of Emperors didn’t capture its interest.","A canopy that could rival an advanced world, when viewed within the sea of origin source, seemed insignificant. From top to bottom, it split into blocks the size of human figures. Through countless canopies, the true spirit could observe anyone in the three major trial grounds.","“Eh! What’s this?” The true spirit’s eyes narrowed. That scene just now pulled it back to ancient times.","He? Or perhaps, it?","The current true spirit was neither human nor ghost. However, when it was first born and met its master for the first time, it was just a spirit of a treasure. But because of its master, it transformed from an it to a ‘he’, possessing all the qualities of a cultivator. It changed from a spirit to a living being.","It couldn’t forget its old master’s instructions, never dared to forget. Even though it had the power equivalent to the Universe Masters of and controlled the entire Qishen Temple, it never dared to forget.","“Stop him!”","The Great Devouring Dao was the Qishen’s main cultivation Dao, a Dao that had reached the pinnacle of levels in ancient times.","After numerous calculations and explorations, he realized that this path was utterly impassable. Even at the ultimate level, within the River of Time and Space, he was but a drop in the ocean.","“This child, the path has been severed,” murmured the true spirit.","Not to mention reaching the level of Oishen, even becoming an Emperor was a formidable challenge! Qishen was a unique being from birth, naturally attuned to the Ultimate Dao. He had become the most dazzling existence within the River of Time and Space.","The path he couldn’t traverse, let alone Jian Wushuang, a mere Six Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal.","Not only was it impassable, but this Dao could also be treacherous.","Qishen’s fall was closely related to the Great Devouring Dao.","Ultimate Dao practitioners were incredibly rare in the Original Universe. Although he had commanded the spirit slaves to plunder other universes for these Ultimate Grand Yan Immortals, successfully merging the Ultimate Dao was exceptionally challenging.","The Original Universe had been fortunate enough to produce an Ultimate","Emperor, but unfortunately, that Emperor had followed the Dao of Destruction, conflicting with the ancestral ways of the Qishen Temple. At most, one could inherit the position of ‘divine master’.","The mantle of Qishen still needed to be chosen from among the Yan Immortals and Grand Yan Immortals. The Ultimate Dao was the best, but if that was impossible, it could be a special secondary-grade Great Dao or someone who pursued the Unity of Myriad Daos.","Even after this selection, there were at least tens of thousands of candidates. Moreover, many individuals would continue to break through during trials, possibly mastering the Ultimate Dao.","While those Emperors might have considered themselves the main force, they were unaware that the true spirit was uninterested in them.","“Intriguing indeed. This little one’s potential can be ranked in the top tier, a raw gem and the ultimate existence born of Zen insight. The old master would probably be very fond of him, ” the true spirit stroked his beard, growing fonder of Hu Qing, the little bald donkey, the more he looked at him.","However, when he saw Jian Wushuang, a sense of regret and a trace of disgust crossed his face.","This trace of disgust came from Qishen’s distaste for his own Great Devouring Dao, so when the true spirit saw someone touching the Great Devouring Dao, he was displeased with Jian Wushuang.","The true spirit, however, was unaware that Jian Wushuang’s devouring was related to the Extreme Dao, not the path Qishen had taken.","“Thirteen!” the true spirit called out, and a stooped old man appeared, holding a dark lamp, within the sea of origin source.","“Have the people from the Fourth Hall retrieve some debris from the ancient ruins and throw it onto the original planet, adding some difficulty for these youngsters,” the true spirit folded his hands behind his back, his gaze leaving that patch of firmament and moving to other patches.","“Also, give these Emperors a little incentive. I feel like they’re slacking off!”","“Yes!” Thirteen’s voice was hoarse. As soon as he spoke, he disappeared above the sea of origin.","A true spirit strolling in the sea of origin source suddenly felt a consciousness piercing through the layers of protection around the Qishen Temple, directly invading the sea of origin source.","“How dare you!” The true spirit erupted instantly.."]},{"number":5191,"title":"Chapter 5191: Forbidden Demon Lord and Qishen","paragraphs":["Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","The originally kind expression vanished in an instant, replaced by an intense sternness.","“You old thing, why do you hinder my path!” A large and hideous head hovered above the sea of origin source.","Its hollow eye sockets emitted a dim light, and the entire head was uneven, exuding an evil aura.","The true spirit, after clearly seeing the newcomer, snorted coldly, “This is what the master ordered. I naturally have to do it. I don’t care whose path I block.”","“You!” Black mist spewed out from the nostrils of the ugly head, roaring, “Don’t forget, I am a part of Qishen. I used to be your master’s Great Dao!”","<font < div>","The true spirit sneered, “A Great Dao cast away by the master dares to claim it’s a part of Qishen.”","Although he said so, he was aware of the immense power of the Great","Devouring Dao. Just now, he noticed the devouring technique displayed by Jian","Wushuang, which had transformed into the taboo Great Devouring Dao of the Forbidden Demon Lord. It had come to the Qishen Temple. There was probably some kind of coincidence behind this.","“Hmph, that old man had no idea about my strength. It was his own blindness. If he hadn’t stripped me off, how could he have fallen!” the grotesque head roared.","“Shut your mouth. The master is someone you, a filthy thing like you, can never insult. If you don’t leave now, I’ll suppress this avatar of yours in the Qishen Temple and torment you for eternity!” the true spirit thundered.","Everything else could be tolerated, except insulting the Qishen Temple. That was his bottom line.","Seeing the old man furious, the evil skull hesitated for a moment. Knowing he couldn’t gain anything here, he began to disintegrate on his own.","Before disintegrating, he couldn’t help but threaten, “Just you wait! One day, I will break free from this seal and completely devour the Original Universe, restoring the glory of the Great Devouring Dao! ”","“Hahaha!!! ”","The true spirit sneered contemptuously. “Feel free to devour; the Original Universe isn’t mine. I wouldn’t care even if you devour yourself.”","“The Forbidden Demon Lord?”","“Just a filthy insect!”","Just an insect that his master had removed from his body. Back then, his master’s Great Devouring Dao was so powerful. He wouldn’t even furrow his brows at devouring an entire universe.","However, that filthy insect did have some abilities back in the day. It had devoured several universes, but in the end, a powerful being suppressed it in the Original Universe. Now, the seal was beginning to collapse, indicating that the being that suppressed it had also perished.","The true spirit sighed.","If the Great Devouring Dao still existed, perhaps his master wouldn’t have fallen back then.","But at that time, the Qishen was too strong, too arrogant. The Great Devouring Dao was a disaster; he had to remove it. One, for his own sake, and secondly, for the sake of the river of time and space.","The fall of an Emperor would give birth to Emperor’s Fall, creating numerous ghosts and monsters capable of destroying a world without an Emperor.","As the peak existence in the River of Time and Space, the Qishen’s Great Dao was incredibly powerful. Even after being stripped away, that Devouring Dao could easily trample over a universe.","Fortunately, when Qishen fell, he attained enlightenment within the Qishen Temple, preserving his complete Great Dao within the temple.","If he had fallen outside, his Great Dao would either enrich a universe or give birth to the powerful Forbidden Demon Lord.","That Forbidden Demon Lord, after being expelled years ago, developed self-awareness and roamed the river of time, causing havoc whenever it could.","Luckily, a powerful being suppressed it later. Now, it re-emerged and encountered the Qishen Temple once again, making the Forbidden Demon Lord extremely wary.","After all, it was something left by Qishen. He had known Qishen’s plan back then. Now that the Qishen Temple had opened in the Original Universe, he feared that it might cause a tremendous upheaval, ruining his plans.","Thinking of threatening the true spirit, he ended up scaring himself away.","At the heart of the Original Universe, within a massive cage, stood an enormous figure stretching billions of miles. No living being could approach this place. The malevolent aura emanating from this colossal figure was incredibly potent, corroding even the origin source. Even a tier 5 Emperor would have their consciousness affected here, damaging their origin source.","This was also the most dangerous place in the Original Universe!","“Heaven’s Prison.”","The towering figure was the true form of the Forbidden Demon Lord.","Although the seal had started to loosen, he still couldn’t move a step.","According to calculations, it would still take tens of thousands of chaos cycles to break open the prison. Each epoch spanned billions of years, and he couldn’t afford to wait for tens of thousands of chaos cycles.","In the Original Universe, the Qishen Temple had appeared. No one knew what the Original Universe would become in the future. What if a Universe Master emerged?","He couldn’t afford to delay any longer.","“Are they really forcing me to reveal my true strength?” The Forbidden Demon Lord sighed, his immense eyes shifting at that moment.","“A million years more, that should suffice! I hope that little one grows up quickly,” the Forbidden Demon Lord sunk into contemplation again. At this moment, the tension in the Original Universe eased slightly.","In the Qishen Temple, on the original planet.","If Jian Wushuang knew that devouring Mi Luo’s origin source would attract the attention of two peak-level existences in the universe, there was no telling how he would react.","In the canyon, after Mi Luo’s fall, the tide turned.","Mi Luo self-destructed his origin source, leaving behind only intact armor on the ruins, along with a dark red pearl.","Both were excellent innate treasures. Jian Wushuang naturally took them without hesitation and handed them to Hu Qing. “Choose one for yourself!”","Hu Qing folded his hands and shook his head. A brown staff was innate to him; the stronger his treasure, the stronger he became. He didn’t need any innate treasures.","“In that case, I won’t hold back!” Jian Wushuang smiled.","He directly acknowledged ownership, immediately putting on the armor and taking the pearl that guarded the origin source.","The pearl floated above the origin source, not only guarding the Great Dao of the origin source but also nourishing it. Jian Wushuang felt refreshed, his mind much clearer.","“Brother Wushuang, what about those three?” Hu Qing pointed to the three frenzied individuals.","Calling them frenzied was not an exaggeration. Three peak-level powerhouses burned their origin sources, fighting in a desperate melee. Punches and kicks were exchanged, nearly trading life for life.","No matter how hard the two Princes from the Daluo Realm fought, they couldn’t kill God -Emperor MO Long. This didn’t mean MO Long was exceptionally strong; despite his numerous innate treasures, his strength was suppressed, making him inferior to the two counterparts of the same level.","The reason he hadn’t fallen was that when he was about to succumb, the pressure from the One Thought Universe would loosen slightly due to Jian Wushuang’s influence. Jian Wushuang would gradually loosen the restrictions to allow him to gain some strength to continue fighting.","Now. all the restrictions had been released. even enhancing MO Long’s","strength by 30 percent, allowing the fight to continue.","The three Princes from the Daluo Realm thought they had an advantage, but in reality, they were evenly matched. After consuming their strength for so long, they were close to exhaustion. Jian Wushuang and Hu Qing could easily deal with them.."]},{"number":5192,"title":"Chapter 5192: Swear","paragraphs":["Chapter 5192: Swear","Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","“It’s time for settlement,” Jian Wushuang said calmly.","With a swift movement, he appeared above the three figures, looking down at the three peak-level experts huddled together.","Smack!","The Prince of the Daluo Realm slapped Emperor God -Emperor MO Long’s forehead, crushing the skull inward.","“Tsk tsk, Junior Brother, just one more blow...”","Spurt!","MO Long spat blood on his opponent’s face, then raised his fist and smashed it into the chest of the Daluo Realm Prince, causing a deep depression.","They had exhausted all their origin source power, unable to even recover their physical strength. Visible wounds marred the bodies of the three peak-level experts.","“Idiot!” MO Long repeated these words without saying anything else.","“Die!” The Daluo Realm prince used the last bit of his Yan power, activated his Universe Ring, and pulled out a supreme treasure dagger. He thrust it into","God -Emperor MO Long’s neck, and golden blood spurted out of the wound.","Splurt!","The Daluo Realm Prince roared, and MO Long roared back. He pulled the dagger out of his neck, no longer repeating the word ‘idiot.’","With a gulp, MO Long’s face became unrecognizable, a wry smile playing on his lips. “You should have stabbed it into my skull.”","As he spoke, MO Long gripped the dagger and squeezed out the last trace of his Yan power, maneuvering the blade to create a streak of light.","The two Daluo Realm Princes, clutching their throats, staggered backward.","Even Jian Wushuang couldn’t bear to watch. Such powerful beings had ended up in this pitiful state.","Whoosh!","With a wave of his hand, the One Thought Universe dissipated under his command, and Jian Wushuang no longer influenced their minds. He spared them a chance to catch their breath.","“MO Long, surrender all your treasures and your achievements. I can spare your life,” Jian Wushuang said calmly.","Separated from each other, the three individuals lost their remaining vigor. Now, they could only sit amidst the ruins, gazing up at Jian Wushuang in his snow-white robes.","“What happened? How could Mi Luo fall!” Only now did the two of them realize that Mi Luo had perished.","“You scoundrel!” The Prince of the Daluo Realm endured the boiling blood within him and cursed in anger.","Jian Wushuang, however, couldn’t be bothered with these two. A Sword Qi swept out and killed one of them instantly.","“Hu Qing, the other one is yours,” Jian Wushuang said casually.","They had agreed on a fifty-fifty split, so it was fifty-fifty. He didn’t even know their rankings. Now, with a casual move, he killed one, leaving the other for Hu Qing.","In essence, they jointly divided the spoils of a peak-level Grand Yan Immortal between the two of them.","Hu Qing hesitated for a moment, then silently muttered something and struck with his palm.","Finally, the remaining Prince of the Daluo Realm’s physical body dissipated, and his divine body, along with his origin source, vanished without a trace, completely obliterated.","The two of them gained corresponding achievement points, but the lion’s share had already been taken by the main culprit, MO Long.","There was only one opponent left. Judging solely by achievement points, Mi Luo had the most. But in terms of treasures, MO Long had the most among them all.","In the entire universe, there were probably very few Grand Yan Immortals who possessed more treasures than God-Emperor MO Long.","After all, not every tier 4 Emperor had just one son.","Perhaps only the direct relatives of tier 5 Emperors could surpass the treasures on MO Long’s body.","“How about this: if you’ve thought it through, hand over all your treasures. Your life isn’t worth much. Considering you helped me stall them for so long, I’ll spare you,” Jian Wushuang said.","Jian Wushuang wasn’t lying. His life was worth at most 100,000 points, a value he couldn’t care less about. The reason he spared him was to gain control of the transcendent innate treasures. The Seal of Suppression and Suppressing Jade Pavilion were a set of innate treasures, the most valuable ones. Once he controlled them, it was like having an extra trump card.","However, what Jian Wushuang wanted most was the Eye of the Beast God. A domain-type innate treasure was exceedingly rare; few Emperors possessed one. let alone Grand Yan Immortals.","Although Jian Wushuang could use One Thought Universe, each use drained his Thought power. With the Eye of the Beast God, he would alleviate a lot of pressure. At least he would have other options besides the One Thought Universe.","Furthermore, the Eye of the Beast God contained a power that made him uneasy. He had to obtain this treasure intact.","Since that tier 4 Emperor gave his son so many treasures, he must have left some hidden measures. Jian Wushuang was afraid that if he killed MO Long, these treasures might be lost too.","“How can I trust you?” MO Long sat on a rock, his arrogance vanishing as he watched the two Daluo Realm Princes who were killed shortly after. In place of his arrogance, there was now the joy of victory.","These two fools had no value even as pawns and were killed outright. Yet, he still lived, negotiating with Jian Wushuang.","In the life-and-death battle, he emerged victorious.","MO Long, his mind clouded, grinned manically.","Jian Wushuang landed gracefully beside him, patting his shoulder and laughing heartily.","“I can swear to it!” Jian Wushuang smiled faintly.","“Who would believe you?” MO Long’s face darkened.","“In that case, there’s nothing more to discuss!”","MO Long raised his hand and hurriedly shouted, “We can talk. I can give you all my treasures and battle achievement points, but you have to give me a guarantee!”","Jian Wushuang extended his left hand, fingers pointing skyward.","“Under the Qishen, I, Jian Wushuang, swear that after obtaining MO Long’s supreme treasures, I will not harm him in the slightest. If I break this oath, I shall face a deadly calamity!”","As his words fell, a strand of karma condensed in the sky and enveloped both of them.","MO Long nodded, then looked at Hu Qing.","Hu Qing understood instantly. He didn’t want more bloodshed either, so he made a vow following Jian Wushuang’s example.","“Now can we proceed?” Jian Wushuang squatted down, eyebrows raised, staring at MO Long.","One item, two items, three items.","A hundred items...","Among them was the pinnacle-level innate treasure, the Blood Jade Tower, the only set of innate treasures of its kind.","There were three top-grade transcendent innate treasures: one guarded the origin source, one protected the divine body, and the last was the Eye of the Beast God.","The remaining 17 were at the level of transcendent innate treasures, while the rest were just ordinary peak treasures, including several excellent peak treasure sets.","Jian Wushuang couldn’t help but swallow saliva, saying casually, “Brother MO Long, did you steal these from the Emperor’s treasury?","Even Hu Qing, standing in the distance, was momentarily stunned. Some of those treasures seemed quite suitable for him.","God -Emperor MO Long didn’t dare to boast. “Jian Wushuang, rest assured, there are absolutely no restrictions on these treasures. Your blood will suffice for their ownership to be trasnferred to you. If you don’t believe me, I can swear to it!”","Jian Wushuang waved his hand dismissively. “No need! Just tell me all the information about this treasure!”","Once the Eye of the Beast God was taken out, it resembled a rhombus-shaped gem. Its pale golden color was understated, but the ancient aura it exuded was authentic.."]},{"number":5193,"title":"Chapter 5193: Eye of the Beast God","paragraphs":["Chapter 5193: Eye of the Beast God","Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","In the original planet, deep within the mountains, Jian Wushuang and Hu Qing arrived at a cave even more secluded than the previous canyon.","“Brother Wushuang, let’s part ways here,” Hu Qing said with a gentle smile, his hands clasped together.","“We’ll meet again on the mainland,” Jian Wushuang nodded. And so, the two of them parted ways.","It was a separation planned from the beginning. Strong individuals were always lonely. Jian Wushuang followed the path of the Ultimate Sword Dao, the way of killing, while Hu Qing pursued the path of meditation and enlightenment. Different paths could not be forced to merge.","In truth, Jian Wushuang wanted to avoid unnecessary trouble. Hu Qing harbored many secrets, intricately tied to the Qishen Temple.","“Farewell!” Jian Wushuang bid farewell, watching Hu Qing’s figure disappear into the horizon. Then, he returned to the cave.","He set up a simple barrier around the cave, allowing him to sense everything within a radius of a million miles. He wouldn’t stay here for long. The Qishen Temple was dangerous, but it also offered tremendous opportunities.","Especially now, after reaching the fourth level of the Extreme Dao and mastering the ability to devour everything with his Thought power, he needed to keep fighting.","During this brief respite, his priority was to refine the Eye of the Beast God. According to God-Emperor MO Long, the Eye of the Beast God was a relic his father had found in the depths of the River of Time, in the remnants of an ancient battlefield. It was called the Eye of the Beast God because the crystal resembled an eye and could summon an ancient beast god.","At that time, MO Long’s father thought he had found a great treasure, but unfortunately, after refining it, the Eye of the Beast God was not as powerful as he had imagined.","It wasn’t of much use to the Emperor, but the power of this ancient treasure was tremendous. It could enhance the divine bodies of ordinary beings tenfold.","Apart from practicing powerful martial arts techniques, enhancing the strength of a divine body was incredibly difficult. However, this artifact could enhance the Grand Yan Immortal’s divine body.","MO Long’s father believed this item was extraordinary and bestowed it upon MO Long.","Indeed, the artifact was powerful. Its effect on the Grand Yan Immortal was perfect, stronger than any innate treasure.","Jian Wushuang sat cross-legged on a flat stone bed, his forehead constantly shimmering as the Eye of the Beast God merged with him.","Although he wasn’t a Special Life Form, his divine body was more robust than that of ordinary Special Life Forms.","At least within the Great Si Region, his divine body could be considered top-notch.","However, in the entire Original Universe, his divine body’s strength was quite ordinary.","Take, for example, the Special Life Forms under the command of Chishui; each one possessed a divine body strength thousands of times greater than his.","God -Emperor MO Long awakened the power of his bloodline because his father was the Emperor. His divine body erupted with 500 times the power. But if you added the tenfold amplification from the Eye of the Beast God, he had a divine body strength of 5,000 times.","5,000 times was exceptionally strong among special beings. Often, it took countless epochs for a universe’s secret realm to nurture a favored one with a divine body strength of 5,000 times.","In the early epochs of the universe, there existed extraordinary beings, born with innate origin sources. These Special Life Forms, nurtured in exceptional realms, were no less formidable than the rare second-tier origin source experts. Some among them even rivaled the Ultimate Dao itself.","The pinnacle of the Original Universe’s potential gave birth to extraordinary beings capable of conceiving 10,000-fold divine bodies from birth. These creatures were unparalleled, and once born, they would be fiercely coveted by major powers, groomed into the prodigies of those powers.","Upon successfully merging the Dao, they became supremely powerful entities among the tier 4 Emperors.","Chishui, a wayfarer of the cosmic early days, was one such extraordinary being.","Possessing a 10,000-told divine body, his understanding ot the origin source was slightly lacking, but he was near perfection in every other aspect. His divine body seemed endless, a surplus that gave him the audacity to challenge even the peak powers.","Moreover, he was currently the most promising candidate in the Original Universe to break through to the tier 5 Emperor. In the future, he held immense potential to become a tier 5 Emperor, the most supreme existence possible.","Jian Wushuang’s divine body, though impressive during his cultivation as a Yan Immortal, paled in comparison to these extraordinary beings after his ascension to Grand Yan Immortal. Fortunately, he had acquired the Eye of the Beast God, a treasure coveted by every Grand Yan Immortal in their dreams.","This treasure directly amplified his divine body 10-fold, not merely accumulating its strength. Now, Jian Wushuang’s divine body was approximately 1,000-fold stronger. With a tenfold increase, wouldn’t it be equivalent to a 10,000-fold genetic divine body?","He could now directly rival the most powerful life forms in the universe.","Buzz!","A resonating hum echoed in his mind, signifying the complete fusion of the","Eye of the Beast God.","“Start!” Jian Wushuang suppressed his excitement.","“Double!” “Triple!”","“Fivefold...","Jian Wushuang hesitated for a moment, pushed his Eye of the Beast God to its limit, and his divine body ultimately multiplied sixfold.","“What’s going on?” Jian Wushuang wondered.","Could it be that God-Emperor MO Long had deceived him?","That shouldn’t be the case!","He uncertainly used his Eye of the Beast God again, stopping only when the shadow of the Beast God behind him solidified. This time, it still amplified sixfold.","Now his divine body had reached over 6,000 times its original strength; his every move could destroy heaven and earth.","Because of his Extreme Dao, his origin source was stronger than any other Grand Yan Immortal’s. Even if he burned his origin source, he could exhaust those controllers of Ultimate Dao.","The only lacking aspect was the strength of his divine body. Now, with a sixfold amplification, possessing 6,000 times the genetic makeup, he rivaled those Special Life Forms nurtured in high-grade worlds.","“Phew, the limits of the Eye of the Beast God are not fixed, ” Jian Wushuang concluded.","The weaker the divine body of the person, the stronger his amplification. For instance, he could increase MO Long’s strength tenfold. If it were those Special Life Forms, perhaps their increase would be only one or two times.","Indeed, the universe was fair.","For ordinary beings, especially humans, their life genes were weak, but their numbers were vast. Many in number and strong in comprehension, they were destined for greatness.","As for ordinary beings, there were countless Emperors who had achieved the Dao. The universe had tens of thousands of Emperors who had ventured out of the Original Universe over countless years.","Unsatisfied with their strength, they chose to drift in the River of Time and Space.","But Special Life Forms numbered only a few. This was the disparity.","Jian Wushuang was quite satisfied with the sixfold amplification. This way, his divine body could carry more Thought Power, significantly enhancing his overall strength.","Now, even if he was alone, he had the confidence to deal with ordinary peak-level Grand Yan Immortals. However, if he encountered someone like MO Long, he would still need to tread carefully.","Jian Wushuang breathed a sigh of relief, retracted his Eye of the Beast God, and everything returned to calm.","His divine body reverted to its original strength of one thousand times.","“I need to find a way to enhance my divine body.”","1,000 times!","That was his limit back in the Great Si Regioon. Now, in the Qishen Temple, if he had the chance, he would prioritize enhancing his divine body. His divine body was his weak point and needed improvement.."]},{"number":5194,"title":"Chapter 5194: Ranking","paragraphs":["Chapter 5194: Ranking","Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","The treasures he acquired from MO Long this time, he was unwilling to incur karmic debts. He forcibly gifted most of the treasures to Hu Qing.","Apart from the Beast God’s Eye, he also chose a transcendent innate treasure battle armor.","The entire battle armor could envelop his entire body. With his divine body enhancement and the innate treasure battle armor, he was no longer afraid of close combat with those peak-level Grand Yan Immortals.","As for the Blood Jade Palace and the innate treasure for guarding the origin source, he gave them all to Hu Qing. Firstly, his origin source was strong enough, and now, with Mi Luo’s innate treasures, it was sufficient. Secondly, Hu Qing’s strength spanned greatly, and his origin source was unstable, requiring an innate treasure to guard it.","The Blood Jade Palace contained many malicious energies, which could allow Hu Qing to refine himself and enhance his own strength. It was also more suitable for Hu Qing.","They divided the remaining treasures based on enhancing their own combat power. Hu Qing didn’t find the remaining ordinary treasures appealing since he came from a major power and followed the Ultimate Dao. The Wuliang Buddha also bestowed him with many valuable items, so he gave all the remaining treasures to Jian Wushuang.","Various Emperor-grade pills and some exotic treasures, such as items that could conceal the aura of a Grand Yan Immortal.","These items were top-grade treasures in the outside world. Even if he didn’t use them, he could sell them for other treasures.","Now that Jian Wushuang was alone, he would need many more treasures in the future. Just the path of enhancing his divine body would require a considerable amount. This alone was a challenging task for him.","The materials needed for a perfected physical body were exorbitantly expensive.","After organizing his treasures once more, Jian Wushuang stowed them away and took out his identity token, checking his achievements.","Triallist: Jian Wushuang","Cultivation Realm: Six Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal (This information cannot be viewed)","Achievements: 43-96 million points","Ranking: 72","In the Original Planet Alpha Nine.","1st: Dao Lord Xue Yue","2nd: PO Jun","3rd: Dao Lord Leng Shuang","68th: Hu Qing","72nd: Jian Wushuang","Both his and Hu Qing’s rankings were within the top 100, and he had gained 30 million achievement points just from Mi Luo alone.","Even if he didn’t venture out further and hid in the mountains, he could ensure a position within the top 1,000, possibly slipping out of the top 100 in the end. However, the rewards from the Qishen Temple only mentioned rewards for those within the top 1,000.","As for whether the value of the treasures bestowed upon the first-place and the thousandth-place experts was the same, he couldn’t know. But he believed the treasure given to the first place was stronger.","If they were all the same, there was no need for everyone to struggle to enter the top 1,000; they could just find a place to cultivate directly.","Cultivating on the original planet was a hundred times better than outside; this place could be said to be an unparalleled seclusion ground.","However, no one believed the treasures given to the first and the thousandth were the same. They, like Jian Wushuang, tried their best to squeeze into the top 100, even the top 10.","Looking at it now, the top three were all experts at the Dao Lord level. The weakest in the top ten were peak-level Grand Yan Immortals, and among the top 100, only a few were peak-level Grand Yan Immortals; most were extreme-level Grand Yan Immortals.","These extreme-level Grand Yan Immortals were ancient relics who had lived through countless Yan ages. Those young Princes and Daoists simply couldn’t compete with them.","The number one on the Universe Deity-Demon List, ‘Xue Yue Dao Lord’, ranked around 400 in the Earth rankings. His power was comparable to that of Jiu Yu.","Jian Wushuang had witnessed Jiu Yu’s terrifying strength. A person capable of slaughtering hundreds or even thousands of Perfected Nine Revolutions experts, this kind of power in a Grand Yan Immortal was enough to kill him with just a glance.","Even in the main continent, he had to avoid these Grand Yan Immortals who were titled as ‘Dao Lords’. Although they hadn’t reached the level of half-step Emperors, the difference was not substantial. At most, they were just slightly weaker than those half-step Emperors who had mastered the Ultimate Dao.","The difference was only in the strength of their origin source.","Jian Wushuang’s path to becoming stronger was still very far ahead. At least on this original planet, he couldn’t claim to be the strongest. On this planet, if his true strength could enter the top 100, it would be considered good. Fortunately, he had a lot of room for improvement.","Unlike those third-grade origin Great Dao practitioners, they had reached the end. When they were about to merge the Dao, their strength would only be at the level of peak Grand Yan Immortals.","Currently at the fourth level of the Extreme Dao, he could use his Thought power to devour others’ origin sources, allowing his strength to increase rapidly.","By devouring a few more peak-level Grand Yan Immortals, he estimated that he could enter the Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal level. At that time, his strength would undergo a qualitative change, and his combat power would be comparable to that of extreme-level Grand Yan Immortals.","However, advancing in the Extreme Dao was not so easy. Only by elevating the level of his Dao could he make a significant breakthrough.","Every three levels in the Dao represented a major threshold!","In the vast expanse of the stars, he achieved the first three levels effortlessly. Then, in the Great Desolate Wilderness, he used his Thought power to consume and stepped into the fourth level.","The most crucial task at the moment was to swiftly elevate his Extreme Dao to the sixth level. At that point, his devouring power would become terrifying. The origin source Dao of a peak-level Grand Yan Immortal, he could now consume 10 percent. At the sixth level of the Extreme Dao, he could even entirely devour the origin source Dao of other Grand Yan Immortals.","Ever since he gained this ability, his thirst for slaughter grew. This bloodlust carried a malevolent aura, which was precisely why the forbidden Demon Lord Fengyu took an interest in him.","It was a mutual attraction among their kind.","Thankfully, they were within the Qishen Temple. Outside, he would undoubtedly have been classified as a Demon.","Just like the Grand Yan Immortals on the original planets, many were considered Demons outside. Yet, they roamed freely, backed by Emperor-level powerhouses; no one dared to touch them.","Jian Wushuang was different. He couldn’t be categorized as purely demonic now; he was an evil Grand Yan Immortal, relying on devouring his equally powerful peers to strengthen himself.","Furthermore, he had no significant background. Once his Extreme Dao reached the sixth level, even if he got stuck there and couldn’t break through, he could still merge Daos.","By that time, his strength would be practically unmatched below the Emperors, capable of devouring any Grand Yan Immortal at will.","This threat was enormous, especially considering his lack of significant backing. When the time came, the entire Original Universe wouldn’t have a place for him.","The Devouring Dao was terrifying enough; what if he successfully merged Daos again? Those Emperors would become his sustenance, wouldn’t they?","They couldn’t possibly turn a blind eye to this. Moreover, at that point, the very origin source of the universe would reject him.","“Devour the Original Universe?” Jian Wushuang sighed deeply.","Although he hadn’t reached that point yet, he could already foresee the future. To contend against the origin source, even to consume it and reach the peak of the universe – it was an arduous enlightenment. Merging Daos was his tribulation. As for devouring the universe, it was nothing but a delusion.","Whether the Devouring Dao would lead anywhere, he didn’t know. But now that he had embarked on this journey, he had to see it through.","It wasn’t about closure; it was about the path he had no choice but to tread.","If he abandoned his devouring nature, his cultivation speed would slow down. That sense of bloodlust would one day become uncontrollable.","Once it backfired!","The consequences were unimaginable. Therefore, the true spirit of the Qishen Temple said his path was different.."]},{"number":5195,"title":"Chapter 5195: Transcendent Immortal Formation","paragraphs":["Chapter 5195: Transcendent Immortal Formation","Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","“This rare trial’s most precious treasures are these Grand Yan Immortals!” Jian Wushuang, his eyes emanating a sinister aura, exclaimed, his eye sockets shrinking at the sight.","The karmic calamity and killing tribulation on his body were likely the cause of his current predicament.","This situation should improve after he elevates his Extreme Dao to the seventh level. Just like when he reached the fourth level, he might gain control over other abilities.","Countless years of cultivation in the starry sky had given him profound insights. Although constant slaughter happened on the primitive stars, he could find moments to catch his breath.","Since encountering Hu Qing, he had either been fighting desperately or fleeing for his life. Now, he finally had some time to stabilize his strength.","Jian Wushuang closed his eyes, conserving his energy, and began consolidating his various Daos.","The battle with MO Long and others not only yielded precious treasures and achievements but also the origin sources devoured. These origin sources, when combined, could rival a Perfected Nine Revolutions complete origin source Dao, and they were second-tier origin source Daos at that.","His task now was to absorb these origin source powers into his Extreme Dao as much as possible.","As for the Ultimate Sword Dao origin source, he had already stepped into the sixth level. He didn’t need to advance it further now, and even if he did, he dared not use the origin sources he had devoured to elevate it.","The Sword Dao was unique, it couldn’t be complicated, and certainly not chaotic.","Sword Dao needed purity, something innate!","The Extreme Dao, on the other hand, was different. It contained the origin sources of all Great Daos, and he could freely devour and merge them.","As for Heart power, it couldn’t be considered a separate Dao; it was intertwined with the Sword Dao. The stronger his Sword Dao, the stronger his Heart power.","Since his Ultimate Sword Dao reached the sixth level, his Heart power had also changed and showed signs of breakthrough.","This was largely due to the Bodhi Heartwood he got from Wuliang Buddha. If he had the chance, he definitely wanted to see that Bodhi Tree.","If he could uproot it entirely, that would be even better.","However, this thought flashed in his mind and disappeared.","This tree had given birth to the Wuliang Realm, an invaluable treasure even the Tongtian Buddha coveted. How could he possibly touch it?","Focusing his mind, he began to merge the origin sources and also allocated a portion of his Thought power to manifest an illusory phantom sword.","He knew quite a lot about sword formations, especially the ancient sword formations.","In the Ancient Era, a remarkable and extraordinary Sword Immortal had emerged in the Great Si Region. This sword immortal had successfully merged the Sword Dao, achieving the status of an Emperor. Moreover, he had created a peerless sword technique, which had been passed down to this day.","Among them, there was the Three-Foot Sword Formation, but this formation was incomplete. The owner of the Three-Foot Sword hadn’t completed the formation before being suppressed by Zhen Wuyang.","The grand formation had six layers. The owner of the Three-Foot Sword had once claimed that the Three-Foot Sword could measure the universe, with a total of thirteen layers. Unfortunately, just after creating the sixth layer, he was suppressed.","However, these six layers were sufficient for Jian Wushuang. As for the thirteen layers mentioned by the Emperor, he didn’t know if it was true or false. It was possible that the Emperor never said such a thing; perhaps someone had fabricated the rumor. After all, claiming to reach the thirteenth layer right after creating the sixth layer to measure the universe sounded too unbelievable.","With a slight movement of his Thought power, countless illusions of Jian Wushuang split off and began to deduce the sword formation together.","The name of this grand formation was quite grandiose, but it ultimately fell into obscurity.","“Transcendent Immortal Formation!” Jian Wushuang murmured.","A formation that could kill Immortals, how domineering!","Unfortunately, it couldn’t kill the Emperor; otherwise, Zhen Wuyang wouldn’t have been a problem.","The first three layers of the Transcendent Immortal Formation corresponded to the Grand Yan Immortal. When that Sword Immortal was at the level of the Grand Yan Immortal, he achieved great fame and strength through this formation.","It’s important to note that not every Grand Yan Immortal could become an Emperor. That Sword Immortal was only a third-grade sword cultivator back then. Even when he reached the Nine Revolutions stage, he was at most comparable to a peak-level Grand Yan Immortal. But with this formation, he could achieve the status of a Dao Lord. In his hands, this grand formation was undoubtedly a terrifying formation that could kill extreme-level Grand Yan","Immortals.","Someone like Luo Hao, a second-grade origin source cultivator at the Perfected Nine Revolutions level, at his best, could only match the strength of a peak-level Grand Yan Immortal. Even if he continued to improve, a third-grade Grand Yan Immortal at best could only be on par with a","peak-level Grand Yan Immortal.","The supremely talented Sword Immortal, who had mastered the third-grade origin source Great Dao as the Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan","Immortal, was no ordinary cultivator. He was comparable to peak-level Grand Yan Immortals and had even established his name as a Dao Lord.","As he delved deeper into the sword formation, Jian Wushuang felt its immense power.","The first layer of the Transcendent Immortal Formation, an entry-level stage, required mastery over 36 sword techniques. Each Sword Intent had to surpass the Perfected Nine Revolutions level. For Jian Wushuang, this was relatively straightforward, but mastering all 36 sword techniques posed a challenge.","With the recent creation of his Illusory Sword Technique, he could divide it into 9 swords. After this power boost, he could possibly split it into 18 swords. However, another division might weaken the inherent Sword Intent significantly.","Fortunately, each of his Sword Intents far surpassed the Perfected Nine Revolutions level. At the sixth stage of the Ultimate Dao, it was equivalent to the ninth stage of a second-grade origin source Dao. His formidable Sword Intent likely wasn’t much different from that supremely talented Sword Immortal during his peak period as a Grand Yan Immortal.","Meeting the requirements was one thing; comprehending the rest was relatively straightforward. He was not inventing a formation but merely mastering a sword formation. The complexity was significantly lower. Plus, with his mastery of the Ultimate Dao and his role as the master of the sword, understanding the sword formation was as natural as a fish in water.","Three years passed in the blink of an eye within the cave.","The silence of the original planet failed to capture the passage of time through blooming and withering flowers. It was Jian Wushuangs strengthened power that lent meaning to the passing time.","Above the mountains.","Two top-grade Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortals tore through the sky and stopped near Jian Wushuang.","One had the peak fighting power of the best Nine Revolutions expert, while the other was a Grand Yan Immortal with a frail divine body on the verge of collapse.","“Madman Yang, I’ve brought you here! This place is the deepest part of the mountains. You won’t encounter powerful Grand Yan Immortals here. With your achievements, after the trial, you can still maintain your position within the top 10,000. By then, you can comprehend the origin source of the Qishen Temple,” the top-tier Grand Yan Immortal persuaded.","The one being persuaded was Madman Yang, whose real name was Yang Feng. Due to his crazed fighting style, he earned the moniker ‘Madman Yang.","However, madness on the original planet was far from a virtue. Despite his strength being among the top of the Nine Revolutions, his tendency to burn his origin source recklessly made him a headache for many experts.","After entering the original planet, he formed a team with a group of friends and accumulated significant achievement points. However, advancing into the top 1,000 was exceedingly difficult with his strength. Thus, he started targeting solitary peak-level Grand Yan Immortals. Yet, every single one of those peak-level Grand Yan Immortals who could roam the main continent alone was a formidable opponent.","Their entire squad was almost obliterated by one such peak-level Grand Yan Immortal. Fortunately, Madman Yang burned half of his origin source to escape the pursuit of the peak-level Grand Yan Immortal, saving them all.."]},{"number":5196,"title":"Chapter 5196: Feather Continent","paragraphs":["Chapter 5196: Feather Continent","Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","Losing half of his origin source and his divine body was on the verge of collapse, Madman Yang couldn’t fight anymore. He could only retire in the mountains.","“Hmph, if it weren’t for your cowardice, I would have killed that bullsh*t Daluo Realm’s Prince long ago.” Madman Yang had almost died, but his mouth was still very tough, not convinced at all.","The peak-level Grand Yan Immortal they had their eyes on was one of the top 10 Princes of the Daluo Realm.","Three years ago, four of the six Great Princes of the Daluo Realm on this original planet had fallen. The remaining two Princes did not dare to be arrogant anymore and had been walking in the main continent in a low-profile manner. Who would have thought that a few top-notch Grand Yan Immortals would dare to surround him and treat him as a pushover? In a fit of anger, they almost killed all the experts in that small team.","His good friend sighed and said indifferently, “Alright, even Little Seven has fallen this time. What else do you want us to do?”","Hearing him mention Little Seven, Madman Yang also fell silent, and his eyes turned red.","Little Seven was the only female among them. In the outside world, he had always treated her as a younger sister. Now, she had fallen on the original planet because of them.","“Little Seven.” Madman Yang lowered his head.","“Alright, don’t be too sad. Rest well here. In a few years, if you really can’t fight anymore, we’ll come to you and wait for the trial to end.”","Their strength was at the top-grade level, and with this strength, they had a chance of entering the top 1,000. Moreover, they had discussed that in the final year, if anyone was the closest to the top 1,000, they would give up the top 10,000 spot and give the identity token to that person so that he could enter the top 1,000 and enter the next round.","As for the treasures bestowed, they were given to those who contributed to the battle.","Madman Yang nodded. This time, he didn’t say anything else and went straight into the mountain range.","The expert who sent him here shook his head and sighed. His figure flashed and disappeared from where he was. The journey was not over yet. He still had to go to the main continent to fight.","After landing in the heart of the mountain range, Madman Yang collected his aura and started to search for a suitable place to hide. Now that he was seriously injured and only had the strength of an ordinary Perfected Nine Revolutions, he naturally had to find the safest place to hide.","He walked over thousands of mountains and searched everywhere.","“I heard that there are more than 100,000 Grand Yan Immortals hidden in this mountain range!” Madman Yang sneered.","Grand Yan Immortals who needed to hide were the weakest. This was also the hinterland of the mountain range, so not many experts would come here.","When some Grand Yan Immortals came in, they saw that the situation was not right and hid in the mountain range. These people were mostly Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortals, they were weak and did not have any battle achievements, so no one went to look for these Grand Yan Immortals.","Killing a Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal only gave him 100 battle achievement points. If he had the time, he might as well participate in a random battle on the continent and obtain 10,000 battle achievement points.","After all these years of trial, the Grand Yan Immortals who were able to survive on the main continent were not weak. Moreover, each of them had hundreds of thousands of battle achievement points.","These people were the real fat meat!","Madman Yang continued to explore the mountain range.","Even though his strength had dropped drastically, he was still at the standard of an ordinary Perfected Nine Revolutions. Naturally, he was not afraid of those cowards who were hiding.","Thud!","Madman Yang stepped into a quiet canyon.","“This place is not bad!” Madman Yang murmured softly.","After fighting for so many years, he was still somewhat unwilling to end up like this. However, his strength had decreased so much that he could no longer stay on the main continent. Otherwise, he would be courting death.","After entering the canyon, his figure flashed and he reached the depths of the canyon.","Looking around, there were natural caves here that extended in all directions. It was very suitable for hiding.","He took another step forward and entered the cave.","Madman Yang, who had just entered the cave, suddenly felt that something was wrong. However, before he could react, he was stunned on the spot. Then, like a puppet, he walked forward mechanically.","Whoosh!","“l see someone took the initiative to come and deliver their battle points to me!” Jian Wushuang controlled the seriously injured Madman Yang with his Heart power.","In the blink of an eye, he had already cultivated for several years. He originally wanted to leave this place in the next few days and go to the main continent to roam around. In the end, before he could move, a silly Grand Yan Immortal barged into his array.","Then, under the interference of his Thought power, he let Madman Yang walk into the cave he was in and directly used his Heart power to control him.","Although he was also ranked in the top 100 of the original planet, he did not know much about the actual battlefields on the original planet.","With a thought, Madman Yang came directly in front of him.","At this moment, Madman Yang was sitting cross-legged opposite Jian Wushuang with a dull look in his eyes.","“Let me ask you, how much do you know about the main continent?” Jian Wushuang waved his hand and a long table appeared in front of him. On it were some rare fruits and a pot of wine.","All of these were obtained from God-Emperor MO Long. This fellow had an Emperor as his father and a territory comparable to a medium-grade world under his control.","It was not an exaggeration to say that he was an Emperor. As an Emperor, it was normal for him to have all kinds of rare treasures, strange fruits, and fine wine.","Jian Wushuang poured himself a glass of wine and drank it calmly. The light fragrance of the wine made him feel refreshed. After drinking it, he felt light and light. It seemed that the wine was refined from a large number of exotic fruits.","It was good to be the master of a force!","All kinds of treasures were offered, but Jian Wushuang had never even smelled this kind of wine. After all, this pot of wine could probably be exchanged for an ordinary treasure in the outside world. Jian Wushuang wasn’t that extravagant.","Although Madman Yang was unconscious, he still swallowed his saliva and replied stiffly, “Continent? Is it the Feather Continent?”","“Yes!” Jian Wushuang nodded. He had heard MO Long mention the Feather Continent before. At that time, he had wanted to ask MO Long about the situation in the Feather Continent. However, he remembered that MO Long had just recovered from his injuries and had not gone to the Feather Continent for a long time. That was the main battlefield. It was different every day.","“Oh right, why is that continent called the Feather Continent?” Jian Wushuang asked curiously.","When they had just arrived at the original planet, it had been deathly silent. They did not know anything about this planet. How did that continent have a name and everyone recognized it?","“That continent was derived from a feather. Dao Lord Xue Yue called it Feather Continent, and everyone followed suit.”","A feather?","Jian Wushuangs eyes narrowed and he exclaimed in shock, “A feather? How could it be so big?!”","A feather the size of a continent, and it was 10 percent the size of the entire original planet. Regardless of where the feather fell from, that existence had to be very large.","This wasn’t the manifestation of some magical heavenly law. This was truly the size of a feather that had fallen off.","That existence’s body was probably comparable to a miniature world. He had never heard of such a huge body.. Even a tier 5 Emperor would find it difficult","to do such a thing!"]},{"number":5197,"title":"Chapter 5197: Dao Lord","paragraphs":["Chapter 5197: Dao Lord","Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","How strong was this body? Although he had never seen the true form of a Special Life Form with a body 10,000 times stronger than his, he had heard that when a Special Life Form reached the Perfected Nine Revolutions stage, its true form would cover the sky and the sun. The largest one was only a few hundred thousand miles in size. An Emperor like Chishui should be tens of millions of miles or even hundreds of millions of miles.","However, the Feather Transformation Continent was too huge. Even a Perfected Nine Revolutions would need four hours to cross the Feather Transformation Continent.","A single feather was already so big. The true body of that existence... He simply did not dare to imagine it.","How powerful must the divine body be to have such a large body? Or rather, that existence was an expert that surpassed the Emperor.","Jian Wushuang waited for Madman Yangs answer with some anticipation, but the result was not satisfactory.","“l don’t know!” Madman Yang replied emotionlessly.","It was not too strange. For people like them, if they wanted to understand the origin of the feather, they had to enter the core of the Qishen Temple through their strength. Only then would they be qualified to know who the owner of the feather was and how powerful he was.","However, it was too difficult to enter the core. In the end, only the first few people would be able to enter the Qishen Temple!","The more he thought about it, the further away Jian Wushuang shook his head and waved his hand.","“Forget it, let’s talk about the current situation in the Feather Continent!”","This time, Madman Yangs answer was very fast. Obviously, these things were deeply imprinted in his mind.","Jian Wushuang listened attentively. He never expected that so many strange things would happen in the small Feather Continent.","Especially when he heard that four of the six Princes of the Daluo Realm had died in a day.","There were also two unfamiliar names that suddenly appeared in the top 100. These two people seemed to have appeared out of thin air and suddenly appeared in the top 100.","Most importantly, they could not find these two people on the Feather Continent. They all felt that there was a problem with the Qishen Temple. They all shouted at the Qishen Temple on the only Holy Mountain on the Feather Continent to explain.","They had been fighting desperately, but in the end, two strangers suddenly appeared in the top 100, and they could not find these two people.","There were only a few hundred thousand experts in the Feather Continent. In such a small place, they would see each other all day long. They were all very familiar with each other. They all felt that this matter was very ridiculous.","There were even rumors that a Three Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal had entered the original planet and was lucky enough to encounter the collective suicide of the four princes of the Daluo Realm. Only by picking up these identity tokens of the top 1,000 experts could he enter the top 100.","There were actually people who believed such a ridiculous rumor. Those who believed it were mostly top-grade Nine Revolutions. Under the circumstances of survival of the fittest, it was very difficult for them to enter the top 1,000.","They all had the mentality of giving it a try and entered the mountain range to find that mysterious Three Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal. In the end, after a year, they did not find anything and returned empty-handed. After all, time was precious.","“Tell me about the distribution of experts on the Feather Continent.” The more Jian Wushuang listened, the more ridiculous he thought things had become. He didn’t want gossip, but information about experts.","It seemed that Madman Yang was daydreaming. Jian Wushuang was speechless.","However, he did not know how crazy those experts were. They tried their very best, even risking their lives to get into the topo 1,000. However, they did not have the strength to enter the top 1,000 and could only daydream and talk about it every day.","“Powerhouses!” Madman Yangs expression changed, and he told the truth about the experts of the entire Feather Continent.","There were five invincible experts in the Feather Continent.","Each of them could be conferred the title of ‘Dao Lord’ in the outside world.","The Feather Continent was divided into five regions due to these five individuals. While other powerful beings could freely traverse, these five invincible experts were bound by a rule they themselves established.","They were restricted to hunting within their respective regions and were not allowed to venture into others.","In the central hunting grounds of Yuhua, it was the domain of “Blood Moon Dao Lord.’","In the northern region, the second-ranked ‘PO Jun’ held sway.","In the southern region, the third-ranked Dao Lord Leng Shuang ruled.","In the eastern region, the fourth-ranked ‘Dao Lord Si Tian’ presided.","In the western region, the fifth-ranked ‘Dao Lord Wan Xing held authority.","Their rankings were closely contested, often changing, but their positions remained unchallenged. The fame they had in the early days was forged through significant battles.","Outside, their true strengths were mostly unknown, but in the ooriginal planet, they became figures of great interest.","Their rankings were connected to their abilities. Dao Lord Xue Yue held the first position due to his unique Special Life Form characteristics; his innate secret technique was a blood moon, doubling his speed. No prey he targeted could escape him, making him unassailable in his top spot.","The lowest-ranked among them, ‘Dao Lord Wan Xing, was the Prince of the Xingluo Realm, exceptionally gifted and the Chief Prince of his realm.","The Xingluo, Daluo, and Tianluo Realms were actually one force. This was also the reason why the Princes of the Daluo Realm were so confident.","Unfortunately, Dao Lord Wan Xing was not interested in them at all. However, those Daluo Realm princes were relentless, causing havoc in the western region.","Among the three higher worlds, Tianluo Realm was the highest and was named ‘Daluo Heaven’.","This faction was highly united externally; even when entering the Qishen Temple, the Emperor had instructed them not to harm each other.","Myriad Stars Dao Lord had lofty ambitions and couldn’t care less about the Daluo princes. He pursued the ultimate. Initially, he couldn’t progress further due to his strength. But now, thanks to the Qishen Temple, he could comprehend the origin source of the Qishen, boosting his strength again. There was hope he could reach the level of a half-step Emperor.","With the strength of a half-step Emperor, his chances of merging the Dao would increase. More importantly, he could gain the experience of merging the Dao from the Qishen Temple or some secret Dao merging technique.","During the Age of Ancient Anticipation, dozens of Emperors suddenly emerged, which was evidence. The Qishen Temple likely held something significant to aid in merging the Dao.","These talented Dao Lords, each with grand ambitions, aimed beyond just being tier 3 Emperors. Their goal was tier 4, even tier 5.","Without this kind of ambition, it was better to choose a fourth-grade origin and merge the Dao. Even if they became Emperors, they would be the weakest among them.","Apart from these Dao Lords, the Feather Continent also harbored individual powerful individuals. Each of them could evade the Dao Lords and had no fear of their threats, freely slaughtering other Grand Yan Immortals.","Each of these experts was ranked in the top 20.","On the Feather Continent.","If the first tier of experts were Dao Lords, then the second tier consisted of the remaining 15 extreme-level Grand Yan Immortals who managed to rank in the top 20. Each of them had touched the threshold of becoming a Dao Lord; their strength was only a step away.","While these Dao Lords remained aloof, not leaving their designated regions, these extreme-level Grand Yan Immortals, on the brink of becoming Dao Lords, were not bound by such restrictions. They could freely slaughter in any region.."]},{"number":5198,"title":"Chapter 5198 Dao Lord Wan Xing","paragraphs":["5198 Dao Lord Wan Xing","So Madman Yang feared these individuals the most. Once they sensed that terrifying aura, they would either flee desperately or conceal their presence as much as possible.","The third-tier Grand Yan Immortals were equally fearsome. They were all extreme-level Grand Yan Immortals who operated independently. Fortunately, there weren't many of these powerful beings, just a few dozen or so.bender","Generally speaking, in the Feather Continent, the true hunters were the extreme-level Grand Yan Immortals of the upper echelons. Each one of them ranked in the top 100, possessing unimaginable strength. Over the many years of warfare, only a few extreme-level Grand Yan Immortals had fallen, and they were unfortunate enough to encounter Dao Lord Xue Yue.","Several extreme-level Grand Yan Immortals had died at the hands of Xue Yue, including one who had touched the threshold of Dao Lord and had directly challenged Xue Yue. In the end, he was slain in the central region at the Falling Moon Divine Mountain.","This incident marked the most powerful Grand Yan Immortal to have fallen on this original planet until now.","With this achievement, Dao Lord Xue Yue ascended to rank 1 and maintained it since then.","On the Universe Deity-Demon List, nearly all the top 1,000 were Dao Lords, and the top two 200 were mostly half-step Emperors. His rankings were consistently high. However, on this original planet, the highest rank on the Universe Deity-Demon List didn't belong to him. It belonged to a remarkably low-key figure, 'Daoist Wan Xing', an unparalleled expert who cultivated the path of myriad origin source Daos.","He was ranked at 208, second only to the half-step Emperors in existence.","Despite his terrifying strength, he remained extremely low-key on this original planet. His rank was the lowest among the five Dao Lords, a fact that Jian Wushuang remembered well. All the information about these individuals was precious, especially since they practiced such profound arts, which made it convenient for him to escape.","Dao Lord Wan Xing, stronger even than Jiu Yu, outpaced Blood Moon Daoist, who was the top speedster on the original planet.","The danger posed by these two individuals was exaggerated, to say the least. One found himself trapped with no escape, while the other lacked the courage to face the confrontation.","In the entire universe, ranked among the top 200 super-strong beings, there was only a step separating them from the half-step Emperor, the Grand Yan Immortal who unified myriad Daos.","Aside from these individuals, Jian Wushuang also meticulously recorded information about those peak-level Grand Yan Immortals. Although the threat from ordinary peak-level Grand Yan Immortals was minimal, he deemed it necessary to keep a record.","Because on the Feather Continent, the most significant enemies were precisely these peak-level Grand Yan Immortals.","Some of these peak-level Grand Yan Immortals preferred a solitary and secluded existence, while others shamelessly formed groups, specifically targeting teams composed of common Nine Revolutions cultivators, numbering three to five people.","On the Feather Continent, below the level of peak-level Grand Yan Immortals, there were hardly any individuals traveling alone. Most of them gathered in groups of ten or more strong cultivators.","Madman Yang and his team had been adventuring in the Western Region because there were fewer peak-level Grand Yan Immortals there. The quality of their team was high; each member was a top- tier Grand Yan Immortal. Comprising nine individuals, they fought far and wide, gaining considerable renown.","However, precisely because of this, they dared to provoke a peak- level Grand Yan Immortal, ultimately depleting half of their origin source in the battle.","\"So, how many achievement points have you gained in total?\" Jian Wushuang said slowly, his eyes revealing a hint of murderous intent.?????????.???","Madman Yang's achievement points now determined his fate. If the number was high, he would be killed; if it was low, he might be spared. A lunatic who had depleted half of his origin source energy, Jian Wushuang couldn't absorb much from him. Considering the valuable information he had provided, sparing his life was not out of the question.","\"97,000!\" Madman Yang said, his voice stiff.","\"So little!\" Jian Wushuang raised an eyebrow. He had battled in the main continent for many years. With such a meager record, even preserving the last 10,000 spots after the trial would be challenging. But considering he fought alongside eight others, he understood. His expression softened as he mused, \"But I guess you got lucky. If you had surpassed a million, I wouldn't have spared you.\"","Setting a clear limit in his mind, he decided he would kill anyone who reached over a million points, but spare those just below, even if the difference was as small as 30,000.","That was Jian Wushuang's current state of mind.","\"Alright, think of anything else interesting,\" Jian Wushuang said, enjoying himself from above, reveling in food and drink.","He hadn't relaxed like this in a long time. Ever since he entered the Great Desolate Wilderness, his life had been a constant struggle - either he was working hard, escaping, breaking through, practicing, feeling lost, or engaging in deadly battles.","Now, every sip and every bite greatly improved his mental state, boosting his confidence in reaching the fifth level of Heart power. \"Yes!\"","\"On the Feathered Continent, there are many alliances formed by weaker individuals. They're elites from some major forces, banding together. Several Dao Lords have tacitly agreed not to attack them.\"","\"Such a bizarre situation!\" Jian Wushuang sneered. He had a premonition that these people would be slaughtered like pigs in the coming years.","What was the Qishen Temple? It was the greatest opportunity in the entire Original Universe. Even Emperors went crazy for it, let alone these Grand Yan Immortals.","Which Dao Lord wouldn't want to successfully merge their Dao and become rank 1? Even if they offended major powers, what did it matter? If they succeeded in merging their Dao and achieved the tier 4 Emperor status, who would be afraid of those major powers?","Everyone beneath an Emperor was insignificant. No one would risk offending a tier 4 Emperor for their sake.","Did these people foolishly believe they could do as they pleased?","When the time came, and the Dao Lords intervened and killed those like pigs, dealing with them all at once would be much quicker than chasing down each peak-level Grand Yan Immortal one by one.","The Qishen Temple had been open for six years now. From millions of Grand Yan Immortals, only a few remained. If everyone was as timid as these people, how many would survive?","According to Madman Yang's words, there were still 300,000 Grand Yan Immortal powerhouses in the Feather Continent. Along with the 100,000 or so hidden in the mountains, in just six years, at least 2 million Grand Yan Immortals had died on the original planet.","His record of over 40 million battle points only ranked him 72nd. Those in the top 10 must have had billions of points. How many Grand Yan Immortals did they have to kill? Even if they managed to kill a few perfected Nine Revolutions, it wouldn't inflate their points 3to this extent.","And this ranking was from three years ago. He must have long fallen out of the top 100 by now.","Two million was an underestimate. When he obtained the identity token, he glanced at it briefly. There were three million Grand Yan Immortals on the original planet. Now, he roughly estimated that there were fewer than 500,000 left. Over two and a half million Grand Yan Immortals had died!","Calculating the ratio of Perfected Nine Revolutions, converted to points, that was in the hundreds of billions.","Especially in the first three years, the madness was extraordinary. At that time, when Hu Qing killed Luo Hao, Luo Hao barely made it into the top 1,000 with just a million battle points.","But now, even with a million points, you couldn't make it into the top 2,000. When the last few years of madness truly arrived, even the top ten thousand couldn't be held.","According to his current calculations, entering the top 1,000 required 5 million battle records, entering the top 100 needed 50 million or more, the top ten required 500 million, and the top five needed over a billion.","However, the crazier, the better. The higher the tier of Grand Yan Immortals he killed, the more his points multiplied.","As long as he killed ten peak-level Grand Yan Immortals, he could firmly sit in first place. Five billion battle record points, even if he couldn't kill Dao Lord Xue Yue, it wouldn't matter."]},{"number":5199,"title":"Chapter 5199: Monster Monk","paragraphs":["Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","The first layer of the Transcendent Immortal Formation was perfected, tripling the power of the sword formation. Originally, with nine phantom illusory swords, he could threaten a peak-level Grand Yan Immortal. With Hu Qings restraint, he managed to kill Mi Luo.","Now, his power had tripled. Facing a peak-level Grand Yan Immortal alone should not pose much difficulty.","However, he set a deadline for himself – 20 years. He had to return to the mountain range after 20 years of conquest. 20 years later, with only three to four years left until the trial ended, the various Dao Lords would definitely settle scores with them.","The ranking on this original planet alone didn’t prove anything. They had to strive for a higher overall ranking.","Of course, this was just Jian Wushuangs speculation.","<font < div>","Whether there were any hidden rules inside the Qishen Temple, no one knew. But everyone wanted to perform well in front of the Qishen Temple. Jian Wushuang put away the scrolls in front of him, stood up slowly, and activated the treasure that suppressed his aura. He became virtually undetectable, with no trace of his presence discernible to the naked eye.","“You’re lucky this time. I’ll spare your life,” he said.","Madman Yang seemed to understand something. A glimmer of light flashed in his dazed eyes.","“Oh, right, when you enter the Feather Continent, you must join an organization. It’s highly beneficial.”","Jian Wushuang raised an eyebrow. Join an organization?","He hadn’t thought about that. With his strength in the Feather Continent, he had reached a point where he didn’t need to team up with anyone. He didn’t need to ally with anyone and be restricted by others.","“Why?” Jian Wushuang asked lightly.","“Three years ago, in the western part of the Feather Continent, a monk suddenly appeared. His strength was incredibly formidable. He single-handedly wiped out several top-tier squads. However, he didn’t kill anyone; he just took their identity tokens without even seizing their treasures.”","Madman Yang spoke with a quivering voice. “This monk leader is known as the Monster Monk. His power rivals the extreme-level, and he keeps getting stronger. He has reached the level of Dao Lord, and even the peak Grand Yan Immortals in the Feather Continent are banding together. The Monster Monk is terrifying; he rampages through the domain of the five Dao Lords, sweeping through with the efficiency of a Dao Lord and the strength to match.”","Madman Yangs voice trembled as he spoke.","Their squad had once watched from afar as the Monster Monk swept through peak-level Grand Yan Immortals. With a long staff, he caused the heavens and earth to change color, defeating several extreme-level Grand Yan Immortals effortlessly.","“Monster Monk?” Jian Wushuang furrowed his brows and quickly took out his identity token to check.","Participant: Hu Qing","Rank: 16","Jian Wushuang inhaled sharply, hardly believing what he saw.","When he and Hu Qing had parted ways, Hu Qings strength was comparable to a Grand Yan Immortal touching the threshold of the extreme-level. How did he become a Dao Lord so quickly?","Hadn’t he just broken through the Nine Revolutions?","Even if he was a Grand Yan Immortal with the Ultimate Dao, at most, he would reach the strength of an extreme-level Grand Yan Immortal. Could it be that he had achieved the Perfected Nine Revolutions level?","Jian Wushuang bit his lip. He knew Hu Qing harbored a great secret, but he hadn’t expected him to be this powerful. He had become so formidable right after Jian Wushuang left.","In just three years, he had made it into the top 20. Hu Qings goal was probably to reach the top 10, maybe even seize victory from the Dao Lords.","However, if he had truly achieved Perfected Nine Revolutions, it would be difficult for him to strive for first place. If he remained at the level of a Nine Revolutions, his chances were significant. After all, he could obtain double the achievement points just by fighting above his cultivation level.","“Where is he now?” Jian Wushuang couldn’t help but ask.","Although they were peers in cultivation, Hu Qings sudden breakthrough was different from Jian Wushuangs steady progress toward the peak.","Even though Hu Qing had practiced for 30 million years, he had not reached the Grand Yan Immortal level before entering the Great Desolate Wilderness. In the end, during his battle against Xiang Bingyun, he had erupted, stepping directly into the Dao, directly challenging the Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal.","At that time, his path was still uncertain. Now, it seems he has completely mastered the Ultimate Dao, which explains his extraordinary power.","Jian Wushuang was different. He had endured trials in life and death for over 20,000 years, progressing from weakness to strength. He walked the path of gods, annihilated god dynasties, received assistance from Xuan Yi, and eventually entered the Great Si Region, receiving many gifts from Emperors.","He barely managed to become an extreme-level Grand Yan Immortal. This was the result of his efforts over two millennia. After entering the vast Great Desolate Wilderness, he awakened his Heart power, practiced in the starry sky for millions of years, mastered the Extreme Dao, and truly took off after that.","He constantly broke through, and within a decade, he possessed the strength of a peak-level Grand Yan Immortal.","But all of this was built on the foundation of over 20,000 years, combined with the special place he practiced in the starry sky for millions of years.","Now, Hu Qing, with just a step or two, had surpassed him significantly, making it difficult for him to accept.","Could it be that Hu Qing had also entered the starry sky at some moment and practiced for millions of years?","The likelihood of this was very low. If Hu Qing had entered the starry sky, he would have at least mastered the Extreme Dao. Yet, Jian Wushuang did not sense any similar aura from Hu Qing.","Apart from these possibilities, only one remained.","Hu Qing was the chosen child of the Qishen Temple!","Qishen Temple was secretly nurturing Hu Qing. The thought left Jian Wushuang even more puzzled.","In all fairness, his talent was not bad. Why didn’t Qishen Temple nurture him?","Or was it that his ability to awaken Heart power and master the Extreme Dao was all because of Qishen Temple?","Jian Wushuang fell into contemplation.","Unbeknownst to him, the true spirit of the Qishen Temple had already pronounced his fate, deeming his future short-lived and not worth investing","in.","Indeed, the temple held greater hope for Hu Qing. Among all the Grand Yan Immortals, Hu Qings talent ranked among the top 10, making him a key candidate for the temple’s nurturing.","Jian Wushuang and others were merely stepping stones for these chosen successors!","Hu Qing was averse to bloodshed, but the others were not. For the sake of these successors, it seemed likely that 90 percent of the Grand Yan Immortals in the entire universe would have to be sacrificed.","Grand Yan Immortals were not Emperors. With each era passing, new Grand Yan Immortals would rise like mushrooms after rain.","Emperors might require more time, but for the Qishen Temple, these matters were inconsequential.","Having comprehended the temple’s intentions, Jian Wushuang involuntarily emitted an aura of malevolence.","The true spirit, despite his formidable strength, was still just a true spirit. They viewed the inhabitants of the Original Universe as creatures to be cultivated, and Jian Wushuang could take this opportunity to transform himself. It was a mutually beneficial arrangement.","If Jian Wushuang were to perish in the end, the true spirit would cheer in victory. Even if he managed to survive without perishing, they could still absorb him into their peripheral forces.","No matter how one looked at it, the true spirit had everything to gain.","However, it all depended on whether Jian Wushuang agreed or not. In the next moment, Jian Wushuangs form reversed, and the malevolent aura transformed into black lightning that surrounded him. It occasionally collided, producing crackling sounds.","This aura filled Madman Yang with fear, forcing him to retreat involuntarily.","Jian Wushuang pierced through the rocks, his gaze penetrating the entire original planet. With a swift movement, he disappeared into the depths of the mountain cave.","At that moment, Madman Yang, left behind in the same spot, regained his senses.."]},{"number":5200,"title":"Chapter 5200: Ren Yinjiu","paragraphs":["Chapter 5200: Ren Yinjiu","Translator: EndlessFantasy Translation Editor: EndlessFantasy Translation","“Huff huff! ”","Madman Yang panted heavily. After his eyes returned to normal, a string of memories appeared in his mind and instantly churned in his mind.","The memory fragments made his back break out in cold sweat!","“I actually encountered such a powerful existence and survived! He couldn’t believe it.","Madman Yang, whose body was a little weak, tried to sense his surroundings. When he found that the existence had left, he let out a sigh of relief. Then, he immediately rushed out of the mountain range and changed directions. After changing seven or eight places, he landed on a quiet mountain.","Although Jian Wushuang had said that he had let him go, he was still afraid that Jian Wushuang would suddenly go back on his word. He had survived with great difficulty and he did not want to die without knowing why.","That existence could be a super expert who could be controlled. He did not even need to do anything to kill him. He could just order him to destroy his own origin source.","He had encountered such a legendary being today. He was lucky to be able to survive.","After entering a cave, he took a long time to recover. Then, he remembered that this existence had gone to the Feather Continent and hurriedly informed his sworn brothers in the Feather Continent.","“Big Brother, be careful of this person...”","Jian Wushuang didn’t travel very fast after he set off from the mountain range. It took him half a day to leave the mountain range.","Along the way, he did not encounter a single living person. He did not know if it was his bad luck or the others who were too lucky.","Although the mountain range was not as crazy as the Feather Continent, there were still many battles.","Especially at the periphery of the mountain range, a checkpoint had been set up.","“Fellow Daoist, are you heading to the Feather Continent?” Above a dry riverbed outside the mountain range stood a scholar-like Grand Yan Immortal. His aura was gentle and his speech was extraordinary.","If they were in the outside world, Jian Wushuang really wanted to sit down and have a good discussion with him.","However, this was the original planet. After more than six years of killing, none of the survivors were easy to talk to.","Even a person like Hu Qing was conferred the title of Monster Monk, let alone this pale-faced scholar in front of him.","Other people might not be able to see through it, but Jian Wushuang could sense the strong resentment and murderous aura from his body with his Thought power. The two auras were suppressed by the pale-faced scholar. If it was anyone else, even top-grade-level Grand Evolution Immortals would be difficult to see through the hidden aura in his body.","Jian Wushuang was not in a hurry to meet such a person as soon as he left the mountain range. He wanted to see what tricks the other party was playing.","“That’s right!” Jian Wushuang cupped his fists.","The aura he emitted gave people the feeling that he was at most a top-grade Nine Revolutions. This strength was considered basic combat strength in the Feather Continent.","“That’s great. I am Ren Yinjiu, and I have just left the mountain range. I want to go to the Feather Continent. Fellow Daoist, you must travel together. You can also travel together on the road. I heard that many experts could not survive in the Feather Continent, so they formed teams outside the mountain range to block the cultivators who were heading to the Feather Continent.”","Ren Yinjiu’s words were perfect. He made it clear that it was his first time leaving the mountain range and he was not as ruthless as the Grand Yan Immortals on the Feather Continent. He also threatened Jian Wushuang that it was best to be in a group if there were people blocking him on the way.","Otherwise, he would not die much if he went to the Feather Continent alone.","This move was good enough to trick a novice monk like Hu Qing, but it was a child’s play to trick Jian Wushuang. Did he really think that he was a fledgling and still wet behind the ears?","They were all Grand Yan Immortals, how could there be so many idiots?!","However, when he thought of the two Grand Yan Immortals in the Great Dream Realm, Jian Wushuang was not so sure. The Original Universe was so big, so there might really be many fools.","“Oh, I see!” Jian Wushuang looked surprised and timid.","It gave Ren Yinjiu a misconception. Moreover, Jian Wushuang had a good grasp of his aura. He wanted to hide it but leaked it out. He would be able to discern the aura of a top-tier Grand Evolution Immortal, let alone a peak-level Grand Evolution Immortal.","Following that, the two of them began to discuss the Feather Continent.","Ren Yinjiu was overjoyed. He secretly thought that he had caught a fish and started to ask about Jian Wushuang’s name.","“Brother Ren, I won’t hide the truth. My ranking has just entered the top 100,000. I came to the Feathered Continent this time to take a chance, seize an opportunity. After all, such opportunities are rare!” Jian Wushuang confessed truthfully.","He wasn’t lying; this trip to the Feathered Continent was indeed about taking a chance, hoping for a stroke of luck. It was also a chance to overshadow those Dao Lords a bit.","His ranking in the top 100,000 was also accurate. He was currently ranked around 100, truly within the top 100,000.","But Ren Yinjiu’s name was a mystery. Jian Wushuang scoured the rankings and finally found him. His record was a meager rank 10,000, placing him at the bottom.","This surprised Jian Wushuang. Were these people now looking for individuals with clean backgrounds? Or perhaps, Ren Yinjiu was a fraud?","From their conversation, Jian Wushuang learned that Ren Yinjiu had already recruited a few like-minded Grand Yan Immortals. He was still looking for a","few more, scattered around, recruiting Grand Yan Immortals emerging from the mountains.","As he explained, the mountains had been sealed off by an extremely powerful force on the Feather Continent a month ago. Going out was possible, but without strength, getting in was impossible. Those weak enough to venture out usually ended up dead; survival was nearly impossible. Those wanting to get in were mostly injured or desperate. The top 10,000 had no hope; staying in the Feather Continent was just benefiting others. Leaving sooner was a better choice.","However, there were far more trying to get in than those leaving. It seemed the power dynamics on the Feather Continent had undergone significant changes.","After all, there were only 10,000 slots. Apart from the top 1,000 peak-level experts, there were 9,000 slots left. After years of screening, those who had persevered were, at the very least, Perfected Nine Revolutions. These Grand Yan Immortals gathered together, forming battle formations of thousands. Even extreme-level Grand Yan Immortals found them troublesome to deal with.","While they had the strength to protect themselves, eliminating others was challenging. After all, it was a battle formation. Once they mobilized, pursuing and killing other Grand Yan Immortals became nearly impossible.","Among these individuals was a prominent figure who devised a brilliant plan: no battle formation could exceed a thousand people. By forming hundreds of battle formations and engaging in chaotic battles, in the end, the last remaining 1,000 people could enter the top 10,000.","This person was none other than the ‘Priest Shuiyue’, who had entered the top 1,000 with the strength of a Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortal. Now, his ranking wasn’t low either. If his battle formation could endure until the end, he might indeed enter the top 1,000.","Jian Wushuang couldn’t help but admire Priest Shuiyue. He thought, what a waste it would be if this man didn’t rear Gu Worms.","“I never expected Brother Ren to be so knowledgeable about the various wonders of the Feather Continent. I am truly enlightened!” Jian Wushuang truly hadn’t heard of this before. When he asked Madman Yang, his inquiries mainly concerned top-tier experts; he had never cared about ordinary Perfected Nine Revolutions Grand Yan Immortals.."]}]);
